ypography scale, elevation, and shape system.\n- Enhanced accessibility features including color contrast and typography adjustments.\n- Documented component composition patterns for banking card layout and transaction items.\n\nfeat: Implement shared-lib package for Axios and Zustand integration\n\n- Created a new package `@nab/shared-lib` to manage Axios instance and Zustand global store.\n- Defined tasks for creating package skeleton, Zustand slices for authentication, UI state, and notifications.\n- Implemented Axios instance with silent refresh logic for token management.\n- Ensured single instance of shared-lib across micro-frontend applications.\n\nfeat: Establish shared-utils package for common utilities and hooks\n\n- Created `@nab/shared-utils` package containing pure functions and React hooks for shared use.\n- Implemented formatting, validation, constants, API helpers, storage, security utilities, and common hooks.\n- Ensured all functions are pure with no side effects, suitable for use across the monorepo.\n\nstyle: Add design tokens for Material Design 3 in shared-ui\n\n- Introduced a new SCSS file for design tokens including surface colors, elevation, color palette, typography scale, and spacing system.\n- Established mixins for typography and elevation to streamline component styling.","tree":{"sha":"2a91a5e4d8313e27c88e2b371a94c0f98c4aa4e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/strangerdeveloper2810/Interview-NAB/git/trees/2a91a5e4d8313e27c88e2b371a94c0f98c4aa4e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/strangerdeveloper2810/Interview-NAB/git/commits/5b6ac2f06e65a01f1952c90fad54dab33879c663","verification":{"payload":"tree 2a91a5e4d8313e27c88e2b371a94c0f98c4aa4e1\nparent 1a6b774e5c6e692f8d61115be33b42e46ba1d65d\nauthor Ethan Nguyen <nguyenmaster3012@gmail.com> 1774411404 +0700\ncommitter Ethan Nguyen <nguyenmaster3012@gmail.com> 1774411404 +0700\n\nfeat: Add Material Design 3 transformation documentation for NAB Banking Portal\n\n- Introduced a new design system document detailing the transformation from a casual to a professional banking interface.\n- Updated component APIs for Card, AccountCard, Alert, Button, and Transaction components to align with Material Design 3 standards.\n- Created a design token system including color palette, typography scale, elevation, and shape system.\n- Enhanced accessibility features including color contrast and typography adjustments.\n- Documented component composition patterns for banking card layout and transaction items.\n\nfeat: Implement shared-lib package for Axios and Zustand integration\n\n- Created a new package `@nab/shared-lib` to manage Axios instance and Zustand global store.\n- Defined tasks for creating package skeleton, Zustand slices for authentication, UI state, and notifications.\n- Implemented Axios instance with silent refresh logic for token management.\n- Ensured single instance of shared-lib across micro-frontend applications.\n\nfeat: Establish shared-utils package for common utilities and hooks\n\n- Created `@nab/shared-utils` package containing pure functions and React hooks for shared use.\n- Implemented formatting, validation, constants, API helpers, storage, security utilities, and common hooks.\n- Ensured all functions are pure with no side effects, suitable for use across the monorepo.\n\nstyle: Add design tokens for Material Design 3 in shared-ui\n\n- Introduced a new SCSS file for design tokens including surface colors, elevation, color palette, typography scale, and spacing system.\n- Established mixins for typography and elevation to streamline component styling.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgP1cZd2BASKRmoHU6VJzQ88XpBe\ntOgzWqT01gpbdr200AAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQELQ1RmtGL0b/QNdY0Kk4JVuLIMxpxCUAwaofKIrbA3J+WSBCPmZSi70P/8PV9f8j5\nQUoX7wUwLxug3N0YKHTQI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T22:20:35Z"}}