s://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/doicovSanya","id":264966161,"login":"doicovSanya","node_id":"U_kgDOD8sQEQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/143954341f8e9000cdede6056bcd3cb5becb8120/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T05:47:42Z","email":"Alexandr.Doicov@carasent.com","name":"doicovSanya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T05:47:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: ASMA-8176 make the badge dot usable on its own and add the unread/filter dot (#238)\n\n* feat: ASMA-8176 add StyledBadgeDot for standalone notification dots\n\nStyledBadge anchors its dot to the corner of a host it wraps, so a dot with no\nhost collapsed onto a zero-width root. Seventeen call sites worked around that\nby hand-rolling an 8px gama-400 circle, which matches neither the documented\nsize nor the documented colours.\n\nStyledBadgeDot renders the same 12px lime circle and 2px Badge/border-dot ring\nin normal flow, so table cells and row markers can use the design system\nwithout rebuilding it. It is aria-hidden by default like the anchored dot, with\nan opt-in ariaLabel for the standalone case where no host carries the state.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* refactor: ASMA-8176 keep the hostless badge dot in flow instead of adding a component\n\nFigma models the dot as a Badge variant (Size=Dot), not a separate component,\nand StyledBadge already had variant=''dot''. Splitting it into StyledBadgeDot\nduplicated that surface for what is really a layout bug.\n\nThe dot is positioned absolutely against the host it decorates, so a badge with\nno children collapses to a 0x0 root. Measured in Chromium: the dot still paints\n12x12, but reserves 0px between its siblings and overlaps both of them. That is\nwhy consumers hand-rolled their own circle rather than use the component.\n\nA dot with no children now renders in normal flow and keeps its 12px box. With\nchildren it anchors to a corner exactly as before, and counts are untouched.\nAn aria-label on a hostless dot is exposed via role=img so the state is not\ncarried by colour alone; without one it stays hidden, like the anchored dot.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* feat: ASMA-8176 add the unread/filter dot from Figma''s Parent axis\n\nFigma''s Badge is one component set with a Parent axis, and we only implemented\nParent=Notification. The 8px solid gama/500-primary dot used for unread items\nand active filters is Parent=Unread / Parent=Filter, which is why it did not\nfit the 12px ringed notification dot and got hand-rolled instead.\n\npurpose=''unread'' and purpose=''filter'' render it. The two are identical in Figma\nand differ only in meaning, so the choice documents why the dot is there. It\napplies to dots; a count badge is always the notification pill.\n\nclassName now applies to the root of a hostless dot. On the inner span it would\nplace the dot inside its own 8px box, which is never what a caller positioning\na dot means. `relative` moves with it, since it only exists to anchor an\nabsolutely positioned badge and would otherwise fight a caller''s `absolute`.\n\nReplaces the `size-2 rounded-full bg-gama-400` circle repeated across the apps,\nwhich was also one shade too light.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* fix: ASMA-8176 correct badge dot class order and add the new VRT baselines\n\neslint flagged ''absolute top-1 right-1'' in the new story and test; Tailwind''s\nclass order puts right before top. No rendering change.\n\nAdds the two missing baselines for the StandaloneDot and UnreadAndFilterDots\nstories, taken from the CI run''s captures so they come from the same pinned\nPlaywright container that compares them. The existing badge baselines are\nuntouched, including Default, which still matches after the flow change.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"8444aec67f93493164b3a7fcf7d6e936c70be242","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/8444aec67f93493164b3a7fcf7d6e936c70be242"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/143954341f8e9000cdede6056bcd3cb5becb8120","verification":{"payload":"tree 8444aec67f93493164b3a7fcf7d6e936c70be242\nparent ecce9727292acc4ff232044605c2aac64c2e263d\nauthor doicovSanya <Alexandr.Doicov@carasent.com> 1791265662 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791265662 +0300\n\nfeat: ASMA-8176 make the badge dot usable on its own and add the unread/filter dot (#238)\n\n* feat: ASMA-8176 add StyledBadgeDot for standalone notification dots\n\nStyledBadge anchors its dot to the corner of a host it wraps, so a dot with no\nhost collapsed onto a zero-width root. Seventeen call sites worked around that\nby hand-rolling an 8px gama-400 circle, which matches neither the documented\nsize nor the documented colours.\n\nStyledBadgeDot renders the same 12px lime circle and 2px Badge/border-dot ring\nin normal flow, so table cells and row markers can use the design system\nwithout rebuilding it. It is aria-hidden by default like the anchored dot, with\nan opt-in ariaLabel for the standalone case where no host carries the state.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* refactor: ASMA-8176 keep the hostless badge dot in flow instead of adding a component\n\nFigma models the dot as a Badge variant (Size=Dot), not a separate component,\nand StyledBadge already had variant=''dot''. Splitting it into StyledBadgeDot\nduplicated that surface for what is really a layout bug.\n\nThe dot is positioned absolutely against the host it decorates, so a badge with\nno children collapses to a 0x0 root. Measured in Chromium: the dot still paints\n12x12, but reserves 0px between its siblings and overlaps both of them. That is\nwhy consumers hand-rolled their own circle rather than use the component.\n\nA dot with no children now renders in normal flow and keeps its 12px box. With\nchildren it anchors to a corner exactly as before, and counts are untouched.\nAn aria-label on a hostless dot is exposed via role=img so the state is not\ncarried by colour alone; without one it stays hidden, like the anchored dot.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* feat: ASMA-8176 add the unread/filter dot from Figma''s Parent axis\n\nFigma''s Badge is one component set with a Parent axis, and we only implemented\nParent=Notification. The 8px solid gama/500-primary dot used for unread items\nand active filters is Parent=Unread / Parent=Filter, which is why it did not\nfit the 12px ringed notification dot and got hand-rolled instead.\n\npurpose=''unread'' and purpose=''filter'' render it. The two are identical in Figma\nand differ only in meaning, so the choice documents why the dot is there. It\napplies to dots; a count badge is always the notification pill.\n\nclassName now applies to the root of a hostless dot. On the inner span it would\nplace the dot inside its own 8px box, which is never what a caller positioning\na dot means. `relative` moves with it, since it only exists to anchor an\nabsolutely positioned badge and would otherwise fight a caller''s `absolute`.\n\nReplaces the `size-2 rounded-full bg-gama-400` circle repeated across the apps,\nwhich was also one shade too light.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* fix: ASMA-8176 correct badge dot class order and add the new VRT baselines\n\neslint flagged ''absolute top-1 right-1'' in the new story and test; Tailwind''s\nclass order puts right before top. No rendering change.\n\nAdds the two missing baselines for the StandaloneDot and UnreadAndFilterDots\nstories, taken from the CI run''s captures so they come from the same pinned\nPlaywright container that compares them. The existing badge baselines are\nuntouched, including Default, which still matches after the flow change.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxIt+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5v8QAIemuqresRjY9A6L9NYNn3tG\nSkXz6qdawsyVv3ieYsQOsYOFlyRT5y73xSmbaXPOkDmaOiejsGJJdMIUgSm8X2g5\n7k2sHpAwvOVCvsxJkrmr/ZNoBXMOUlbwT3+sTseDZdFpoJ5rw5kqEPgBTOUhLItI\nlPaFuTE3Cc1nO4IebV1XndSo3DgBTve+YtjJM4eV1tNS9QWmU2jEfikhfTrViVGp\nt8aa6GpsHK4FSqDAyv8kf/V5XKOC9wiCjSBbE3s3KJA2Cwt2Zvhu9pYypMCxJiux\n4+Kl4lpydnM5fNeQEzYstZ/tgT4RzeRFxCA7duugj81CG9hfaSgK11wdhpiVvp0P\nvZnyaHJzXxyCqMmP23ypl0kbI7IKH/dfkgwENgkRLAnoOxmFaWw7SkdrntZ+hFS8\neVUjM6SielNrikkkH9lGSsoh6Ie15qTW/co2ZLORm8AxC7hd005QexxuVcnWTewe\ns86eA2jbIFjy8FKVEZRU/AP9fwkEe8uoV8a6xO8NUTMICeIBZBRaHvkw9vcUTLv4\n5R0D4s4VeQ5smdVV+LwI6JIzbKzLO6lHAarbjhg7Xv6QJgvOznhtZKDpFOjTgCQm\nBr1skR1AMGBR2dHPA2ZX0dQfCTbOMCPkZNWkSaTz/Wynh04ndQT1iAs5SSKptIgr\nMFFVCjguMUqQYMPKba6f\n=aVEe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T05:47:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://a