"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/8715869b0997e3af737bfa5447e77109cf4b74da","node_id":"C_kwDORvrv4doAKDg3MTU4NjliMDk5N2UzYWY3MzdiZmE1NDQ3ZTc3MTA5Y2Y0Yjc0ZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/00c3cd0fece1d1214548372177904a2083be32e8","sha":"00c3cd0fece1d1214548372177904a2083be32e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/00c3cd0fece1d1214548372177904a2083be32e8"}],"sha":"8715869b0997e3af737bfa5447e77109cf4b74da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/8715869b0997e3af737bfa5447e77109cf4b74da"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/264966161?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/doicovSanya","id":264966161,"login":"doicovSanya","node_id":"U_kgDOD8sQEQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/00c3cd0fece1d1214548372177904a2083be32e8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T07:26:49Z","email":"Alexandr.Doicov@carasent.com","name":"doicovSanya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T07:26:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(dialog-footer): ASMA-7099 choose the More menu by action count, not width (#219)\n\nFigma states the left cluster by count, not by room: at the same 600px frame it\ndraws both `State=Edit` (one action, inline and labelled) and `State=More` (the\nicon-only overflow trigger). I originally read that as a width problem, so two or\nthree actions rendered as separate inline buttons on a wide dialog and only folded\ninto the menu once they stopped fitting — which also made the menu appear and\ndisappear as a dialog was resized.\n\nFrom two actions up the cluster is now always the icon-only More menu. A lone\naction stays inline, and width still governs the one thing it should: that\naction''s label, which collapses to icon-only when it no longer fits (the Reflow\nstory now demonstrates exactly that, and nothing else).\n\nThis restores the pre-migration behaviour for the three footers that had\nhand-built a permanent More popover — calendar''s event-template and task-template\nfooters, and notification''s sms-template footer — which the ASMA-7099 migration\nhad turned into inline buttons on wide dialogs, and which those PRs flagged at the\ntime as a deliberate change. It was not the right call.\n\nOn the tests: my first attempt asserted this in the SSR unit suite and the\nassertions were vacuous — they passed with the rule disabled, because SSR always\nmeasures 0px and so cannot tell a count rule from a width rule. They are replaced\nby a browser story, TwoActionsAlwaysUseMoreMenu, which renders two actions in a\nroomy 600px container and is verified to fail when the rule is reverted.\n\nThree baselines legitimately change (gallery, reflow, overflow-menu-opens-upward)\nand one is added. While re-baselining, a Gallery caption that had claimed\n\"destructive collapses to icon-only\" while plainly rendering a label — wrong since\nthe component landed — is corrected.\n\nVerified: tsc clean, eslint clean, unit 529/529, storybook 379/379, VRT 9/9.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"eb4574016bdac41ded4f4ad2282bf6d5bc8302c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/eb4574016bdac41ded4f4ad2282bf6d5bc8302c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/00c3cd0fece1d1214548372177904a2083be32e8","verification":{"payload":"tree eb4574016bdac41ded4f4ad2282bf6d5bc8302c5\nparent bc36917fc5ab8769ea6dc4b4ca25cc70313038ae\nauthor doicovSanya <Alexandr.Doicov@carasent.com> 1790580409 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790580409 +0300\n\nfeat(dialog-footer): ASMA-7099 choose the More menu by action count, not width (#219)\n\nFigma states the left cluster by count, not by room: at the same 600px frame it\ndraws both `State=Edit` (one action, inline and labelled) and `State=More` (the\nicon-only overflow trigger). I originally read that as a width problem, so two or\nthree actions rendered as separate inline buttons on a wide dialog and only folded\ninto the menu once they stopped fitting — which also made the menu appear and\ndisappear as a dialog was resized.\n\nFrom two actions up the cluster is now always the icon-only More menu. A lone\naction stays inline, and width still governs the one thing it should: that\naction''s label, which collapses to icon-only when it no longer fits (the Reflow\nstory now demonstrates exactly that, and nothing else).\n\nThis restores the pre-migration behaviour for the three footers that had\nhand-built a permanent More popover — calendar''s event-template and task-template\nfooters, and notification''s sms-template footer — which the ASMA-7099 migration\nhad turned into inline buttons on wide dialogs, and which those PRs flagged at the\ntime as a deliberate change. It was not the right call.\n\nOn the tests: my first attempt asserted this in the SSR unit suite and the\nassertions were vacuous — they passed with the rule disabled, because SSR always\nmeasures 0px and so cannot tell a count rule from a width rule. They are replaced\nby a browser story, TwoActionsAlwaysUseMoreMenu, which renders two actions in a\nroomy 600px container and is verified to fail when the rule is reverted.\n\nThree baselines legitimately change (gallery, reflow, overflow-menu-opens-upward)\nand one is added. While re-baselining, a Gallery caption that had claimed\n\"destructive collapses to icon-only\" while plainly rendering a label — wrong since\nthe component landed — is corrected.\n\nVerified: tsc clean, eslint clean, unit 529/529, storybook 379/379, VRT 9/9.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquha5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaXgQAE88GVK4H3oCKeQrmtP388PI\n634dFbvyLX2M8FXr45WIntB2USujZZFOhPuV5e5OvxXR4sS9mtsf+2IwdrINye3g\nOo91HarOSjmyTaPj2VJ7ioYYdbj0UPBP9OtOBaBK99KnV/r4V30Ck0x779b9P+fa\nAY2agiHgP6mAJ0Wmkchbmfya3lUPVeIMHnkvJ2wGX82vyY4dwlUdBYCv403FKddP\nZdEJPfdMPV7L9C1lFH5ettExDDfJiGU8b20bbJ4S1YKsZdxZgZvfNuV1FVDwQeNV\nVtqiV+HEOnn1sQxpjMcqQgQ3UIbLx8CUO/x3+jQk5uHST4vO60rRZiSz7ja8lpDZ\nQ/kz00LuWxwRXYWm9bV1s+pkMtw2MOWkG0vDIfLX17acKOf1BHX3vRKGKVsj5wg5\n3i5UuhuNGKgOOkLakE7LDA8UcmfEzOi7x771vj+6+KkQlqxAzZUnBN54BK+CpmD6\nkhxmLrh5HFe77zMh6Dp4y1TBYlJ7O9pI5zaNqD9EhRhT1Z/TS0v3tweovDdBkSPZ\nexohNf/H8QnysZMwjnwvttpxJdzIRyJLo+JA34LskzaDboynwmpp7LuMIy3lAGjH\n3OdhNr/DTztTPeCaTC37IAYdlX+l2hcpkuuMkEL5JIoc5khoPe2pVNWlPDFAOAFa\nkm4Rn5TsL+6EGjegtFty\n=DkEN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T07:26:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/00c3cd0fece1d1214548372177904a2083be32e8","node_id":"C_kwDORvrv4doAKDAwYzNjZDBmZWNlMWQxMjE0NTQ4MzcyMTc3OTA0YTIwODNiZTMyZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/bc36917fc5ab8769ea6dc4b4ca25cc70313038ae","sha":"bc36917fc5ab8769ea6dc4b4ca25cc70313038ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/bc36917fc5ab8769ea6dc4b4ca25cc70313038ae"}],"sha":"00c3cd0fece1d1214548372177904a2083be32e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/00c3cd0fece1d1214548372177904a2083be32e8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/264966161?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/doicovSanya","id":264966161,"login":"doicovSanya","node_id":"U_kgDOD8sQEQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/bc36917fc5ab8769ea6dc4b4ca25cc70313038ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T07:01:22Z","email":"Alexandr.Doicov@carasent.com","name":"doicovSanya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T07:01:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(a11y): ASMA-8143 stop Pointer Cancellation flaking on the Enter activation (#220)\n\nThe Pointer Cancellation story intermittently fails CI on\n\n    await waitFor(() => expect(input).toHaveValue(''''))\n\nreceiving ''Ada'' — the value never changes at all. #193 already widened this\nassertion into a waitFor on the theory that the rerender lags; it still flakes,\nwhich is the evidence that lag is not the (only) cause: a waitFor cannot help if\nthe key never reached the button.\n\nThe likelier cause is focus. `clear` lives inside the autocomplete, which\nrefocuses its own input on its own schedule after the cancelled press just above.\nIf that lands between `clear.focus()` and the keypress, Enter goes to the INPUT —\nselecting the highlighted option — instead of activating Clear, and nothing\nclears. So the test now waits for focus to actually settle on Clear before\ntyping, which closes that race deterministically.\n\nThe existing value assertion keeps its waitFor and gains an explicit 5s timeout:\nthe default 1s is tight on a loaded runner with all 65 story files in parallel,\nwhich covers the lag theory too. Between them both candidate causes are handled\nwithout weakening what the story proves — that Enter on Clear clears the input.\n\nNot reproducible locally: 12/12 green in isolation even with a strict\n`toHaveFocus()` probe before the keypress, so this is load-dependent and the fix\nis reasoned from the CI failure mode rather than from a local repro. Full\nstorybook suite green (378/378).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"85a78bef13fbdef72ea492108c742025c0d3fc39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/85a78bef13fbdef72ea492108c742025c0d3fc39"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/bc36917fc5ab8769ea6dc4b4ca25cc70313038ae","verification":{"payload":"tree 85a78bef13fbdef72ea492108c742025c0d3fc39\nparent 7ebf3923beb23d7c665dd99843df725a69278ca0\nauthor doicovSanya <Alexandr.Doicov@carasent.com> 1790578882 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790578882 +0300\n\ntest(a11y): ASMA-8143 stop Pointer Cancellation flaking on the Enter activation (#220)\n\nThe Pointer Cancellation story intermittently fails CI on\n\n    await waitFor(() => expect(input).toHaveValue(''''))\n\nreceiving ''Ada'' — the value never changes at all. #193 already widened this\nassertion into a waitFor on the theory that the rerender lags; it still flakes,\nwhich is the evidence that lag is not the (only) cause: a waitFor cannot help if\nthe key never reached the button.\n\nThe likelier cause is focus. `clear` lives inside the autocomplete, which\nrefocuses its own input on its own schedule after the cancelled press just above.\nIf that lands between `clear.focus()` and the keypress, Enter goes to the INPUT —\nselecting the highlighted option — instead of activating Clear, and nothing\nclears. So the test now waits for focus to actually settle on Clear before\ntyping, which closes that race deterministically.\n\nThe existing value assertion keeps its waitFor and gains an explicit 5s timeout:\nthe default 1s is tight on a loaded runner with all 65 story files in parallel,\nwhich covers the lag theory too. Between them both candidate causes are handled\nwithout weakening what the story proves — that Enter on Clear clears the input.\n\nNot reproducible locally: 12/12 green in isolation even with a strict\n`toHaveFocus()` probe before the keypress, so this is load-dependent and the fix\nis reasoned from the CI failure mode rather than from a local repro. Full\nstorybook suite green (378/378).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquhDCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAK6wQAAdOrC6R1ID5fi7WhAw1fbIQ\nebuQD3VrBCaagBEigz1C81mDFSinlfaeIKnzXNd++LtjweduAyYPHain7ogeF0LY\njuxy6/kU4p4AxWrDaEsmqVSkNjCq7iyx4pxEfRSMJkgr7ZxrmQNHXINhiBypJVTl\nkMdDOtNIiBum/AZPsdkva2c41CLoJbMwKNXCvFdZxkz0CvlDHy5vAYS3gWoXJqLH\nsAJg6ZryTjPeplUVCnSUdC3gIF7FlASnyDOL7NMS0jTpJxzzInGFfdUmUYFjag5l\nn4pVntBHtdXhQmcNq7AVFcESAC/Eu5DWI7/GuWZ8L1+iX0Ju8IRfY+70lmhu2zO5\namFCS/jJhMyO1HatwISx3XJsvHAU9JqvF9IuF8flugwKVv71D7UIqbDoOfnC/qDf\nUpRc4GeuFTugaxL6fkX0QG+C6AhH1ncpgy33nOvKx+WrPGBEpuCwwZlx4uTxHBt+\nNCh+c2/Id9g/1KOZYs4xHYSWvGn+6UiXFcRXkXIBQqD4GWrS51724sd14loVOE3a\n+VWfRlntr5J2aVePCOgSnH9FIEAU5qxd92NhXU1TuUKnzhglSSIVWRW0KnFzjdZy\ngJRtyn3WwnokGpcdySrzT1m/o349W3ldpy3STXUzSBnJbOlcRmv0dL8C4ZqJol38\nSeE/RhHGL8RZi+qqEVCN\n=mX8T\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T07:01:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_