id":"C_kwDORvrv4doAKDdkNGEyZjllMGE0ODczZGU5MTE4Mjk2MDYyZGU3YzUzOWQ0YzQ3MTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/4988ecf2e7b290a0114e6f85f1fe4999fe50bfab","sha":"4988ecf2e7b290a0114e6f85f1fe4999fe50bfab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/4988ecf2e7b290a0114e6f85f1fe4999fe50bfab"}],"sha":"7d4a2f9e0a4873de9118296062de7c539d4c4711","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/7d4a2f9e0a4873de9118296062de7c539d4c4711"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/263779196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/VasiliiPeicov","id":263779196,"login":"VasiliiPeicov","node_id":"U_kgDOD7jzfA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/4988ecf2e7b290a0114e6f85f1fe4999fe50bfab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T17:46:35Z","email":"vasilii.peicov@carasent.com","name":"VasiliiPeicov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T17:46:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(bottom-sheet): ASMA-8184 add StyledBottomSheet, wire into PopoverSheet (#217)\n\n* feat(bottom-sheet): ASMA-8184 add StyledBottomSheet, wire into StyledPopoverV2\n\nAdd the Design System Bottom Sheet: the mobile (0-743px) form of the Action\npopover. StyledPopoverV2 with variant=''action'' now renders it automatically\nbelow 744px, so the same props produce an anchored popover on tablet/desktop\nand a modal sheet on phones. variant=''info'' stays anchored at every size, per\nspec, since the spatial link to its term is the point.\n\nNative <dialog>.showModal(), same pattern as StyledDialog: page behind is\ninert and scroll-locked, top-layer stacking, registerOpenModalDialog so\nsnackbars land inside. useFocusTrap wraps Tab within the sheet (a native\nmodal alone lets Tab escape to browser chrome). Five equivalent dismiss\nroutes -- close button, \"Vis resultater\", scrim tap, Escape, drag down past\n30% of the sheet height -- none of which commits or discards anything.\n\nHeight fits content up to 90vh (body scrolls, header/footer fixed); a phone\nin landscape (max-height: 480px) gets a full-screen dialog instead, per spec.\nTop radius 28px and width capped at 640px, both pixel-matched against the\nFigma \"_bottom sheet\" component (9Q7C7JYPgnUSsrX1L8v40t#5354-169163) rather\nthan the spec''s \"same as Modal\" / \"100% viewport\" text, confirmed with\nVasilii where the two disagreed.\n\nNew resultCount prop (on both components) renders the standard \"Vis\nresultater (N)\" control per the spec''s copy table: debounced ~500ms via a new\nuseDebouncedValue hook, \"Ingen treff\" at zero and always enabled, capped at\n\"9999+\". In the sheet it also announces from a live region inside the sheet,\nbecause the list behind is inert and cannot announce its own. New\nformatResultsLabel is exported and unit-tested against every row of that\ntable.\n\nNew useBodyScrollLock and useShortViewportMediaQuery ((max-height: 480px)).\nuseDismiss on the floating popover is disabled in sheet mode -- with no\nfloating element every press inside the sheet would otherwise read as an\noutside press and close it.\n\nDeliberate additions to the frozen API surface (DEC-003): StyledBottomSheet\nand formatResultsLabel.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(popover): rename StyledPopoverV2 to StyledAdaptiveSurface, document migration story\n\nStyledPopoverV2 silently renders as a completely different thing (a modal\nbottom sheet) below 744px -- \"V2\" no longer describes what it is. Renamed to\nStyledAdaptiveSurface, which names the one entity rather than a version.\nNothing has shipped yet (neither commit is on origin/master), so this is a\nmechanical rename, not a breaking change under DEC-003, which governs shipped\nexports surviving a migration unchanged.\n\ngit mv preserves file history on the three renamed files and their VRT\nbaselines (git recognises the untouched screenshots as pure renames).\nStyledBottomSheet is untouched -- it stays its own name, its own export, for\nscreens that only ever need a sheet. Shared prop-shape types\n(PopoverTrigger/PopoverTriggerProps/PopoverSlot/PopoverContentApi) are left\nas-is; renaming them would be unrelated churn.\n\nAlso, per a fresh audit of every real StyledPopover consumer under src/:\nStyledFilterMenu is the one real migration candidate (its\npopoverContent({isOpen,onClose}) + anchorNode render-props are the shape\nStyledAdaptiveSurface''s Filter pattern was modeled on, but the shapes differ\nenough that it needs a rewrite, not an import swap -- tracked as a follow-up,\nnot done here). Everything with role=\"menu\" (StyledMenu, RowActionMenu, and\ntransitively ToolbarActionGroup) or listbox/combobox semantics\n(TableRowCountSelect, TablePagination, CountryCodeSelect''s desktop panel) or\nnon-list content (the date-picker calendar, which already has its own mobile\nDrawer fallback) is explicitly NOT a migration candidate -- StyledPopover\nstays their permanent primitive. Written up in Readme.md so the question\nisn''t re-litigated per consumer later.\n\nDocuments two findings from a skeptical re-read of the sheet wiring that\nwere true but missing from visual-tests/FIGMA-PARITY.md''s ledger: (a)\nBottomSheetCloseReason is discarded when the sheet is driven through\nStyledAdaptiveSurface, because its close is () => void -- left as-is\ndeliberately, since the desktop path has never exposed a dismiss reason\neither, so this is parity with the existing minimal contract rather than a\nregression; (b) footerActions still renders as its own extra row in the\nsheet even though Figma''s sheet anatomy has only one footer, kept so a\nconsumer passing both slots together doesn''t lose one on mobile. Also\nreconfirms, per PR #216''s existing note, that a landscape phone wider than\n744px never becomes a sheet -- the width/height media queries are\nindependent, by design, not a bug.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(lint): register border-b-solid/border-t-solid with better-tailwindcss\n\nCI''s ESLint runs from a clean checkout with no .eslintcache, so it caught what\na stale local cache had been silently hiding: eslint-plugin-better-tailwindcss\ndoesn''t know this package''s own side-specific border-style utilities\n(border-{l,b,t,y}-solid, src/styles/index.css) unless each is explicitly\nlisted in the rule''s ignore array -- real Tailwind only ships the unsided\nborder-solid, which the plugin already recognises on its own.\n\nOnly border-l-solid was ever added (when something first used it); nothing\nhad used border-b-solid/border-t-solid before StyledBottomSheet, so the gap\nwas latent until now. Add both -- border-r-solid/border-y-solid stay\nunlisted until something needs them, same precedent. Also re-run eslint --fix\nfor the class-order rule''s now-different expectation once the classes became\nregistered.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(popover): designer decision -- rename StyledAdaptiveSurface to PopoverSheet\n\nDropping the `Styled` prefix per the design team''s naming call -- this is now the\nonly export in the package without it (every other component, including the\nStyledBottomSheet it wraps, keeps the prefix). Flagged that inconsistency for\nthe record; proceeding since it''s a deliberate, already-made decision.\n\nMechanical rename only, same as the previous StyledPopoverV2 -> StyledAdaptiveSurface\npass: git mv preserves file history, VRT baselines re-captured under the new\nstory ids (utils-popover-sheet--*), pixel-identical to the prior baselines.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e2b66b46ee9204c1044e68169fd25ed0c7e46aad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/e2b66b46ee9204c1044e68169fd25ed0c7e46aad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/4988ecf2e7b290a0114e6f85f1fe4999fe50bfab","verification":{"payload":"tree e2b66b46ee9204c1044e68169fd25ed0c7e46aad\nparent fc7b4e6f3fe896292120a444d36684cacc789629\nauthor VasiliiPeicov <vasilii.peicov@carasent.com> 1790531195 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790531195 +0300\n\nfeat(bottom-sheet): ASMA-8184 add StyledBottomSheet, wire into PopoverSheet (#217)\n\n* feat(bottom-sheet): ASMA-8184 add StyledBottomSheet, wire into StyledPopoverV2\n\nAdd the Design System Bottom Sheet: the mobile (0-743px) form of the Action\npopover. StyledPopoverV2 with variant=''action'' now renders it automatically\nbelow 744px, so the same props produce an anchored popover on tablet/desktop\nand a modal sheet on phones. variant=''info'' stays anchored at every size, per\nspec, since the spatial link to its term is the point.\n\nNative <dialog>.showModal(), same pattern as StyledDialog: page behind is\ninert and scroll-locked, top-layer stacking, registerOpenModalDialog so\nsnackbars land inside. useFocusTrap wraps Tab within the sheet (a native\nmodal alone lets Tab escape to browser chrome). Five equivalent dismiss\nroutes -- close button, \"Vis resultater\", scrim tap, Escape, drag down past\n30% of the sheet height -- none of which commits or discards anything.\n\nHeight fits content up to 90vh (body scrolls, header/footer fixed); a phone\nin landscape (max-height: 480px) gets a full-screen dialog instead, per spec.\nTop radius 28px and width capped at 640px, both pixel-matched against the\nFigma \"_bottom sheet\" component (9Q7C7JYPgnUSsrX1L8v40t#5354-169163) rather\nthan the spec''s \"same as Modal\" / \"100% viewport\" text, confirmed with\nVasilii where the two disagreed.\n\nNew resultCount prop (on both components) renders the standard \"Vis\nresultater (N)\" control per the spec''s copy table: debounced ~500ms via a new\nuseDebouncedValue hook, \"Ingen treff\" at zero and always enabled, capped at\n\"9999+\". In the sheet it also announces from a live region inside the sheet,\nbecause the list behind is inert and cannot announce its own. New\nformatResultsLabel is exported and unit-tested against every row of that\ntable.\n\nNew useBodyScrollLock and useShortViewportMediaQuery ((max-height: 480px)).\nuseDismiss on the floating popover is disabled in sheet mode -- with no\nfloating element every press inside the sheet would otherwise read as an\noutside press and close it.\n\nDeliberate additions to the frozen API surface (DEC-003): StyledBottomSheet\nand formatResultsLabel.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(popover): rename StyledPopoverV2 to StyledAdaptiveSurface, document migration story\n\nStyledPopoverV2 silently renders as a completely different thing (a modal\nbottom sheet) below 744px -- \"V2\" no longer describes what it is. Renamed to\nStyledAdaptiveSurface, which names the one entity rather than a version.\nNothing has shipped yet (neither commit is on origin/master), so this is a\nmechanical rename, not a breaking change under DEC-003, which governs shipped\nexports surviving a migration unchanged.\n\ngit mv preserves file history on the three renamed files and their VRT\nbaselines (git recognises the untouched screenshots as pure renames).\nStyledBottomSheet is untouched -- it stays its own name, its own export, for\nscreens that only ever need a sheet. Shared prop-shape types\n(PopoverTrigger/PopoverTriggerProps/PopoverSlot/PopoverContentApi) are left\nas-is; renaming them would be unrelated churn.\n\nAlso, per a fresh audit of every real StyledPopover consumer under src/:\nStyledFilterMenu is the one real migration candidate (its\npopoverContent({isOpen,onClose}) + anchorNode render-props are the shape\nStyledAdaptiveSurface''s Filter pattern was modeled on, but the shapes differ\nenough that it needs a rewrite, not an import swap -- tracked as a follow-up,\nnot done here). Everything with role=\"menu\" (StyledMenu, RowActionMenu, and\ntransitively ToolbarActionGroup) or listbox/combobox semantics\n(TableRowCountSelect, TablePagination, CountryCodeSelect''s desktop panel) or\nnon-list content (the date-picker calendar, which already has its own mobile\nDrawer fallback) is explicitly NOT a migration candidate -- StyledPopover\nstays their permanent primitive. Written up in Readme.md so the question\nisn''t re-litigated per consumer later.\n\nDocuments two findings from a skeptical re-read of the sheet wiring that\nwere true but missing from visual-tests/FIGMA-PARITY.md''s ledger: (a)\nBottomSheetCloseReason is discarded when the sheet is driven through\nStyledAdaptiveSurface, because its close is () => void -- left as-is\ndeliberately, since the desktop path has never exposed a dismiss reason\neither, so this is parity with the existing minimal contract rather than a\nregression; (b) footerActions still renders as its own extra row in the\nsheet even though Figma''s sheet anatomy has only one footer, kept so a\nconsumer passing both slots together doesn''t lose one on mobile. Also\nreconfirms, per PR #216''s existing note, that a landscape phone wider than\n744px never becomes a sheet -- the width/height media queries are\nindependent, by design, not a bug.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(lint): register border-b-solid/border-t-solid with better-tailwindcss\n\nCI''s ESLint runs from a clean checkout with no .eslintcache, so it caught what\na stale local cache had been silently hiding: eslint-plugin-better-tailwindcss\ndoesn''t know this package''s own side-specific border-style utilities\n(border-{l,b,t,y}-solid, src/styles/index.css) unless each is explicitly\nlisted in the rule''s ignore array -- real Tailwind only ships the unsided\nborder-solid, which the plugin already recognises on its own.\n\nOnly border-l-solid was ever added (when something first used it); nothing\nhad used border-b-solid/border-t-solid before StyledBottomSheet, so the gap\nwas latent until now. Add both -- border-r-solid/border-y-solid stay\nunlisted until something needs them, same precedent. Also re-run eslint --fix\nfor the class-order rule''s now-different expectation once the classes became\nregistered.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(popover): designer decision -- rename StyledAdaptiveSurface to PopoverSheet\n\nDropping the `Styled` prefix per the design team''s naming call -- this is now the\nonly export in the package without it (every other component, including the\nStyledBottomSheet it wraps, keeps the prefix). Flagged that inconsistency for\nthe record; proceeding since it''s a deliberate, already-made decision.\n\nMechanical rename only, same as the previous StyledPopoverV2 -> StyledAdaptiveSurface\npass: git mv preserves file history, VRT baselines re-captured under the new\nstory ids (utils-popover-sheet--*), pixel-identical to the prior baselines.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquVZ7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhrwQADHYXa6yAOtlKg1xH+JPF8fu\ngW9DB06BmkEyzarxm8L0X7G16B5eKOT3gwwFiKjGK/vGMzGtjCsSaXhV1pG2T75x\n86BYMdwuJchMdpqanWVImU+8XdmJTNAQMPi2a88UPIybH5r74shw07x+uedp4GKK\nJr/Y9RssareuGmUZqqSFAPhv2e5Khf9ZSXWSMdUSkOsdpeYgHL6kiTXpTpbAfJeE\nAvX7/iRpsQLRzvRYWuRfE7KPlcg/ncYdSQ+J+pifqAsbSTEbEy1nVYfASvF8tk1v\nqg+cDKTmjSUeke3e9+TTzkpub39LcD9REOWee8MAOAdoGx+/ImGFWfV92b8xLCdz\ns8fqhu6Y1j9uKB8e9UjMKPb050HfJtqWhIEGGHuNU/3gXbmwl+7ptvQ91OULw49X\nz646TM9CTbqTW4CVd4QcOUIsEQBeKsx6lucepDukyNS0kMk97VKZytSYUX1sNmj3\nYwZA7fy6Sod+cKfl6kkkCXvfJwmDXAoM6kT6K9HBG+GkdDVavT746/xJlrBKzAd6\nG4WTFNdDwZC7Gb6KAEGN5YDzlUND/P8tEr2e7cgW0y2nLQeuS9WbhbDjWVbsR6cP\nwh1DZgzgZ2sv02/NIfN1Q9OLMLz3JXqGoHMaCFH9AkA7n5SYMi8lAl4uyvKf3VDo\naLjife3hHZF8+C7DtRXa\n=4rD8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T17:46:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/4988ecf2e7b290a0114e6f85f1fe4999fe50bfab","node_id":"C_kwDORvrv4doAKDQ5ODhlY2YyZTdiMjkwYTAxMTRlNmY4NWYxZmU0OTk5ZmU1MGJmYWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/fc7b4e6f3fe896292120a444d36684cacc789629","sha":"fc7b4e6f3fe896292120a444d36684cacc789629","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/fc7b4e6f3fe896292120a444d36684cacc789629"}],"sha":"4988ecf2e7b290a0114e6f85f1fe4999fe50bfab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/4988ecf2e7b290a0114e6f85f1fe4999fe50bfab"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/263779196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/VasiliiPeicov","id":263779196,"login":"VasiliiPeicov","node_id":"U_kgDOD7jzfA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/fc7b4e6f3fe896292120a444d36684cacc789629/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T17:35:03Z","email":"vasilii.peicov@carasent.com","name":"VasiliiPeicov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T17:35:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(popover): ASMA-8183 add StyledPopoverV2 design system popover (#204)\n\n* feat(popover): ASMA-8183 add StyledPopoverV2 design system popover\n\nAdd the Design System Popover: an anchored surface with an optional title, a\nrequired close control and two optional footer rows, in two content-driven\nvariants.\n\n- info: read-only, referenced by aria-describedby, not focus-trapped. Tab\n  leaves the surface and closes it.\n- action: role=\"dialog\" with a focus trap. Covers the Filter pattern (every\n  change applies immediately, Nullstill clears) and the Actions pattern (a list\n  of buttons; activation closes via the close() render-prop argument).\n\nDeliberately no role=\"menu\" and no arrow-key navigation: menu semantics cannot\ncoexist with the dialog model Filter uses, so everything inside is reached with\nTab. Deliberately no arrow/anchor pointer either -- the surface is edge-aligned\nat an 8px offset.\n\nFooter rows follow the Figma frames exactly. The Reset filter row is\nspace-between (viewResultsAction left, resetAction right); the Actions row is a\nsingle right-aligned outlined button. children and all three footer slots may be\nrender-props receiving close().\n\nFocus is managed by hand rather than with FloatingFocusManager: its focus guards\nare tabindex=0 + aria-hidden, which axe fails as aria-hidden-focus (a rule this\npackage drove to zero in ASMA-8143 by fixing, not waiving), and disabling the\nguards is not an option because they are what implement both the trap''s Tab\nwrap-around and the info variant''s \"Tab leaves and closes\". The package''s own\nuseFocusTrap covers the action variant; a focus-out listener covers info.\nEscape stays with useDismiss alone, which also keeps the trap effect from\nre-subscribing on every parent render.\n\nSeparate from StyledPopover, which is untouched and remains the MUI-parity\npositioning primitive its eight internal consumers depend on; those migrate\nacross gradually. Deliberate addition to the frozen API surface (DEC-003): one\nnew runtime export, no existing export changed.\n\nStorybook ships a static Gallery (every Title x Reset filter x Actions\ncombination side by side) and an interactive Playground (the same properties on\na real popover, with an event log).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(popover): ASMA-8183 replace the Playground story with per-case popovers\n\nThe Playground configured one popover through toggles; browsing the variants\nmeant reconfiguring it. AllCases instead gives each case its own trigger, so a\nreviewer clicks straight down the grid: both variants, every footer\ncombination, a long title, the 240px minimum, 60vh scrolling, and the live\nFilter and Actions patterns.\n\nPressing another trigger dismisses the open surface, which is the \"only one\npopover at a time\" rule demonstrating itself rather than being described.\n\nThe static Gallery stays as the side-by-side visual comparison and its VRT\ncoverage of every anatomy.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(popover): ASMA-8183 put the scrollbar in the right gutter, as Figma draws it\n\nFigma''s \"Windows scroll\" element sits at absolute x 385-400 of the 400 frame --\nflush with the surface edge, starting at y 40 below the close control. Scrolling\nthe text column instead parked the bar ~40px inboard, against the text.\n\nThe scroll container now spans the full width and the 40px close gutter is its\nright padding, so the bar lands in the gutter. The close control floats over the\ntop-right corner rather than occupying a column, but stays last in the DOM so the\naction variant still opens on the first body control rather than on close.\n\nEasy to miss on macOS, where overlay scrollbars take no layout width and the bar\nis only drawn while scrolling -- the gutter earns its keep on Windows, which is\nwhat the Figma element is named after.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(popover): follow useFocusTrap''s ASMA-8087 rewrite, drop FOCUSABLE_SELECTOR\n\nASMA-8087 (merged to master, just merged into this branch) rewrote\nuseFocusTrap.hook.ts and removed the FOCUSABLE_SELECTOR export this\ncomponent''s first-control-focus effect depended on, replacing it with a\nshared src/helpers/focusable module. Swap the one call site over to\nfirstTabbable, which is exactly the \"root itself if tabbable, else its first\ntabbable descendant\" shape this effect already wanted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"25de19d22f48171be2712f5c2fa1763d327a5938","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/25de19d22f48171be2712f5c2fa1763d327a5938"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/fc7b4e6f3fe896292120a444d36684cacc789629","verification":{"payload":"tree 25de19d22f48171be2712f5c2fa1763d327a5938\nparent db4fea257e4e5d8cac6017425e8090a095c15102\nauthor VasiliiPeicov <vasilii.peicov@carasent.com> 1790530503 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790530503 +0300\n\nfeat(popover): ASMA-8183 add StyledPopoverV2 design system popover (#204)\n\n* feat(popover): ASMA-8183 add StyledPopoverV2 design system popover\n\nAdd the Design System Popover: an anchored surface with an optional title, a\nrequired close control and two optional footer rows, in two content-driven\nvariants.\n\n- info: read-only, referenced by aria-describedby, not focus-trapped. Tab\n  leaves the surface and closes it.\n- action: role=\"dialog\" with a focus trap. Covers the Filter pattern (every\n  change applies immediately, Nullstill clears) and the Actions pattern (a list\n  of buttons; activation closes via the close() render-prop argument).\n\nDeliberately no role=\"menu\" and no arrow-key navigation: menu semantics cannot\ncoexist with the dialog model Filter uses, so everything inside is reached with\nTab. Deliberately no arrow/anchor pointer either -- the surface is edge-aligned\nat an 8px offset.\n\nFooter rows follow the Figma frames exactly. The Reset filter row is\nspace-between (viewResultsAction left, resetAction right); the Actions row is a\nsingle right-aligned outlined button. children and all three footer slots may be\nrender-props receiving close().\n\nFocus is managed by hand rather than with FloatingFocusManager: its focus guards\nare tabindex=0 + aria-hidden, which axe fails as aria-hidden-focus (a rule this\npackage drove to zero in ASMA-8143 by fixing, not waiving), and disabling the\nguards is not an option because they are what implement both the trap''s Tab\nwrap-around and the info variant''s \"Tab leaves and closes\". The package''s own\nuseFocusTrap covers the action variant; a focus-out listener covers info.\nEscape stays with useDismiss alone, which also keeps the trap effect from\nre-subscribing on every parent render.\n\nSeparate from StyledPopover, which is untouched and remains the MUI-parity\npositioning primitive its eight internal consumers depend on; those migrate\nacross gradually. Deliberate addition to the frozen API surface (DEC-003): one\nnew runtime export, no existing export changed.\n\nStorybook ships a static Gallery (every Title x Reset filter x Actions\ncombination side by side) and an interactive Playground (the same properties on\na real popover, with an event log).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(popover): ASMA-8183 replace the Playground story with per-case popovers\n\nThe Playground configured one popover through toggles; browsing the variants\nmeant reconfiguring it. AllCases instead gives each case its own trigger, so a\nreviewer clicks straight down the grid: both variants, every footer\ncombination, a long title, the 240px minimum, 60vh scrolling, and the live\nFilter and Actions patterns.\n\nPressing another trigger dismisses the open surface, which is the \"only one\npopover at a time\" rule demonstrating itself rather than being described.\n\nThe static Gallery stays as the side-by-side visual comparison and its VRT\ncoverage of every anatomy.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(popover): ASMA-8183 put the scrollbar in the right gutter, as Figma draws it\n\nFigma''s \"Windows scroll\" element sits at absolute x 385-400 of the 400 frame --\nflush with the surface edge, starting at y 40 below the close control. Scrolling\nthe text column instead parked the bar ~40px inboard, against the text.\n\nThe scroll container now spans the full width and the 40px close gutter is its\nright padding, so the bar lands in the gutter. The close control floats over the\ntop-right corner rather than occupying a column, but stays last in the DOM so the\naction variant still opens on the first body control rather than on close.\n\nEasy to miss on macOS, where overlay scrollbars take no layout width and the bar\nis only drawn while scrolling -- the gutter earns its keep on Windows, which is\nwhat the Figma element is named after.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(popover): follow useFocusTrap''s ASMA-8087 rewrite, drop FOCUSABLE_SELECTOR\n\nASMA-8087 (merged to master, just merged into this branch) rewrote\nuseFocusTrap.hook.ts and removed the FOCUSABLE_SELECTOR export this\ncomponent''s first-control-focus effect depended on, replacing it with a\nshared src/helpers/focusable module. Swap the one call site over to\nfirstTabbable, which is exactly the \"root itself if tabbable, else its first\ntabbable descendant\" shape this effect already wanted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquVPHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADUMQAJDuDPmALKY8dibXju54/c/x\nz2IJPhnbSNb/8nvbRLwm2PXb0l4RyBzd3LYX2038xxqtOPeTNwa3GOJyQ1xrX8Cw\nlqTxdSFDXFROQ5K1XsNd3cduiHiDPFgus13Ljv/49Ma6MwiBt0WBnMG3jynQ6s7P\ntWY5In5SqebXdaEl+ZGDDxFomWK6CppHdPYvq4zrtkKw+nyprH1MELlepSRHWzXh\ngFWcpqO47qNbefA3Oyr6DW2BrjH84EJ5veNzPTJ0ZkkWEcUxTW+aWsvqnM0tgy3G\nnTtvCMWJTHptZKPqPvix8wwTmVscelTi4unLpWIJry9mJwZWW44uP+erJghTKFW4\n2tQRgh/nz5OePBOup7Cl4g+XyKlcjs386Cc8nkH3i2KLJfA30T2YUN