nt — crm''s \"Edit\nperson details\" form — that shrank the footer to the width of its buttons and\nleft the separator floating in the middle of the dialog instead of spanning it.\n\nThe hand-rolled footers this component replaced carried an explicit `w-full`, so\nthe regression only surfaced after the ASMA-7099 migration. A scan of all ten\nconsumer repos found exactly one parent with this shape, which is the one\nreported.\n\nFixed with `self-stretch`, which overrides the parent''s align-items for this\nelement only. Deliberately NOT `w-full`: combined with the footer''s own `p-4` a\n100% width overflows the parent wherever box-sizing is content-box, and that\nalso perturbs the width the action planner measures — trying `w-full` first\nbroke the overflow-menu interaction story, which is how the distinction was\nfound.\n\nCovered two ways, both verified to fail without the fix: a unit test asserting\nthe class, and a SpansCentringParent interaction story that reproduces the\noffending parent and measures the rendered footer against the parent''s content\nbox (248px vs 600px when broken).\n\nVerified: tsc clean, eslint clean, unit 461/461, storybook 364/364, VRT 8/8 with\nthe seven pre-existing footer baselines unchanged — the fix is inert wherever\nthe parent already stretched its children.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5a54f307ee5971512dbe45d15ddc4da94e2851a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/5a54f307ee5971512dbe45d15ddc4da94e2851a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/de6983c39c99422a59d3ea66137dcbdb017499d8","verification":{"payload":"tree 5a54f307ee5971512dbe45d15ddc4da94e2851a2\nparent 7859c53d01a1be7540514e194c839323f3acd9fb\nauthor doicovSanya <Alexandr.Doicov@carasent.com> 1790056004 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790056004 +0300\n\nfix(dialog-footer): ASMA-7099 stop the footer collapsing in a centring parent (#211)\n\nStyledDialogFooter set no cross-axis sizing of its own, so it inherited the\nparent''s align-items. In a `flex flex-col items-center` parent — crm''s \"Edit\nperson details\" form — that shrank the footer to the width of its buttons and\nleft the separator floating in the middle of the dialog instead of spanning it.\n\nThe hand-rolled footers this component replaced carried an explicit `w-full`, so\nthe regression only surfaced after the ASMA-7099 migration. A scan of all ten\nconsumer repos found exactly one parent with this shape, which is the one\nreported.\n\nFixed with `self-stretch`, which overrides the parent''s align-items for this\nelement only. Deliberately NOT `w-full`: combined with the footer''s own `p-4` a\n100% width overflows the parent wherever box-sizing is content-box, and that\nalso perturbs the width the action planner measures — trying `w-full` first\nbroke the overflow-menu interaction story, which is how the distinction was\nfound.\n\nCovered two ways, both verified to fail without the fix: a unit test asserting\nthe class, and a SpansCentringParent interaction story that reproduces the\noffending parent and measures the rendered footer against the parent''s content\nbox (248px vs 600px when broken).\n\nVerified: tsc clean, eslint clean, unit 461/461, storybook 364/364, VRT 8/8 with\nthe seven pre-existing footer baselines unchanged — the fix is inert wherever\nthe parent already stretched its children.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqshZECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAD8AQAIfXe04s+Nu1SO0k6W/v6Nqc\nswIOb5qoesV4I/v8uZninv+NTYQRgy9ImZycp+rEw7evQP3iDsFG9vWiee6FAvGf\nkcdrtHsoacKaqG8PnABLTpoRvOE22cvFA1apohpbhB4zsz3TK4vjVKdHEldQA/5h\nfTtrZedl/Bdkh+8sJIuZu2DjfuPVfSJZUUPA/KaXis2LcBjnHfkwknkuV7Vu+wKb\n1AHm0xVjbNiXgIc6LSzZPmbCNJUpvT8aOiuCgO5c2uXevhjzTfsUqhKm4PcNHVBx\n6U0KJT5Kg6//aeMIiSyjvU+JpQ2UqOVBTkk+XCzZmvLm+E3y0hXmL8eLzDbBANm/\n6z6PqoUDGl7+A3vFZi+u66OTfa4g9eejLN