,"login":"mark31072","node_id":"U_kgDOBXWBqQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/c5a1052aad097ff5d325c4bcf6039319ef3a1577/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T08:18:55Z","email":"91586985+mark31072@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Marin Pesterean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T08:18:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: ASMA-8210 cut release for the pressable primitive and touch-readiness\n\nThe TB-02 merge (#202) used a Jira-prefixed subject, which the release gate\ndoes not count, so the pressable primitive was never published. Conventional\nfeat: subject cuts the pending minor release.","tree":{"sha":"0fb55da90ae13f54d4dd9632e200f27bd1c93a48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/0fb55da90ae13f54d4dd9632e200f27bd1c93a48"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/c5a1052aad097ff5d325c4bcf6039319ef3a1577","verification":{"payload":"tree 0fb55da90ae13f54d4dd9632e200f27bd1c93a48\nparent ff8b3445105292db4741b6b27b5dd336fe8429e1\nauthor Marin Pesterean <91586985+mark31072@users.noreply.github.com> 1789978735 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789978735 +0300\n\nfeat: ASMA-8210 cut release for the pressable primitive and touch-readiness\n\nThe TB-02 merge (#202) used a Jira-prefixed subject, which the release gate\ndoes not count, so the pressable primitive was never published. Conventional\nfeat: subject cuts the pending minor release.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsOhvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAE0IQAJ4hVx/96kBpCS9XJHfujUng\nNVEXOWgbNOqy0rnWvlbXyGgeIC1Fnhm2gVt8euN39jp2+2emjXT6Juh/02udBSLM\nRuK/92VF50WQ7E4XXX38iqhnZ0/rPlmTcdTQuFlEasJGN7rY9PVDsO2pGGwaeNdO\nWqknM5VUrEHreqRJ3BwgrgGV5j2/NJML85o/K+knB88oKgh0MaHjG+a/39ceyx0Z\n1Ivw6R1JMq1PU/8ThAueLbxZ8hZY8w2vWnly1mp7GEw+qXFdPWGb3scxg+287EgR\nXNIEl1fHQyk9apCtYGtiYFzsXXkj5D6dPCOpDiRoVTOI8vnBsMGNY/1Wc3k3zM05\nn1SZdKhQ6e2grmyBr8U0KS2dBxP6R+UAptmycI5v3fdg/w9C/Wg3+sV2Qzh95S9U\npccCm8gWKJ4uc5/Yec0ud3/jU2eIg2Ishl+8fwO0GkRD3DIlNf3Xp6s/8U+Ab5qu\nsUCUSOr/vILdiMT/cEnaZ4rK41z9vZDSJZj4ScD8VsXlS3RBJKSQgAUdj6emV7Kg\nvG911zjL/Oor2HdI+X1usNjkXDpzqNSNXCFMJYK/guBezu0749ax3TVQsxpaLh5q\n9aLagFcZvjfYuXl2d3UE12ET+wKElELBFrRBA6uvOGGYjUnBBQ6R5HLd1sNclRDq\nFtTxcDRlNLRaGwKbm0Kh\n=r67e\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T08:18:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/c5a1052aad097ff5d325c4bcf6039319ef3a1577","node_id":"C_kwDORvrv4doAKGM1YTEwNTJhYWQwOTdmZjVkMzI1YzRiY2Y2MDM5MzE5ZWYzYTE1Nzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/ff8b3445105292db4741b6b27b5dd336fe8429e1","sha":"ff8b3445105292db4741b6b27b5dd336fe8429e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/ff8b3445105292db4741b6b27b5dd336fe8429e1"}],"sha":"c5a1052aad097ff5d325c4bcf6039319ef3a1577","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/c5a1052aad097ff5d325c4bcf6039319ef3a1577"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91586985?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mark31072","id":91586985,"login":"mark31072","node_id":"U_kgDOBXWBqQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/ff8b3445105292db4741b6b27b5dd336fe8429e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T08:10:11Z","email":"91586985+mark31072@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Marin Pesterean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T08:10:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ASMA-8210 TB-02: pressable primitive + touch-readiness (#202)\n\n* ASMA-8210 add CSS touch-readiness primitives and opt in Button, Tab, MenuItem\n\nFour opt-in utility classes in src/styles/index.css, shipped via dist/style.css:\n- .asma-touch-ready: kills the iOS/Android tap flash and the 300ms double-tap\n  delay on controls that already own a designed :active (Button).\n- .asma-pressable: same, plus 0.7-opacity :active feedback for controls that\n  had no pressed state at all (Tab, MenuItem).\n- .asma-hit-area: transparent centred ::after overlay giving isolated controls\n  a 44px pointer target without changing the drawn size.\n- .asma-touch-target: 44px min-width/min-height gated to the mobile breakpoint\n  (max-width: 743px) for rows in a stack, where overlap would steal presses.\n\nAll utilities are inert at rest and on fine pointers, so the frozen public API\n(api-surface.test.ts) and the desktop VRT baselines are unchanged. Interaction\ntest covers hit-area geometry, tap-flash suppression, the mobile-only gating\nand the Button/pressable split.\n\n* ASMA-8210 move touch primitives out of @layer utilities to escape important: true\n\nReview finding: tailwind.config.ts sets important: true, and Tailwind v3\nimportantifies custom utilities declared inside @layer utilities too. That\ncompiled .asma-hit-area''s position: relative to !important, contradicting the\ndocumented override contract in both directions — a Tailwind position utility\ncould not override it (equal specificity, later source order) and an inline\nstyle lost to !important as well. The interaction test''s fixed-position probe\nonly passed because the flow origin happened to be (0,0).\n\nFix: the four primitives now live as unlayered CSS, the same technique the\nfile already uses for the prefers-reduced-motion block. Unlayered rules keep\ntheir source position after the @tailwind utilities output, so the one\ndeliberate !important (.asma-touch-target vs importantified min-h-*) still\nwins by source order, while .asma-hit-area emits WITHOUT !important (verified\nby compiling through the repo Tailwind config). Comments corrected, and the\ntest now asserts the probe''s computed position is ''fixed'', so the inline-wins\ncontract is actually exercised. Added .asma-hit-area caveats: not mobile-gated\n(desktop mouse targets grow too) and it clobbers a consumer ::after.\n\n* ASMA-8210 make touch-target a height-only floor and drop it from tabs\n\nReview finding B1: .asma-touch-target was a later-source override with equal\nspecificity and importance to Tailwind''s importantified min-h-*/min-w-*, so at\n<=743px it REPLACED designed minimums rather than flooring them — shrinking the\ndefault tab from min 48x90 to 44x44 and the small tab''s min-width from 90 to 44.\n\nFix, two parts:\n- The utility now sets min-height only. A min-width override can only replace\n  designed widths like the tab''s min-w-[90px]; width floors stay per-component.\n- StyledTab drops the class entirely. Measuring the real cascade showed BOTH\n  tab variants rest at an effective 48px min-height: the small variant''s\n  min-h-10 loses to the base min-h-12 because Tailwind emits .min-h-12 later\n  and cn (plain clsx, no tailwind-merge) keeps both classes on the element.\n  There is no 40->44 improvement to keep — any tab opt-in shrinks 48 to 44.\n  The pre-existing min-h stacking quirk (small tabs render 48px, not the Figma\n  40px) is documented and left for the ASMA-8220 sweep, since resolving it\n  moves VRT baselines. StyledMenuItem keeps the opt-in: 40px (32px dense) grows\n  to 44px on phones, and it declares no min-width.\n\nNew guard: a phone-viewport (390x700) interaction test pins the mobile cascade\nCI never saw (interaction + VRT run at 1280px) — both tab variants keep min\n48x90 and carry no touch-target class, the menu item grows to 44px min-height\nand gains no min-width. Uses page.viewport() from @vitest/browser/context;\n@vitest/browser@4.1.7 (already in the store as the provider''s own dependency)\nbecomes an explicit devDependency so tsc and typed lint resolve the module.\n\n* ASMA-8210 drop @vitest/browser devDep; source page from vitest/browser\n\nThe devDependency existed only so tsc and typed lint could resolve the\npage.viewport import — but adding it made pnpm re-resolve unrelated peer\ncontexts across the lockfile (supports-color combinatorics plus a sourcemap-\ncodec drift). The repo already had the right pattern: interaction-api.ts\nexports userEvent from ''vitest/browser'', whose context.d.ts chains to the\nprovider''s types with no extra install. page rides the same module, so the\ntest now imports it through interaction-api.ts, and package.json plus\npnpm-lock.yaml are byte-identical to master again (verified with\npnpm install --frozen-lockfile).","tree":{"sha":"23046583cf065c917934dc6689bc8dc075d37f83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/23046583cf065c917934dc6689bc8dc075d37f83"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/ff8b3445105292db4741b6b27b5dd336fe8429e1","verification":{"payload":"tree 23046583cf065c917934dc6689bc8dc075d37f83\nparent d4ad9a8f2a70dd8c8b46ab15f2634abc178724ad\nauthor Marin Pesterean <91586985+mark31072@users.noreply.github.com> 1789978211 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789978211 +0300\n\nASMA-8210 TB-02: pressable primitive + touch-readiness (#202)\n\n* ASMA-8210 add CSS touch-readiness primitives and opt in Button, Tab, MenuItem\n\nFour opt-in utility classes in src/styles/index.css, shipped via dist/style.css:\n- .asma-touch-ready: kills the iOS/Android tap flash and the 300ms double-tap\n  delay on controls that already own a designed :active (Button).\n- .asma-pressable: same, plus 0.7-opacity :active feedback for controls that\n  had no pressed state at all (Tab, MenuItem).\n- .asma-hit-area: transparent centred ::after overlay giving isolated controls\n  a 44px pointer target without changing the drawn size.\n- .asma-touch-target: 44px min-width/min-height gated to the mobile breakpoint\n  (max-width: 743px) for rows in a stack, where overlap would steal presses.\n\nAll utilities are inert at rest and on fine pointers, so the frozen public API\n(api-surface.test.ts) and the desktop VRT baselines are unchanged. Interaction\ntest covers hit-area geometry, tap-flash suppression, the mobile-only gating\nand the Button/pressable split.\n\n* ASMA-8210 move touch primitives out of @layer utilities to escape important: true\n\nReview finding: tailwind.config.ts sets important: true, and Tailwind v3\nimportantifies custom utilities declared inside @layer utilities too. That\ncompiled .asma-hit-area''s position: relative to !important, contradicting the\ndocumented override contract in both directions — a Tailwind position utility\ncould not override it (equal specificity, later source order) and an inline\nstyle lost to !important as well. The interaction test''s fixed-position probe\nonly passed because the flow origin happened to be (0,0).\n\nFix: the four primitives now live as unlayered CSS, the same technique the\nfile already uses for the prefers-reduced-motion block. Unlayered rules keep\ntheir source position after the @tailwind utilities output, so the one\ndeliberate !important (.asma-touch-target vs importantified min-h-*) still\nwins by source order, while .asma-hit-area emits WITHOUT !important (verified\nby compiling through the repo Tailwind config). Comments corrected, and the\ntest now asserts the probe''s computed position is ''fixed'', so the inline-wins\ncontract is actually exercised. Added .asma-hit-area caveats: not mobile-gated\n(desktop mouse targets grow too) and it clobbers a consumer ::after.\n\n* ASMA-8210 make touch-target a height-only floor and drop it from tabs\n\nReview finding B1: .asma-touch-target was a later-source override with equal\nspecificity and importance to Tailwind''s importantified min-h-*/min-w-*, so at\n<=743px it REPLACED designed minimums rather than flooring them — shrinking the\ndefault tab from min 48x90 to 44x44 and the small tab''s min-width from 90 to 44.\n\nFix, two parts:\n- The utility now sets min-height only. A min-width override can only replace\n  designed widths like the tab''s min-w-[90px]; width floors stay per-component.\n- StyledTab drops the class entirely. Measuring the real cascade showed BOTH\n  tab variants rest at an effective 48px min-height: the small variant''s\n  min-h-10 loses to the base min-h-12 because Tailwind emits .min-h-12 later\n  and cn (plain clsx, no tailwind-merge) keeps both classes on the element.\n  There is no 40->44 improvement to keep — any tab opt-in shrinks 48 to 44.\n  The pre-existing min-h stacking quirk (small tabs render 48px, not the Figma\n  40px) is documented and left for the ASMA-8220 sweep, since resolving it\n  moves VRT baselines. StyledMenuItem keeps the opt-in: 40px (32px dense) grows\n  to 44px on phones, and it declares no min-width.\n\nNew guard: a phone-viewport (390x700) interaction test pins the mobile cascade\nCI never saw (interaction + VRT run at 1280px) — both tab variants keep min\n48x90 and carry no touch-target class, the menu item grows to 44px min-height\nand gains no min-width. Uses page.viewport() from @vitest/browser/context;\n@vitest/browser@4.1.7 (already in the store as the provider''s own dependency)\nbecomes an explicit devDependency so tsc and typed lint resolve the module.\n\n* ASMA-8210 drop @vitest/browser devDep; source page from vitest/browser\n\nThe devDependency existed only so tsc and typed lint could resolve the\npage.viewport import — but adding it made pnpm re-resolve unrelated peer\ncontexts across the lockfile (supports-color combinatorics plus a sourcemap-\ncodec drift). The repo already had the right pattern: interaction-api.ts\nexports userEvent from ''vitest/browser'', whose context.d.ts chains to the\nprovider''s types with no extra install. page rides the same module, so the\ntest now imports it through interaction-api.ts, and package.json plus\npnpm-lock.yaml are byte-identical to master again (verified with\npnpm install --frozen-lockfile).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsOZjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxCEQAAqjlVcB6n1FHcyYcMVW9zub\n/X7OpqLoZBL/72sqmSes7NQclS+pt3/Mf36XBkjsxRuQo9UPRsOr5KTPaY5uSjkU\n5qf5KNoG5yaakgtDhQYPODwcVmq+jd8IdAL54R5+pXnrIxBcKKPbkAMHH8bIlVqT\nG6pC7tvecJgpmxVxsI9YypMdSRGAGqiJ+HPMixUVlmbzZQ2ydRY5stjutpYGfXfZ\nQLBq5auA1gFN8sgsK3z5Rd4B+mSSv17qf4bs2Um3govWHgZGsJq5I9Xngci0QhtC\nBT/dBkryWU6K3h0so2Y+NBEt2lSUpfWpfuJJtBHNQaEU4qYq4rrTXgpnXRVCCW/z\nLr2XIjIYjBN5lomQSVGyxGhH4qmvaC+eLEPXuun5ihIcXc4TGMKzG6hbGI2dHXHd\nfJSfEnFklJNKO2xxui5pXdlT0JpQz77k32YcrntgYbPT3rzboupYc8KlxFaP8+Ju\nQoYGZki3wsE8s2+cwyAqRrl4dcoZCrNa8PLFgbtkWqdnOhy5CV2wqGpLMZlKkwuE\nzrGUN5NoGf7SWYZQ4MLmWTbmRL5keeAi6Th3TaM/OTRXLJZZNe58Mnb60g3XaujT\n4VcKtsRjr+fmksna/Ox/Vq3n52m4LfYAd1RtDmOKZTNg2f3qSt3YZyXPSLh+b3Fx\nLPbG8RCekcq/0fJhtZnd\n=MTTq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T08:10:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/ff8b3445105292db4741b6b27b5dd336fe8429e1","node_id":"C_kwDORvrv4doAKGZmOGIzNDQ1MTA1MjkyZGI0NzQxYjZiM