":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/a2225ef53fec6f847e36fcb3f1d8d0a6f79aec10","node_id":"C_kwDORvrv4doAKGEyMjI1ZWY1M2ZlYzZmODQ3ZTM2ZmNiM2YxZDhkMGE2Zjc5YWVjMTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/ad2a316c1b7047a0f8a29507d2da4634cbaeb777","sha":"ad2a316c1b7047a0f8a29507d2da4634cbaeb777","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/ad2a316c1b7047a0f8a29507d2da4634cbaeb777"}],"sha":"a2225ef53fec6f847e36fcb3f1d8d0a6f79aec10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/a2225ef53fec6f847e36fcb3f1d8d0a6f79aec10"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/263779196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/VasiliiPeicov","id":263779196,"login":"VasiliiPeicov","node_id":"U_kgDOD7jzfA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/VasiliiPeicov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/ad2a316c1b7047a0f8a29507d2da4634cbaeb777/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T18:35:29Z","email":"vasilii.peicov@carasent.com","name":"VasiliiPeicov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T18:35:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix/asma 8179 uicore chevron flip and select width (#195)\n\n* fix(inputs): ASMA-8179 Flip the chevron with a name Tailwind 4 cannot also claim\n\n`rotate-180` is not safe to write in this package. It is a Tailwind 3 build and\nemits that class as `transform: … rotate(var(--tw-rotate)) …`, while a consuming\napp on Tailwind 4 emits the same name as the individual `rotate` property. Both\nrules match the icon, both apply, and 180° + 180° lands back at 360° — which is\nwhy the chevron flipped correctly in this package''s own Storybook and never\nflipped in the product (ASMA-7890). Verified in the running app: the DOM carried\n`rotate-180`, `getComputedStyle` reported `rotate: 180deg` *and*\n`transform: matrix(-1, 0, 0, -1, 0, 0)`, and the rendered chevron still pointed\ndown.\n\nEvery usage now goes through a new `flip-180` utility defined here alone, so it\ncan only be applied once. It sets `transform` rather than `rotate` so\n`transition-transform` keeps animating it under Tailwind 3. `rotate-180` is\nblocklisted rather than merely unused — Tailwind generates a class from any\noccurrence of the string, including one in a comment — so it no longer ships at\nall and a consumer writing it in its own JSX gets only its own build''s rule.\n\nAlso: `StyledSelect`''s size middleware hardcoded `reference.width + 20`, so every\ndropdown was 20px wider than the field that opened it and `shift` then slid it\nsideways. It now starts at the reference width, as `StyledSelectAutocomplete`\nalready did. `minWidth` is kept rather than a hard `width`, so a long option\nlabel can still widen the list instead of being clipped.\n\nTwo interaction tests cover both; both fail against the previous code.\n\nVRT baselines for stories with an open select move — the list is 20px narrower.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(vrt): ASMA-8179 Re-baseline the two open-select stories\n\nThe list is 20px narrower now that the size middleware stops adding `+ 20` to\nthe reference width, so these two are intended changes, not drift. A full local\n`vrt check` moved only these: 378 passed, 2 failed, 9 skipped — re-baselined with\n`--grep` rather than `--update-snapshots=all`, so nothing else was rewritten.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: trim verbose ASMA-8179 comments\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d59a6b2cf66de3b35388ac7b2a9bced2bfadfaca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/d59a6b2cf66de3b35388ac7b2a9bced2bfadfaca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/ad2a316c1b7047a0f8a29507d2da4634cbaeb777","verification":{"payload":"tree d59a6b2cf66de3b35388ac7b2a9bced2bfadfaca\nparent b8ea7ee2afed5719d6476e466414ef6ce7aefb61\nauthor VasiliiPeicov <vasilii.peicov@carasent.com> 1789497329 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789497329 +0300\n\nFix/asma 8179 uicore chevron flip and select width (#195)\n\n* fix(inputs): ASMA-8179 Flip the chevron with a name Tailwind 4 cannot also claim\n\n`rotate-180` is not safe to write in this package. It is a Tailwind 3 build and\nemits that class as `transform: … rotate(var(--tw-rotate)) …`, while a consuming\napp on Tailwind 4 emits the same name as the individual `rotate` property. Both\nrules match the icon, both apply, and 180° + 180° lands back at 360° — which is\nwhy the chevron flipped correctly in this package''s own Storybook and never\nflipped in the product (ASMA-7890). Verified in the running app: the DOM carried\n`rotate-180`, `getComputedStyle` reported `rotate: 180deg` *and*\n`transform: matrix(-1, 0, 0, -1, 0, 0)`, and the rendered chevron still pointed\ndown.\n\nEvery usage now goes through a new `flip-180` utility defined here alone, so it\ncan only be applied once. It sets `transform` rather than `rotate` so\n`transition-transform` keeps animating it under Tailwind 3. `rotate-180` is\nblocklisted rather than merely unused — Tailwind generates a class from any\noccurrence of the string, including one in a comment — so it no longer ships at\nall and a consumer writing it in its own JSX gets only its own build''s rule.\n\nAlso: `StyledSelect`''s size middleware hardcoded `reference.width + 20`, so every\ndropdown was 20px wider than the field that opened it and `shift` then slid it\nsideways. It now starts at the reference width, as `StyledSelectAutocomplete`\nalready did. `minWidth` is kept rather than a hard `width`, so a long option\nlabel can still widen the list instead of being clipped.\n\nTwo interaction tests cover both; both fail against the previous code.\n\nVRT baselines for stories with an open select move — the list is 20px narrower.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(vrt): ASMA-8179 Re-baseline the two open-select stories\n\nThe list is 20px narrower now that the size middleware stops adding `+ 20` to\nthe reference width, so these two are intended changes, not drift. A full local\n`vrt check` moved only these: 378 passed, 2 failed, 9 skipped — re-baselined with\n`--grep` rather than `--update-snapshots=all`, so nothing else was rewritten.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: trim verbose ASMA-8179 comments\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqY/xCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvNgQAJLBPYE2fCM8Few1zWwf8n