11d5fb6734","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/21500cb5c01437946d7298527147a311d5fb6734"}],"sha":"c163f2296df7ccdfc8da3af13765d689efc60143","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/c163f2296df7ccdfc8da3af13765d689efc60143"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91586985?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mark31072","id":91586985,"login":"mark31072","node_id":"U_kgDOBXWBqQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/21500cb5c01437946d7298527147a311d5fb6734/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T12:23:00Z","email":"91586985+mark31072@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Marin Pesterean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T12:23:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ASMA-8143 burn down the cheap-markup axe allowlist (124 -> 67 entries) (#191)\n\n* fix(a11y): ASMA-8143 burn down 57 cheap-markup axe allowlist entries\n\n`.storybook/preview.ts` gates the suite at `a11y.test = ''error''`; stories that\nwere already failing when ASMA-8136 landed carry a per-story `test: ''todo''`\noverride. This clears the entries that are fixable with markup alone.\n\nScoped to the five cheap markup rules. Measured before/after by flipping every\nremaining override to `''error''` and reading the rule ids back out of the\nfailures (recipe now recorded in docs/a11y-allowlist.md):\n\n  label                49 -> 0\n  button-name          23 -> 1\n  aria-allowed-attr     7 -> 0\n  aria-hidden-focus     4 -> 0\n  nested-interactive    5 -> 4\n  color-contrast       54 -> 54   (untouched - needs design decisions)\n\nEvery other rule is unchanged by construction. 124 -> 67 entries, 6 story files\ncleared outright.\n\nThe fixes that were not just a call-site `aria-label`:\n\n- StyledFormControlLabel names its control with `aria-labelledby` from the same\n  visible text. StyledCheckbox/StyledRadio render their own `<label>` around the\n  real `<input>`, so an outer `<label>` nests and axe''s `closest(''label'')`\n  resolves to the inner, textless one. Also covers `<button role=\"switch\">`,\n  which a `<label>` cannot name at all.\n- StyledInteractiveChip emits `aria-readonly` only for the checkbox type. The\n  attribute is not allowed on `role=\"radio\"` (ARIA 1.2 puts it on `radiogroup`),\n  so every radio chip shipped a disallowed attribute, `aria-readonly=\"false\"`\n  included.\n- PathfinderCard''s off-screen measure layer is `inert`. It duplicates slots that\n  can hold real buttons, so Tab landed on an invisible second copy of the card''s\n  own action - a real bug, not only an axe finding.\n- The table checkbox gains `decorative` (mirroring the core component) and the\n  select column adopts it. The wrapping `div` was already the real control;\n  axe is explicit that `aria-hidden` + `tabIndex={-1}` never satisfied\n  `nested-interactive`.\n\nNo visual change: every name is `aria-label`/`aria-labelledby`, `decorative`\nkeeps the same classes and `data-*` state attributes, and `inert` does not\nrender. VRT confirms pixel-identity.\n\nOut of scope and deliberately left allowlisted, each with its rationale intact:\ncolor-contrast (54), aria-valid-attr-value (4), nested-interactive in\nPathfinderCard (4, a structural change to the card''s interaction model),\nempty-table-header (3), heading-order (2), label-title-only (2),\nscrollable-region-focusable (2), landmark-unique (2), duplicate-id-active (1),\naria-input-field-name (1), aria-required-children (1).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(vrt): ASMA-8143 skip racy pointer-cancellation screenshot\n\nThe story''s long interactive play races the DOM-settle screenshot; its end\nstate is focus/hover-dependent since the autocomplete clear button became\nfocus-conditional (#188). Same treatment as the existing SKIP entries; the\nplay''s assertions still run in the interaction suite.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"42372c790ea966d508a1938405d40534357bd6c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/42372c790ea966d508a1938405d40534357bd6c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/21500cb5c01437946d7298527147a311d5fb6734","verification":{"payload":"tree 42372c790ea966d508a1938405d40534357bd6c4\nparent fab24d58ee7d36263fdb954aea4532c34c4ecc9a\nauthor Marin Pesterean <91586985+mark31072@users.noreply.github.com> 1789388580 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789388580 +0300\n\nASMA-8143 burn down the cheap-markup axe allowlist (124 -> 67 entries) (#191)\n\n* fix(a11y): ASMA-8143 burn down 57 cheap-markup axe allowlist entries\n\n`.storybook/preview.ts` gates the suite at `a11y.test = ''error''`; stories that\nwere already failing when ASMA-8136 landed carry a per-story `test: ''todo''`\noverride. This clears the entries that are fixable with markup alone.\n\nScoped to the five cheap markup rules. Measured before/after by flipping every\nremaining override to `''error''` and reading the rule ids back out of the\nfailures (recipe now recorded in docs/a11y-allowlist.md):\n\n  label                49 -> 0\n  button-name          23 -> 1\n  aria-allowed-attr     7 -> 0\n  aria-hidden-focus     4 -> 0\n  nested-interactive    5 -> 4\n  color-contrast       54 -> 54   (untouched - needs design decisions)\n\nEvery other rule is unchanged by construction. 124 -> 67 entries, 6 story files\ncleared outright.\n\nThe fixes that were not just a call-site `aria-label`:\n\n- StyledFormControlLabel names its control with `aria-labelledby` from the same\n  visible text. StyledCheckbox/StyledRadio render their own `<label>` around the\n  real `<input>`, so an outer `<label>` nests and axe''s `closest(''label'')`\n  resolves to the inner, textless one. Also covers `<button role=\"switch\">`,\n  which a `<label>` cannot name at all.\n- StyledInteractiveChip emits `aria-readonly` only for the checkbox type. The\n  attribute is not allowed on `role=\"radio\"` (ARIA 1.2 puts it on `radiogroup`),\n  so every radio chip shipped a disallowed attribute, `aria-readonly=\"false\"`\n  included.\n- PathfinderCard''s off-screen measure layer is `inert`. It duplicates slots that\n  can hold real buttons, so Tab landed on an invisible second copy of the card''s\n  own action - a real bug, not only an axe finding.\n- The table checkbox gains `decorative` (mirroring the core component) and the\n  select column adopts it. The wrapping `div` was already the real control;\n  axe is explicit that `aria-hidden` + `tabIndex={-1}` never satisfied\n  `nested-interactive`.\n\nNo visual change: every name is `aria-label`/`aria-labelledby`, `decorative`\nkeeps the same classes and `data-*` state attributes, and `inert` does not\nrender. VRT confirms pixel-identity.\n\nOut of scope and deliberately left allowlisted, each with its rationale intact:\ncolor-contrast (54), aria-valid-attr-value (4), nested-interactive in\nPathfinderCard (4, a structural change to the card''s interaction model),\nempty-table-header (3), heading-order (2), label-title-only (2),\nscrollable-region-focusable (2), landmark-unique (2), duplicate-id-active (1),\naria-input-field-name (1), aria-required-children (1).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(vrt): ASMA-8143 skip racy pointer-cancellation screenshot\n\nThe story''s long interactive play races the DOM-settle screenshot; its end\nstate is focus/hover-dependent since the autocomplete clear button became\nfocus-conditional (#188). Same treatment as the existing SKIP entries; the\nplay''s assertions still run in the interaction suite.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp+ckCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzPcQAAJ/SvuRXwnGTZE5kLLJD+av\nai8Qmi5XSZtjbE4Z/VZjwnpr67+zj34VqzqrnuV1YYWdNm9sxyGW1jPeaMVvWqCz\nQryxSTrIZXKMfi3Ir4kh1adZP6b0TFUuO5/gG1jcUUOVRHytSAXso8BamRZqmTsx\nri4FPMVztTk1EErVykEJTsxn9uzbnEbFKdxaJSXS3YfoB8vo6+zimWnSZrNeG/kq\nn42vGuJpb8i6c0y0ttkGaBIDR4b/JpXAHTXovTitXjcDKfD0YLG/4Zv7m3v0Y2PC\nWkCxCq+eejuwAhWVIJZPPL15GpluOY7Xk9L+nqkP4rECPxp3xTVgEmF+NdcI8yY9\nhwwu4siQTO5eKqdEoR+FiMvnCo2OFcZO5/OxCJWdYMPYvRwTAqUrNv7h+0TIUOKL\nPmtkZJxL2N6M31p1/1WO+pTsCkSsiZ76/a58OgqVYKkQseUdkxeKfdC9Is5bYc49\n8k0Bysxs79julmtl5SWS6Qm6/M1MoEI+T1OT++2LqYVvoez/NWl1VQscsSe0A+GV\nZzKMHx2k2r77P0IF5pGfXTcKkG1K7QnMWHrmDM2eFNdx5mnZ/9vzH6unJWeWkEYZ\nOTrXCzizFVGpASEeQ2j1+dGg5M+RxrtO57wWP7i6BBWXD7ZCPZVIzUphIMSrNahk\nJ/xOHkMlW43p6lgddxgW\n=S+Xa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T12:23:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.gi