cb4ae025da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/8ca6e658f5fe369778c24c9b725a49cb4ae025da"}],"sha":"d507dd2f6e94f5e5d0198d2a3f86d0ad3fcf7dc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/d507dd2f6e94f5e5d0198d2a3f86d0ad3fcf7dc1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/264966161?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/doicovSanya","id":264966161,"login":"doicovSanya","node_id":"U_kgDOD8sQEQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/8ca6e658f5fe369778c24c9b725a49cb4ae025da/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T09:00:11Z","email":"Alexandr.Doicov@carasent.com","name":"doicovSanya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T09:00:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(dialog-footer): ASMA-7099 add loading, endIcon and tooltip to footer buttons (#185)\n\nConsumer-driven additions to StyledDialogFooter''s right-cluster buttons, found by\nmigrating the real hand-rolled footers rather than by guesswork.\n\n- `loading` shows a spinner after the label and disables the button, marking it\n  aria-busy. The footers being replaced swapped the label FOR a spinner, which\n  changes the button''s width mid-submit — that is exactly what the hard-coded\n  `w-[98px]` / `w-[103px]` workarounds in crm were compensating for. Keeping the\n  label makes the width stable on its own.\n- `endIcon` mirrors StyledButton, for footers that already render a trailing\n  indicator.\n- `tooltip` wraps the button in a StyledTooltip. A falsy value renders no tooltip,\n  so the prevailing `tooltip={disabled && ''Locked for editing''}` idiom reads\n  naturally. It anchors on a wrapper around the button because a disabled button\n  emits no pointer events — and explaining why the primary action is disabled is\n  the only reason these footers use a tooltip at all.\n\nNote the commit type: this repo''s release gate derives the version bump from\nconventional-commit subjects (asma-workflows release_gate.py; its file-pattern\ncheck is commented out), so a subject without a `feat:`/`fix:` prefix publishes\nnothing. The ASMA-7099 component commit had no prefix and skipped its own\nrelease — it only reached npm by riding the next `fix(select):` commit into\n3.79.1, which understates a new public component as a patch. The .changeset\nfiles in this repo do NOT drive CI; they only feed the manual publish-version.sh\npath.\n\nVerified: tsc clean, unit 454/454, storybook 341/341, interaction 88 passed /\n11 skipped, eslint clean, VRT 7/7 (the 5 pre-existing footer baselines are\nunchanged, confirming the additions are opt-in).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6495b77605065bb02f2544e289289227ea6c6cc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/6495b77605065bb02f2544e289289227ea6c6cc2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/8ca6e658f5fe369778c24c9b725a49cb4ae025da","verification":{"payload":"tree 6495b77605065bb02f2544e289289227ea6c6cc2\nparent 8edfb2897565d6abdb8b0d2307566dc386e0dd1a\nauthor doicovSanya <Alexandr.Doicov@carasent.com> 1789117211 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789117211 +0300\n\nfeat(dialog-footer): ASMA-7099 add loading, endIcon and tooltip to footer buttons (#185)\n\nConsumer-driven additions to StyledDialogFooter''s right-cluster buttons, found by\nmigrating the real hand-rolled footers rather than by guesswork.\n\n- `loading` shows a spinner after the label and disables the button, marking it\n  aria-busy. The footers being replaced swapped the label FOR a spinner, which\n  changes the button''s width mid-submit — that is exactly what the hard-coded\n  `w-[98px]` / `w-[103px]` workarounds in crm were compensating for. Keeping the\n  label makes the width stable on its own.\n- `endIcon` mirrors StyledButton, for footers that already render a trailing\n  indicator.\n- `tooltip` wraps the button in a StyledTooltip. A falsy value renders no tooltip,\n  so the prevailing `tooltip={disabled && ''Locked for editing''}` idiom reads\n  naturally. It anchors on a wrapper around the button because a disabled button\n  emits no pointer events — and explaining why the primary action is disabled is\n  the only reason these footers use a tooltip at all.\n\nNote the commit type: this repo''s release gate derives the version bump from\nconventional-commit subjects (asma-workflows release_gate.py; its file-pattern\ncheck is commented out), so a subject without a `feat:`/`fix:` prefix publishes\nnothing. The ASMA-7099 component commit had no prefix and skipped its own\nrelease — it only reached npm by riding the next `fix(select):` commit into\n3.79.1, which understates a new public component as a patch. The .changeset\nfiles in this repo do NOT drive CI; they only feed the manual publish-version.sh\npath.\n\nVerified: tsc clean, unit 454/454, storybook 341/341, interaction 88 passed /\n11 skipped, eslint clean, VRT 7/7 (the 5 pre-existing footer baselines are\nunchanged, confirming the additions are opt-in).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo8MbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWhEQAJrhnKHm2EhPy6Gjw4inUdSp\nPjs9/vASChHB1wxRjJJRIX5KZeVdMbP4iglzqVv1jFhP4yEGRWnoNRkWgtuIapW2\n94oWopmLDQ3Brm7Fr9b3vsdlVKvnhfhsTTu0dH8WbljCK5nFzFQDDD0Jfsn0TMcI\nt6Y4KpSuoDfnm2H/1BK5LEjxR73nXeSvWup/P2+v0TSuqo9LimGGYLssfoh1drpL\n+GtL/amI23dENAL0D/BQ9Fv4puUmbQK08g1y7F2QI7PzKSV15BwPs2R4ZIOrPo1M\nHkk2435DB+86Nu55mF8/5zEFs9GBmOScm96oy7WIUh40fodosDJIa2NAlije2nqW\ngvpiHx/fVo4YJ7QeX4Xm9gvuNSLMFP59EtbJRSpFn9BFDuRr4cI48cgTdyLe+4v7\nvKVwxDJ4i51mWE3+QmRZGC/RZS6Kx0EzeAT51LUl1DvkdgU51TwMtmksPHNnwOzJ\ni1Frt5O0bdOiQJw9BecjssZzhhqRRImnZWqSDaZCxYYaHkhjNaOajq4W6J3AuDJF\nLAbvoslWiGZu8RrJIsj+efG0k+kA+APjeRsTS8DXlDjZmG3vR8S/8l7dkU8vakk/\ngjFnXYfQG5uYb9SYxP0Bz/EnjjB873/bKc/p6X7dTHoUcCwyEPmSSZULcoQ8j4aV\nzJMrPe3Fmz7ZVCvVYu8E\n=MXZP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T09:00:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/8ca6e658f5fe369778c24c9b725a49cb4ae025da","node_id":"C_kwDORvrv4doAKDhjYTZlNjU4ZjVmZTM2OTc3OGMyNGM5YjcyNWE0OWNiNGFlMDI1ZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/8edfb2897565d6abdb8b0d2307566dc386e0dd1a","sha":"8edfb2897565d6abdb8b0d2307566dc386e0dd1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/8edfb2897565d6abdb8b0d2307566dc386e0dd1a"}],"sha":"8ca6e658f5fe369778c24c9b725a49cb4ae025da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/8ca6e658f5fe369778c24c9b725a49cb4ae025da"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/264966161?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/doicovSanya","id":264966161,"login":"doicovSanya","node_id":"U_kgDOD8sQEQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/8edfb2897565d6abdb8b0d2307566dc386e0dd1a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T08:33:23Z","email":"Alexandr.Doicov@carasent.com","name":"doicovSanya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T08:33:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(select): ASMA-8080 set the select popover radius to 4px (#184)\n\nThe listbox used rounded-lg (8px) while its own trigger draws a 4px border\n(field-styles outline overlay), which became obvious once the popover was\nattached flush to the field.\n\nFigma exposes the radius as a token rather than a measurement: get_variable_defs\non the Menus node 16073-19226 returns menus: 4, alongside button: 4 and\ntext-field: 4. StyledMenu and StyledPopover were already `rounded`, so the two\nselect listboxes were the only Menus-family surfaces at 8px — this removes the\noutlier. Stale `rounded-lg` claims in the components'' comments corrected too.\n\nNote: VRT cannot see this on its own. The change moves only the corner arc of a\nwhite surface with a 1px border — 6-10 differing px per frame, under the\nharness''s maxDiffPixels: 120 — so `pnpm vrt` was 365/365 green without ever\ncomparing the corners. Verified instead by reading the computed border-radius in\nthe container (4px, matching the field) and by a temporary maxDiffPixels: 0 run\n(config restored, verified identical to committed). The 20 affected baselines\nwere re-accepted so the committed screenshots show the shipped 4px corners.\n\ntsc + eslint clean, vitest 878 passed / 11 skipped, full vrt 365/365 green.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"24a557b0c19dafb4397039127fc8b4bd9ad83bf4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/24a557b0c19dafb4397039127fc8b4bd9ad83bf4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/8edfb2897565d6abdb8b0d2307566dc386e0dd1a","verification":{"payload":"tree 24a557b0c19dafb4397039127fc8b4bd9ad83bf4\nparent de43b32a01ee77c666d5054cbce3727189de17d2\nauthor doicovSanya <Alexandr.Doicov@carasent.com> 1789115603 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789115603 +0300\n\nfix(select): ASMA-8080 set the select popover radius to 4px (#184)\n\nThe listbox used rounded-lg (8px) while its own trigger draws a 4px border\n(field-styles outline overlay), which became obvious once the popover was\nattached flush to the field.\n\nFigma exposes the radius as a token rather than a measurement: get_variable_defs\non the Menus node 16073-19226 returns menus: 4, alongside button: 4 and\ntext-field: 4. StyledMenu and StyledPopover were already `rounded`, so the two\nselect listboxes were the only Menus-family surfaces at 8px — this removes the\noutlier. Stale `rounded-lg` claims in the components'' comments corrected too.\n\nNote: VRT cannot see this on its own. The change moves only the corner arc of a\nwhite surface with a 1px border — 6-10 differing px per frame, under the\nharness''s maxDiffPixels: 120 — so `pnpm vrt` was 365/365 green without ever\ncomparing the corners. Verified instead by reading the computed border-radius in\nthe container (4px, matching the field) and by a temporary maxDiffPixels: 0 run\n(config restored, verified identical to committed). The 20 affected baselines\nwere re-accepted so the committed screenshots show the shipped 4px corners.\n\ntsc + eslint clean, vitest 878 passed / 11 skipped, full vrt 365/365 green.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo7zTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAliEQAJvhD3kjBEdeINNBdokJSZi8\n5/Egl7Li5zVy9ZfcDrcpfFW780WybSh2Sn51FBSQEzjOm4jOKBxbal+dvUFt8Juu\nlKYckMGqyrHr3V9M96CgZLQMsrwgdFW2W1+PuaSSlnPtLAYomJ5qX/74T8FnAWEq\ntccRHVhmSR7MGVEKszbnLYLVJQ23H/+ohVYVHsARc4gCjTtErGos9K53ZaWtQkhO\n+cDRS9uE8kyp7jsORgOueZTJT3P8lTLpmSIrX4Y4B+VCHb7aeX8Xa26SVo2OeGO2\nrYNx24LD+515WtRdL1eXnY1v+CMGxdCLsDYM0f9ZFT6PbZN8o6En8/i94HjO2fmF\n2AXNvf/4xw+JttecO9BkAEoC1i+59DNpo0SZbhUIP+FqYsQF0THgDMv0lvNh9N2/\nmkmXlT5YdWImzWcucHe5uGvTeFqO2RjsflXYwZx1QTQ9BD7ZkGlOjzsnXldzeNIb\nddSr9R/4YBKRII2Fpt/+PULIXgsv//l129BDVU4l8FCS+sBePHSaH2FgJnR5Pezs\nNaMW+1tsj9bcvb568Ut3mmSqM5Dsb/aDBmuCfX0NSTmKseOcKzL87IaflEBcBAEr\nRKKgUPKbdUqEpqfSoJuMKJ/kGAYGyZR3DmqxZp9RaOlDDJsndID3zUpwIqKiBWML\n0wLf6lANvxDasFIccfvX\n=r+Yo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T08:33:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/8edfb2897565d6abdb8b0d2307566dc386e0dd1a","node_id":"C_kwDORvrv4doAKDhlZGZiMjg5NzU2NWQ2YWJkYjhiMGQyMzA3NTY2ZGMzODZlMGRkMWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/de43b32a01ee77c666d5054cbce3727189de17d2","sha":"de43b32a01ee77c666d5054cbce3727189de17d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/de43b32a01ee77c666d5054cbce3727189de17d2"}],"sha":"8edfb2897565d6abdb8b0d2307566dc386e0dd1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/8edfb2897565d6abdb8b0d2307566dc386e0dd1a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/264966161?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/doicovSanya","id":264966161,"login":"doicovSanya","node_id":"U_kgDOD8sQEQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/de43b32a01ee77c666d5054cbce3727189de17d2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T08:06:50Z","email":"Alexandr.Doicov@carasent.com","name":"doicovSanya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T08:06:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ASMA-7099 add shared StyledDialogFooter bottom actions pattern (#183)\n\nOne responsive fixed bottom actions footer for dialogues and other layouts\nacross Ad Opus, Samhandling, Genesis and Ad Voca, replacing the pattern each\napp had hand-rolled as `flex justify-between border-t p-4` (75 files across 10\nrepos, plus 15 one-off *FormFooter components).\n\nImplements the Figma \"Dialog footer\" component set (26769-135283) as two\nclusters: a Left cluster of destructive/utility actions and a Right cluster of\nCancel plus the primary action. The Figma State property (Create/Edit/More/\nReset filter) is deliberately not a prop — it is the emergent result of which\nactions the caller passes and how much room the container leaves, which is the\npoint of the ticket. Callers describe their actions once and the same footer\nresolves to the approved 1-, 2-, 3- and 3+-action layouts.\n\nLeft-cluster planning reuses the planToolbarActions engine already behind\nDynamicToolbar and PageHeader, driven by measured widths through the width\nregistry: labels hold while they fit, collapse to icon-only next, and retreat\ninto an icon-only More menu once even that overflows. The menu opens upward,\nbecause a footer sits at the bottom edge of its container. The right cluster is\nmeasured but never collapsed or overflowed — the primary action must stay\nreachable at every width, and the measured node is the inner non-growing span\nso a flex-1 wrapper cannot report the width it grew to.\n\nMobile is derived from the container width, not the viewport, so a footer in a\nnarrow popover compacts on a desktop screen too; the hand-rolled footers keyed\noff useIsMobileView() and got that wrong. Padding and gap step 16px -> 8px below\n470px, the breakpoint adopus-app-directory''s NoteFormFooter already shipped.\n\nTwo defects found while verifying this, both fixed here:\n\n- Toolbar action buttons and the More trigger carried no `type`, so a bare\n  <button> inside a <form> defaults to type=\"submit\" and fired the form instead\n  of its own handler. Footers commonly sit inside a form, and the calendar\n  event-crud footer had been working around it with preventDefault(). Now\n  type=\"button\" in ToolbarActionButton and MoreTriggerButton — visually inert,\n  confirmed by unchanged PageHeader/DynamicToolbar VRT baselines.\n- An icon-less action collapsing its label rendered a blank button. Guarded in\n  the footer; an explicit canHideLabel from the caller still wins. The same\n  hazard remains in collapseLabelsFromLeft for every planner consumer, but\n  fixing it there changes PageHeader/DynamicToolbar width decisions, so it is\n  reported separately rather than folded into this ticket.\n\nAlso: leadingSlot for Figma''s Checkbox+Label left variant or footer info text,\n`fixed` for a sticky footer carrying the DS \"Fixed bottom\" shadow, `rounded`\nfor a dialog paper''s bottom corners, `type: ''submit''` so the primary action can\ndrive a surrounding form, and `locale` for the More trigger''s accessible name.\n\nThe api-surface snapshot moves by exactly one additive line; nothing is removed\nor renamed. The Gallery story is axe-clean without an a11y-allowlist entry.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"91bd7c33490bc672ac188f7443f6d48d8ffc2fdb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/91bd7c33490bc672ac188f7443f6d48d8ffc2fdb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/de43b32a01ee77c666d5054cbce3727189de17d2","verification":{"payload":"tree 91bd7c33490bc672ac188f7443f6d48d8ffc2fdb\nparent d29b72f8ad22c7dcb30b052007dc5826f3037512\nauthor doicovSanya <Alexandr.Doicov@carasent.com> 1789114010 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789114010 +0300\n\nASMA-7099 add shared StyledDialogFooter bottom actions pattern (#183)\n\nOne responsive fixed bottom actions footer for dialogues and other layouts\nacross Ad Opus, Samhandling, Genesis and Ad Voca, replacing the pattern each\napp had hand-rolled as `flex justify-between border-t p-4` (75 files across 10\nrepos, plus 15 one-off *FormFooter components).\n\nImplements the Figma \"Dialog footer\" component set (26769-135283) as two\nclusters: a Left cluster of destructive/utility actions and a Right cluster of\nCancel plus the primary action. The Figma State property (Create/Edit/More/\nReset filter) is deliberately not a prop — it is the emergent result of which\nactions the caller passes and how much room the container leaves, which is the\npoint of the ticket. Callers describe their actions once and the same footer\nresolves to the approved 1-, 2-, 3- and 3+-action layouts.\n\nLeft-cluster planning reuses the planToolbarActions engine already behind\nDynamicToolbar and PageHeader, driven by measured widths through the width\nregistry: labels hold while they fit, collapse to icon-only next, and retreat\ninto an icon-only More menu once even that overflows. The menu opens upward,\nbecause a footer sits at the bottom edge of its container. The right cluster is\nmeasured but never collapsed or overflowed — the primary action must stay\nreachable at every width, and the measured node is the inner non-growing span\nso a flex-1 wrapper cannot report the width it grew to.\n\nMobile is derived from the container width, not the viewport, so a footer in a\nnarrow popover compacts on a desktop screen too; the hand-rolled footers keyed\noff useIsMobileView() and got that wrong. Padding and gap step 16px -> 8px below\n470px, the breakpoint adopus-app-directory''s NoteFormFooter already shipped.\n\nTwo defects found while verifying this, both fixed here:\n\n- Toolbar action buttons and the More trigger carried no `type`, so a bare\n  <button> inside a <form> defaults to type=\"submit\" and fired the form instead\n  of its own handler. Footers commonly sit inside a form, and the calendar\n  event-crud footer had been working around it with preventDefault(). Now\n  type=\"button\" in ToolbarActionButton and MoreTriggerButton — visually inert,\n  confirmed by unchanged PageHeader/DynamicToolbar VRT baselines.\n- An icon-less action collapsing its label rendered a blank button. Guarded in\n  the footer; an explicit canHideLabel from the caller still wins. The same\n  hazard remains in collapseLabelsFromLeft for every planner consumer, but\n  fixing it there changes PageHeader/DynamicToolbar width decisions, so it is\n  reported separately rather than folded into this ticket.\n\nAlso: leadingSlot for Figma''s Checkbox+Label left variant or footer info text,\n`fixed` for a sticky footer carrying the DS \"Fixed bottom\" shadow, `rounded`\nfor a dialog paper''s bottom corners, `type: ''submit''` so the primary action can\ndrive a surrounding form, and `locale` for the More trigger''s accessible name.\n\nThe api-surface snapshot moves by exactly one additive line; nothing is removed\nor renamed. The Gallery story is axe-clean without an a11y-allowlist entry.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo7aaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADKsQAICeUDa3dMZxjs7YWOkN