.githubusercontent.com/u/91586985?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mark31072","id":91586985,"login":"mark31072","node_id":"U_kgDOBXWBqQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/bc0c5e6d8dbe08d95da115cb3547260e0a95f815/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T13:19:48Z","email":"91586985+mark31072@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Marin Pesterean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T13:19:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ASMA-8134 dedupe the remaining re-exportable table/datetime icons (#181)\n\nrefactor(dedupe): ASMA-8134 re-export six more table/datetime icons\n\nPR #170 closed most of ASMA-8134 but left all 18 remaining icon copies alone,\non the grounds that core''s narrow IIcon API would have to be widened first.\nThat holds for some of them, not all: six copies already pass only\nIIcon-expressible props at every call site, so they need no core API change.\nts:check passing unmodified is the proof.\n\nConverted to plain re-exports of the core icon they duplicate:\n- table/ChevronLeftIcon, table/ChevronRightIcon, table/DotsVerticalIcon\n- datetime/ChevronLeftIcon, datetime/ChevronRightIcon, datetime/CloseIcon\n\nEvery one of the 7 call sites passes both width and height explicitly, so\nthese copies'' 1rem/1em/20px defaults were never observable. That is what\nmakes them safe, and what is not true of the ones left behind.\n\nRendered-DOM diff, measured by server-rendering the old copy against the new\nre-export at each call site''s real props (not inferred from source): artwork\nand width/height identical everywhere. Three deltas, none geometric:\naria-hidden=''true'' focusable=''false'' added; class='''' where no className is\npassed; and at SubmenuExample.tsx:28 `color` moves from SVG attribute to\ninline style (same computed colour). The aria-hidden addition removes no\naccessible name -- none of these SVGs had a title, aria-label or text. VRT\n357 passed with no baseline PNG modified.\n\nStill not re-exportable, deliberately: table/ChevronDownIcon (call sites pass\nstyle={{transform: rotate()}} for the expand animation; IIcon has no style),\ntable/DropDownIcon and DropUpIcon (rely on the 1rem default, and IIcon.width\nis number so a wrapper can pin 16 but not 1rem), and four with no core\ncounterpart or different artwork. StyledButton/StyledCheckbox/StyledMenuItem\nremain design-gated in ASMA-8137 and are untouched.\n\nNo data-test, data-testid or root class changes. src/index.ts exports nothing\nfrom shared-components, so the frozen api-surface snapshot is unaffected.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"01b8ca8bb3b59f853ac8a4505d8bd2b863b717fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/01b8ca8bb3b59f853ac8a4505d8bd2b863b717fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/bc0c5e6d8dbe08d95da115cb3547260e0a95f815","verification":{"payload":"tree 01b8ca8bb3b59f853ac8a4505d8bd2b863b717fe\nparent 92347720b34f8fd48c4a0d517ab9861ea07b17bf\nauthor Marin Pesterean <91586985+mark31072@users.noreply.github.com> 1789046388 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789046388 +0300\n\nASMA-8134 dedupe the remaining re-exportable table/datetime icons (#181)\n\nrefactor(dedupe): ASMA-8134 re-export six more table/datetime icons\n\nPR #170 closed most of ASMA-8134 but left all 18 remaining icon copies alone,\non the grounds that core''s narrow IIcon API would have to be widened first.\nThat holds for some of them, not all: six copies already pass only\nIIcon-expressible props at every call site, so they need no core API change.\nts:check passing unmodified is the proof.\n\nConverted to plain re-exports of the core icon they duplicate:\n- table/ChevronLeftIcon, table/ChevronRightIcon, table/DotsVerticalIcon\n- datetime/ChevronLeftIcon, datetime/ChevronRightIcon, datetime/CloseIcon\n\nEvery one of the 7 call sites passes both width and height explicitly, so\nthese copies'' 1rem/1em/20px defaults were never observable. That is what\nmakes them safe, and what is not true of the ones left behind.\n\nRendered-DOM diff, measured by server-rendering the old copy against the new\nre-export at each call site''s real props (not inferred from source): artwork\nand width/height identical everywhere. Three deltas, none geometric:\naria-hidden=''true'' focusable=''false'' added; class='''' where no className is\npassed; and at SubmenuExample.tsx:28 `color` moves from SVG attribute to\ninline style (same computed colour). The aria-hidden addition removes no\naccessible name -- none of these SVGs had a title, aria-label or text. VRT\n357 passed with no baseline PNG modified.\n\nStill not re-exportable, deliberately: table/ChevronDownIcon (call sites pass\nstyle={{transform: rotate()}} for the expand animation; IIcon has no style),\ntable/DropDownIcon and DropUpIcon (rely on the 1rem default, and IIcon.width\nis number so a wrapper can pin 16 but not 1rem), and four with no core\ncounterpart or different artwork. StyledButton/StyledCheckbox/StyledMenuItem\nremain design-gated in ASMA-8137 and are untouched.\n\nNo data-test, data-testid or root class changes. src/index.ts exports nothing\nfrom shared-components, so the frozen api-surface snapshot is unaffected.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoq50CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8CkQAId51xn/A57WnaVTnjaYddD3\nHXPrEToJeyNufe1wWawpaZPiKGuEFENC+V7LbtEQ2gzhFlkD5EDILI0744KtEaKl\n34J1d0EUxl3Kqxo6tG6/dXXqQwAv6XyRPcah3/dBI/u1avCQbcuNM2HiZNmYh/rw\nNarLpDdfpSvT7cJblNOBFtqV55lHcP2QN0wAoLS4tu7raMCUUQqpMnA2BAh5/Sji\naGso9ZB/oR0wFRhJRDauPmFyXVjyKOfSHdOp/Z6v1ep1UvjSc/PvvdmWIZIURRxZ\nh46tkqnwTGw/z4bbAyCX43PyzrZePmSIbEP0y+UGvMkfxs/bF6EF/+C8i2elrV0Y\nhIgnBHWP1PTxFgdo1npoKPKQG4M/nIZVkONCNVWI94iwXpFKxiPLt7wGOMaACXqE\n8s4Kuvg+2FTzmqRX1O30ZOjGHf2RxX75VSkNlBZpRWxYxBR3RW9o+2jqXOQkKGdw\nT6SMdPF0vknl2K5jOs4YRs9H5gvjF28epMj+dqY7/mNLitOvDX1M3K39KJRQLX3W\nRqhfL76Oq1TDhbJYQxbPu7I22aHkgqxyjrFVR3dAsQ4d7AbbtA11S+5JlCjk9MlJ\nk+dJG+0jTaYzf/KYrXBQ7LRy0LuYbGB2T7lwMdGmRI9qzRtGTJz0TgHgz+7eWgga\nTKATfrrwex27Gy55oiON\n=AV8C\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-10T13:19:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public