SMA-8138 split 2.4.7 from 1.4.11, quantify F-07 scope\n\nF-15''s real first failure is SC 2.4.7 Focus Visible (AA) -- whether an\nindicator exists at all -- not 1.4.11, which governs the contrast of an\nindicator that does render. The dropped declaration means there was nothing\nin the DOM to measure, which is the sharpest statement of why only a\ntoken-level check could catch it.\n\nRecords what ASMA-8133''s PR #172 should and should not be read as clearing:\n2.4.7 pass, 1.4.11 pass, 2.4.13 Focus Appearance not claimed and out of AA\nscope. It would not pass anyway -- red-700 against the unfocused beta-500\nborder is 1.68, short of 2.4.13''s 3:1 focused/unfocused requirement.\n\nQuantifies F-07 from the repo rather than by estimate: 17 declarations\nresolve to gama-400 (15 button focus borders plus two input outline tokens),\nnone touched by #172, failing under default and fretex and passing under\ngreenish. So the primary focus indicator still fails 1.4.11 in two of three\nthemes after #172, and no CI gate can see it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(a11y): ASMA-8138 record F-07 blocking ASMA-8139 findings B and F\n\nCross-links a11y-keyboard-contract.md. Fixing those findings with the\nlibrary''s standard gama-400 focus ring before F-07 is resolved would trade an\ninvisible focus indicator for one failing 1.4.11 in two of three themes, which\nno gate can catch: axe has no wcag1411 rule and VRT would be green because the\nbaseline records the failing colour as correct.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(a11y): ASMA-8138 fail on a regression floor left by a lifted quarantine\n\nA floor for a pair that is no longer quarantined is dead weight that reads as\nif the pair were still failing. Verified by lifting F-11 and leaving its floor:\nthe orphan check goes red, and the pair correctly becomes a live failing\n1.4.11 assertion at 1.75 against the 3:1 requirement.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(a11y): ASMA-8138 refresh contrast gates after token repairs\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqonOTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATYgQAD4AWQb7iKb8T6V/AxUVr8dr\nnmTgTLFJGcUoMCDz+NRl5mLG3hZ8WGr72iOpNxui63UrA4xMkDG1IqIPrBvoa0cg\nljprT59QOMbhtULujEGkJGBhkG4pSAZbnbLwtVcdJHYW17igSvZzRuQZE2mnPkkf\nmDUTM7Oo7WA4qpq+AP+WAOXD1/4x20TaKJnA9fcteTgp0j3IGDTQeOherUV4kpbc\nK9sq1RrTqWUMzX29vahdr8NeSZyioHr0RUXZ3LjH5fxj9eSyPCvjgzn3JLK8pDzd\ntoKEQPvI+PAPBN9eT2SDxNfpes4DyjuY3DudCuOgadonBuIiNXaWxBmJ4q33MWPE\nEn05xEoGOgzWFZJ4PWf7WF+Nj7v9a2l8U6chaJpnN8whFw/ayH0QRAyYtDBj7uHl\n7OaiqjFsYaNtKr9/RUQ2Z2wValW6tPr6dPwKdpExG3EZPzv53Zk5tsjr++Y65uNL\nxyMTuJ/hVH6l/6IaM83t6YtX+Et5V5h2/X6SfSzBemJ9d8JOc0LjzjY18s2ESw/M\nT2pFuCLfkKhs9hRegJT7LbWtAEZr5bbGCBQEx/PlvMpNK4C8vvexuVail8nMQJBn\negksSNXEQ3e2XGAI7nbzRNuIenQvWJfwC5uRFtB5tEZ6T3sYD6FCNcT2e1eS8EQb\nIa5z44+xpspxOf+hc/Hl\n=LhwY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-10T09:08:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/e71d62793add7213f7f4674436143dce77a8df6c","node_id":"C_kwDORvrv4doAKGU3MWQ2Mjc5M2FkZDcyMTNmN2Y0Njc0NDM2MTQzZGNlNzdhOGRmNmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/924198a4f7ddca1741e8c02ac30de639b1b041bf","sha":"924198a4f7ddca1741e8c02ac30de639b1b041bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/924198a4f7ddca1741e8c02ac30de639b1b041bf"}],"sha":"e71d62793add7213f7f4674436143dce77a8df6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/e71d62793add7213f7f4674436143dce77a8df6c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91586985?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mark31072","id":91586985,"login":"mark31072","node_id":"U_kgDOBXWBqQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/924198a4f7ddca1741e8c02ac30de639b1b041bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T09:03:57Z","email":"91586985+mark31072@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Marin Pesterean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T09:03:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(a11y): ASMA-8139 verify focus tokens after theme repairs (#178)\n\n* test(a11y): ASMA-8139 keyboard and focus contract tests\n\nWave 3b of ASMA-8132. Adds a real-browser keyboard/focus contract suite for\nevery interactive component: Select, Autocomplete, Dialog, Tabs, Menu, Slider,\nTooltip, Snackbar, DatePicker and TimePicker. 81 passing assertions covering\nWCAG 2.1.1, 2.1.2, 2.4.3, 2.4.7, 1.4.13, 3.2.1, 4.1.2 and 4.1.3.\n\nNew `interaction` vitest project (real Chromium, Playwright/CDP key events),\nrun in CI by the new \"Keyboard & focus contract\" workflow. No stories are\nadded and no *.stories.tsx is touched, so VRT baselines and the axe gate are\nunaffected; components are mounted directly instead.\n\n11 contract defects found and reproduced. Per the wave-3 rule these are NOT\nfixed here — each is an it.skip naming the SC and the offending file, written\nup in docs/a11y-keyboard-contract.md and escalated. Every skip was verified by\nun-skipping and confirming it genuinely fails. Zero component source changed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(a11y): ASMA-8139 fix WCAG citation, add 2.4.11 coverage\n\nThe doc cited \"SC 2.4.11 focus appearance\", which is wrong on both counts:\n2.4.11 is Focus Not Obscured (Minimum) and says nothing about contrast, while\nFocus Appearance is 2.4.13 and is AAA. The AA criterion carrying the 3:1\nfocus-indicator requirement — the one actually being measured — is 1.4.11\nNon-text Contrast. Corrected throughout; no finding changes.\n\nActing on the same review note, adds real SC 2.4.11 coverage, which nothing\nelse in the epic checks: a library overlay must not entirely cover the control\nthat opened it. Five assertions across Select, Autocomplete, DatePicker and\nTooltip, using elementFromPoint so paint order and the top layer are respected,\nplus a self-check that deliberately covers a button and confirms the helper\nreports it — without that, a helper regression would leave the whole file\npassing while measuring nothing.\n\nNeither axe nor VRT can see this: axe has no rule for it, and a VRT baseline\nwould record an obscured control as correct.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(a11y): ASMA-8139 separate the four focus criteria\n\nAdds the 2.4.7 / 1.4.11 / 2.4.11 / 2.4.13 split, with levels and owners.\nFindings B and F are 2.4.7 failures first — no indicator exists at all — and\nonly become 1.4.11 questions once there is a ring to measure; collapsing the\ntwo is what produced the citation error in the first place. None of the four\nis gated: all four axe tags match zero rules.\n\nRecords ASMA-8138''s counts on the B/F blocker: 17 declarations resolve to\ngama-400, none touched by the token work, so a gama-400 ring would join an\nexisting failure rather than create an isolated one. Also their more hopeful\nnumber — greenish already passes at 3.15 with jade-400, so a shade near that\nluminance clears all three themes.\n\nElevates the outline-none trap out of a single finding: Tailwind compiles it\nto a transparent outline, not an absent one, so the obvious\n`outline-style !== ''none''` check reports a ring nobody can see. Invisible to\nthat check and to axe alike, which is why the harness rejects transparent and\nzero-width outlines.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(a11y): ASMA-8139 verify focus tokens after theme repairs\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"f049ad6dfc9d3fa0858fc950be8dc44c5fdbd3f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/f049ad6dfc9d3fa0858fc950be8dc44c5fdbd3f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/924198a4f7ddca1741e8c02ac30de639b1b041bf","verification":{"payload":"tree f049ad6dfc9d3fa0858fc950be8dc44c5fdbd3f5\nparent dd67e47e5482e4e68d4d241891399db90cae0af1\nauthor Marin Pesterean <91586985+mark31072@users.noreply.github.com> 1789031037 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789031037 +0300\n\ntest(a11y): ASMA-8139 verify focus tokens after theme repairs (#178)\n\n* test(a11y): ASMA-8139 keyboard and focus contract tests\n\nWave 3b of ASMA-8132. Adds a real-browser keyboard/focus contract suite for\nevery interactive component: Select, Autocomplete, Dialog, Tabs, Menu, Slider,\nTooltip, Snackbar, DatePicker and TimePicker. 81 passing assertions covering\nWCAG 2.1.1, 2.1.2, 2.4.3, 2.4.7, 1.4.13, 3.2.1, 4.1.2 and 4.1.3.\n\nNew `interaction` vitest project (real Chromium, Playwright/CDP key events),\nrun in CI by the new \"Keyboard & focus contract\" workflow. No stories are\nadded and no *.stories.tsx is touched, so VRT baselines and the axe gate are\nunaffected; components are mounted directly instead.\n\n11 contract defects found and reproduced. Per the wave-3 rule these are NOT\nfixed here — each is an it.skip naming the SC and the offending file, written\nup in docs/a11y-keyboard-contract.md and escalated. Every skip was verified by\nun-skipping and confirming it genuinely fails. Zero component source changed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(a11y): ASMA-8139 fix WCAG citation, add 2.4.11 coverage\n\nThe doc cited \"SC 2.4.11 focus appearance\", which is wrong on both counts:\n2.4.11 is Focus Not Obscured (Minimum) and says nothing about contrast, while\nFocus Appearance is 2.4.13 and is AAA. The AA criterion carrying the 3:1\nfocus-indicator requirement — the one actually being measured — is 1.4.11\nNon-text Contrast. Corrected throughout; no finding changes.\n\nActing on the same review note, adds real SC 2.4.11 coverage, which nothing\nelse in the epic checks: a library overlay must not entirely cover the control\nthat opened it. Five assertions across Select, Autocomplete, DatePicker and\nTooltip, using elementFromPoint so paint order and the top layer are respected,\nplus a self-check that deliberately covers a button and confirms the helper\nreports it — without that, a helper regression would leave the whole file\npassing while measuring nothing.\n\nNeither axe nor VRT can see this: axe has no rule for it, and a VRT baseline\nwould record an obscured control as correct.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(a11y): ASMA-8139 separate the four focus criteria\n\nAdds the 2.4.7 / 1.4.11 / 2.4.11 / 2.4.13 split, with levels and owners.\nFindings B and F are 2.4.7 failures first — no indicator exists at all — and\nonly become 1.4.11 questions once there is a ring to measure; collapsing the\ntwo is what produced the citation error in the first place. None of the four\nis gated: all four axe tags match zero rules.\n\nRecords ASMA-8138''s counts on the B/F blocker: 17 declarations resolve to\ngama-400, none touched by the token work, so a gama-400 ring would join an\nexisting failure rather than create an isolated one. Also their more hopeful\nnumber — greenish already passes at 3.15 with jade-400, so a shade near that\nluminance clears all three themes.\n\nElevates the outline-none trap out of a single finding: Tailwind compiles it\nto a transparent outline, not an absent one, so the obvious\n`outline-style !== ''none''` check reports a ring nobody can see. Invisible to\nthat check and to axe alike, which is why the harness rejects transparent and\nzero-width outlines.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(a11y): ASMA-8139 verify focus tokens after theme repairs\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqonJ9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAl8MQAE1xddLW3SUyO0j0+4LX+f0K\nqlOBHOE6M04pHJS773ZbmhdbP7GpnD3c0/F4D5GYk54gJVhQ7EN6prLeGVq4qgvr\ndL7oki4c0TqYXY2xJz9+VvM8PgqidyZpIgo9oBSF2uUEarEffyhrS/ZHi5rhqTRQ\n3/ilqe1Ysi8mMvX3m3Eo3vqk5t/L8vJ70vT1JYxkRtOAvsjR31aMV84n4LAO1lHE\n2Q