 exercise the dangling-chain detector against a synthetic\n  broken declaration map instead of live tokens, so the test never again\n  depends on a defect existing in the repo.\n\nVerified: vitest unit 429 passed / 4 skipped, pnpm ts:check clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"16c0bae0632b4cef5185949a6db14b0da8bcdab1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/16c0bae0632b4cef5185949a6db14b0da8bcdab1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/dd67e47e5482e4e68d4d241891399db90cae0af1","verification":{"payload":"tree 16c0bae0632b4cef5185949a6db14b0da8bcdab1\nparent a4fdbcf742d2a93dd3b953489997a75c0ca6d0d3\nauthor Marin Pesterean <91586985+mark31072@users.noreply.github.com> 1789030475 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789030475 +0300\n\ntest(a11y): ASMA-8138 drop stale dangling-chain fixtures after token fix (#179)\n\nThe contrast suite''s EXPECTED_UNRESOLVABLE fixtures asserted the three\ndangling --colors-beta-400 chains (F-15) still existed. ASMA-8133 (PR #172)\nmerged first and defined beta-400, fixing the defect the fixtures expected,\nwhich turned master''s unit job red.\n\n- themeContrast: expect zero unresolvable tokens in every theme; a future\n  dangling chain fails the test and must be fixed or quarantined explicitly.\n- themeTokens: exercise the dangling-chain detector against a synthetic\n  broken declaration map instead of live tokens, so the test never again\n  depends on a defect existing in the repo.\n\nVerified: vitest unit 429 passed / 4 skipped, pnpm ts:check clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqonBLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyFMQAIsMEHUeGYvd05jY/cZ4Toys\nlTpM4UdqT+f04AB4Kt9KL0TRS6NjrdYeYwWRp88z4CQpKtzgyKyF5K92yXeKH6YU\nWorpkn5HB3sPaXoV39ZX5o6DOYqG3XY1+yNfcdjQQ9eFid4ySbJZaDcNE/TiCheM\nkyzY86neKcJSxcSrgzT5OOBaeFq0Gz32qGy0+lcced3sHd2GDTiSr9XfAra4D80i\n