"site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/a4fdbcf742d2a93dd3b953489997a75c0ca6d0d3","node_id":"C_kwDORvrv4doAKGE0ZmRiY2Y3NDJkMmE5M2RkM2I5NTM0ODk5OTdhNzVjMGNhNmQwZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/57a667fe90342c9be1d43f74541cbe3b338acc84","sha":"57a667fe90342c9be1d43f74541cbe3b338acc84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/57a667fe90342c9be1d43f74541cbe3b338acc84"}],"sha":"a4fdbcf742d2a93dd3b953489997a75c0ca6d0d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/a4fdbcf742d2a93dd3b953489997a75c0ca6d0d3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91586985?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mark31072","id":91586985,"login":"mark31072","node_id":"U_kgDOBXWBqQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/57a667fe90342c9be1d43f74541cbe3b338acc84/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T08:40:14Z","email":"91586985+mark31072@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Marin Pesterean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T08:40:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ASMA-8139 keyboard and focus contract tests for interactive components (#174)\n\n* test(a11y): ASMA-8139 keyboard and focus contract tests\n\nWave 3b of ASMA-8132. Adds a real-browser keyboard/focus contract suite for\nevery interactive component: Select, Autocomplete, Dialog, Tabs, Menu, Slider,\nTooltip, Snackbar, DatePicker and TimePicker. 81 passing assertions covering\nWCAG 2.1.1, 2.1.2, 2.4.3, 2.4.7, 1.4.13, 3.2.1, 4.1.2 and 4.1.3.\n\nNew `interaction` vitest project (real Chromium, Playwright/CDP key events),\nrun in CI by the new \"Keyboard & focus contract\" workflow. No stories are\nadded and no *.stories.tsx is touched, so VRT baselines and the axe gate are\nunaffected; components are mounted directly instead.\n\n11 contract defects found and reproduced. Per the wave-3 rule these are NOT\nfixed here — each is an it.skip naming the SC and the offending file, written\nup in docs/a11y-keyboard-contract.md and escalated. Every skip was verified by\nun-skipping and confirming it genuinely fails. Zero component source changed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(a11y): ASMA-8139 fix WCAG citation, add 2.4.11 coverage\n\nThe doc cited \"SC 2.4.11 focus appearance\", which is wrong on both counts:\n2.4.11 is Focus Not Obscured (Minimum) and says nothing about contrast, while\nFocus Appearance is 2.4.13 and is AAA. The AA criterion carrying the 3:1\nfocus-indicator requirement — the one actually being measured — is 1.4.11\nNon-text Contrast. Corrected throughout; no finding changes.\n\nActing on the same review note, adds real SC 2.4.11 coverage, which nothing\nelse in the epic checks: a library overlay must not entirely cover the control\nthat opened it. Five assertions across Select, Autocomplete, DatePicker and\nTooltip, using elementFromPoint so paint order and the top layer are respected,\nplus a self-check that deliberately covers a button and confirms the helper\nreports it — without that, a helper regression would leave the whole file\npassing while measuring nothing.\n\nNeither axe nor VRT can see this: axe has no rule for it, and a VRT baseline\nwould record an obscured control as correct.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(a11y): ASMA-8139 separate the four focus criteria\n\nAdds the 2.4.7 / 1.4.11 / 2.4.11 / 2.4.13 split, with levels and owners.\nFindings B and F are 2.4.7 failures first — no indicator exists at all — and\nonly become 1.4.11 questions once there is a ring to measure; collapsing the\ntwo is what produced the citation error in the first place. None of the four\nis gated: all four axe tags match zero rules.\n\nRecords ASMA-8138''s counts on the B/F blocker: 17 declarations resolve to\ngama-400, none touched by the token work, so a gama-400 ring would join an\nexisting failure rather than create an isolated one. Also their more hopeful\nnumber — greenish already passes at 3.15 with jade-400, so a shade near that\nluminance clears all three themes.\n\nElevates the outline-none trap out of a single finding: Tailwind compiles it\nto a transparent outline, not an absent one, so the obvious\n`outline-style !== ''none''` check reports a ring nobody can see. Invisible to\nthat check and to axe alike, which is why the harness rejects transparent and\nzero-width outlines.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"72a5f3a13b397d689a7be488dd7a5ae9282d22eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/72a5f3a13b397d689a7be488dd7a5ae9282d22eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/57a667fe90342c9be1d43f74541cbe3b338acc84","verification":{"payload":"tree 72a5f3a13b397d689a7be488dd7a5ae9282d22eb\nparent fee8af30f7d75936d5ad1ec91d4cf41f12abb4e7\nauthor Marin Pesterean <91586985+mark31072@users.noreply.github.com> 1789029614 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789029614 +0300\n\nASMA-8139 keyboard and focus contract tests for interactive components (#174)\n\n* test(a11y): ASMA-8139 keyboard and focus contract tests\n\nWave 3b of ASMA-8132. Adds a real-browser keyboard/focus contract suite for\nevery interactive component: Select, Autocomplete, Dialog, Tabs, Menu, Slider,\nTooltip, Snackbar, DatePicker and TimePicker. 81 passing assertions covering\nWCAG 2.1.1, 2.1.2, 2.4.3, 2.4.7, 1.4.13, 3.2.1, 4.1.2 and 4.1.3.\n\nNew `interaction` vitest project (real Chromium, Playwright/CDP key events),\nrun in CI by the new \"Keyboard & focus contract\" workflow. No stories are\nadded and no *.stories.tsx is touched, so VRT baselines and the axe gate are\nunaffected; components are mounted directly instead.\n\n11 contract defects found and reproduced. Per the wave-3 rule these are NOT\nfixed here — each is an it.skip naming the SC and the offending file, written\nup in docs/a11y-keyboard-contract.md and escalated. Every skip was verified by\nun-skipping and confirming it genuinely fails. Zero component source changed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(a11y): ASMA-8139 fix WCAG citation, add 2.4.11 coverage\n\nThe doc cited \"SC 2.4.11 focus appearance\", which is wrong on both counts:\n2.4.11 is Focus Not Obscured (Minimum) and says nothing about contrast, while\nFocus Appearance is 2.4.13 and is AAA. The AA criterion carrying the 3:1\nfocus-indicator requirement — the one actually being measured — is 1.4.11\nNon-text Contrast. Corrected throughout; no finding changes.\n\nActing on the same review note, adds real SC 2.4.11 coverage, which nothing\nelse in the epic checks: a library overlay must not entirely cover the control\nthat opened it. Five assertions across Select, Autocomplete, DatePicker and\nTooltip, using elementFromPoint so paint order and the top layer are respected,\nplus a self-check that deliberately covers a button and confirms the helper\nreports it — without that, a helper regression would leave the whole file\npassing while measuring nothing.\n\nNeither axe nor VRT can see this: axe has no rule for it, and a VRT baseline\nwould record an obscured control as correct.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(a11y): ASMA-8139 separate the four focus criteria\n\nAdds the 2.4.7 / 1.4.11 / 2.4.11 / 2.4.13 split, with levels and owners.\nFindings B and F are 2.4.7 failures first — no indicator exists at all — and\nonly become 1.4.11 questions once there is a ring to measure; collapsing the\ntwo is what produced the citation error in the first place. None of the four\nis gated: all four axe tags match zero rules.\n\nRecords ASMA-8138''s counts on the B/F blocker: 17 declarations resolve to\ngama-400, none touched by the token work, so a gama-400 ring would join an\nexisting failure rather than create an isolated one. Also their more hopeful\nnumber — greenish already passes at 3.15 with jade-400, so a shade near that\nluminance clears all three themes.\n\nElevates the outline-none trap out of a single finding: Tailwind compiles it\nto a transparent outline, not an absent one, so the obvious\n`outline-style !== ''none''` check reports a ring nobody can see. Invisible to\nthat check and to axe alike, which is why the harness rejects transparent and\nzero-width outlines.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqomzuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKEkQAHS3sxNA1DQHlCUM37485acr\nyuSE12gqdQ76Frign1BXXy2uLKzLgghyZp0tnVQFznfg85mWEJJvhRhORAn3AqDE\nc++6e0gATPOFpJXlPWkqwUTsDTGRACC0JXpTZ9/iyi++tYWJErIejTzkebGKtOnQ\np7RnHaKKQYPxJ90TH0ZB72eJhZFmHk9Tk4VsRJnzS65ZRofM6f4ecKkj+mY8entn\nLyuTzT3jp4nGNLypqL1hrZDkp3ZeUYpHUVY7rkjvwiacQ6eMgGOCYp1gTcKgyArO\n2qZj/o12UXNqsRL2WPnbvQcplEcRAjHTlaucMWx0NsFKyxv9vRYeAXA7ZHpq5G2n\nFi0M7S5A2d8i638Qd37jEnZCsVFv2PvQ5V+uscDu9mm+5s30kHfzL1xarUdAHrXo\nEzAC/x1kQKSINLDtQyQYahrCw8nha9dfR51zS3K2yxGGY3c9VlFpPvQofiN8yf3Z\nJt2vfSMqOqktVk5RLfjtd3Rwcldz0WZhSNqw+YgwCn0Ii7nn19We9Gu6RSkyTaHh\nskV3If/+NTa2PerDRYxoIrCtc8jCMqDi2FOoJQJdYSvGx6CHcmDKqxIXFIlgNdv/\nny/DQP4+JLJS8sCTkQcISnlJBAwps/+ktNN6qWU6aQguVgKr5WadAO2vmpYn2AQu\nQGNQpG9qXdYDZ9PCntyu\n=A0Yi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-10T08:40:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/57a667fe90342c9be1d43f74541cbe3b338acc84","node_id":"C_kwDORvrv4doAKDU3YTY2N2ZlOTAzNDJjOWJlMWQ0M2Y3NDU0MWNiZTNiMzM4YWNjODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/fee8af30f7d75936d5ad1ec91d4cf41f12abb4e7","sha":"fee8af30f7d75936d5ad1ec91d4cf41f12abb4e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/fee8af30f7d75936d5ad1ec91d4cf41f12abb4e7"}],"sha":"57a667fe90342c9be1d43f74541cbe3b338acc84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/57a667fe90342c9be1d43f74541cbe3b338acc84"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91586985?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mark31072","id":91586985,"login":"mark31072","node_id":"U_kgDOBXWBqQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/fee8af30f7d75936d5ad1ec91d4cf41f12abb4e7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T08:34:36Z","email":"91586985+mark31072@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Marin Pesterean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T08:34:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ASMA-8138 asma-ui-core: per-theme colour contrast tests (WCAG 1.4.3, 1.4.11) (#173)\n\n* test(a11y): ASMA-8138 per-theme WCAG contrast gate for 1.4.3 and 1.4.11\n\nAdds an automated contrast check that resolves the design tokens straight out\nof the theme CSS and computes ratios for the pairs components actually render,\nacross all three themes (default, fretex, greenish).\n\nStorybook''s axe run only ever renders the default theme, and axe ships no rule\nfor SC 1.4.11 at all -- its only contrast rules are color-contrast (1.4.3) and\ncolor-contrast-enhanced (AAA, disabled by default). Both gaps are closed here.\n\n243 assertions pass. 90 are quarantined as `it.skip` against 15 measured\nfindings, each written up in docs/a11y-contrast.md with the token, the exact\nconsumer file, the resolved hex pair, the ratio and the criterion. No token\nvalue is changed: that is a visual, potentially breaking change to a brand\ntheme and belongs to ASMA-8133 plus design sign-off.\n\nNotable findings: the fretex theta ramp collapses five rungs to #ffffff, which\ninverts the info snackbar to 3.55:1; --colors-gama-400 is the library-wide\nfocus colour and misses 3:1 in two of three themes; and\n--colors-button-*-error-focused-border-color points at --colors-beta-400,\nwhich no theme defines, so those buttons render no focus border at all in\ndefault and greenish -- a defect no rendered test can see, because the browser\ndrops the invalid declaration entirely.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(a11y): ASMA-8138 hold quarantined pairs to a regression floor\n\nReplaces it.skip on quarantined pairs with a characterization assertion: each\nmust hold the ratio it measures on master (REGRESSION_FLOORS). The suite now\ngoes red if an already-failing pair decays, and stays green if a token change\nlegitimately improves it -- 90 skipped assertions detected nothing, which is\nthe same vacuous-gate problem this epic keeps finding.\n\nOnly 4 assertions remain skipped: F-15''s dangling var() chains, where the\ndeclaration is dropped entirely so there is no ratio to floor.\n\nAlso corrects F-15''s contained/error analysis. The earlier conclusion that no\nred shade could work, and that the ring needed to be near-black, assumed the\nfocus ring is adjacent to the #e10700 fill. ASMA-8133''s decoded VRT baselines\nshow a 2px white inset ring separates them, so the ring is white-on-both-sides\nand red-700 clears 3:1 at 8.37. The arithmetic was right; the premise was not.\nRecords the same pixel evidence confirming the indicator is missing rather\nthan weak, and resolves the cardea var mismatch as covered by PR #172.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(a11y): ASMA-8138 cite 1.4.11 for focus contrast, not 2.4.11\n\nF-15 cited \"SC 2.4.11 Focus Appearance\", which is wrong on both the number\nand the level. In WCAG 2.2, 2.4.11 is Focus Not Obscured (Minimum) and says\nnothing about contrast; Focus Appearance is 2.4.13 and is AAA. The correct AA\ncitation for focus-indicator contrast is 1.4.11 Non-text Contrast, which is\nwhat this suite has been measuring all along.\n\nThe finding is unchanged -- a dropped focus ring still fails 1.4.11 at AA --\nbut these docs read as a conformance record, so the citation has to be right.\nAdds an explicit criterion-scope note so the same slip is not repeated, and\nnotes that Focus Not Obscured (2.4.11) is a real AA criterion nothing in this\nepic checks, though it is a layout concern rather than a token one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(a11y): ASMA-8138 split 2.4.7 from 1.4.11, quantify F-07 scope\n\nF-15''s real first failure is SC 2.4.7 Focus Visible (AA) -- whether an\nindicator exists at all -- not 1.4.11, which governs the contrast of an\nindicator that does render. The dropped declaration means there was nothing\nin the DOM to measure, which is the sharpest statement of why only a\ntoken-level check could catch it.\n\nRecords what ASMA-8133''s PR #172 should and should not be read as clearing:\n2.4.7 pass, 1.4.11 pass, 2.4.13 Focus Appearance not claimed and out of AA\nscope. It would not pass anyway -- red-700 against the unfocused beta-500\nborder is 1.68, short of 2.4.13''s 3:1 focused/unfocused requirement.\n\nQuantifies F-07 from the repo rather than by estimate: 17 declarations\nresolve to gama-400 (15 button focus borders plus two input outline tokens),\nnone touched by #172, failing under default and fretex and passing under\ngreenish. So the primary focus indicator still fails 1.4.11 in two of three\nthemes after #172, and no CI gate can see it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(a11y): ASMA-8138 record F-07 blocking ASMA-8139 findings B and F\n\nCross-links a11y-keyboard-contract.md. Fixing those findings with the\nlibrary''s standard gama-400 focus ring before F-07 is resolved would trade an\ninvisible focus indicator for one failing 1.4.11 in two of three themes, which\nno gate can catch: axe has no wcag1411 rule and VRT would be green because the\nbaseline records the failing colour as correct.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(a11y): ASMA-8138 fail on a regression floor left by a lifted quarantine\n\nA floor for a pair that is no longer quarantined is dead weight that reads as\nif the pair were still failing. Verified by lifting F-11 and leaving its floor:\nthe orphan check goes red, and the pair correctly becomes a live failing\n1.4.11 assertion at 1.75 against the 3:1 requirement.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9e6a57c169f2aba3c2b164ae6e3910bc1a5993a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/9e6a57c169f2aba3c2b164ae6e3910bc1a5993a5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/fee8af30f7d75936d5ad1ec91d4cf41f12abb4e7","verification":{"payload":"tree 9e6a57c169f2aba3c2b164ae6e3910bc1a5993a5\nparent 380617454ddf83fa3ad146db2d7756f7fa58e29c\nauthor Marin Pesterean <91586985+mark31072@users.noreply.github.com> 1789029276 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789029276 +0300\n\nASMA-8138 asma-ui-core: per-theme colour contrast tests (WCAG 1.4.3, 1.4.11) (#173)\n\n* test(a11y): ASMA-8138 per-theme WCAG contrast gate for 1.4.3 and 1.4.11\n\nAdds an automated contrast check that resolves the design tokens straight out\nof the theme CSS and computes ratios for the pairs components actually render,\nacross all three themes (default, fretex, greenish).\n\nStorybook''s axe run only ever renders the default theme, and axe ships no rule\nfor SC 1.4.11 at all -- its only contrast rules are color-contrast (1.4.3) and\ncolor-contrast-enhanced (AAA, disabled by default). Both gaps are closed here.\n\n243 assertions pass. 90 are quarantined as `it.skip` against 15 measured\nfindings, each written up in docs/a11y-contrast.md with the token, the exact\nconsumer file, the resolved hex pair, the ratio and the criterion. No token\nvalue is changed: that is a visual, potentially breaking change to a brand\ntheme and belongs to ASMA-8133 plus design sign-off.\n\nNotable findings: the fretex theta ramp collapses five rungs to #ffffff, which\ninverts the info snackbar to 3.55:1; --colors-gama-400 is the library-wide\nfocus colour and misses 3:1 in two of three themes; and\n--colors-button-*-error-focused-border-color points at --colors-beta-400,\nwhich no theme defines, so those buttons render no focus border at all in\ndefault and greenish -- a defect no rendered test can see, because the browser\ndrops the invalid declaration entirely.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(a11y): ASMA-8138 hold quarantined pairs to a regression floor\n\nReplaces it.skip on quarantined pairs with a characterization assertion: each\nmust hold the ratio it measures on master (REGRESSION_FLOORS). The suite now\ngoes red if an already-failing pair decays, and stays green if a token change\nlegitimately improves it -- 90 skipped assertions detected nothing, which is\nthe same vacuous-gate problem this epic keeps finding.\n\nOnly 4 assertions remain skipped: F-15''s dangling var() chains, where the\ndeclaration is dropped entirely so there is no ratio to floor.\n\nAlso corrects F-15''s contained/error analysis. The earlier conclusion that no\nred shade could work, and that the ring needed to be near-black, assumed the\nfocus ring is adjacent to the #e10700 fill. ASMA-8133''s decoded VRT baselines\nshow a 2px white inset ring separates them, so the ring is white-on-both-sides\nand red-700 clears 3:1 at 8.37. The arithmetic was right; the premise was not.\nRecords the same pixel evidence confirming the indicator is missing rather\nthan weak, and resolves the cardea var mismatch as covered by PR #172.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(a11y): ASMA-8138 cite 1.4.11 for focus contrast, not 2.4.11\n\nF-15 cited \"SC 2.4.11 Focus Appearance\", which is wrong on both the number\nand the level. In WCAG 2.2, 2.4.11 is Focus Not Obscured (Minimum) and says\nnothing about contrast; Focus Appearance is 2.4.13 and is AAA. The correct AA\ncitation for focus-indicator contrast is 1.4.11 Non-text Contrast, which is\nwhat this suite has been measuring all along.\n\nThe finding is unchanged -- a dropped focus ring still fails 1.4.11 at AA --\nbut these docs read as a conformance record, so the citation has to be right.\nAdds an explicit criterion-scope note so the same slip is not repeated, and\nnotes that Focus Not Obscured (2.4.11) is a real AA criterion nothing in this\nepic checks, though it is a layout concern rather than a token one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(a11y): ASMA-8138 split 2.4.7 from 1.4.11, quantify F-07 scope\n\nF-15''s real first failure is SC 2.4.7 Focus Visible (AA) -- whether an\nindicator exists at all -- not 1.4.11, which governs the contrast of an\nindicator that does render. The dropped declaration means there was nothing\nin the DOM to measure, which is the sharpest statement of why only a\ntoken-level check could catch it.\n\nRecords what ASMA-8133''s PR #172 should and should not be read as clearing:\n2.4.7 pass, 1.4.11 pass, 2.4.13 Focus Appearance not claimed and out of AA\nscope. It would not pass anyway -- red-700 against the unfocused beta-500\nborder is 1.68, short of 2.4.13''s 3:1 focused/unfocused requirement.\n\nQuantifies F-07 from the repo rather than by estimate: 17 declarations\nresolve to gama-400 (15 button focus borders plus two input outline tokens),\nnone touched by #172, failing under default and fretex and passing under\ngreenish. So the primary focus indicator still fails 1.4.11 in two of three\nthemes after #172, and no CI gate can see it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(a11y): ASMA-8138 record F-07 blocking ASMA-8139 findings B and F\n\nCross-links a11y-keyboard-contract.md. Fixing those findings with the\nlibrary''s standard gama-400 focus ring before F-07 is resolved would trade an\ninvisible focus indicator for one failing 1.4.11 in two of three themes, which\nno gate can catch: axe has no wcag1411 rule and VRT would be green because the\nbaseline records the failing colour as correct.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(a11y): ASMA-8138 fail on a regression floor left by a lifted quarantine\n\nA floor for a pair that is no longer quarantined is dead weight that reads as\nif the pair were still failing. Verified by lifting F-11 and leaving its floor:\nthe orphan check goes red, and the pair correctly becomes a live failing\n1.4.11 assertion at 1.75 against the 3:1 requirement.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqomudCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzLoQABqroWyYoPSq0My+/foA5ylG\njNVW2VStcMB+1IymKM97DEL0D5+ZGRFxTcWFDfUuxNSefbj/KOQqhepwCwPCCrnx\nA0jxmxXalv0gJVltq4u7dV/JqjG/fE9a0LT31MoTzsVKma9ny+iEcQmjMeSd94xR\nX/xw5wT2plG8tafJHnqXBQrwcUkMewbAD29r3ZA5JOcJbbvHFkjU7KajkhXzd7yR\n35ozQxKC72FJ0z/3cC3LQG9tlCKFABTqh/gCrFzHLRQ+irfOz/L5ne35/uooPOb0\nBXkAIaR+1nD04pvwP6N6AFKHoaCRWiwCBJ3wlvR6LM4MLUleq7bv2ojO514AT6fH\nwN7fM5dF8yzHc4552vwaosWvwcKMQG45uwN6J2R+6qjK7DbKUBvzawq+z2Z5Guc5\nEm6vqCQ4u9mHSvyN5h4KsjWrnJB5m0xBrZ7z9fSg3pvDbMuG5wqc21fHlEKX6Yik\nX0K+aMqoEvpN2fYOH6wFHXTyuPWnCQCmjLfzDR7GYJxJkEdDy5JkWpkcxnyNZP0b\nOybXP2h2LsB/bPAcLK540/nW793CIIwiG5vUKKn+u/kAAdmpHztUXcr7Tf6Mf7Mz\n3RWhlswCV4S5ax+TUvXJZqNdVrz8rRbmUMooKIlB5jNF0X2bXGrbXrppq4kp5n12\n6uiRltLyK1+a2MHgAyhq\n=arkm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-10T08:34:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/fee8af30f7d75936d5ad1ec91d4cf41f12abb4e7","node_id":"C_kwDORvrv4doAKGZlZThhZjMwZjdkNzU5MzZkNWFkMWVjOTFkNGNmNDFmMTJhYmI0ZTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/380617454ddf83fa3ad146db2d7756f7fa58e29c","sha":"380617454ddf83fa3ad146db2d7756f7fa58e29c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/380617454ddf83fa3ad146db2d7756f7fa58e29c"}],"sha":"fee8af30f7d75936d5ad1ec91d4cf41f12abb4e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/fee8af30f7d75936d5ad1ec91d4cf41f12abb4e7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91586985?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mark31072","id":91586985,"login":"mark31072","node_id":"U_kgDOBXWBqQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/380617454ddf83fa3ad146db2d7756f7fa58e29c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T08:28:54Z","email":"91586985+mark31072@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Marin Pesterean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T08:28:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(tokens): ASMA-8133 repair broken token references and add a token completeness test (#172)\n\n* fix(tokens): ASMA-8133 repair broken token refs, add completeness test\n\nThe token layer is plain CSS custom properties, so every one of these\ndefects failed silently: `var(--typo)` is invalid at computed-value time\nand the browser just drops the declaration.\n\n- inputVariables.css declared the whole --colors-input-* / --input-* set\n  only under [data-theme=default|fretex|greenish], so a host page that\n  never sets data-theme rendered StyledTextarea with invalid colors.\n  :root now leads the same selector list; all three themes share these\n  values, so themed output is byte-identical and the theme selectors\n  stay in place to win on equal specificity if a theme ever overrides.\n- Defined --colors-beta-400 (red-300) in the default and greenish beta\n  ramps. Three error-button focused-border rules referenced it and it\n  was declared nowhere; the red palette has no red-400, so it takes the\n  one shade between beta-100 and beta-500, mirroring gama-400 sitting a\n  step lighter than gama-500.\n- fretexTokens.css had doubled-prefix typos --colors-colors-btn-bg-mini-\n  action(-hover) and --colors-colors-topbar-text, so those three Fretex\n  overrides never applied and silently fell through to the :root values.\n- twConfigs.json custom-grey-01..04/06 read var(--color-cardea--grey-0x)\n  but the palette defines --colors-cardea--grey-0x. Fixed the reference\n  rather than dropping the keys: they are part of the published Tailwind\n  preset, so deleting them would break consumers outside this repo.\n- twConfigs.json delta-9000 reached past --colors-delta-9000 into the raw\n  --colors-gray-9000, bypassing the semantic layer every theme defines.\n  Both resolve to #1a1d23, so no rendered colour changes.\n- inputVariables.css declared --colors-input-active-hover-text-color\n  three times and --colors-input-readOnly-active-text-color twice; the\n  strays were the notEditable and readOnly hover slots plus the readOnly\n  disabled slot. All copies carried the same value and StyledTextarea\n  only instantiates the ''active'' and ''error'' variants, so restoring the\n  distinct names changes no rendered output.\n- Removed a leftover console.log from PathfinderCard''s ResizeObserver\n  subscribe fallback.\n\nsrc/styles/tokens.test.ts parses src/styles/**/*.css and twConfigs.json,\ncollects declarations per selector block and every var() reference, and\nasserts: nothing referenced is undeclared; the --colors-input-* set\nresolves transitively with no data-theme attribute; no block declares a\nproperty twice; theme blocks only override tokens the base layer already\ndeclares; and Tailwind keys consume their matching semantic token. Five\nof its six assertions fail on the pre-fix tree.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(tokens): ASMA-8133 add changeset for token layer repair\n\nThe Readme (''Changelog and releases'', line 543) requires a changeset for\neach feature or fix. This is a consumer-visible fix to a published\npackage, so it needs a patch bump to reach consumers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(tokens): ASMA-8133 make error focus ring meet 1.4.11, gate unit tests in CI\n\nAddresses three verification findings on #172.\n\n1. `return () => {}` tripped @typescript-eslint/no-empty-function. Now\n   returns `() => undefined`: an expression body is not \"empty\", so the\n   rule passes and the unsubscribe contract is unchanged. No disable\n   comment.\n\n   This slipped through because `pnpm lint` is `eslint src/**/*.{ts,tsx}`\n   unquoted, and the npm script runs under sh, which lacks globstar --\n   `**` collapses so the shell hands eslint 33 files exactly two levels\n   deep. PathfinderCard.tsx is four levels deep and was never linted\n   locally. Verified with the quoted form (`pnpm exec eslint\n   ''src/**/*.{ts,tsx}''`), which covers 692 files: 0 errors. The lint\n   script itself is deliberately left alone -- fixing it would change\n   every builder''s CI surface mid-epic.\n\n2. --colors-beta-400 is now red-700, not red-300. red-300 was chosen on\n   ramp shape and is wrong on measurement: as a focus indicator it clears\n   3:1 against nothing, and it made two of the three slots WORSE than the\n   broken var, which fell back to currentColor rather than to nothing\n   (text-error 5.34:1 -> 1.31:1, contained-error 4.96:1 -> 2.97:1).\n   red-700 clears 3:1 against both adjacent surfaces on the outlined and\n   text variants (6.56:1 vs fill, 8.37:1 vs page). The contained variant\n   is unsatisfiable for any single border colour: 3:1 vs the white page\n   needs L<=0.300 while 3:1 vs the beta-500 fill needs L>=0.585, so it\n   takes the best available worst case, 1.69:1, which is exactly the\n   shipped *-common-focused-border-color convention.\n\n3. Added a `unit` job to lint-and-a11y.yml. `pnpm test-storybook` only\n   runs the ''storybook'' vitest project, so the node ''unit'' project had no\n   CI gate: the new token test AND the pre-existing api-surface export\n   guard both passed locally while being inert in CI. Scope extension\n   into .github/workflows/ authorized by the coordinator and recorded in\n   the PR body. Additive only -- the lint and a11y jobs are untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(tokens): ASMA-8133 move the token test out of the published source tree\n\n`pnpm build` + `npm pack --dry-run` surfaced that src/styles/tokens.test.ts\nwas being published to consumers: package.json `files` ships\n\"src/styles/**/*\" as raw source, and this was the only test file under that\npath. 9.5 kB of test code in the tarball, which cuts against ASMA-8135''s\nwork bringing it down to 298.7 kB.\n\nMoved to src/tokens.test.ts, matching the existing src/api-surface.test.ts\nplacement. Still inside the vitest ''unit'' project glob (src/**/*.test.ts),\nso the new CI job still runs it, and re-verified that it still goes red on a\nseeded token break from the new location. Packed size 302.6 kB -> 299.6 kB;\nthe only remaining artifact is dist/src/tokens.test.d.ts (11 B), consistent\nwith the ~13 pre-existing *.test.d.ts files the dts plugin already emits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(vrt): ASMA-8133 re-baseline the styled-button gallery for the error focus ring\n\nOnly inputs-styled-button--gallery.png changes: the Primary/Danger and\nSecondary/Danger \"Focused\" cells, which are the three\n*-error-focused-border-color rules that --colors-beta-400 feeds. Deliberate\nconsequence of defining that token; every other baseline is untouched.\n\nPost-accept state: 1 modified, 0 deleted, 336 baselines (unchanged count).\nA full serial `vrt.sh check` afterwards is 317/317.\n\nNote for whoever re-baselines next: `vrt.sh accept` cannot do a targeted\nre-baseline. It hardcodes --update-snapshots=all, which unconditionally\nrewrites every PNG whether or not it differed, so it churned 28 files here\nwhile `check` on the same commit and build failed only 1. The other 27 were\nsub-tolerance noise -- they passed `check` against the committed baselines.\nI reverted them and kept only the legitimate one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(tokens): ASMA-8133 correct the shipped beta-400 comment and two stale paths\n\nsrc/styles/**/* is in package.json `files`, so these comments ship to\nconsumers. The beta-400 comment still carried a conclusion I had already\ndisproved in the PR discussion but never came back and fixed in the CSS.\n\nIt claimed the contained variant was \"unsatisfiable for any single border\ncolour\" and that 1.69:1 was an accepted worst case. Both wrong:\n\n- Unsatisfiable only in the branch I solved. 3:1 against the beta-500 fill\n  (L=0.1616) also has a darker branch, L<=0.021, which simultaneously\n  satisfies L<=0.300 against the white page. A near-black border clears\n  both.\n- Moot regardless, because the ring is never adjacent to the fill.\n  Decoding the baseline PNG shows contained renders\n  #ffffff | #9d0f0f x2 | #ffffff x1 | #e10700 -- a 1px white inset sits\n  between ring and fill, so both of the ring''s real adjacencies are white\n  at 8.37:1, and the inset is 4.96:1 against the fill. There is no worst\n  case to accept.\n- 1.69:1 is the focused-vs-unfocused indicator comparison (red-700 against\n  the unfocused beta-500 border), which belongs to 2.4.13 Focus Appearance\n  at AAA and is out of this library''s AA scope. Attributing it to 1.4.11\n  read as \"we knowingly shipped a 1.69:1 focus indicator\", which is not\n  what the pixels show.\n\nReplaced with a short three-row criterion summary (2.4.7 PASS, 1.4.11\nPASS, 2.4.13 not claimed) and a pointer to the derivation rather than the\nderivation itself, since a shipped stylesheet is not the place for it.\n\nAlso two stale references to the test''s old path, both of which would have\nmisled the next reader: the CI job comment that documents why the job\nexists, and the changeset, which feeds the published CHANGELOG.\n\nComments only. Verified the built CSS is unaffected: cssnano strips all\ncomments, and --colors-beta-400 still resolves to var(--colors-red-700),\nso VRT cannot be affected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8d2549deff9584061ec9df1e543a0768abf407eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/8d2549deff9584061ec9df1e543a0768abf407eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/380617454ddf83fa3ad146db2d7756f7fa58e29c","verification":{"payload":"tree 8d2549deff9584061ec9df1e543a0768abf407eb\nparent d21712aedb8b854709c3ab29485bd44d145f7ff0\nauthor Marin Pesterean <91586985+mark31072@users.noreply.github.com> 1789028934 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789028934 +0300\n\nfix(tokens): ASMA-8133 repair broken token references and add a token completeness test (#172)\n\n* fix(tokens): ASMA-8133 repair broken token refs, add completeness test\n\nThe token layer is plain CSS custom properties, so every one of these\ndefects failed silently: `var(--typo)` is invalid at computed-value time\nand the browser just drops the declaration.\n\n- inputVariables.css declared the whole --colors-input-* / --input-* set\n  only under [data-theme=default|fretex|greenish], so a host page that\n  never sets data-theme rendered StyledTextarea with invalid colors.\n  :root now leads the same selector list; all three themes share these\n  values, so themed output is byte-identical and the theme selectors\n  stay in place to win on equal specificity if a theme ever overrides.\n- Defined --colors-beta-400 (red-300) in the default and greenish beta\n  ramps. Three error-button focused-border rules referenced it and it\n  was declared nowhere; the red palette has no red-400, so it takes the\n  one shade between beta-100 and beta-500, mirroring gama-400 sitting a\n  step lighter than gama-500.\n- fretexTokens.css had doubled-prefix typos --colors-colors-btn-bg-mini-\n  action(-hover) and --colors-colors-topbar-text, so those three Fretex\n  overrides never applied and silently fell through to the :root values.\n- twConfigs.json custom-grey-01..04/06 read var(--color-cardea--grey-0x)\n  but the palette defines --colors-cardea--grey-0x. Fixed the reference\n  rather than dropping the keys: they are part of the published Tailwind\n  preset, so deleting them would break consumers outside this repo.\n- twConfigs.json delta-9000 reached past --colors-delta-9000 into the raw\n  --colors-gray-9000, bypassing the semantic layer every theme defines.\n  Both resolve to #1a1d23, so no rendered colour changes.\n- inputVariables.css declared --colors-input-active-hover-text-color\n  three times and --colors-input-readOnly-active-text-color twice; the\n  strays were the notEditable and readOnly hover slots plus the readOnly\n  disabled slot. All copies carried the same value and StyledTextarea\n  only instantiates the ''active'' and ''error'' variants, so restoring the\n  distinct names changes no rendered output.\n- Removed a leftover console.log from PathfinderCard''s ResizeObserver\n  subscribe fallback.\n\nsrc/styles/tokens.test.ts parses src/styles/**/*.css and twConfigs.json,\ncollects declarations per selector block and every var() reference, and\nasserts: nothing referenced is undeclared; the --colors-input-* set\nresolves transitively with no data-theme attribute; no block declares a\nproperty twice; theme blocks only override tokens the base layer already\ndeclares; and Tailwind keys consume their matching semantic token. Five\nof its six assertions fail on the pre-fix tree.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(tokens): ASMA-8133 add changeset for token layer repair\n\nThe Readme (''Changelog and releases'', line 543) requires a changeset for\neach feature or fix. This is a consumer-visible fix to a published\npackage, so it needs a patch bump to reach consumers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(tokens): ASMA-8133 make error focus ring meet 1.4.11, gate unit tests in CI\n\nAddresses three verification findings on #172.\n\n1. `return () => {}` tripped @typescript-eslint/no-empty-function. Now\n   returns `() => undefined`: an expression body is not \"empty\", so the\n   rule passes and the unsubscribe contract is unchanged. No disable\n   comment.\n\n   This slipped through because `pnpm lint` is `eslint src/**/*.{ts,tsx}`\n   unquoted, and the npm script runs under sh, which lacks globstar --\n   `**` collapses so the shell hands eslint 33 files exactly two levels\n   deep. PathfinderCard.tsx is four levels deep and was never linted\n   locally. Verified with the quoted form (`pnpm exec eslint\n   ''src/**/*.{ts,tsx}''`), which covers 692 files: 0 errors. The lint\n   script itself is deliberately left alone -- fixing it would change\n   every builder''s CI surface mid-epic.\n\n2. --colors-beta-400 is now red-700, not red-300. red-300 was chosen on\n   ramp shape and is wrong on measurement: as a focus indicator it clears\n   3:1 against nothing, and it made two of the three slots WORSE than the\n   broken var, which fell back to currentColor rather than to nothing\n   (text-error 5.34:1 -> 1.31:1, contained-error 4.96:1 -> 2.97:1).\n   red-700 clears 3:1 against both adjacent surfaces on the outlined and\n   text variants (6.56:1 vs fill, 8.37:1 vs page). The contained variant\n   is unsatisfiable for any single border colour: 3:1 vs the white page\n   needs L<=0.300 while 3:1 vs the beta-500 fill needs L>=0.585, so it\n   takes the best available worst case, 1.69:1, which is exactly the\n   shipped *-common-focused-border-color convention.\n\n3. Added a `unit` job to lint-and-a11y.yml. `pnpm test-storybook` only\n   runs the ''storybook'' vitest project, so the node ''unit'' project had no\n   CI gate: the new token test AND the pre-existing api-surface export\n   guard both passed locally while being inert in CI. Scope extension\n   into .github/workflows/ authorized by the coordinator and recorded in\n   the PR body. Additive only -- the lint and a11y jobs are untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(tokens): ASMA-8133 move the token test out of the published source tree\n\n`pnpm build` + `npm pack --dry-run` surfaced that src/styles/tokens.test.ts\nwas being published to consumers: package.json `files` ships\n\"src/styles/**/*\" as raw source, and this was the only test file under that\npath. 9.5 kB of test code in the tarball, which cuts against ASMA-8135''s\nwork bringing it down to 298.7 kB.\n\nMoved to src/tokens.test.ts, matching the existing src/api-surface.test.ts\nplacement. Still inside the vitest ''unit'' project glob (src/**/*.test.ts),\nso the new CI job still runs it, and re-verified that it still goes red on a\nseeded token break from the new location. Packed size 302.6 kB -> 299.6 kB;\nthe only remaining artifact is dist/src/tokens.test.d.ts (11 B), consistent\nwith the ~13 pre-existing *.test.d.ts files the dts plugin already emits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(vrt): ASMA-8133 re-baseline the styled-button gallery for the error focus ring\n\nOnly inputs-styled-button--gallery.png changes: the Primary/Danger and\nSecondary/Danger \"Focused\" cells, which are the three\n*-error-focused-border-color rules that --colors-beta-400 feeds. Deliberate\nconsequence of defining that token; every other baseline is untouched.\n\nPost-accept state: 1 modified, 0 deleted, 336 baselines (unchanged count).\nA full serial `vrt.sh check` afterwards is 317/317.\n\nNote for whoever re-baselines next: `vrt.sh accept` cannot do a targeted\nre-baseline. It hardcodes --update-snapshots=all, which unconditionally\nrewrites every PNG whether or not it differed, so it churned 28 files here\nwhile `check` on the same commit and build failed only 1. The other 27 were\nsub-tolerance noise -- they passed `check` against the committed baselines.\nI reverted them and kept only the legitimate one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(tokens): ASMA-8133 correct the shipped beta-400 comment and two stale paths\n\nsrc/styles/**/* is in package.json `files`, so these comments ship to\nconsumers. The beta-400 comment still carried a conclusion I had already\ndisproved in the PR discussion but never came back and fixed in the CSS.\n\nIt claimed the contained variant was \"unsatisfiable for any single border\ncolour\" and that 1.69:1 was an accepted worst case. Both wrong:\n\n- Unsatisfiable only in the branch I solved. 3:1 against the beta-500 fill\n  (L=0.1616) also has a darker branch, L<=0.021, which simultaneously\n  satisfies L<=0.300 against the white page. A near-black border clears\n  both.\n- Moot regardless, because the ring is never adjacent to the fill.\n  Decoding the baseline PNG shows contained renders\n  #ffffff | #9d0f0f x2 | #ffffff x1 | #e10700 -- a 1px white inset sits\n  between ring and fill, so both of the ring''s real adjacencies are white\n  at 8.37:1, and the inset is 4.96:1 against the fill. There is no worst\n  case to accept.\n- 1.69:1 is the focused-vs-unfocused indicator comparison (red-700 against\n  the unfocused beta-500 border), which belongs to 2.4.13 Focus Appearance\n  at AAA and is out of this library''s AA scope. Attributing it to 1.4.11\n  read as \"we knowingly shipped a 1.69:1 focus indicator\", which is not\n  what the pixels show.\n\nReplaced with a short three-row criterion summary (2.4.7 PASS, 1.4.11\nPASS, 2.4.13 not claimed) and a pointer to the derivation rather than the\nderivation itself, since a shipped stylesheet is not the place for it.\n\nAlso two stale references to the test''s old path, both of which would have\nmisled the next reader: the CI job comment that documents why the job\nexists, and the changeset, which feeds the published CHANGELOG.\n\nComments only. Verified the built CSS is unaffected: cssnano strips all\ncomments, and --colors-beta-400 still resolves to var(--colors-red-700),\nso VRT cannot be affected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqompGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0OEQAJlg45ULF9Q+Gal+FzeMt48Y\ns6esOBfAzLYijjWTO1w3DswFFDZ+lSxMDcPuNAWtuQC1t7pMJEFQva3a2aSr9W77\ne50R/ITO58bm88hKpbwzwy+6uUCRomm4W6eXfNqRup05scR1+vZg56uDDd67oI2F\nGF7eBQngWY4JwVj6xKIShw4TniOqGHoLYGWXdFIfNifKexyJpcoQ61kXNKjbAU/L\nSfFMT2/LSRZWuHOn7ZwNci1I+USyoCCckCnooneUW3xLniIYIsi9E3p8pxTqBQCP\nPNiZO5AntJGA6QSgFSkgB9ZeYf4egejXvW1McssGR458CJccP+NfRu1RY4+Qt4gC\nPlG5biFvXnjFyPxFP/Fjrfrt64P5JdWx67gK67W5X0lE6KFz5dyVA0qa8Tkz59eS\nNfFgjSw/XHiYwemGu8IYcRjDBazo+QcQyDuuDs1QudoV0QfTH4dUofV27STKFbZ3\nls8yGyVth/8UUiMuc/paIYDAp5UYjWFhnFCV+BvaW36W+15DcNdm+cwl7kU6RIXg\nzOddgiGXRxCaRpHfL3P7cRk6qgUNlwJw7aovYTiv3nhx7XhuDjxvPSwi/pMHUFst\nf/eylZne4sOxiRZA0K7KlnhKlfsrAg5x0SVSs7VCTbqV/vrZd/cKYm4DIgmwNC2E\nElAD9AwiGY8uW/TlyK3I\n=jcr9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-10T08:28:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/380617454ddf83fa3ad146db2d7756f7fa58e29c","node_id":"C_kwDORvrv4doAKDM4MDYxNzQ1NGRkZjgzZmEzYWQxNDZkYjJkNzc1NmY3ZmE1OGUyOWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/d21712aedb8b854709c3ab29485bd44d145f7ff0","sha":"d21712aedb8b854709c3ab29485bd44d145f7ff0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/d21712aedb8b854709c3ab29485bd44d145f7ff0"}],"sha":"380617454ddf83fa3ad146db2d7756f7fa58e29c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/380617454ddf83fa3ad146db2d7756f7fa58e29c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91586985?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mark31072","id":91586985,"login":"mark31072","node_id":"U_kgDOBXWBqQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/d21712aedb8b854709c3ab29485bd44d145f7ff0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T08:15:56Z","email":"91586985+mark31072@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Marin Pesterean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T08:15:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ASMA-8136 enforce Storybook axe checks: fail builds on new a11y violations (#171)\n\nci(a11y): ASMA-8136 fail builds on new axe violations\n\n.storybook/preview.ts set parameters.a11y.test to ''todo'', so every axe\nviolation was reported and none of them failed anything: the baseline\nstorybook run was 327/327 green while 120 stories were violating axe.\nThe Readme claimed accessibility shipped with each component and nothing\nenforced it.\n\nFlip the fleet-wide a11y test mode to ''error'' so any axe violation fails\npnpm test-storybook, and therefore the Lint & Accessibility workflow.\n\nThe 120 stories that were already failing carry an explicit per-story\nparameters.a11y.test = ''todo'' override with a one-line comment naming the\nrule. ''todo'' still runs axe and still reports in the Storybook test UI, so\nthe debt stays visible rather than hidden, while new stories and\nregressions in currently-clean stories fail immediately.\n\ndocs/a11y-allowlist.md documents every allowlisted story with its rule ids\nand violation, a per-rule breakdown, and burn-down notes with the concrete\ncall sites to fix.\n\nVerified: ts:check, lint and test-storybook --run all green (327/327).\nEnforcement proven both ways - removing one override fails that story on\ncolor-contrast, and a brand-new story with an unnamed button fails on\nbutton-name.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c223f017ea2094a34e4584794dbfc78245f206bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/c223f017ea2094a34e4584794dbfc78245f206bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/d21712aedb8b854709c3ab29485bd44d145f7ff0","verification":{"payload":"tree c223f017ea2094a34e4584794dbfc78245f206bc\nparent 0915bcdd344dd5987a485b4e8b1bb4a4541eb583\nauthor Marin Pesterean <91586985+mark31072@users.noreply.github.com> 1789028156 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789028156 +0300\n\nASMA-8136 enforce Storybook axe checks: fail builds on new a11y violations (#171)\n\nci(a11y): ASMA-8136 fail builds on new axe violations\n\n.storybook/preview.ts set parameters.a11y.test to ''todo'', so every axe\nviolation was reported and none of them failed anything: the baseline\nstorybook run was 327/327 green while 120 stories were violating axe.\nThe Readme claimed accessibility shipped with each component and nothing\nenforced it.\n\nFlip the fleet-wide a11y test mode to ''error'' so any axe violation fails\npnpm test-storybook, and therefore the Lint & Accessibility workflow.\n\nThe 120 stories that were already failing carry an explicit per-story\nparameters.a11y.test = ''todo'' override with a one-line comment naming the\nrule. ''todo'' still runs axe and still reports in the Storybook test UI, so\nthe debt stays visible rather than hidden, while new stories and\nregressions in currently-clean stories fail immediately.\n\ndocs/a11y-allowlist.md documents every allowlisted story with its rule ids\nand violation, a per-rule breakdown, and burn-down notes with the concrete\ncall sites to fix.\n\nVerified: ts:check, lint and test-storybook --run all green (327/327).\nEnforcement proven both ways - removing one override fails that story on\ncolor-contrast, and a brand-new story with an unnamed button fails on\nbutton-name.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqomc8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgUUQAEfDCSelRjyUXCiaknegh960\n09Ryi15U1Esnuc/kw6H6lRty1mjiEuVtvqG4hra7ZxtEnSqYt8