987a485b4e8b1bb4a4541eb583","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/0915bcdd344dd5987a485b4e8b1bb4a4541eb583"}],"sha":"d21712aedb8b854709c3ab29485bd44d145f7ff0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/d21712aedb8b854709c3ab29485bd44d145f7ff0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91586985?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mark31072","id":91586985,"login":"mark31072","node_id":"U_kgDOBXWBqQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/0915bcdd344dd5987a485b4e8b1bb4a4541eb583/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T12:39:31Z","email":"91586985+mark31072@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Marin Pesterean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T12:39:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ASMA-8134 dedupe drifted component copies in table and datetime (#170)\n\nrefactor(dedupe): ASMA-8134 re-export core primitives in table and datetime\n\nCollapse drifted duplicates under table/ and datetime/ onto the existing core\nimplementations, without changing any rendered output.\n\n- cn(): src/table/helpers/cn.ts and src/datetime/helpers/cn.ts were byte-identical\n  to src/helpers/cn.ts; both are now re-exports. One implementation remains.\n- Icons: table PinIcon, table CircleWarningOutlineIcon and datetime ClockOutlineIcon\n  were byte-identical to their core counterparts (modulo an unused `import React`)\n  and are now plain re-exports. table CheckIcon has identical artwork but a 1rem\n  default where core defaults to 24px, and call sites override width without\n  height, so it becomes a thin wrapper pinning the 1rem default; it also inherits\n  core''s aria-hidden, which the copy was missing (decorative glyphs).\n- Dead duplicates deleted: table ChevronUpIcon, table FilterIcon, datetime\n  ExpandIcon, datetime StyledTooltip. All four were unreferenced.\n\nDeliberately unchanged: StyledButton (table + datetime), table StyledCheckbox and\ntable StyledMenuItem. These have drifted in geometry, not just in root class and\ndata-test hook, so converging them on core would change rendered pixels. Per\ncoordinator ruling on the ASMA-8132 epic that is a design decision, not a refactor;\nmeasurements are recorded for the follow-up.\n\nsrc/index.ts exports nothing from shared-components, so the frozen api-surface\nsnapshot is untouched.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1e6b7a30cd906019527f1797ac48d053efab099a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/1e6b7a30cd906019527f1797ac48d053efab099a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/0915bcdd344dd5987a485b4e8b1bb4a4541eb583","verification":{"payload":"tree 1e6b7a30cd906019527f1797ac48d053efab099a\nparent a5f8adffaf57e162259523c6b26676dfed3b737f\nauthor Marin Pesterean <91586985+mark31072@users.noreply.github.com> 1788957571 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788957571 +0300\n\nASMA-8134 dedupe drifted component copies in table and datetime (#170)\n\nrefactor(dedupe): ASMA-8134 re-export core primitives in table and datetime\n\nCollapse drifted duplicates under table/ and datetime/ onto the existing core\nimplementations, without changing any rendered output.\n\n- cn(): src/table/helpers/cn.ts and src/datetime/helpers/cn.ts were byte-identical\n  to src/helpers/cn.ts; both are now re-exports. One implementation remains.\n- Icons: table PinIcon, table CircleWarningOutlineIcon and datetime ClockOutlineIcon\n  were byte-identical to their core counterparts (modulo an unused `import React`)\n  and are now plain re-exports. table CheckIcon has identical artwork but a 1rem\n  default where core defaults to 24px, and call sites override width without\n  height, so it becomes a thin wrapper pinning the 1rem default; it also inherits\n  core''s aria-hidden, which the copy was missing (decorative glyphs).\n- Dead duplicates deleted: table ChevronUpIcon, table FilterIcon, datetime\n  ExpandIcon, datetime StyledTooltip. All four were unreferenced.\n\nDeliberately unchanged: StyledButton (table + datetime), table StyledCheckbox and\ntable StyledMenuItem. These have drifted in geometry, not just in root class and\ndata-test hook, so converging them on core would change rendered pixels. Per\ncoordinator ruling on the ASMA-8132 epic that is a design decision, not a refactor;\nmeasurements are recorded for the follow-up.\n\nsrc/index.ts exports nothing from shared-components, so the frozen api-surface\nsnapshot is untouched.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoVODCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOxMQAB5u+9KDfoSSemLImsAZwpB0\nndw8lYi84qot9UoxSAqgdYKzKli61MId7kbGxyrd1gEzrka+eBVt8PRv1kU+dPDL\n6LcejFyKZYL4C520tOyan8MMqMCVRam0FiPk/syhJi9A9tAj6/4OTe0+9PYiO1Zc\nzOfrqurtAx2eYN0M6/N089HJxr5w7nVw9dPLvpKAlmh7Ps/4AimksaujBrGVvQ2q\nhwgxKB3NUvi+wQGYQvy+ozU4xsYpANkzANM4Nf28OcVRFwhIN5kqiozA9DjWTKwf\n7rV0LKCoLvNDS96+ZVeYh2qC5qaeebCu5Lb3KciXWHHqpCSGjpmfAvmX3GT3OPoS\nP9+4suxxVHqSx0fehVXRIcp6waB38+2XwLRImCWTnKaIqkHcPWHTM4m5W6v3gGM+\n+IJbGoTJR1EQ/4TrYbgLuSbGKKWDoi5+nlUDs1yV00loWVyL3eNcA3jpORX6CRvt\nfICIBUhiGRIM+cXn8a8vYP8JTFKb1LHEXnsPVgrVx7Mz2g6DuVGQMAFhrl0FbwQq\nLuJc/yEW5k0naQlknyP5n8mTAXEIuxLa0pQv8hXp55HxWdnjXTV6dpYLVY93CiqL\nJx9NKoR8BiIT35elN11g53zRpLP7GNYKDeuxVJxV/5EW37T0l/1TJNkR8F/xp4ys\nu72JWUeN8UGXfPddl6ov\n=3Tdg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T12:39:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/0915bcdd344dd5987a485b4e8b1bb4a4541eb583","node_id":"C_kwDORvrv4doAKDA5MTViY2RkMzQ0ZGQ1OTg3YTQ4NWI0ZThiMWJiNGE0NTQxZWI1ODM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/a5f8adffaf57e162259523c6b26676dfed3b737f","sha":"a5f8adffaf57e162259523c6b26676dfed3b737f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/a5f8adffaf57e162259523c6b26676dfed3b737f"}],"sha":"0915bcdd344dd5987a485b4e8b1bb4a4541eb583","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/0915bcdd344dd5987a485b4e8b1bb4a4541eb583"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91586985?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mark31072","id":91586985,"login":"mark31072","node_id":"U_kgDOBXWBqQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/a5f8adffaf57e162259523c6b26676dfed3b737f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T12:33:12Z","email":"91586985+mark31072@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Marin Pesterean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T12:33:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ASMA-8135 stop shipping unused Roboto font files (tarball 1.34 MB -> 0.28 MB) (#169)\n\nfix(pkg): ASMA-8135 stop shipping unused Roboto font files\n\nThe published tarball carried 12 Roboto .ttf weights plus their license\nunder src/styles/fonts/roboto/ (~1.96 MB) that nothing referenced.\n\nEvery @font-face rule in src/styles/index.css is inside a single\ncommented-out block (lines 109-202), so no build output has ever pointed\nat these files: `pnpm build` emits no font binaries and dist/ contains no\n@font-face or .ttf string. Components set `font-family: Roboto` by name\nonly, and the Tailwind stacks in tw-configs/twConfigs.json are\n`{\"sans\":[\"Roboto\"],\"roboto\":[\"Roboto\"]}` -- family names, not files. The\nconsuming app has always supplied the font.\n\nThe shipped set was also incoherent with what the library uses: it\nincluded Thin (100), Black (900) and all six italics, none of which the\nlibrary ever asks for, while omitting SemiBold (600) entirely -- the\nsingle most-used weight (22 occurrences). Real usage is 300/400/500/600/\n700 upright, no italics.\n\nExcluding src/styles/fonts/** from the `files` field takes the tarball\nfrom 1.34 MB to 0.28 MB packed (-78.7%) and 3.04 MB to 1.08 MB unpacked\n(-64.4%). Exactly the 13 font entries drop; the 1306 dist/ entries and\nthe rest of src/styles (token CSS, typographyTokens.css,\ninputVariables.css, and _breakpoints.scss, which the exports map points\nat) are untouched.\n\nThe .ttf files stay on disk -- removing them from the repo is a separate\nconcern and belongs to the owner of src/styles/.\n\nReadme gains a \"A note on fonts\" section under Quick start, a\nRequirements row and a Troubleshooting row recording that the consumer\napp must load Roboto, with the five weights actually needed.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"108e1c8bce5f5c5fa9998fe516d71aa8ac555fbd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/108e1c8bce5f5c5fa9998fe516d71aa8ac555fbd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/a5f8adffaf57e162259523c6b26676dfed3b737f","verification":{"payload":"tree 108e1c8bce5f5c5fa9998fe516d71aa8ac555fbd\nparent 518156ada4abb110c3ea81551fc5d842f556a8b2\nauthor Marin Pesterean <91586985+mark31072@users.noreply.github.com> 1788957192 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788957192 +0300\n\nASMA-8135 stop shipping unused Roboto font files (tarball 1.34 MB -> 0.28 MB) (#169)\n\nfix(pkg): ASMA-8135 stop shipping unused Roboto font files\n\nThe published tarball carried 12 Roboto .ttf weights plus their license\nunder src/styles/fonts/roboto/ (~1.96 MB) that nothing referenced.\n\nEvery @font-face rule in src/styles/index.css is inside a single\ncommented-out block (lines 109-202), so no build output has ever pointed\nat these files: `pnpm build` emits no font binaries and dist/ contains no\n@font-face or .ttf string. Components set `font-family: Roboto` by name\nonly, and the Tailwind stacks in tw-configs/twConfigs.json are\n`{\"sans\":[\"Roboto\"],\"roboto\":[\"Roboto\"]}` -- family names, not files. The\nconsuming app has always supplied the font.\n\nThe shipped set was also incoherent with what the library uses: it\nincluded Thin (100), Black (900) and all six italics, none of which the\nlibrary ever asks for, while omitting SemiBold (600) entirely -- the\nsingle most-used weight (22 occurrences). Real usage is 300/400/500/600/\n700 upright, no italics.\n\nExcluding src/styles/fonts/** from the `files` field takes the tarball\nfrom 1.34 MB to 0.28 MB packed (-78.7%) and 3.04 MB to 1.08 MB unpacked\n(-64.4%). Exactly the 13 font entries drop; the 1306 dist/ entries and\nthe rest of src/styles (token CSS, typographyTokens.css,\ninputVariables.css, and _breakpoints.scss, which the exports map points\nat) are untouched.\n\nThe .ttf files stay on disk -- removing them from the repo is a separate\nconcern and belongs to the owner of src/styles/.\n\nReadme gains a \"A note on fonts\" section under Quick start, a\nRequirements row and a Troubleshooting row recording that the consumer\napp must load Roboto, with the five weights actually needed.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoVIICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFG0QAEWKAqWZ+hez/SlugLWfSAIw\nBW/Ve+MTkrjQ2BDe41ZnFvu++bIazywLM/PtnP2aGe0CgGKdAEfSBkrVspOa98hg\n+rPyXXI0XoewlAdND3pYk5hW37u9btCxtQ3AALYTxWuZCf9FtrhGh8W91U8hE0IX\nm62vew+MJgT28UUlHTiKQR+SbcXvvKMj4RAqxwE7mV6LhhZVx0zMKVBnLYlNonPB\nQZC93Q1/SrUqmNmRNeMDmLvCqp6R/B7IVA4+kzkSi8E8lVM4PAhwv7L09cLEB4Ex\nFgEpc96HNOL3L8DQ7YqzKT3CFyfnkbPODd4E+Fu+VL7FrB1WSj9vjPpxbA2Olu81\n98sBdyjbWu4XGg2bmgYTaSyL4Ho5L9w5icgd31kN5xUxTOypNZuK2RWL21wihM7l\n2K4QuBKVRWmJ64Sf4kfeCwkLogujiLQ8zKRoKW3Y9wE9ZnS9EMFJ+QChcADfzdc8\nAt6LV4VvIn8RRdCjwAa7ynylFNeanEdtvl+2U2Ibua49/wifBMtjyxyix4Ik68j8\nccwJlAfhkEDTb39hrdk/J3b9p/0Lcc5/GdEB7zfIeiaBuK8HhtvsAGpv+eyNMocl\nupPiHumY+npGSg0W20TGJ8QqZbFGglqa6kxP8ige9/UeOdBQt8wmCjsQ6zdMc0gx\n3QR9v25RFmYdJ2YRd2m9\n=6r/M\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T12:33:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/a5f8adffaf57e162259523c6b26676dfed3b737f","node_id":"C_kwDORvrv4doAKGE1ZjhhZGZmYWY1N2UxNjIyNTk1MjNjNmIyNjY3NmRmZWQzYjczN2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/518156ada4abb110c3ea81551fc5d842f556a8b2","sha":"518156ada4abb110c3ea81551fc5d842f556a8b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/518156ada4abb110c3ea81551fc5d842f556a8b2"}],"sha":"a5f8adffaf57e162259523c6b26676dfed3b737f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/a5f8adffaf57e162259523c6b26676dfed3b737f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/264966161?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/doicovSanya","id":264966161,"login":"doicovSanya","node_id":"U_kgDOD8sQEQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/518156ada4abb110c3ea81551fc5d842f556a8b2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T06:49:17Z","email":"Alexandr.Doicov@carasent.com","name":"doicovSanya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T06:49:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(select): ASMA-8080 attach the select popover flush to the field (#167)\n\nThe dropdown sat 4px below its field on StyledSelect, StyledSelectAutocomplete\nand StyledDynamicSelect. The gap was introduced by the MUI-removal rewrite\n(ASMA-7573, a2110a5) — MUI''s own Select/Autocomplete popper sat flush — so this\nrestores the previous behaviour rather than changing the design.\n\nFigma agrees: in the Dynamic select reference (node 34523-166798) the Menus\nsurface abuts the field''s bottom edge in every cell (35046-160161 field h68 ->\nMenus y68; multiple 34634-153389 h92 -> y92).\n\nfloating-ui offset(4) -> offset(0) at the only two useFloating call sites in the\nselect family; StyledDynamicSelect composes StyledSelectAutocomplete and\ndatetime/shared-components/StyledSelect re-exports the core select, so both are\ncovered. The middleware is kept at 0 rather than deleted so a flip to\n''top-start'' also lands flush. StyledPopover/StyledTooltip keep their offsets —\nthey are not select surfaces.\n\nVerified: measured field bottom 56 / listbox top 56 (gap 0px) for all four\nselect surfaces in the VRT container. All 19 red VRT frames proven to be a pure\n4px upward translation before re-baselining (best-fit shift search: shift=4px,\n0.000% residual on 16; empty-options is end-cap curvature in a 21px bbox,\nasync-loading is LoadingIcon rotation phase inside the stationary field).\ntsc + eslint clean, vitest 420/420, full vrt 317/317 green.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"55437701a0920443cf21db4c20de37903ca72b31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/55437701a0920443cf21db4c20de37903ca72b31"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/518156ada4abb110c3ea81551fc5d842f556a8b2","verification":{"payload":"tree 55437701a0920443cf21db4c20de37903ca72b31\nparent 8bbb1793e3c3e437afaa57e40deac92af2084334\nauthor doicovSanya <Alexandr.Doicov@carasent.com> 1788936557 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788936557 +0300\n\nfix(select): ASMA-8080 attach the select popover flush to the field (#167)\n\nThe dropdown sat 4px below its field on StyledSelect, StyledSelectAutocomplete\nand StyledDynamicSelect. The gap was introduced by the MUI-removal rewrite\n(ASMA-7573, a2110a5) — MUI''s own Select/Autocomplete popper sat flush — so this\nrestores the previous behaviour rather than changing the design.\n\nFigma agrees: in the Dynamic select reference (node 34523-166798) the Menus\nsurface abuts the field''s bottom edge in every cell (35046-160161 field h68 ->\nMenus y68; multiple 34634-153389 h92 -> y92).\n\nfloating-ui offset(4) -> offset(0) at the only two useFloating call sites in the\nselect family; StyledDynamicSelect composes StyledSelectAutocomplete and\ndatetime/shared-components/StyledSelect re-exports the core select, so both are\ncovered. The middleware is kept at 0 rather than deleted so a flip to\n''top-start'' also lands flush. StyledPopover/StyledTooltip keep their offsets —\nthey are not select surfaces.\n\nVerified: measured field bottom 56 / listbox top 56 (gap 0px) for all four\nselect surfaces in the VRT container. All 19 red VRT frames proven to be a pure\n4px upward translation before re-baselining (best-fit shift search: shift=4px,\n0.000% residual on 16; empty-options is end-cap curvature in a 21px bbox,\nasync-loading is LoadingIcon rotation phase inside the stationary field).\ntsc + eslint clean, vitest 420/420, full vrt 317/317 green.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoQFtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALKQQAEZFPvtG8mVvEPW255qvrpHC\ntX0l303drENlnUPUmvFEHHSrEcGovuVGJocIWLq+RGz05whiRGptFrmarAfPp0yV\ny1RWsIArCsuQejS1BNNRzFqQKQD95fuJtg5jKcNQ9AVPSgVGIgwhZ6fMrwYjW3C/\nEzc2Gg2w8rRB1Se+NGGG36iASTwInIqYgwB2RNCUApk7TGx7lq/V8+fZVEA20XS0\nvkfFP8AXPq5/3WvyiV1r/QM1PhTHFSHZOfAUqGmLdOIZ/O7GI41bQRRGISJ14tGh\n6/c6NVf9C0tMNOfLfkRDMPlkZZLu57Zo7Y/TuiDw+mNOL7l6HLKrp3S3TSUzgadD\nFqUVkmDA5xMwjF+pzMgznW0NaBap+BSNztC2Aa7q/eq/wyxw6/Roek5wcwcTCBhv\nyQBR8yHQSo7HcnOoFOqXkVmVi65l81mzjAM9HqVmIhOtjVvuHfIFNnKFF5FYhOVk\n3OllG3KrOJT+uaTmhRGVDAMM6T01xnzZ2fGHL4Fw9w4KjgIMvuLu1KssLekoLtSK\nP4odAIRGpXcuF0ZRKhFa4b86fUgHy20/KjEj5pgIw+Kg8sNDyHdH9DdGq5lQSYoa\n2v6oAKitQ/EJ3+s0CE1/v3ip/ysp8ccC44lvzRn2zEWPfpHV/afVUMi8KWwLPu8a\neLb1fQ7x7jvBecHdODkV\n=b59p\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T06:49:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/518156ada4abb110c3ea81551fc5d842f556a8b2","node_id":"C_kwDORvrv4doAKDUxODE1NmFkYTRhYmIxMTBjM2VhODE1NTFmYzVkODQyZjU1NmE4YjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/8bbb1793e3c3e437afaa57e40deac92af2084334","sha":"8bbb1793e3c3e437afaa57e40deac92af2084334","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/8bbb1793e3c3e437afaa57e40deac92af2084334"}],"sha":"518156ada4abb110c3ea81551fc5d842f556a8b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/518156ada4abb110c3ea81551fc5d842f556a8b2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91586985?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mark31072","id":91586985,"login":"mark31072","node_id":"U_kgDOBXWBqQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mark31072","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/8bbb1793e3c3e437afaa57e40deac92af2084334/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T14:08:22Z","email":"91586985+mark31072@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Marin Pesterean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T14:08:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ASMA-7622 page header (#166)\n\n* ASMA-7622 add shared PageHeader component\n\nOne container-width-adaptive page header for all systems (Ad Voca,\nSamhandling, Ad Opus, Genesis), composing the header-layout planning\nengine. Title clamps to 2 lines (full string stays the accessible\nname), back/menu leading control or custom leadingSlot for\nwidget-hosted back buttons, adaptive actions with badge counts and\nMore overflow, subtitle/status slots, search mode, loading skeleton,\nsticky variant. Toolbar translations gain back/menu/close (en/no).\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* ASMA-7622 PageHeader review fixes: content-box planning, badge a11y\n\nCross-model review follow-ups: plan against the content box (px-4\nsubtracted) so actions no longer overestimate space by 32px near\nbreakpoints; badge counts survive collapse and the More overflow\n(count appended to label/ariaLabel, explicit ariaLabel now always\napplied in ToolbarActionButton); stale leading width no longer\nreserved after the control is removed; titleSlot wraps in a block\nelement; aria-busy while loading; badge chip standardized on\ndata-testid and hidden from AT (name carries the count).\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* ASMA-7622 PageHeader: icon-less actions never collapse to blank buttons\n\nThe planner treats undefined canHideLabel as collapsible; the\nPageHeader adapter now only allows label collapse when an icon\nremains. Adapter exported from the module file for direct unit\ntesting; the package barrel keeps exporting only the component\nand its types.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* ASMA-7622 PageHeader review corrections: owned heading, real title measurement, route focus, stable states, single base height\n\n- Measure the title as an unconstrained nowrap copy in the measurement strip\n  (inline spans report scrollWidth 0, so the planner always fell back to the\n  120px minimum reserve)\n- PageHeader owns the heading: titleSlot removed; titleDataTest keeps host\n  selector contracts (data-test=page-title) and titleRef allows imperative\n  targeting; focusTitleOnMount replaced by focusKey which focuses the heading\n  on every route change without stealing focus on first render\n- Loading and search keep the leading navigation control and preserve heading\n  semantics via a visually hidden h1; search mode moves focus into the search\n  slot and restores it on close (falling back to the heading when the invoker\n  unmounted)\n- Same base height (64px) at every width per the AC; sticky headers compact\n  once scrolled (data-stuck via sentinel + IntersectionObserver): tighter\n  padding, smaller type, subtitle hidden\n- Measurement strip copies no longer duplicate production data-testids;\n  actions support measureInStrip:false + estimatedWidthPx so stateful\n  renderers (quick-access widget) can join planning while mounting once\n- Browser-level acceptance stories: title measurement, route focus, search\n  focus transfer/restore, loading nav stability, sticky compaction\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* ASMA-7622 PageHeader: merge heading refs via useMergeRefs, derive stuck state\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* ASMA-7622 PageHeader: render no heading for an empty title (empty h1 is an a11y defect)\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* ASMA-7622 PageHeader: remount-safe route focus, measured sticky scroll padding, real widths for out-of-strip actions\n\n- Route focus compares the previous route key (module state), so it works\n  across header remounts and StrictMode effect replays; search/sticky logic\n  extracted into small focused hooks.\n- Sticky headers write their measured height as scroll-padding-top on the\n  nearest scroll container, so a 2-line title never covers focused content.\n- measureInStrip:false actions register their visible mount in the width\n  registry; estimatedWidthPx only bridges until the first measurement.\n- Measurement acceptance story uses accessible-role queries and asserts real\n  layout (verified red when measurement is deliberately broken); sticky story\n  asserts focused content stays uncovered.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* feat: Add useRouteHeadingFocus hook and improve PageHeader focus handlin\n\n- Add `useRouteHeadingFocus` hook for route-change heading focus, replacing `focusKey` prop\n- Keep heading element mounted across loading/search states to preserve focus\n- Measure status slot width in toolbar planning to prevent overflow\n- Add native tooltip only when title is actually clamped\n- Emit `data-testid` alongside `data-test` for heading selector contracts\n- Refactor PageHeader hooks into separate file for better organization\n\n* chore: Add pageheader visual test screenshots\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"660ebb42d36c41af9d05b1f74d3bc081e2e3bb9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/660ebb42d36c41af9d05b1f74d3bc081e2e3bb9d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/8bbb1793e3c3e437afaa57e40deac92af2084334","verification":{"payload":"tree 660ebb42d36c41af9d05b1f74d3bc081e2e3bb9d\nparent a001dca0f85e0466b44dfdd5b684acca36b99796\nauthor Marin Pesterean <91586985+mark31072@users.noreply.github.com> 1788876502 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788876502 +0300\n\nASMA-7622 page header (#166)\n\n* ASMA-7622 add shared PageHeader component\n\nOne container-width-adaptive page header for all systems (Ad Voca,\nSamhandling, Ad Opus, Genesis), composing the header-layout planning\nengine. Title clamps to 2 lines (full string stays the accessible\nname), back/menu leading control or custom leadingSlot for\nwidget-hosted back buttons, adaptive actions with badge counts and\nMore overflow, subtitle/status slots, search mode, loading skeleton,\nsticky variant. Toolbar translations gain back/menu/close (en/no).\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* ASMA-7622 PageHeader review fixes: content-box planning, badge a11y\n\nCross-model review follow-ups: plan against the content box (px-4\nsubtracted) so actions no longer overestimate space by 32px near\nbreakpoints; badge counts survive collapse and the More overflow\n(count appended to label/ariaLabel, explicit ariaLabel now always\napplied in ToolbarActionButton); stale leading width no longer\nreserved after the control is removed; titleSlot wraps in a block\nelement; aria-busy while loading; badge chip standardized on\ndata-testid and hidden from AT (name carries the count).\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* ASMA-7622 PageHeader: icon-less actions never collapse to blank buttons\n\nThe planner treats undefined canHideLabel as collapsible; the\nPageHeader adapter now only allows label collapse when an icon\nremains. Adapter exported from the module file for direct unit\ntesting; the package barrel keeps exporting only the component\nand its types.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* ASMA-7622 PageHeader review corrections: owned heading, real title measurement, route focus, stable states, single base height\n\n- Measure the title as an unconstrained nowrap copy in the measurement strip\n  (inline spans report scrollWidth 0, so the planner always fell back to the\n  120px minimum reserve)\n- PageHeader owns the heading: titleSlot removed; titleDataTest keeps host\n  selector contracts (data-test=page-title) and titleRef allows imperative\n  targeting; focusTitleOnMount replaced by focusKey which focuses the heading\n  on every route change without stealing focus on first render\n- Loading and search keep the leading navigation control and preserve heading\n  semantics via a visually hidden h1; search mode moves focus into the search\n  slot and restores it on close (falling back to the heading when the invoker\n  unmounted)\n- Same base height (64px) at every width per the AC; sticky headers compact\n  once scrolled (data-stuck via sentinel + IntersectionObserver): tighter\n  padding, smaller type, subtitle hidden\n- Measurement strip copies no longer duplicate production data-testids;\n  actions support measureInStrip:false + estimatedWidthPx so stateful\n  renderers (quick-access widget) can join planning while mounting once\n- Browser-level acceptance stories: title measurement, route focus, search\n  focus transfer/restore, loading nav stability, sticky compaction\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* ASMA-7622 PageHeader: merge heading refs via useMergeRefs, derive stuck state\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* ASMA-7622 PageHeader: render no heading for an empty title (empty h1 is an a11y defect)\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* ASMA-7622 PageHeader: remount-safe route focus, measured sticky scroll padding, real widths for out-of-strip actions\n\n- Route focus compares the previous route key (module state), so it works\n  across header remounts and StrictMode effect replays; search/sticky logic\n  extracted into small focused hooks.\n- Sticky headers write their measured height as scroll-padding-top on the\n  nearest scroll container, so a 2-line title never covers focused content.\n- measureInStrip:false actions register their visible mount in the width\n  registry; estimatedWidthPx only bridges until the first measurement.\n- Measurement acceptance story uses accessible-role queries and asserts real\n  layout (verified red when measurement is deliberately broken); sticky story\n  asserts focused content stays uncovered.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* feat: Add useRouteHeadingFocus hook and improve PageHeader focus handlin\n\n- Add `useRouteHeadingFocus` hook for route-change heading focus, replacing `focusKey` prop\n- Keep heading element mounted across loading/search states to preserve focus\n- Measure status slot width in toolbar planning to prevent overflow\n- Add native tooltip only when title is actually clamped\n- Emit `data-testid` alongside `data-test` for heading selector contracts\n- Refactor PageHeader hooks into separate file for better organization\n\n* chore: Add pageheader visual test screenshots\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoBbWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPBYQAE10Y3eKTsm7JB7TmQTw1GWO\nAxeY3SW8LanGq2HfzBlveCi4eC4jp4/VUX+LzZNzySLbmHCIEpe8hOotQOjPw3Kz\n3HmBy+FFuxFhR2RV/WciujUziXCwWf5vy/sHfDXFoKfIyfbZwelQMrucLFQjHoyR\nctVwR5o2y9QsdmCWJUKMcYT/ibhqwJXA/sfk92bF7clJJfF+z5KWunkUOtdzdh77\nrCC+Qd6CsJA04HIRDd4bMzRmIPEz9Pg3Y51bS68X1v3+bMJJSyZpFQaJ8je1kAGJ\n6W4gBXRSrbwV/BG2VwjfhxmYfG+lG1v0IPifSe+122uhLUzmN8xZyaWGRQy9AfUh\n6VlH3mw0yW/l8KvYfVz/ItNvv4WTH6glCoijEJYcrc36xENFqvAHM0wmHTJ9KRH2\naJbi3iYG6/hKzm0XYB2FhWz/u18sBhO54J5QPFS/KduGeDqdZ7P9gi4WbmDUvf8M\nCgPsFVaUhlFkg2Eyfo3iQiTfrUFNmcDVWJ8STpwjqIk6GiaEMeBurR2KysV6yrtI\nvI5s7BCVxC9TAacbTjXmFi5jKBDjn8PCKR4plI9k9DeloN8k6nHNo2qT2iamC5NR\nvmOXl+KEvz7DzLfKHiuVg42N7urSm0dJ1Yp9d+lMZuCrHwifZ4D+zwX/F5+UGIJp\nK5NHmUFFhnu/6NtVDTut\n=zyoL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T14:08:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/8bbb1793e3c3e437afaa57e40deac92af2084334","node_id":"C_kwDORvrv4doAKDhiYmIxNzkzZTNjM2U0MzdhZmFhNTdlNDBkZWFjOTJhZjIwODQzMzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/a001dca0f85e0466b44dfdd5b684acca36b99796","sha":"a001dca0f85e0466b44dfdd5b684acca36b99796","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/a001dca0f85e0466b44dfdd5b684acca36b99796"}],"sha":"8bbb1793e3c3e437afaa57e40deac92af2084334","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/8bbb1793e3c3e437afaa57e40deac92af2084334"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/264966161?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/doicovSanya","id":264966161,"login":"doicovSanya","node_id":"U_kgDOD8sQEQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/doicovSanya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/a001dca0f85e0466b44dfdd5b684acca36b99796/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T21:23:05Z","email":"Alexandr.Doicov@carasent.com","name":"doicovSanya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T21:23:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ASMA-8069 Fix RTF document view: keep the dialog paper a flex column for scroll=''body'' (#165)\n\n* fix(dialog): ASMA-8069 Keep the dialog paper a flex column for scroll=''body''\n\n`flex-col` was gated on `scroll === ''paper''`, so a `scroll=''body''` paper stayed\na flex row and laid its header bar out beside the content at roughly half width\neach. The storage RTF draft/generate dialogs use `fullScreen scroll=''body''`, so\ntheir embedded DevExpress editor was squeezed into the right half of the screen\nand the document layout looked broken.\n\n`scroll` now only decides where overflow lives, matching MUI''s always-column\n`.MuiDialog-paper`. Locked by a new `BodyScrollFullScreen` story whose play\nassertion fails (reports `row`) without the fix, plus its VRT baseline. Existing\ndialog baselines are unchanged - `DialogStoryFrame` forces `flexDirection:\n''column''` via paper `sx`, which is why no story caught this.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* refactor(dialog): drop story sx that masked the flex-row paper\n\nThe story frame forced display/flexDirection on the paper via slotProps.sx,\nwhich ui-core''s !important utilities already win over, so it never took effect\nand only hid that the paper''s main axis came from the scroll prop.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"1052eb5e1ee9c2db3f880b514f7d880a1d17d292","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/1052eb5e1ee9c2db3f880b514f7d880a1d17d292"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/a001dca0f85e0466b44dfdd5b684acca36b99796","verification":{"payload":"tree 1052eb5e1ee9c2db3f880b514f7d880a1d17d292\nparent 0f44d44953c494a05bb970b523e3ee9a6dfea5d0\nauthor doicovSanya <Alexandr.Doicov@carasent.com> 1788384185 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788384185 +0300\n\nASMA-8069 Fix RTF document view: keep the dialog paper a flex column for scroll=''body'' (#165)\n\n* fix(dialog): ASMA-8069 Keep the dialog paper a flex column for scroll=''body''\n\n`flex-col` was gated on `scroll === ''paper''`, so a `scroll=''body''` paper stayed\na flex row and laid its header bar out beside the content at roughly half width\neach. The storage RTF draft/generate dialogs use `fullScreen scroll=''body''`, so\ntheir embedded DevExpress editor was squeezed into the right half of the screen\nand the document layout looked broken.\n\n`scroll` now only decides where overflow lives, matching MUI''s always-column\n`.MuiDialog-paper`. Locked by a new `BodyScrollFullScreen` story whose play\nassertion fails (reports `row`) without the fix, plus its VRT baseline. Existing\ndialog baselines are unchanged - `DialogStoryFrame` forces `flexDirection:\n''column''` via paper `sx`, which is why no story caught this.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* refactor(dialog): drop story sx that masked the flex-row paper\n\nThe story frame forced display/flexDirection on the paper via slotProps.sx,\nwhich ui-core''s !important utilities already win over, so it never took effect\nand only hid that the paper''s main axis came from the scroll prop.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmJO5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMLkQAD2oHsrJmrvKWkvMe4lBZzYM\nt6qvu1qmO5Ast7JARrx8C36oa0DDQ9o7/NIipcgRXhu+usoqQ7iCFAoDCtthy7bQ\n+qKuU1GNevru2K1aSXaDH6m8LWrfe3zlc+6UPVQ1guQbYp9QHtiFygaFzAuTH99M\nkjIS5C+2ekoP6Q7bwvn4PSyjXM2pRH19TYRBNF8gr5aIc3I4jAR5OlwN8Ix0cRTt\nebpMwk4seTW8AhVOLvAanpkjC1HhmUv8l+Llv/UzzEGZN/Btk2iohDKATBiaJa89\nCSUd5fPUw2MQ0/QfzneDCgQZTwXLrDHlAb+LY0j1tBqsNvJrBgh6EByHElmfDyi1\npLNQpQeGlGeSsYcAD5vYBOBkCTEauH1bn/Am9FyHA4cne5kKn0iOxDcIXEp88otv\nh+vYD5mbYicI7LbUxswJLRHmz8fUYswvmvk/ZuyDVJCc3ZVYTASW62jtt3xEYcTc\njYuwVvPWrikVXxRMfp5vnUIG9pjPf2DgrG7zFYwx4YB+QTN43g43Jh675k3t1CS+\nRqFpliJCybbkvSFT20IPQPA/3DBktt3wpN7vjzG1kCTf9XZXBGHvBz4yI2wm6S72\nFFXdE4Zs5zUdKeTrzkoKDF5oGATHHHq1zX8Kav243r8WqB/Gs+t3b7dYJFHSKwr2\nCg4yHaE0WSxP/zLedPNL\n=wu7B\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T21:23:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/user