hub.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/a37afe24e21193160464eaa1da13c7215e1eb16e","node_id":"C_kwDORvrv4doAKGEzN2FmZTI0ZTIxMTkzMTYwNDY0ZWFhMWRhMTNjNzIxNWUxZWIxNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/ad7ec56e30f632041f506c9001f29c5391d7e363","sha":"ad7ec56e30f632041f506c9001f29c5391d7e363","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/ad7ec56e30f632041f506c9001f29c5391d7e363"}],"sha":"a37afe24e21193160464eaa1da13c7215e1eb16e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/a37afe24e21193160464eaa1da13c7215e1eb16e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118059335?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nikeedw","id":118059335,"login":"nikeedw","node_id":"U_kgDOBwlxRw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/ad7ec56e30f632041f506c9001f29c5391d7e363/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T19:13:55Z","email":"118059335+nikeedw@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nicolaev Eduard"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T19:13:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(select): ASMA-7847 own the option separator from the listbox, not the row (#159)\n\nThe separator survived only as long as every consumer kept ui-core''s row\n`className` and every page loaded ui-core''s `last:border-b-0` rule. Neither\nholds:\n\n- A custom `renderOption` that sets `className` after spreading `props` drops\n  the row rule entirely - a real pattern in asma-app-directory, where the\n  Overrides autocomplete lost both the separator exclusion and the hover state.\n- The separator (`border-b`) and its exclusion (`last:border-b-0`) were two\n  utilities that can arrive from two different bundles. A page carrying a\n  generic `.border-b{border-bottom-width:1px!important}` from one stylesheet\n  without our `last:` rule from another paints a line under the final option -\n  the trailing separator reported on genesis prod, which does not reproduce on\n  dev because there both rules load together.\n\nMoving the rule to the listbox (`[&>li:not(:last-child)]:…`) makes it\nstructural: the separator and the last-row exclusion are the same declaration,\nso they cannot come apart, and a row whose className was replaced still gets\nseparated. The degraded case is now benign - no stylesheet means no separators\nat all, never a stray trailing line.\n\n`border-0` stays in the variant group deliberately: `border-solid` styles all\nfour sides, and without a width reset the other three fall back to the initial\n`medium` (3px). VRT caught that in the first pass.\n\nVerified in Storybook: first row 1px bottom / last row 0px on all three select\nfamilies; a row stripped down to `class=\"flex items-center gap-1 p-2\"` is still\nseparated; listbox padding still 8px 0. 292 interaction tests pass. VRT is\n282/282 with **no baseline changes** - pixel-identical to 3.74.1, only robust.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"af68195b347d77304f54fb787832a89e63c5299d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/af68195b347d77304f54fb787832a89e63c5299d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/ad7ec56e30f632041f506c9001f29c5391d7e363","verification":{"payload":"tree af68195b347d77304f54fb787832a89e63c5299d\nparent a9615e2b6199f9d208d69db6dad003ab74ae4586\nauthor Nicolaev Eduard <118059335+nikeedw@users.noreply.github.com> 1788117235 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788117235 +0300\n\nfix(select): ASMA-7847 own the option separator from the listbox, not the row (#159)\n\nThe separator survived only as long as every consumer kept ui-core''s row\n`className` and every page loaded ui-core''s `last:border-b-0` rule. Neither\nholds:\n\n- A custom `renderOption` that sets `className` after spreading `props` drops\n  the row rule entirely - a real pattern in asma-app-directory, where the\n  Overrides autocomplete lost both the separator exclusion and the hover state.\n- The separator (`border-b`) and its exclusion (`last:border-b-0`) were two\n  utilities that can arrive from two different bundles. A page carrying a\n  generic `.border-b{border-bottom-width:1px!important}` from one stylesheet\n  without our `last:` rule from another paints a line under the final option -\n  the trailing separator reported on genesis prod, which does not reproduce on\n  dev because there both rules load together.\n\nMoving the rule to the listbox (`[&>li:not(:last-child)]:…`) makes it\nstructural: the separator and the last-row exclusion are the same declaration,\nso they cannot come apart, and a row whose className was replaced still gets\nseparated. The degraded case is now benign - no stylesheet means no separators\nat all, never a stray trailing line.\n\n`border-0` stays in the variant group deliberately: `border-solid` styles all\nfour sides, and without a width reset the other three fall back to the initial\n`medium` (3px). VRT caught that in the first pass.\n\nVerified in Storybook: first row 1px bottom / last row 0px on all three select\nfamilies; a row stripped down to `class=\"flex items-center gap-1 p-2\"` is still\nseparated; listbox padding still 8px 0. 292 interaction tests pass. VRT is\n282/282 with **no baseline changes** - pixel-identical to 3.74.1, only robust.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlIDzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAB98QAKsGVTc/642W5r+vW9qaGoRf\naX4aYO078kViinE/s23vnOhbrGswAWO6gscCiNRJ08SLZabjuknLhyBTBc9zZ9mk\nvP8P/6CZdd6kH6Wq7eNLru89bDFexcIo83rgfG3MuwDS9xvHD095VCNsHf0u4f1l\nLRsOUIx4oAk53x6zbxdygYPZW0SeIGG+8E0QUkw/VV0zNPvA379FusbCJAWAMA8d\n1XTZD715izf20/CMiyUZAvT01Lk5l9KtDvdgPj0XBYBq2cd6wCZ21RBbSy+PWLz7\nlA9SupXjSAgdzbFGcA646xSYDIAq34lnEXgB7lOb2jPkDWZTRhP7HnDohxSmmGX/\niF2B98fWKjssqBE62T75nQsZvj5c+IUvmBv+FqwjZDLlj5l6S8J4naDN3AwY+Pmr\nJZR2hkIGcZSv3kXtxPC4i6mmGX75fdJnpgqxT5Av3e78QIXOGEFv9h0S/LN+CdLe\nx/0/u9W9XAlIKn4QVU/rLGOWEMXQ+K1+LMAGMo9SOYg9t75hgQTAeWpKra4ZrIUz\n30A9bcxODyYtw5TRZLKKrWgkeLsn7ld8zFwTWGSHNRZt2bubYHfuq0iXqmAOd6O6\n/87XY+FV1jqqKVTH8mkWh2eu2/kxOboMlXQ0kvA5ku676duARvPLSvsmrQJsvBhF\nbzRllxU2/4ir//BXX/yR\n=Bybt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T19:13:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/ad7ec56e30f632041f506c9001f29c5391d7e363","node_id":"C_kwDORvrv4doAKGFkN2VjNTZlMzBmNjMyMDQxZjUwNmM5MDAxZjI5YzUzOTFkN2UzNjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commit/a9615e2b6199f9d208d69db6dad003ab74ae4586","sha":"a9615e2b6199f9d208d69db6dad003ab74ae4586","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/a9615e2b6199f9d208d69db6dad003ab74ae4586"}],"sha":"ad7ec56e30f632041f506c9001f29c5391d7e363","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/ad7ec56e30f632041f506c9001f29c5391d7e363"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118059335?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nikeedw","id":118059335,"login":"nikeedw","node_id":"U_kgDOBwlxRw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/commits/a9615e2b6199f9d208d69db6dad003ab74ae4586/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T16:31:00Z","email":"118059335+nikeedw@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nicolaev Eduard"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T16:31:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(select): ASMA-7847 wrap long option labels to two lines and add DS separators (#158)\n\n* fix(select): ASMA-7847 wrap long option labels to two lines and add DS separators\n\nLong organisation names in the revman multiversion/features dropdowns were cut\nmid-word on a single line with no way to read the rest (\"Røde Kors Haugland\nRehabiliteringsss...\"). The clipping lives in ui-core rather than the app, so\nall three select families are fixed at the source:\n\n- option labels are `line-clamp-2 break-words` - two lines, then the ellipsis\n  (Figma `word-break: break-word`). DynamicSelect''s labels had no limit at all\n  and grew the row without bound.\n- every option row carries the Figma `border/separator` rule (delta-200 =\n  #d3d8df), dropped on the last row. Previously only multi-select rows had one.\n\nSpec: Figma Design-System wXrXt5uKNNzV2DnQCgyYZH node 34522-151497 (Menus).\n\nVerified live in Storybook via computed styles and measured boxes: first row\n`1px solid rgb(211,216,223)`, last row `0px`; a 378-char label renders 48px\n(2 x lh24) against 72px/144px with the clamp removed; a 200-char unbreakable\ntoken stays inside the row. 292 interaction tests and the api-surface snapshot\npass. VRT was not run - it needs Docker, which this machine does not have, and\nthe select baselines were re-captured on master in #154, so they need a scoped\nre-accept for the separator and the wrap.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(vrt): ASMA-7847 re-accept the seven select baselines the separator changes\n\nScoped `scripts/vrt.sh accept --grep ...` over exactly the stories that failed\nthe PR''s visual-regression run - every one of them renders an open listbox,\nwhich is where the new `border/separator` rule shows up:\n\n  inputs-select--select-option--open\n  inputs-select--multiple-select-behavior\n  inputs-select--rapid-open-close\n  inputs-select--option-and-value-are-16-px\n  inputs-styled-dynamic-select--multiple-select-autocomplete\n  inputs-styled-dynamic-select--large-multiple-select-autocomplete\n  inputs-styled-dynamic-select--multiple-primitive-options\n\nEyeballed before accepting: rows are now divided by a 1px delta-200 rule with\nno rule under the final option, and nothing else moved. No other baseline was\ntouched and the orphan prune was a no-op.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(select): ASMA-7847 pad the dropdown list 8px 0 per the Design System\n\nFigma pads the Menus list `8px 0` (node 34522-151497: the 256px reference frame\nis 8 + 6x40 + 8). The autocomplete listbox had no padding at all and pulled its\nfirst row up another 4px with `first:-mt-1` - a leftover that faked MUI''s old\nlistbox padding away - and StyledSelect''s listbox had 4px.\n\nBoth listboxes are now `px-0 py-2` and the negative margin is gone. Measured in\nStorybook: computed padding `8px 0px 8px 0px`, 8px above the first option and\n8px below the last, rows still full-bleed horizontally.\n\n292 interaction tests pass. VRT: 18 stories moved - every one of them renders an\nopen listbox of these three components - re-accepted in a scoped run and\nreviewed before committing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"43d882fee1c64b489e582a05602406266885460c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/trees/43d882fee1c64b489e582a05602406266885460c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-ui-core/git/commits/a9615e2b6199f9d208d69db6dad003ab74ae4586","verification":{"payload":"tree 43d882fee1c64b489e582a05602406266885460c\nparent 1401181741f5b4b4a29e40b993aab9935582de09\nauthor Nicolaev Eduard <118059335+nikeedw@users.noreply.github.com> 1788107460 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788107460 +0300\n\nfix(select): ASMA-7847 wrap long option labels to two lines and add DS separators (#158)\n\n* fix(select): ASMA-7847 wrap long option labels to two lines and add DS separators\n\nLong organisation names in the revman multiversion/features dropdowns were cut\nmid-word on a single line with no way to read the rest (\"Røde Kors Haugland\nRehabiliteringsss...\"). The clipping lives in ui-core rather than the app, so\nall three select families are fixed at the source:\n\n- option labels are `line-clamp-2 break-words` - two lines, then the ellipsis\n  (Figma `word-break: break-word`). DynamicSelect''s labels had no limit at all\n  and grew the row without bound.\n- every option row carries the Figma `border/separator` rule (delta-200 =\n  #d3d8df), dropped on the last row. Previously only multi-select rows had one.\n\nSpec: Figma Design-System wXrXt5uKNNzV2DnQCgyYZH node 34522-151497 (Menus).\n\nVerified live in Storybook via computed styles and measured boxes: first row\n`1px solid rgb(211,216,223)`, last row `0px`; a 378-char label renders 48px\n(2 x lh24) against 72px/144px with the clamp removed; a 200-char unbreakable\ntoken stays inside the row. 292 interaction tests and the api-surface snapshot\npass. VRT was not run - it needs Docker, which this machine does not have, and\nthe select baselines were re-captured on master in #154, so they need a scoped\nre-accept for the separator and the wrap.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(vrt): ASMA-7847 re-accept the seven select baselines the separator changes\n\nScoped `scripts/vrt.sh accept --grep ...` over exactly the stories that failed\nthe PR''s visual-regression run - every one of them renders an open listbox,\nwhich is where the new `border/separator` rule shows up:\n\n  inputs-select--select-option--open\n  inputs-select--multiple-select-behavior\n  inputs-select--rapid-open-close\n  inputs-select--option-and-value-are-16-px\n  inputs-styled-dynamic-select--multiple-select-autocomplete\n  inputs-styled-dynamic-select--large-multiple-select-autocomplete\n  inputs-styled-dynamic-select--multiple-primitive-options\n\nEyeballed before accepting: rows are now divided by a 1px delta-200 rule with\nno rule under the final option, and nothing else moved. No other baseline was\ntouched and the orphan prune was a no-op.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(select): ASMA-7847 pad the dropdown list 8px 0 per the Design System\n\nFigma pads the Menus list `8px 0` (node 34522-151497: the 256px reference frame\nis 8 + 6x40 + 8). The autocomplete listbox had no padding at all and pulled its\nfirst row up another 4px with `first:-mt-1` - a leftover that faked MUI''s old\nlistbox padding away - and StyledSelect''s listbox had 4px.\n\nBoth listboxes are now `px-0 py-2` and the negative margin is gone. Measured in\nStorybook: computed padding `8px 0px 8px 0px`, 8px above the first option and\n8px below the last, rows still full-bleed horizontally.\n\n292 interaction tests pass. VRT: 18 stories moved - every one of them renders an\nopen listbox of these three components - re-accepted in a scoped run and\nreviewed before committing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlFrECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAy0QQAI6iMp7lNdemgnH2K6UFiqC1\nf1gWgsEUmAcu8rb3FoP4ftZ5s56YTd2f/2MMTgDpxrxppfsyBD1OZ8SKFfHbaSpZ\numVBHKyk4ooHFKXJ/Z0R2cW1Lg34DPuSEPXuxcdT5hSPSE1SFYB45HtkyDR4XMfX\nrmkP4Z2DiENfZMOhMrgTnACFotwT/HIJlw98nwxZGn9mf3tlYs6NiAcEWrlj3bw/\nxZXzBsxgNwAskrCyUTLyP7xSiLGtMo6cyaZs431M8MmkEqsgXqLjjt8y8ewDDEss\ng0/+1NUxrN1KXPQXawKmZmUfNfu0uD6pg8yJTc4ZFsRpR4BdYEbA2+/Wkdo7BId1\ncda4ecRQQPqWRj/18SK1SzGC3MVqcnbUL7eF45vO0aJ/kcOeTICduxRmFWbWRhwW\nuHKkYZxJ3yuqCOWg06dXzSMCHM/fdqG+34Zx7/FfH4FLt8qPfvUV0dGPm6AmP2oW\nFBbXHSnSuUWXEIYrENqWy/kNoF12GbFRaml7z94DNgwaT6kBqD6Vk3RLk6bhOsd8\n0WvdPA0QmqYdd0y05KCD6a+V2kZuMQFFfu