rl":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/750a5b51490b4c7c879b31ae0a4ffb8de4373273/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T07:58:49Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T07:59:14Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat(answers): group pronoun questions into one family\n\nVanta asked as free text and took \"He/Him\"; Affirm asks with a picker and\nblocked two applications on it. Grouped, the dashboard pre-fills Affirm''s\n\"He/him/his\" from the earlier answer. A question that also asks for a name\n(Samsara''s \"preferred name and pronouns\") stays alone.","tree":{"sha":"d08f6097d785e3aadcfcd6a6269fd412d2e4a7b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/d08f6097d785e3aadcfcd6a6269fd412d2e4a7b2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/750a5b51490b4c7c879b31ae0a4ffb8de4373273","verification":{"payload":"tree d08f6097d785e3aadcfcd6a6269fd412d2e4a7b2\nparent b947dc9299e900d07e8b24655dc5ce02940fb932\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1790927929 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1790927954 -0700\n\nfeat(answers): group pronoun questions into one family\n\nVanta asked as free text and took \"He/Him\"; Affirm asks with a picker and\nblocked two applications on it. Grouped, the dashboard pre-fills Affirm''s\n\"He/him/his\" from the earlier answer. A question that also asks for a name\n(Samsara''s \"preferred name and pronouns\") stays alone.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQFqhVttRGkAAtyvrZMiLML4S+G7RLzc2BDtgrP3RSivdAbLuEI98dEEbirEZnAZFkX\nc+daWSTV22L44KPJWgwQ8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T07:59:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/750a5b51490b4c7c879b31ae0a4ffb8de4373273","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKDc1MGE1YjUxNDkwYjRjN2M4NzliMzFhZTBhNGZmYjhkZTQzNzMyNzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/b947dc9299e900d07e8b24655dc5ce02940fb932","sha":"b947dc9299e900d07e8b24655dc5ce02940fb932","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/b947dc9299e900d07e8b24655dc5ce02940fb932"}],"sha":"750a5b51490b4c7c879b31ae0a4ffb8de4373273","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/750a5b51490b4c7c879b31ae0a4ffb8de4373273"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/b947dc9299e900d07e8b24655dc5ce02940fb932/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T06:54:22Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T06:54:36Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat: answer one personal fact once, however many ways employers ask it\n\nThe owner re-answered the same fact in every employer''s phrasing — on\n2026-10-01 sponsorship alone came up nine times, work authorization three,\n\"have you worked here before\" twice for one company. The runner refuses to\ncarry an answer across wordings, and rightly: \"entitled to work in Canada\"\nshares nearly every word with the US question, and copying \"Yes\" across is a\nfalse statement. Overlap scoring had already produced four.\n\nA question family is the narrow middle ground (worker/src/questionFamily.ts):\na small set of facts that do not vary by employer — sponsorship, work\nauthorization, race, Hispanic/Latino, veteran, disability, LGBTQ+, current\nemployer and title, state, postal code, current city, how you heard,\nworked-here-before (listed per company), website, GitHub. Each rule was\nderived from the 125 real questions the owner had seen and reviewed by hand;\nthat review caught the first employer rule admitting \"Are you a current\ngovernment official…\", whose answer would have been offered for Most Recent\nEmployer. Never grouped: another country, a legal agreement, a follow-up\n(\"If you do require…\"), a future intent (\"the state you plan to…\"), \"U.S.\nperson\", and negated phrasing on the legal-status facts, where the answer\nflips.\n\nThe dashboard shows each family ONCE: every employer''s wording listed with\nits own picker, pre-filled with the owner''s previous answer matched to THAT\nboard''s option text (matchOption: normalised equality — so \"do not\" is\n\"don''t\" — then an unambiguous yes/no, then a unique whole-word containment;\nanything less is left blank and unticked for the owner to pick). All prior\nanswers are shown, newest first, because the owner''s answers to one fact\nsometimes differ (race: \"I don''t wish to answer\", later \"White\"). Nothing is\nsaved until they press Save. On today''s real data: 46 questions become 13\nfamilies and 23 standalone; sponsorship''s five wordings are one button.\n\nTwo fixes that fell out of building it:\n\n- A saved answer that BLOCKED a row was hidden as \"answered\". Toast''s\n  Disability Status is answered, the saved wording is not one of Toast''s\n  options, the runner cannot enter it, seven rows block — and the queue showed\n  nothing. Now shown again with the saved answer, the board''s options and a\n  suggestion.\n- \"Similar answered\" offered \"White\" (a race answer) for \"Where have you\n  learned about Samsara?\" and a US work-authorization \"Yes\" for Canada. It now\n  crosses only within a family — except a polarity flip, still shown, as the\n  warning it is.\n\nThe dashboard''s copy of matchOption is pinned to the worker''s by a parity\ntest; its first table missed contractions entirely (a copy with them deleted\nstill passed every row), so it now carries cases reachable only through\nnormalisation, and fails on that drift. Rendered against today''s real data in\na real browser before shipping: 13 family cards, 23 standalone rows, no page\nerrors.","tree":{"sha":"463947e817145835397b2ee06e0edce615042624","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/463947e817145835397b2ee06e0edce615042624"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/b947dc9299e900d07e8b24655dc5ce02940fb932","verification":{"payload":"tree 463947e817145835397b2ee06e0edce615042624\nparent 930c9fed5d4112dcffc59e3bc74ec9e6a7034ad0\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1790924062 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1790924076 -0700\n\nfeat: answer one personal fact once, however many ways employers ask it\n\nThe owner re-answered the same fact in every employer''s phrasing — on\n2026-10-01 sponsorship alone came up nine times, work authorization three,\n\"have you worked here before\" twice for one company. The runner refuses to\ncarry an answer across wordings, and rightly: \"entitled to work in Canada\"\nshares nearly every word with the US question, and copying \"Yes\" across is a\nfalse statement. Overlap scoring had already produced four.\n\nA question family is the narrow middle ground (worker/src/questionFamily.ts):\na small set of facts that do not vary by employer — sponsorship, work\nauthorization, race, Hispanic/Latino, veteran, disability, LGBTQ+, current\nemployer and title, state, postal code, current city, how you heard,\nworked-here-before (listed per company), website, GitHub. Each rule was\nderived from the 125 real questions the owner had seen and reviewed by hand;\nthat review caught the first employer rule admitting \"Are you a current\ngovernment official…\", whose answer would have been offered for Most Recent\nEmployer. Never grouped: another country, a legal agreement, a follow-up\n(\"If you do require…\"), a future intent (\"the state you plan to…\"), \"U.S.\nperson\", and negated phrasing on the legal-status facts, where the answer\nflips.\n\nThe dashboard shows each family ONCE: every employer''s wording listed with\nits own picker, pre-filled with the owner''s previous answer matched to THAT\nboard''s option text (matchOption: normalised equality — so \"do not\" is\n\"don''t\" — then an unambiguous yes/no, then a unique whole-word containment;\nanything less is left blank and unticked for the owner to pick). All prior\nanswers are shown, newest first, because the owner''s answers to one fact\nsometimes differ (race: \"I don''t wish to answer\", later \"White\"). Nothing is\nsaved until they press Save. On today''s real data: 46 questions become 13\nfamilies and 23 standalone; sponsorship''s five wordings are one button.\n\nTwo fixes that fell out of building it:\n\n- A saved answer that BLOCKED a row was hidden as \"answered\". Toast''s\n  Disability Status is answered, the saved wording is not one of Toast''s\n  options, the runner cannot enter it, seven rows block — and the queue showed\n  nothing. Now shown again with the saved answer, the board''s options and a\n  suggestion.\n- \"Similar answered\" offered \"White\" (a race answer) for \"Where have you\n  learned about Samsara?\" and a US work-authorization \"Yes\" for Canada. It now\n  crosses only within a family — except a polarity flip, still shown, as the\n  warning it is.\n\nThe dashboard''s copy of matchOption is pinned to the worker''s by a parity\ntest; its first table missed contractions entirely (a copy with them deleted\nstill passed every row), so it now carries cases reachable only through\nnormalisation, and fails on that drift. Rendered against today''s real data in\na real browser before shipping: 13 family cards, 23 standalone rows, no page\nerrors.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQM96ZCbU82ckEsZ6jHJGUUA30a2jVM6rGOo1f1965+JsLXWnv8VtIY4b+AP5HK0tXO\n560mjzygvekzv4sxbUrQ4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T06:54:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/b947dc9299e900d07e8b24655dc5ce02940fb932","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKGI5NDdkYzkyOTllOTAwZDA3ZThiMjQ2NTVkYzVjZTAyOTQwZmI5MzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/930c9fed5d4112dcffc59e3bc74ec9e6a7034ad0","sha":"930c9fed5d4112dcffc59e3bc74ec9e6a7034ad0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/930c9fed5d4112dcffc59e3bc74ec9e6a7034ad0"}],"sha":"b947dc9299e900d07e8b24655dc5ce02940fb932","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/b947dc9299e900d07e8b24655dc5ce02940fb932"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/930c9fed5d4112dcffc59e3bc74ec9e6a7034ad0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T21:22:46Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T21:22:46Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(worker): the unanswered-questions list counted optional blanks as blockers\n\n`blocking` was incremented for every unanswered question on a needs_manual\nrow, so an optional question that merely sat blank beside the real blocker\nwas ranked as one. On 2026-10-01 this list — the owner''s work list, sorted\nmost-blocking first — led with Toast''s optional \"Race/Ethnicity (Select all\nthat apply)\", \"blocking 7\", when Disability Status had stopped all seven and\nRace held nothing up.\n\nThe runner now records which blanks actually stopped a row (scraper bab1ee2,\n`evidence.blocking`). When that is present, only those count; the optional\nones are still listed with their application count, because the owner may\nwant to answer them anyway. Evidence written before the field existed cannot\nsay, so it keeps the whole-row count until the row is filled again — the\nsafe direction, since it over-reports rather than hiding a real blocker.\n\nTwo tests; the first fails against the old counting.","tree":{"sha":"071994e5ba43b55942c944db0d6616bf15312785","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/071994e5ba43b55942c944db0d6616bf15312785"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/930c9fed5d4112dcffc59e3bc74ec9e6a7034ad0","verification":{"payload":"tree 071994e5ba43b55942c944db0d6616bf15312785\nparent dba60f17c1bf948ffc1052c8174da04e81eb0da5\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1790889766 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1790889766 -0700\n\nfix(worker): the unanswered-questions list counted optional blanks as blockers\n\n`blocking` was incremented for every unanswered question on a needs_manual\nrow, so an optional question that merely sat blank beside the real blocker\nwas ranked as one. On 2026-10-01 this list — the owner''s work list, sorted\nmost-blocking first — led with Toast''s optional \"Race/Ethnicity (Select all\nthat apply)\", \"blocking 7\", when Disability Status had stopped all seven and\nRace held nothing up.\n\nThe runner now records which blanks actually stopped a row (scraper bab1ee2,\n`evidence.blocking`). When that is present, only those count; the optional\nones are still listed with their application count, because the owner may\nwant to answer them anyway. Evidence written before the field existed cannot\nsay, so it keeps the whole-row count until the row is filled again — the\nsafe direction, since it over-reports rather than hiding a real blocker.\n\nTwo tests; the first fails against the old counting.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQPdKtq9sX4bz6amz4I+xM9dyLTjo1R3w1ozDqHd/QBgPikq0NAGZHwOziIgOJOAAh8\ndJ0B1wrdaA4laTAuEC1wU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T21:23:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/930c9fed5d4112dcffc59e3bc74ec9e6a7034ad0","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKDkzMGM5ZmVkNWQ0MTEyZGNmZmM1OWUzYmM3NGVjOWU2YTcwMzRhZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/dba60f17c1bf948ffc1052c8174da04e81eb0da5","sha":"dba60f17c1bf948ffc1052c8174da04e81eb0da5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/dba60f17c1bf948ffc1052c8174da04e81eb0da5"}],"sha":"930c9fed5d4112dcffc59e3bc74ec9e6a7034ad0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/930c9fed5d4112dcffc59e3bc74ec9e6a7034ad0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/dba60f17c1bf948ffc1052c8174da04e81eb0da5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T18:47:36Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T18:47:36Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"docs: the API table was missing 17 routes, including the whole apply queue\n\nGenerated the list from the createRoute calls and diffed it against\nAGENTS.md rather than writing it from memory. Undocumented until now: every\napply-queue route (/jobs/:id/apply, /applications, its status, approve and\nowner hand-off), the standing-answers routes and /unanswered-questions, vote\nfeedback, /jobs/packets, and four operator routes including the new\n/ingest/reconcile-mail.\n\nAdds a footnote on `ownerName`, the convention every per-owner route shares,\nbecause the failure it guards against is silent: a route that ignores it\nanswers for the SERVICE identity, which owns nothing, and no error says so.\nGET /jobs was that bug until 4b609e7.\n\nAlso corrects /jobs/:id/apply''s OpenAPI summary, which still said the packet\nwas required at queue time. It has been minted at fill since the route\nstopped 409ing without one, and that summary is what the published API docs\nrender.","tree":{"sha":"169a8b7de30a1d6f5207f4af3df1c47865489235","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/169a8b7de30a1d6f5207f4af3df1c47865489235"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/dba60f17c1bf948ffc1052c8174da04e81eb0da5","verification":{"payload":"tree 169a8b7de30a1d6f5207f4af3df1c47865489235\nparent 4b609e7c46bf49473438cde5b1f214525322be6c\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1790880456 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1790880456 -0700\n\ndocs: the API table was missing 17 routes, including the whole apply queue\n\nGenerated the list from the createRoute calls and diffed it against\nAGENTS.md rather than writing it from memory. Undocumented until now: every\napply-queue route (/jobs/:id/apply, /applications, its status, approve and\nowner hand-off), the standing-answers routes and /unanswered-questions, vote\nfeedback, /jobs/packets, and four operator routes including the new\n/ingest/reconcile-mail.\n\nAdds a footnote on `ownerName`, the convention every per-owner route shares,\nbecause the failure it guards against is silent: a route that ignores it\nanswers for the SERVICE identity, which owns nothing, and no error says so.\nGET /jobs was that bug until 4b609e7.\n\nAlso corrects /jobs/:id/apply''s OpenAPI summary, which still said the packet\nwas required at queue time. It has been minted at fill since the route\nstopped 409ing without one, and that summary is what the published API docs\nrender.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQAi+PfNmbuqYH1/t9uEQrXFsRa7bQR9aSPS1Slu1PCzibpl7qlrzY2cpS14c70mQd+\nY8tCZGu0ro+ybFdF4ofw4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T18:47:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/dba60f17c1bf948ffc1052c8174da04e81eb0da5","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKGRiYTYwZjE3YzFiZjk0OGZmYzEwNTJjODE3NGRhMDRlODFlYjBkYTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/4b609e7c46bf49473438cde5b1f214525322be6c","sha":"4b609e7c46bf49473438cde5b1f214525322be6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/4b609e7c46bf49473438cde5b1f214525322be6c"}],"sha":"dba60f17c1bf948ffc1052c8174da04e81eb0da5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/dba60f17c1bf948ffc1052c8174da04e81eb0da5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/4b609e7c46bf49473438cde5b1f214525322be6c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T17:50:16Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T17:50:16Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(worker): the feed ignored ownerName and showed the owner their own applications\n\nGET /jobs resolved its user with maybeUserId and silently dropped\n`ownerName`, so a service acting for a person got the feed computed for the\nSERVICE identity — which owns no applications. Every per-user part of the\nfeed was evaluated against nobody: hide_queued, application_status,\ndismissals, and the company saturation penalty.\n\nMeasured, not hypothetical: on 2026-10-01 a service-key read of hadoku''s feed\nput 23 of hadoku''s own applications in the top 400 as fresh postings, every\none reporting `application_status: null`, plus two reposts of applied roles.\nPinterest and Toast — 13 and 10 applications out, so x0.6 — ranked as though\nuntouched. Nothing errored; the list was just wrong, which is the dangerous\nkind. The owner''s browser was never affected, since a signed-in human is\ntheir own user.\n\nNow matches /applications and /application-answers: with `ownerName`,\neffectiveUserId resolves the person (service/admin only); without it,\nmaybeUserId as before, so anonymous browsing of the public feed is\nunchanged. An anonymous or friend caller naming someone is refused (403)\nrather than ignored — ignoring it would return a list that looks like an\nanswer about the named person.\n\nFour tests, each failing against the old handler and passing now.","tree":{"sha":"28e2a2980c9da7715fc9e427203a3ab245921d68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/28e2a2980c9da7715fc9e427203a3ab245921d68"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/4b609e7c46bf49473438cde5b1f214525322be6c","verification":{"payload":"tree 28e2a2980c9da7715fc9e427203a3ab245921d68\nparent b8916d80ad489ea4caf489984625293f84dc0987\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1790877016 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1790877016 -0700\n\nfix(worker): the feed ignored ownerName and showed the owner their own applications\n\nGET /jobs resolved its user with maybeUserId and silently dropped\n`ownerName`, so a service acting for a person got the feed computed for the\nSERVICE identity — which owns no applications. Every per-user part of the\nfeed was evaluated against nobody: hide_queued, application_status,\ndismissals, and the company saturation penalty.\n\nMeasured, not hypothetical: on 2026-10-01 a service-key read of hadoku''s feed\nput 23 of hadoku''s own applications in the top 400 as fresh postings, every\none reporting `application_status: null`, plus two reposts of applied roles.\nPinterest and Toast — 13 and 10 applications out, so x0.6 — ranked as though\nuntouched. Nothing errored; the list was just wrong, which is the dangerous\nkind. The owner''s browser was never affected, since a signed-in human is\ntheir own user.\n\nNow matches /applications and /application-answers: with `ownerName`,\neffectiveUserId resolves the person (service/admin only); without it,\nmaybeUserId as before, so anonymous browsing of the public feed is\nunchanged. An anonymous or friend caller naming someone is refused (403)\nrather than ignored — ignoring it would return a list that looks like an\nanswer about the named person.\n\nFour tests, each failing against the old handler and passing now.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQCdSjCzkGhZiefuRpTzABKVBXZjTXnWCyrDGqKYyJhZoJKBlolbAjIo0LKvTSS3BwD\nYVeNLDqMrGWHBlfnAXfwo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T17:50:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/4b609e7c46bf49473438cde5b1f214525322be6c","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKDRiNjA5ZTdjNDZiZjQ5NDczNDM4Y2RlNWIxZjIxNDUyNTMyMmJlNmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/b8916d80ad489ea4caf489984625293f84dc0987","sha":"b8916d80ad489ea4caf489984625293f84dc0987","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/b8916d80ad489ea4caf489984625293f84dc0987"}],"sha":"4b609e7c46bf49473438cde5b1f214525322be6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/4b609e7c46bf49473438cde5b1f214525322be6c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following