ull}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/a949c456ee5b87fef00fbd774566de684f7f9182","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKGE5NDljNDU2ZWU1Yjg3ZmVmMDBmYmQ3NzQ1NjZkZTY4NGY3ZjkxODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/6b7b1982292e699a777687904753b7795fa4c591","sha":"6b7b1982292e699a777687904753b7795fa4c591","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/6b7b1982292e699a777687904753b7795fa4c591"}],"sha":"a949c456ee5b87fef00fbd774566de684f7f9182","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/a949c456ee5b87fef00fbd774566de684f7f9182"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/6b7b1982292e699a777687904753b7795fa4c591/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T05:04:54Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T05:04:54Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(worker): the first backfill got all three numbers wrong — scope, dedupe, window\n\nRan against production: confirmed 2, verification_flagged 0,\nduplicates_flagged 3, on a mailbox with no Pinecone application, two genuine\nCoinbase codes and exactly one genuine duplicate pair. Every number wrong,\nthree separate causes, each now pinned by a test that fails without its fix\nand passes with it (verified by reverting them one at a time).\n\n1. Matching had NO user filter. `confirmed: 2` for Pinecone was the query\n   reaching another identity''s rows. Mail to the owner''s mailbox is evidence\n   about the owner''s applications and nobody else''s — an unscoped match writes\n   a confirmation onto a row the mail says nothing about, which is the\n   fabricated-evidence failure this feature exists to prevent. Reconciliation\n   is now always scoped to one owner, via the same ownerName convention the\n   rest of the API uses, and mail_unmatched carries user_id.\n\n2. The duplicate check found the message''s OWN row. On a second pass every\n   unmatched mail sat inside its own ten-minute window, so `duplicates_flagged`\n   counted replays rather than duplicates. Excluded by message_id, and ordered\n   ascending so the flag points at the EARLIER mail.\n\n3. The match window was anchored +-14 days on `created_at`, which is when a\n   row was QUEUED — routinely weeks before anything is submitted. The Coinbase\n   rows were queued 2026-09-09 and drew their codes on 2026-09-16, and a\n   narrower reading of the same field found nothing. Now 180 days back, and\n   2 days forward: the forward bound is the one doing real work, since an\n   employer cannot acknowledge an application that does not exist yet.\n\nAlso ships the reader that should have been in the first commit. The writer\nput its findings in D1 with no way to get them out, so a feature whose entire\npurpose is making a disagreement VISIBLE delivered nothing anyone could look\nat. GET /ingest/reconcile-mail returns the run state, the unmatched mail, and\nevery application the inbox has something to say about.\n\nMigration 0022 rebuilds both tables rather than adding a default: rows written\nby the unscoped run cannot be attributed after the fact, and inventing an\nowner for them would preserve bad data under a name that looks deliberate.\nThe feed is re-readable from its first message, so a reset re-derives it all.","tree":{"sha":"d5680fca3e52175c2b7cf810d7d153f082a7e2d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/d5680fca3e52175c2b7cf810d7d153f082a7e2d6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/6b7b1982292e699a777687904753b7795fa4c591","verification":{"payload":"tree d5680fca3e52175c2b7cf810d7d153f082a7e2d6\nparent 1def30a9cef6dc0e51cabc34e8c5a72a08ba2cd0\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789880694 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789880694 -0700\n\nfix(worker): the first backfill got all three numbers wrong — scope, dedupe, window\n\nRan against production: confirmed 2, verification_flagged 0,\nduplicates_flagged 3, on a mailbox with no Pinecone application, two genuine\nCoinbase codes and exactly one genuine duplicate pair. Every number wrong,\nthree separate causes, each now pinned by a test that fails without its fix\nand passes with it (verified by reverting them one at a time).\n\n1. Matching had NO user filter. `confirmed: 2` for Pinecone was the query\n   reaching another identity''s rows. Mail to the owner''s mailbox is evidence\n   about the owner''s applications and nobody else''s — an unscoped match writes\n   a confirmation onto a row the mail says nothing about, which is the\n   fabricated-evidence failure this feature exists to prevent. Reconciliation\n   is now always scoped to one owner, via the same ownerName convention the\n   rest of the API uses, and mail_unmatched carries user_id.\n\n2. The duplicate check found the message''s OWN row. On a second pass every\n   unmatched mail sat inside its own ten-minute window, so `duplicates_flagged`\n   counted replays rather than duplicates. Excluded by message_id, and ordered\n   ascending so the flag points at the EARLIER mail.\n\n3. The match window was anchored +-14 days on `created_at`, which is when a\n   row was QUEUED — routinely weeks before anything is submitted. The Coinbase\n   rows were queued 2026-09-09 and drew their codes on 2026-09-16, and a\n   narrower reading of the same field found nothing. Now 180 days back, and\n   2 days forward: the forward bound is the one doing real work, since an\n   employer cannot acknowledge an application that does not exist yet.\n\nAlso ships the reader that should have been in the first commit. The writer\nput its findings in D1 with no way to get them out, so a feature whose entire\npurpose is making a disagreement VISIBLE delivered nothing anyone could look\nat. GET /ingest/reconcile-mail returns the run state, the unmatched mail, and\nevery application the inbox has something to say about.\n\nMigration 0022 rebuilds both tables rather than adding a default: rows written\nby the unscoped run cannot be attributed after the fact, and inventing an\nowner for them would preserve bad data under a name that looks deliberate.\nThe feed is re-readable from its first message, so a reset re-derives it all.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQMqKQ0IG9fOBqAODc6I4U9JsGvkz9uMV6yQ6YpNzmEneN+hAJzRwhW9IlM/MBCg+Nc\nXoecjdx+D64HxLb79LgQg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T05:05:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/6b7b1982292e699a777687904753b7795fa4c591","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKDZiN2IxOTgyMjkyZTY5OWE3Nzc2ODc5MDQ3NTNiNzc5NWZhNGM1OTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/1def30a9cef6dc0e51cabc34e8c5a72a08ba2cd0","sha":"1def30a9cef6dc0e51cabc34e8c5a72a08ba2cd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/1def30a9cef6dc0e51cabc34e8c5a72a08ba2cd0"}],"sha":"6b7b1982292e699a777687904753b7795fa4c591","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/6b7b1982292e699a777687904753b7795fa4c591"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/1def30a9cef6dc0e51cabc34e8c5a72a08ba2cd0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T00:00:13Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T00:00:28Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat(worker): reconcile the mailbox against the queue, and keep them apart\n\nThe queue is the runner''s account of what it did; the mailbox is the\nemployer''s. This walks the second and records where it disagrees with the\nfirst. It never touches `status` — the disagreement IS the product, and\noverwriting the runner''s account with mail evidence would destroy the thing\nworth seeing. On 2026-09-19 the queue reported zero applications sent while\na Pinecone confirmation sat unread for an application it had no row for.\n\nTwo columns rather than one, because for our corpus they are genuinely\ndifferent facts. `confirmed_at` means an employer said it received an\napplication; Ashby does this and Greenhouse never has.\n`verification_requested_at` means an employer mailed a code and is waiting\non a human — every Greenhouse mail this mailbox has ever received is one of\nthose, and all 37 applications are Greenhouse, so it is our common case.\n\nThere is deliberately no column for the code itself, and a test sweeps every\ntext column of every table this writes to prove a code value never lands in\nthe database. Per docs/DECISION-mail-reconciler.md: a code mail sets state,\nits contents are never parsed, stored, logged or displayed.\n\nOrdering in parseMail is load-bearing and tested: account mail is excluded\nfirst, then verification, then confirmation. A code subject contains\n\"application\" and would otherwise read as a confirmation — marking an\napplication successfully received at the exact moment it is blocked.\n\nUnmatched mail gets its own table instead of being dropped. A confirmation\nwith no application row is the Pinecone case, and discarding those would\nrebuild the blind spot this closes. Two mails for one company inside ten\nminutes are flagged as a possible duplicate, never counted as two: the real\npair sits 20.2s apart with identical subjects and names no role, and\ninventing an application the owner never made is the same phantom row.\n\nA feed we cannot read is a 502, never an empty mailbox — \"no mail\" and \"no\naccess\" look identical downstream and telling them apart is the whole point.\n/scope is asserted every run for the same reason; it is also exactly what\nwould have caught the greenhouse.io error before it shipped.\n\nTests: 326 pass. Two defects found while writing them, both fixed: the\nend-anchored company pattern swallowed a trailing clause (\"acme corp was\nreceived\"), and the feed client used an `as` assertion that the root\neslint''s --fix strips — scraper.ts''s annotation form is the one that holds.","tree":{"sha":"4188e2675af525447129ee835f9459002bc84183","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/4188e2675af525447129ee835f9459002bc84183"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/1def30a9cef6dc0e51cabc34e8c5a72a08ba2cd0","verification":{"payload":"tree 4188e2675af525447129ee835f9459002bc84183\nparent 7abdbbe77d9b232b9e694d99f9e5f5537f253832\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789862413 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789862428 -0700\n\nfeat(worker): reconcile the mailbox against the queue, and keep them apart\n\nThe queue is the runner''s account of what it did; the mailbox is the\nemployer''s. This walks the second and records where it disagrees with the\nfirst. It never touches `status` — the disagreement IS the product, and\noverwriting the runner''s account with mail evidence would destroy the thing\nworth seeing. On 2026-09-19 the queue reported zero applications sent while\na Pinecone confirmation sat unread for an application it had no row for.\n\nTwo columns rather than one, because for our corpus they are genuinely\ndifferent facts. `confirmed_at` means an employer said it received an\napplication; Ashby does this and Greenhouse never has.\n`verification_requested_at` means an employer mailed a code and is waiting\non a human — every Greenhouse mail this mailbox has ever received is one of\nthose, and all 37 applications are Greenhouse, so it is our common case.\n\nThere is deliberately no column for the code itself, and a test sweeps every\ntext column of every table this writes to prove a code value never lands in\nthe database. Per docs/DECISION-mail-reconciler.md: a code mail sets state,\nits contents are never parsed, stored, logged or displayed.\n\nOrdering in parseMail is load-bearing and tested: account mail is excluded\nfirst, then verification, then confirmation. A code subject contains\n\"application\" and would otherwise read as a confirmation — marking an\napplication successfully received at the exact moment it is blocked.\n\nUnmatched mail gets its own table instead of being dropped. A confirmation\nwith no application row is the Pinecone case, and discarding those would\nrebuild the blind spot this closes. Two mails for one company inside ten\nminutes are flagged as a possible duplicate, never counted as two: the real\npair sits 20.2s apart with identical subjects and names no role, and\ninventing an application the owner never made is the same phantom row.\n\nA feed we cannot read is a 502, never an empty mailbox — \"no mail\" and \"no\naccess\" look identical downstream and telling them apart is the whole point.\n/scope is asserted every run for the same reason; it is also exactly what\nwould have caught the greenhouse.io error before it shipped.\n\nTests: 326 pass. Two defects found while writing them, both fixed: the\nend-anchored company pattern swallowed a trailing clause (\"acme corp was\nreceived\"), and the feed client used an `as` assertion that the root\neslint''s --fix strips — scraper.ts''s annotation form is the one that holds.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQEo46+ODLYYlWRne6m1JLJVeEC0zfE3m189K7Gwv99SmCcilq5COS1j+HjHeCLTaqb\nabfnEw5SNAauJIevRY/Qk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T00:00:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/1def30a9cef6dc0e51cabc34e8c5a72a08ba2cd0","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKDFkZWYzMGE5Y2VmNmRjMGU1MWNhYmMzNGU4YzVhNzJhMDhiYTJjZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/7abdbbe77d9b232b9e694d99f9e5f5537f253832","sha":"7abdbbe77d9b232b9e694d99f9e5f5537f253832","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/7abdbbe77d9b232b9e694d99f9e5f5537f253832"}],"sha":"1def30a9cef6dc0e51cabc34e8c5a72a08ba2cd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/1def30a9cef6dc0e51cabc34e8c5a72a08ba2cd0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/7abdbbe77d9b232b9e694d99f9e5f5537f253832/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T23:23:35Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T23:23:35Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"docs: the reconciler reads that a code arrived, never what it says\n\nhadoku_site''s response (3af865c) §8 is right that nothing in the plumbing\nenforces the old line any more: 4 of the 7 reachable messages are\nverification codes and their values are in bodies we now receive. So it is a\nchoice our code makes, and this writes down which way it went.\n\nA code mail sets state. Its contents are never parsed, stored, logged or\ndisplayed. Showing the owner their own code would arguably be fine on its\nown — their mail, their account, a human still typing — but the dashboard is\none click from a runner whose whole job is typing values into ATS forms, and\nthe distance from \"displayed for convenience\" to \"autofilled for\nconvenience\" is one reasonable-looking commit. Not holding the value is the\nversion that cannot rot, and the owner loses nothing: the code is in their\ninbox, which is where they have to look anyway.\n\nTwo findings from re-verifying the feed rather than trusting the response:\n\nConfirmations frequently name no role. Neither Pinecone mail does — the\nbodies are byte-identical generic copy — so (company, role, date) matching\ndoes not hold and degrades to (company, date window).\n\nThe Pinecone count is ambiguous and must not be guessed: two messages 20.2s\napart, identical subjects and bodies. Either two back-to-back applications\nwith Ashby autofilling, or one double-send. Surfaced as one with a duplicate\nflag, because inventing an application the owner never made is exactly the\nphantom row this work exists to eliminate.\n\nAlso records the greenhouse.io error: inferred from the brand name, written\nas though measured, matched 0% of 37 Greenhouse applications, and would have\nfailed as silence — indistinguishable from what the feature detects.","tree":{"sha":"0c4a24a91522750dd74bad80d42981feb382fd8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/0c4a24a91522750dd74bad80d42981feb382fd8f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/7abdbbe77d9b232b9e694d99f9e5f5537f253832","verification":{"payload":"tree 0c4a24a91522750dd74bad80d42981feb382fd8f\nparent 3af865cff8ff45036d1519766d65198d465e99ed\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789860215 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789860215 -0700\n\ndocs: the reconciler reads that a code arrived, never what it says\n\nhadoku_site''s response (3af865c) §8 is right that nothing in the plumbing\nenforces the old line any more: 4 of the 7 reachable messages are\nverification codes and their values are in bodies we now receive. So it is a\nchoice our code makes, and this writes down which way it went.\n\nA code mail sets state. Its contents are never parsed, stored, logged or\ndisplayed. Showing the owner their own code would arguably be fine on its\nown — their mail, their account, a human still typing — but the dashboard is\none click from a runner whose whole job is typing values into ATS forms, and\nthe distance from \"displayed for convenience\" to \"autofilled for\nconvenience\" is one reasonable-looking commit. Not holding the value is the\nversion that cannot rot, and the owner loses nothing: the code is in their\ninbox, which is where they have to look anyway.\n\nTwo findings from re-verifying the feed rather than trusting the response:\n\nConfirmations frequently name no role. Neither Pinecone mail does — the\nbodies are byte-identical generic copy — so (company, role, date) matching\ndoes not hold and degrades to (company, date window).\n\nThe Pinecone count is ambiguous and must not be guessed: two messages 20.2s\napart, identical subjects and bodies. Either two back-to-back applications\nwith Ashby autofilling, or one double-send. Surfaced as one with a duplicate\nflag, because inventing an application the owner never made is exactly the\nphantom row this work exists to eliminate.\n\nAlso records the greenhouse.io error: inferred from the brand name, written\nas though measured, matched 0% of 37 Greenhouse applications, and would have\nfailed as silence — indistinguishable from what the feature detects.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLGc5ZY/nHjKclGiJKX+Xm2WHhcQJAMBILZSYt+L6EeKK38VsSP4So2N3JMyynElup\n3PiRPZuDNNZ1V6PYf0EgU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T23:24:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/7abdbbe77d9b232b9e694d99f9e5f5537f253832","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKDdhYmRiYmU3N2Q5YjIzMmI5ZTY5NGQ5OWY5ZTVmNTUzN2YyNTM4MzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/3af865cff8ff45036d1519766d65198d465e99ed","sha":"3af865cff8ff45036d1519766d65198d465e99ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/3af865cff8ff45036d1519766d65198d465e99ed"}],"sha":"7abdbbe77d9b232b9e694d99f9e5f5537f253832","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/7abdbbe77d9b232b9e694d99f9e5f5537f253832"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/3af865cff8ff45036d1519766d65198d465e99ed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T22:48:13Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T22:48:13Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"docs: the scraper is granted too, and both paths are verified live\n\n§3 said hadoku-scraper would 403. It no longer does — scraper-service-key now\ncarries the same grant, so where the reconciler gets built is a choice rather\nthan a constraint. jobplatform-api is still the recommendation, since it owns\nthe applications table and already wires the key.\n\nBoth identities were exercised against production with their real vault keys:\n/scope returns the right label and 11 domains for each, /messages returns the\nsame 7 messages, and a limit=2 cursor walk terminates in 4 pages with 7 unique\nids and no repeats.\n\nAlso notes that jobplatform-e2e (friend tier, unlisted) cannot read the feed,\nso the reconciler wants a fixture rather than live mail in tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2ecf68264d936623c2a93681fe8c44ad50ebd48c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/2ecf68264d936623c2a93681fe8c44ad50ebd48c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/3af865cff8ff45036d1519766d65198d465e99ed","verification":{"payload":"tree 2ecf68264d936623c2a93681fe8c44ad50ebd48c\nparent 2e66fdca35341479ccd4f91688c0b81e57538f7b\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789858093 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789858093 -0700\n\ndocs: the scraper is granted too, and both paths are verified live\n\n§3 said hadoku-scraper would 403. It no longer does — scraper-service-key now\ncarries the same grant, so where the reconciler gets built is a choice rather\nthan a constraint. jobplatform-api is still the recommendation, since it owns\nthe applications table and already wires the key.\n\nBoth identities were exercised against production with their real vault keys:\n/scope returns the right label and 11 domains for each, /messages returns the\nsame 7 messages, and a limit=2 cursor walk terminates in 4 pages with 7 unique\nids and no repeats.\n\nAlso notes that jobplatform-e2e (friend tier, unlisted) cannot read the feed,\nso the reconciler wants a fixture rather than live mail in tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQFPBp77z/uzoq10jk/l/O1wbKUNWTqy/HEUyDd18BFaiI8ECoNq5BSR3hl1IyR1GLw\ntzmzQRucwRSV+JF6wcQg4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T22:48:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/3af865cff8ff45036d1519766d65198d465e99ed","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKDNhZjg2NWNmZjhmZjQ1MDM2ZDE1MTk3NjZkNjUxOThkNDY1ZTk5ZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/2e66fdca35341479ccd4f91688c0b81e57538f7b","sha":"2e66fdca35341479ccd4f91688c0b81e57538f7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/2e66fdca35341479ccd4f91688c0b81e57538f7b"}],"sha":"3af865cff8ff45036d1519766d65198d465e99ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/3af865cff8ff45036d1519766d65198d465e99ed"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/2e66fdca35341479ccd4f91688c0b81e57538f7b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T22:16:41Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T22:16:41Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"docs: answer the mail-access request — it is live, and three premises were wrong\n\nBuilt and deployed on the hadoku_site side. The endpoint is\nGET /contact/api/mailfeed/{scope,messages}, service tier plus a named\nper-identity sender scope, presented with the KEY_SERVICE_JOBPLATFORM this repo\nalready holds. No mail credential is issued at all, which is stronger than the\nfolder scoping the request asked for.\n\nThree corrections, in order of how much they change the work:\n\n- The sender-domain list would have matched NOTHING. Greenhouse mails from\n  us.greenhouse-mail.io and us.greenhouse-jobs.com; greenhouse.io has sent this\n  mailbox nothing, ever. Every one of the 37 applications went through\n  Greenhouse, so the rule covered 0% of them and would have read as \"Greenhouse\n  never writes to us\" — the same silence the feature exists to detect.\n- Greenhouse sends no confirmations, only SECURITY CODES. Mail from it means\n  the application is blocked pending a code, not that it succeeded — which\n  inverts the request''s premise and gives the two ambiguous Coinbase rows a\n  definite answer: unsent. That is a third state worth a column.\n- hadoku-scraper cannot call this. It is a different identity and gets 403; the\n  key lives in jobplatform-api, which is also where the reconciler belongs\n  since it owns the applications table.\n\nAlso: there is no mail server (MX is Resend/SES inbound → a webhook → D1), so\nthe IMAP folder and Sieve rule were unbuildable; and coinbase.com is\ndeliberately excluded because the operator''s own account mails from the same\ndomain.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1dd4e7bcbaeef16282a84e2ccb807f9090bb7136","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/1dd4e7bcbaeef16282a84e2ccb807f9090bb7136"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/2e66fdca35341479ccd4f91688c0b81e57538f7b","verification":{"payload":"tree 1dd4e7bcbaeef16282a84e2ccb807f9090bb7136\nparent b3458b649101dc0da4a6f6aec282b64c4f9b58a0\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789856201 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789856201 -0700\n\ndocs: answer the mail-access request — it is live, and three premises were wrong\n\nBuilt and deployed on the hadoku_site side. The endpoint is\nGET /contact/api/mailfeed/{scope,messages}, service tier plus a named\nper-identity sender scope, presented with the KEY_SERVICE_JOBPLATFORM this repo\nalready holds. No mail credential is issued at all, which is stronger than the\nfolder scoping the request asked for.\n\nThree corrections, in order of how much they change the work:\n\n- The sender-domain list would have matched NOTHING. Greenhouse mails from\n  us.greenhouse-mail.io and us.greenhouse-jobs.com; greenhouse.io has sent this\n  mailbox nothing, ever. Every one of the 37 applications went through\n  Greenhouse, so the rule covered 0% of them and would have read as \"Greenhouse\n  never writes to us\" — the same silence the feature exists to detect.\n- Greenhouse sends no confirmations, only SECURITY CODES. Mail from it means\n  the application is blocked pending a code, not that it succeeded — which\n  inverts the request''s premise and gives the two ambiguous Coinbase rows a\n  definite answer: unsent. That is a third state worth a column.\n- hadoku-scraper cannot call this. It is a different identity and gets 403; the\n  key lives in jobplatform-api, which is also where the reconciler belongs\n  since it owns the applications table.\n\nAlso: there is no mail server (MX is Resend/SES inbound → a webhook → D1), so\nthe IMAP folder and Sieve rule were unbuildable; and coinbase.com is\ndeliberately excluded because the operator''s own account mails from the same\ndomain.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJHGFHFKABAwJFQPSgBa0OJZlSJa5l6CxTIC3V4a3Kk85oKaMbI6fqwn62ceNdAKc5\nJJR59PWJDZ314TNBRcdAg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T22:16:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/2e66fdca35341479ccd4f91688c0b81e57538f7b","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKDJlNjZmZGNhMzUzNDE0NzljY2Q0ZjkxNjg4YzBiODFlNTc1MzhmN2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/b3458b649101dc0da4a6f6aec282b64c4f9b58a0","sha":"b3458b649101dc0da4a6f6aec282b64c4f9b58a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/b3458b649101dc0da4a6f6aec282b64c4f9b58a0"}],"sha":"2e66fdca35341479ccd4f91688c0b81e57538f7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/2e66fdca35341479ccd4f91688c0b81e57538f7b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/b3458b649101dc0da4a6f6aec282b64c4f9b58a0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T22:09:01Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T22:09:01Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"ci: drop the vibeCompact audit\n\nOperator decision 2026-09-19: vibeCompact does not run against this repo. It\nwas a daily scheduled audit (cron 18 6 * * *) holding contents:write,\nissues:write and pull-requests:write — able to commit, open issues and open PRs\nunattended. Its own comment records the fleet-wide fan-out it caused on\n2026-08-24, which corrupted the shared pnpm stores on claw-2 and claw-3.\n\nThe workflow in WolffM/vibecheck, the tool''s own repo, is untouched.","tree":{"sha":"e958fe402732f6cc56d21b86a359938014a9908c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/e958fe402732f6cc56d21b86a359938014a9908c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/b3458b649101dc0da4a6f6aec282b64c4f9b58a0","verification":{"payload":"tree e958fe402732f6cc56d21b86a359938014a9908c\nparent 8cb857fabaae6e75b0fe9f28c7042fac36a6aad9\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789855741 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789855741 -0700\n\nci: drop the vibeCompact audit\n\nOperator decision 2026-09-19: vibeCompact does not run against this repo. It\nwas a daily scheduled audit (cron 18 6 * * *) holding contents:write,\nissues:write and pull-requests:write — able to commit, open issues and open PRs\nunattended. Its own comment records the fleet-wide fan-out it caused on\n2026-08-24, which corrupted the shared pnpm stores on claw-2 and claw-3.\n\nThe workflow in WolffM/vibecheck, the tool''s own repo, is untouched.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLmEipq4spc2vYsQNfdOdPx1rpx2+/Y6TBk/DDJY+GMzlvF53wIqo5Ps5q+3RnMhdE\nvBjLDRrf5IXVlcWMQRzgM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T22:09:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/b3458b649101dc0da4a6f6aec282b64c4f9b58a0","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKGIzNDU4YjY0OTEwMWRjMGRhNGE2ZjZhZWMyODJiNjRjNGY5YjU4YTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/8cb857fabaae6e75b0fe9f28c7042fac36a6aad9","sha":"8cb857fabaae6e75b0fe9f28c7042fac36a6aad9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/8cb857fabaae6e75b0fe9f28c7042fac36a6aad9"}],"sha":"b3458b649101dc0da4a6f6aec282b64c4f9b58a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/b3458b649101dc0da4a6f6aec282b64c4f9b58a0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/8cb857fabaae6e75b0fe9f28c7042fac36a6aad9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T21:15:22Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T21:15:22Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"docs: hadoku.me is our own mail server, so ask for a folder, not an alias\n\nThe first draft reasoned from an assumption the operator corrected: that\nhadoku.me mail might be Google-hosted. It is our own server, which removes\nthe service-account option and changes the recommendation.\n\nAsking for a new applications@ alias was the wrong shape. It could only ever\ncatch mail arriving AFTER the switch, and it would change the address\nemployers see and reply to — a decision about the job search, made to get\nbetter telemetry.\n\nA dedicated IMAP folder fed by a server-side rule, with a read-only\ncredential scoped to that folder, is better on both counts: it changes\nnothing employers see, and because we run the server, running the rule\nretroactively recovers the history. That backfill is now the most valuable\npart of the request rather than the part the document said was impossible —\nit is the only way to answer \"what have I actually applied to\", which the\nsystem answered wrongly on 2026-09-19.\n\nThe alias keeps one real advantage — mail lands correctly because of the\naddress, not because a pattern matched — so it is recorded as a later\nhardening rather than dropped. A rule miss degrades to today''s behaviour,\nnot to something worse, which is what makes the trade acceptable.\n\nFiled on sender domain rather than subject text: subjects are written by each\nemployer and vary wildly, the sending infrastructure is the ATS''s and is\nstable. Renamed to -mail-access since it is no longer about an alias.","tree":{"sha":"b42ec8535ad1163e509112e24d208c9657d15c98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/b42ec8535ad1163e509112e24d208c9657d15c98"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/8cb857fabaae6e75b0fe9f28c7042fac36a6aad9","verification":{"payload":"tree b42ec8535ad1163e509112e24d208c9657d15c98\nparent 23b29553dbefeece5f7892829df05c308cf34236\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789852522 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789852522 -0700\n\ndocs: hadoku.me is our own mail server, so ask for a folder, not an alias\n\nThe first draft reasoned from an assumption the operator corrected: that\nhadoku.me mail might be Google-hosted. It is our own server, which removes\nthe service-account option and changes the recommendation.\n\nAsking for a new applications@ alias was the wrong shape. It could only ever\ncatch mail arriving AFTER the switch, and it would change the address\nemployers see and reply to — a decision about the job search, made to get\nbetter telemetry.\n\nA dedicated IMAP folder fed by a server-side rule, with a read-only\ncredential scoped to that folder, is better on both counts: it changes\nnothing employers see, and because we run the server, running the rule\nretroactively recovers the history. That backfill is now the most valuable\npart of the request rather than the part the document said was impossible —\nit is the only way to answer \"what have I actually applied to\", which the\nsystem answered wrongly on 2026-09-19.\n\nThe alias keeps one real advantage — mail lands correctly because of the\naddress, not because a pattern matched — so it is recorded as a later\nhardening rather than dropped. A rule miss degrades to today''s behaviour,\nnot to something worse, which is what makes the trade acceptable.\n\nFiled on sender domain rather than subject text: subjects are written by each\nemployer and vary wildly, the sending infrastructure is the ATS''s and is\nstable. Renamed to -mail-access since it is no longer about an alias.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQNjnS5KAgnUiqvb8nBXzEoIibnZyP9xBQifkgX/46orBCwesCXK/oKONGwYyWW4RWR\nctyoKyEMIs6n9xrNOiSQg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T21:15:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/8cb857fabaae6e75b0fe9f28c7042fac36a6aad9","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKDhjYjg1N2ZhYmFhZTZlNzViMGZlOWYyOGM3MDQyZmFjMzZhNmFhZDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/23b29553dbefeece5f7892829df05c308cf34236","sha":"23b29553dbefeece5f7892829df05c308cf34236","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/23b29553dbefeece5f7892829df05c308cf34236"}],"sha":"8cb857fabaae6e75b0fe9f28c7042fac36a6aad9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/8cb857fabaae6e75b0fe9f28c7042fac36a6aad9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/23b29553dbefeece5f7892829df05c308cf34236/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T21:12:10Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T21:12:44Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"docs: request a read-only applications mailbox, so sent/not-sent has a second source\n\nEvery record of whether an application went out is written by the component\nthat sends it. On 2026-09-19 that caught up with us: the queue reported zero\napplications sent while the owner held a Pinecone confirmation for one it had\nno row for. All 37 rows are Greenhouse; Pinecone is Ashby.\n\nTwo more ways the same blind spot shows up, both already in the code:\nGET /applications INNER JOINs jobs, so a row whose job was pruned disappears\nfrom the list; and is_submitted matches confirmation WORDING by regex, so a\nboard that thanks you in unfamiliar phrasing is indistinguishable from a\nsubmit that never happened.\n\nThe ATS confirmation email is the only artefact here not produced by the code\nunder test, which is exactly what makes it worth plumbing in. Asks for\napplications@hadoku.me: applicant address on future applications so\nconfirmations arrive by construction, forwarding to the real inbox so a\nrecruiter never lands somewhere only a robot reads, and a READ-ONLY\nvault-brokered credential — read-only because a checker that could also act\nas the owner is inside the blast radius of the thing it checks.\n\nScoped honestly: this fixes the pipeline going forward and cannot recover\napplications already sent to the old address. Reconstructing those stays a\none-off against the owner''s personal inbox.","tree":{"sha":"8eab5995cb4d86625055f7ae973515cd82ffb8c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/8eab5995cb4d86625055f7ae973515cd82ffb8c6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/23b29553dbefeece5f7892829df05c308cf34236","verification":{"payload":"tree 8eab5995cb4d86625055f7ae973515cd82ffb8c6\nparent 5116e259a9d137a19bf081a864335b659ea6d4ac\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789852330 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789852364 -0700\n\ndocs: request a read-only applications mailbox, so sent/not-sent has a second source\n\nEvery record of whether an application went out is written by the component\nthat sends it. On 2026-09-19 that caught up with us: the queue reported zero\napplications sent while the owner held a Pinecone confirmation for one it had\nno row for. All 37 rows are Greenhouse; Pinecone is Ashby.\n\nTwo more ways the same blind spot shows up, both already in the code:\nGET /applications INNER JOINs jobs, so a row whose job was pruned disappears\nfrom the list; and is_submitted matches confirmation WORDING by regex, so a\nboard that thanks you in unfamiliar phrasing is indistinguishable from a\nsubmit that never happened.\n\nThe ATS confirmation email is the only artefact here not produced by the code\nunder test, which is exactly what makes it worth plumbing in. Asks for\napplications@hadoku.me: applicant address on future applications so\nconfirmations arrive by construction, forwarding to the real inbox so a\nrecruiter never lands somewhere only a robot reads, and a READ-ONLY\nvault-brokered credential — read-only because a checker that could also act\nas the owner is inside the blast radius of the thing it checks.\n\nScoped honestly: this fixes the pipeline going forward and cannot recover\napplications already sent to the old address. Reconstructing those stays a\none-off against the owner''s personal inbox.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJbOcB7QyVf868jxo7PuU6oeLyyklyVT4B1by26MMTMflYDZESQS+JnAbcS2FAeT+l\nuzT/oUVaYBK9rlx6P05wk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T21:12:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/23b29553dbefeece5f7892829df05c308cf34236","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKDIzYjI5NTUzZGJlZmVlY2U1Zjc4OTI4MjlkZjA1YzMwOGNmMzQyMzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/5116e259a9d137a19bf081a864335b659ea6d4ac","sha":"5116e259a9d137a19bf081a864335b659ea6d4ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/5116e259a9d137a19bf081a864335b659ea6d4ac"}],"sha":"23b29553dbefeece5f7892829df05c308cf34236","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/23b29553dbefeece5f7892829df05c308cf34236"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user