epos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/bcd4038f2e3c9988f75bfde4e9b3d5cbd8de8b58","verification":{"payload":"tree 13e3eb78c2f6bd7cbfe3a29c7d334556e1ad9e98\nparent 482bffc2d6d457b3917af459f644652328a94ccd\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788890349 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788890349 -0700\n\ndocs: the feed''s candidate query pins its join order on purpose\n\nA plain INNER JOIN reintroduces the 61,673-row walk, and the rank tests guard\nthe result rather than the plan, so nothing would catch it.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQNvXqJNdn7sWbKJkGScFjW47jO5F4qdPc7QzGpxFBgv+UAZ6+GPByO/1O5N/vuZ6yt\nOAWiO1Bo7YtIAkJuzavAA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T17:59:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/bcd4038f2e3c9988f75bfde4e9b3d5cbd8de8b58","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKGJjZDQwMzhmMmUzYzk5ODhmNzViZmRlNGU5YjNkNWNiZDhkZThiNTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/482bffc2d6d457b3917af459f644652328a94ccd","sha":"482bffc2d6d457b3917af459f644652328a94ccd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/482bffc2d6d457b3917af459f644652328a94ccd"}],"sha":"bcd4038f2e3c9988f75bfde4e9b3d5cbd8de8b58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/bcd4038f2e3c9988f75bfde4e9b3d5cbd8de8b58"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/482bffc2d6d457b3917af459f644652328a94ccd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T17:57:05Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T17:57:05Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"perf(feed): pin the join order so a company-scoped feed reads its slice, not the corpus\n\nThe owner deep-linked one posting and waited seconds for it. GET /jobs/:id is\n~200ms on its own; measured concurrently with the feed the same deep link fires\nbehind it, it was 2.3s and the feed itself 8.1s. One isolate, one thread — the\ndrawer was starved by the dashboard rendering behind it.\n\nThe feed''s own cost was the candidate query. `job_profile_rank` covers every\njob, so with `ORDER BY r.bound DESC` in view SQLite leads with\nidx_job_profile_rank_order and probes jobs + profile_companies per rank row it\nwalks. The owner''s profile is three companies — 953 of 33,103 jobs — so LIMIT\n800 never fills until nearly the whole corpus has been walked: 61,673 rows read,\n1,975ms of SQL, every request. A CTE does not help; the planner leads with the\nrank index inside it too. CROSS JOIN does, because it pins the loop order:\nlead with profile_companies and the same page costs 2,866 rows and 32ms.\n\nSame reordering for the live fallback, which had the same shape.\n\nAlso on the feed: `application_url`, selected in stage 2 for the shortlist only.\nThe card''s Apply now resolves the same `application_url ?? url` the drawer does,\nso the two buttons cannot open different pages.\n\nfeat(feed): Apply straight from the card\n\nOpens the posting in a new tab and marks the job applied, so ripping a feed\ncosts one click per posting instead of card -> drawer -> scroll -> Apply. A real\n<a target=\"_blank\">, not a scripted window.open: the state write is an await,\nand a popup opened after it would be blocked. The mark is optimistic and does\nnot wait for the tab — a failed write says so above the list rather than\nsilently reverting, since the form is open either way.\n\nfeat(drawer): hand a posting to the runner in one click\n\nThe runner''s Apply button was hidden until \"Prepare application\" had minted a\npacket, which read as \"the runner cannot drive this board\" on exactly the\npostings where the tier chip above it says the opposite. It is now always\npresent as \"Hand to runner\", and builds the packet first when there isn''t one.\nprepareApplication() returns the slug rather than leaving it in state, because\nthe queue call happens in the same tick and would read null back.","tree":{"sha":"5c67a940022bf5b348042cf13ed2ee633b11f7b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/5c67a940022bf5b348042cf13ed2ee633b11f7b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/482bffc2d6d457b3917af459f644652328a94ccd","verification":{"payload":"tree 5c67a940022bf5b348042cf13ed2ee633b11f7b1\nparent ee59c531bd9257acf49a789f8e948e2664a02c2a\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788890225 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788890225 -0700\n\nperf(feed): pin the join order so a company-scoped feed reads its slice, not the corpus\n\nThe owner deep-linked one posting and waited seconds for it. GET /jobs/:id is\n~200ms on its own; measured concurrently with the feed the same deep link fires\nbehind it, it was 2.3s and the feed itself 8.1s. One isolate, one thread — the\ndrawer was starved by the dashboard rendering behind it.\n\nThe feed''s own cost was the candidate query. `job_profile_rank` covers every\njob, so with `ORDER BY r.bound DESC` in view SQLite leads with\nidx_job_profile_rank_order and probes jobs + profile_companies per rank row it\nwalks. The owner''s profile is three companies — 953 of 33,103 jobs — so LIMIT\n800 never fills until nearly the whole corpus has been walked: 61,673 rows read,\n1,975ms of SQL, every request. A CTE does not help; the planner leads with the\nrank index inside it too. CROSS JOIN does, because it pins the loop order:\nlead with profile_companies and the same page costs 2,866 rows and 32ms.\n\nSame reordering for the live fallback, which had the same shape.\n\nAlso on the feed: `application_url`, selected in stage 2 for the shortlist only.\nThe card''s Apply now resolves the same `application_url ?? url` the drawer does,\nso the two buttons cannot open different pages.\n\nfeat(feed): Apply straight from the card\n\nOpens the posting in a new tab and marks the job applied, so ripping a feed\ncosts one click per posting instead of card -> drawer -> scroll -> Apply. A real\n<a target=\"_blank\">, not a scripted window.open: the state write is an await,\nand a popup opened after it would be blocked. The mark is optimistic and does\nnot wait for the tab — a failed write says so above the list rather than\nsilently reverting, since the form is open either way.\n\nfeat(drawer): hand a posting to the runner in one click\n\nThe runner''s Apply button was hidden until \"Prepare application\" had minted a\npacket, which read as \"the runner cannot drive this board\" on exactly the\npostings where the tier chip above it says the opposite. It is now always\npresent as \"Hand to runner\", and builds the packet first when there isn''t one.\nprepareApplication() returns the slug rather than leaving it in state, because\nthe queue call happens in the same tick and would read null back.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQDrykOPRgCx+4NaudQLc0yQbtDai4O2eelEBqiGPGYqAdcgnPNV4Z/Xv/wetwR+6eP\nIS3ut6Lqtgply9A3ULzgA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T17:57:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/482bffc2d6d457b3917af459f644652328a94ccd","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKDQ4MmJmZmMyZDZkNDU3YjM5MTdhZjQ1OWY2NDQ2NTIzMjhhOTRjY2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/ee59c531bd9257acf49a789f8e948e2664a02c2a","sha":"ee59c531bd9257acf49a789f8e948e2664a02c2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/ee59c531bd9257acf49a789f8e948e2664a02c2a"}],"sha":"482bffc2d6d457b3917af459f644652328a94ccd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/482bffc2d6d457b3917af459f644652328a94ccd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/ee59c531bd9257acf49a789f8e948e2664a02c2a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T17:42:05Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T17:42:05Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(identity): read ownerName from the query on POSTs too\n\nThe routes split by method: a GET read `?ownerName=`, a POST read it from the\nJSON body. So `POST /jobs/:id/apply?ownerName=Hadoku` was accepted, ignored, and\nqueued the application onto the CALLER''s rows.\n\nNothing in the response says so. It is a 200 carrying a valid-looking\napplication that simply belongs to the wrong person, and the only symptom is\nthe owner''s dashboard staying empty while the runner reports success — which is\nthe exact failure `effectiveUserId` was written to end, one method down. It\ncost a debugging round on 2026-09-07 and three applications queued onto the\nservice account.\n\nRead both in `effectiveUserId` rather than per-route, so no future route can\nreintroduce it, and let the body win where both are given: writing it into the\nbody is the explicit act. Accepting the query grants nothing new — the\nservice-or-admin gate and the resolve-never-trust rule (R5) apply to the value\nwhatever carried it.\n\n`ownerName` is now declared once as a shared query schema and used by all four\nroutes that honour it, so the OpenAPI documents the query half everywhere\ninstead of only on the GETs.\n\nAlso declares `ExecutionContext` for the tests eslint config. It is a type, not\na value, and `no-undef` cannot tell the difference in TS — `npm run lint` in\nworker/ was failing on main because of it.\n\nThree of the four new tests fail without this change; the fourth guards the\nbody-wins precedence and passes either way.","tree":{"sha":"315575a4f3b1aa1832c5af1a26e2158099aa0d41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/315575a4f3b1aa1832c5af1a26e2158099aa0d41"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/ee59c531bd9257acf49a789f8e948e2664a02c2a","verification":{"payload":"tree 315575a4f3b1aa1832c5af1a26e2158099aa0d41\nparent 69fd020a2440d8dc1abc30cebfd9037b65b5b56b\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788889325 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788889325 -0700\n\nfix(identity): read ownerName from the query on POSTs too\n\nThe routes split by method: a GET read `?ownerName=`, a POST read it from the\nJSON body. So `POST /jobs/:id/apply?ownerName=Hadoku` was accepted, ignored, and\nqueued the application onto the CALLER''s rows.\n\nNothing in the response says so. It is a 200 carrying a valid-looking\napplication that simply belongs to the wrong person, and the only symptom is\nthe owner''s dashboard staying empty while the runner reports success — which is\nthe exact failure `effectiveUserId` was written to end, one method down. It\ncost a debugging round on 2026-09-07 and three applications queued onto the\nservice account.\n\nRead both in `effectiveUserId` rather than per-route, so no future route can\nreintroduce it, and let the body win where both are given: writing it into the\nbody is the explicit act. Accepting the query grants nothing new — the\nservice-or-admin gate and the resolve-never-trust rule (R5) apply to the value\nwhatever carried it.\n\n`ownerName` is now declared once as a shared query schema and used by all four\nroutes that honour it, so the OpenAPI documents the query half everywhere\ninstead of only on the GETs.\n\nAlso declares `ExecutionContext` for the tests eslint config. It is a type, not\na value, and `no-undef` cannot tell the difference in TS — `npm run lint` in\nworker/ was failing on main because of it.\n\nThree of the four new tests fail without this change; the fourth guards the\nbody-wins precedence and passes either way.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQH3Kl1CsWNlnjccIviuwg/PFKPfjuD/37QINa+vkoRdP7aSfjjwjoSxcsHQ16bQ3Ci\n0/cnIOSJMoLB3hyYSEQAA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T17:42:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/ee59c531bd9257acf49a789f8e948e2664a02c2a","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKGVlNTljNTMxYmQ5MjU3YWNmNDlhNzg5ZjhlOTQ4ZTI2NjRhMDJjMmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/69fd020a2440d8dc1abc30cebfd9037b65b5b56b","sha":"69fd020a2440d8dc1abc30cebfd9037b65b5b56b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/69fd020a2440d8dc1abc30cebfd9037b65b5b56b"}],"sha":"ee59c531bd9257acf49a789f8e948e2664a02c2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/ee59c531bd9257acf49a789f8e948e2664a02c2a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/69fd020a2440d8dc1abc30cebfd9037b65b5b56b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T22:01:10Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T22:01:10Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"ci: staggered vibeCompact schedule, non-fatal alert-close tidy-up (P6.6, P6.7)\n\nvibeCompact: restore the daily schedule disabled 2026-08-24, on :03 instead of the verbatim :00 line that caused the fleet-wide fan-out.\n\nupdate-wolffm: continue-on-error on ''Close alert issue on recovery'' so a transient gh-issue-close failure (tidy-up) can''t flip a genuinely green @wolffm update to red and page @here.","tree":{"sha":"f1a0d6432e40b2a6150cbfffdf9c12114c4d0833","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/f1a0d6432e40b2a6150cbfffdf9c12114c4d0833"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/69fd020a2440d8dc1abc30cebfd9037b65b5b56b","verification":{"payload":"tree f1a0d6432e40b2a6150cbfffdf9c12114c4d0833\nparent fd285b579fccf611e20b942f6a1c278ef3bf6bd5\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788818470 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788818470 -0700\n\nci: staggered vibeCompact schedule, non-fatal alert-close tidy-up (P6.6, P6.7)\n\nvibeCompact: restore the daily schedule disabled 2026-08-24, on :03 instead of the verbatim :00 line that caused the fleet-wide fan-out.\n\nupdate-wolffm: continue-on-error on ''Close alert issue on recovery'' so a transient gh-issue-close failure (tidy-up) can''t flip a genuinely green @wolffm update to red and page @here.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQOMExpJNLOKzV+akchjphYkKxwn9kaisscmVjmNkLKXRRn8ojaeiTiLfPUbp5cYFse\nLdosnu/WiGpARl2h7CogU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T22:01:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/69fd020a2440d8dc1abc30cebfd9037b65b5b56b","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKDY5ZmQwMjBhMjQ0MGQ4ZGMxYWJjMzBjZWJmZDkwMzdiNjViNWI1NmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/fd285b579fccf611e20b942f6a1c278ef3bf6bd5","sha":"fd285b579fccf611e20b942f6a1c278ef3bf6bd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/fd285b579fccf611e20b942f6a1c278ef3bf6bd5"}],"sha":"69fd020a2440d8dc1abc30cebfd9037b65b5b56b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/69fd020a2440d8dc1abc30cebfd9037b65b5b56b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/fd285b579fccf611e20b942f6a1c278ef3bf6bd5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T05:57:39Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T05:57:39Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"test(ci): assert the pre-commit hook stands down in CI\n\nThe hook firing on a CI runner broke the @wolffm auto-update workflow: its\ncommit step fired the hook, whose typecheck triggers a `pnpm install` with no\nNODE_AUTH_TOKEN in that step, so the commit died on ERR_PNPM_FETCH_401. The\nguard that fixed it was only ever verified by hand, because the failure needs\nthat workflow to actually have something to commit — rare enough that watching\nfor it is not verification.\n\nscripts/check-husky-ci-guard.sh runs the real hook under CI conditions and\nchecks four things: CI=true exits 0 and says why, GITHUB_ACTIONS alone is\nenough, standing down is CONDITIONAL (so a guard that skips for everyone fails\ntoo), and no backticks hide inside a double-quoted string — that last one is\nhow the hook came to run `--no-verify` and print its own advice with a hole in\nit. It does not run the hook outside CI, because that would bump versions and\nrewrite the lockfile; it asserts on the file instead.\n\nVerified by breaking it three ways: removing the guard, making it\nunconditional, and reintroducing the backticks. Each fails, with exit 1.\n\nTwo supporting fixes. The scope filter did not watch .husky/, so a change to\nthe hook did not even run CI — added. And the comment at the top of this file\nstill said the hook \"never ran there either\", which stopped being true when\ncore.hooksPath moved to the tracked .husky and is precisely why this broke;\nit now says so.","tree":{"sha":"13abd0685de2eace1463f36b22fdd79fb0b41506","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/13abd0685de2eace1463f36b22fdd79fb0b41506"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/fd285b579fccf611e20b942f6a1c278ef3bf6bd5","verification":{"payload":"tree 13abd0685de2eace1463f36b22fdd79fb0b41506\nparent 1cabbbcef7362c7d5875ec50b77a033912637f46\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788760659 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788760659 -0700\n\ntest(ci): assert the pre-commit hook stands down in CI\n\nThe hook firing on a CI runner broke the @wolffm auto-update workflow: its\ncommit step fired the hook, whose typecheck triggers a `pnpm install` with no\nNODE_AUTH_TOKEN in that step, so the commit died on ERR_PNPM_FETCH_401. The\nguard that fixed it was only ever verified by hand, because the failure needs\nthat workflow to actually have something to commit — rare enough that watching\nfor it is not verification.\n\nscripts/check-husky-ci-guard.sh runs the real hook under CI conditions and\nchecks four things: CI=true exits 0 and says why, GITHUB_ACTIONS alone is\nenough, standing down is CONDITIONAL (so a guard that skips for everyone fails\ntoo), and no backticks hide inside a double-quoted string — that last one is\nhow the hook came to run `--no-verify` and print its own advice with a hole in\nit. It does not run the hook outside CI, because that would bump versions and\nrewrite the lockfile; it asserts on the file instead.\n\nVerified by breaking it three ways: removing the guard, making it\nunconditional, and reintroducing the backticks. Each fails, with exit 1.\n\nTwo supporting fixes. The scope filter did not watch .husky/, so a change to\nthe hook did not even run CI — added. And the comment at the top of this file\nstill said the hook \"never ran there either\", which stopped being true when\ncore.hooksPath moved to the tracked .husky and is precisely why this broke;\nit now says so.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQOyRsW6VDl8Or0BGh76vweDdFeX/ZvrrQrn+dUx8TcPN3dxS1dCSUKYtc4lcuxl1E/\nHgIBkJQFmodF0Smg/Qzwc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T05:58:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/fd285b579fccf611e20b942f6a1c278ef3bf6bd5","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKGZkMjg1YjU3OWZjY2Y2MTFlMjBiOTQyZjZhMWMyNzhlZjNiZjZiZDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/1cabbbcef7362c7d5875ec50b77a033912637f46","sha":"1cabbbcef7362c7d5875ec50b77a033912637f46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/1cabbbcef7362c7d5875ec50b77a033912637f46"}],"sha":"fd285b579fccf611e20b942f6a1c278ef3bf6bd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/fd285b579fccf611e20b942f6a1c278ef3bf6bd5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/1cabbbcef7362c7d5875ec50b77a033912637f46/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T02:30:10Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T02:30:10Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix: the profile routes'' on-behalf-of parameter is `ownerName`\n\nAdded with the old spelling `owner`, after 54903fd had already renamed it\neverywhere else. Hono hands an undeclared query key to nobody, so the route\nsilently ignored it, fell back to the CALLER''s own rows, and returned 200 — a\nservice asking for the owner''s profiles got its own empty ones and no\nindication anything was wrong.\n\nThat is the second time today this exact shape has cost real time: the runner\nwas sending `owner` to /applications for the same reason, and the empty result\nwas read as evidence of a duplicate registry name rather than a typo.\n\nA parameter that decides WHOSE data comes back must not fail by returning\nsomebody else''s. The added test asserts the stale spelling does NOT act on\nbehalf of anyone, so the next rename breaks a test rather than a production\nread.","tree":{"sha":"6594939e9433c656a77cec8cae2e3b40783492fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/6594939e9433c656a77cec8cae2e3b40783492fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/1cabbbcef7362c7d5875ec50b77a033912637f46","verification":{"payload":"tree 6594939e9433c656a77cec8cae2e3b40783492fe\nparent 17643dce7984ffa627d8f98e448dc6887c49dd45\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788748210 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788748210 -0700\n\nfix: the profile routes'' on-behalf-of parameter is `ownerName`\n\nAdded with the old spelling `owner`, after 54903fd had already renamed it\neverywhere else. Hono hands an undeclared query key to nobody, so the route\nsilently ignored it, fell back to the CALLER''s own rows, and returned 200 — a\nservice asking for the owner''s profiles got its own empty ones and no\nindication anything was wrong.\n\nThat is the second time today this exact shape has cost real time: the runner\nwas sending `owner` to /applications for the same reason, and the empty result\nwas read as evidence of a duplicate registry name rather than a typo.\n\nA parameter that decides WHOSE data comes back must not fail by returning\nsomebody else''s. The added test asserts the stale spelling does NOT act on\nbehalf of anyone, so the next rename breaks a test rather than a production\nread.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQGE8aG5Bv+aipvUO+gUohxVLQiF4P1oQKqWO0cD3FV0PRQJrsUgDXIvqpc4f5RIEWg\ngN4emlgcsG6YNox0WqMQM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T02:30:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/1cabbbcef7362c7d5875ec50b77a033912637f46","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKDFjYWJiYmNlZjczNjJjN2Q1ODc1ZWM1MGI3N2EwMzM5MTI2MzdmNDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/17643dce7984ffa627d8f98e448dc6887c49dd45","sha":"17643dce7984ffa627d8f98e448dc6887c49dd45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/17643dce7984ffa627d8f98e448dc6887c49dd45"}],"sha":"1cabbbcef7362c7d5875ec50b77a033912637f46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/1cabbbcef7362c7d5875ec50b77a033912637f46"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/17643dce7984ffa627d8f98e448dc6887c49dd45/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T22:11:02Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T22:11:02Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"revert: the commit step no longer runs the hook, so its token is dead config\n\nReverts 4e7399d. That commit gave \"Commit and push if changed\" a\nNODE_AUTH_TOKEN so the pre-commit hook could authenticate its pnpm install.\n1f61c63 landed concurrently and fixed the same 401 at the root instead: the\nhook now exits early under CI, because every gate it runs is already a CI job\nand publish.yml has its own version-bump fallback.\n\nSo the env var is never read, and worse, the comment justifying it now states\nthe opposite of what happens — it opens \"THE COMMIT RUNS THE PRE-COMMIT HOOK\",\nwhich is exactly what 1f61c63 stopped. A comment that explains a mechanism the\ncode no longer has is how the next reader gets misled.","tree":{"sha":"7dde3092e6afa7bc6bba7d9403136c19cb5c66c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/7dde3092e6afa7bc6bba7d9403136c19cb5c66c6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/17643dce7984ffa627d8f98e448dc6887c49dd45","verification":{"payload":"tree 7dde3092e6afa7bc6bba7d9403136c19cb5c66c6\nparent 5bc0167744e80dd2f2643433857556e82e45b51c\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788646262 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788646262 -0700\n\nrevert: the commit step no longer runs the hook, so its token is dead config\n\nReverts 4e7399d. That commit gave \"Commit and push if changed\" a\nNODE_AUTH_TOKEN so the pre-commit hook could authenticate its pnpm install.\n1f61c63 landed concurrently and fixed the same 401 at the root instead: the\nhook now exits early under CI, because every gate it runs is already a CI job\nand publish.yml has its own version-bump fallback.\n\nSo the env var is never read, and worse, the comment justifying it now states\nthe opposite of what happens — it opens \"THE COMMIT RUNS THE PRE-COMMIT HOOK\",\nwhich is exactly what 1f61c63 stopped. A comment that explains a mechanism the\ncode no longer has is how the next reader gets misled.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQCl+rH6OU9evskBk4shMecLT28fLEvEGv7tdNNmHMicAip6P7sR9FAwZYkx0sAusxh\n1qao1/KJWsIWsKjsY/1QE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-05T22:11:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/17643dce7984ffa627d8f98e448dc6887c49dd45","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKDE3NjQzZGNlNzk4NGZmYTYyN2Q4Zjk4ZTQ0OGRjNjg4N2M0OWRkNDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/5bc0167744e80dd2f2643433857556e82e45b51c","sha":"5bc0167744e80dd2f2643433857556e82e45b51c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/5bc0167744e80dd2f2643433857556e82e45b51c"}],"sha":"17643dce7984ffa627d8f98e448dc6887c49dd45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/17643dce7984ffa627d8f98e448dc6887c49dd45"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/5bc0167744e80dd2f2643433857556e82e45b51c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T22:09:19Z","email":"github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T22:09:19Z","email":"github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"message":"chore: auto-update @wolffm/* to latest","tree":{"sha":"944768b0a39f7be64aca8b20991351ca213a6440","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/944768b0a39f7be64aca8b20991351ca213a6440"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/5bc0167744e80dd2f2643433857556e82e45b51c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/5bc0167744e80dd2f2643433857556e82e45b51c","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKDViYzAxNjc3NDRlODBkZDJmMjY0MzQzMzg1NzU1NmU4MmU0NWI1MWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/4e7399dbbfec90e8e3f1c4aed19288de9cccddf5","sha":"4e7399dbbfec90e8e3f1c4aed19288de9cccddf5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/4e7399dbbfec90e8e3f1c4aed19288de9cccddf5"}],"sha":"5bc0167744e80dd2f2643433857556e82e45b51c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/5bc0167744e80dd2f2643433857556e82e45b51c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/4e7399dbbfec90e8e3f1c4aed19288de9cccddf5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T22:08:20Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T22:08:20Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(ci): the commit step runs the pre-commit hook, so it needs the registry token\n\nThe pre-commit hook shells out to `pnpm install --lockfile-only` and\n`pnpm run typecheck`, both of which read npm.pkg.github.com. The commit step\nset no NODE_AUTH_TOKEN, so setup-node''s .npmrc resolved ${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN} to\nits own placeholder literal and the fetch answered 401:\n\n  [ERR_PNPM_FETCH_401] GET https://npm.pkg.github.com/download/@wolffm/prefs-client/1.0.12/…\n\nIt stayed green for months because the \"Update @wolffm/* to latest\" step above\ninstalls WITH the token, leaving the store warm enough that the hook''s install\nnever had to fetch. It breaks on the one package not in the store yet — a\nversion published minutes earlier, which is precisely what this workflow exists\nto pick up. Every prior run either had nothing to commit (the early exit) or\nfound everything cached.\n\nThe two steps that already set this use the same secret; this is the third.","tree":{"sha":"b89a846e86fa9241b2e5149772504989eb71a591","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/b89a846e86fa9241b2e5149772504989eb71a591"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/4e7399dbbfec90e8e3f1c4aed19288de9cccddf5","verification":{"payload":"tree b89a846e86fa9241b2e5149772504989eb71a591\nparent 1f61c63c85e3d960a9564596f1e581eeb670a549\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788646100 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788646100 -0700\n\nfix(ci): the commit step runs the pre-commit hook, so it needs the registry token\n\nThe pre-commit hook shells out to `pnpm install --lockfile-only` and\n`pnpm run typecheck`, both of which read npm.pkg.github.com. The commit step\nset no NODE_AUTH_TOKEN, so setup-node''s .npmrc resolved ${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN} to\nits own placeholder literal and the fetch answered 401:\n\n  [ERR_PNPM_FETCH_401] GET https://npm.pkg.github.com/download/@wolffm/prefs-client/1.0.12/…\n\nIt stayed green for months because the \"Update @wolffm/* to latest\" step above\ninstalls WITH the token, leaving the store warm enough that the hook''s install\nnever had to fetch. It breaks on the one package not in the store yet — a\nversion published minutes earlier, which is precisely what this workflow exists\nto pick up. Every prior run either had nothing to commit (the early exit) or\nfound everything cached.\n\nThe two steps that already set this use the same secret; this is the third.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQE8RYYufCPTewrP7Ue2I7Iv8VD8BVoj9irJ0rAtE8etMvCdkArd6+pC5RN7xpage/0\n7aRkDcbujgo7ngEfRxRQE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-05T22:08:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/4e7399dbbfec90e8e3f1c4aed19288de9cccddf5","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKDRlNzM5OWRiYmZlYzkwZThlM2YxYzRhZWQxOTI4OGRlOWNjY2RkZjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/1f61c63c85e3d960a9564596f1e581eeb670a549","sha":"1f61c63c85e3d960a9564596f1e581eeb670a549","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/1f61c63c85e3d960a9564596f1e581eeb670a549"}],"sha":"4e7399dbbfec90e8e3f1c4aed19288de9cccddf5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/4e7399dbbfec90e8e3f1c4aed19288de9cccddf5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/1f61c63c85e3d960a9564596f1e581eeb670a549/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T22:06:50Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T22:06:50Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(husky): the hook ran in CI, and its own error message ran a command\n\nTwo defects, both visible in the same failed run of the @wolffm auto-update\nworkflow''s \"Commit and push if changed\" step.\n\nThe hook fired in CI at all. Its typecheck triggers a `pnpm install`, and that\nstep has no NODE_AUTH_TOKEN, so it died on ERR_PNPM_FETCH_401 fetching a\nprivate @wolffm package — a dependency-update commit failing on the registry\nauth of a gate CI had already run as its own job. Nothing here is load-bearing\nin CI: ci.yml typechecks separately, and publish.yml has its own version-bump\nfallback that walks to an unpublished version. So it now exits early on CI /\nGITHUB_ACTIONS, alongside the HUSKY=0 escape that was already there.\n\nAnd the failure message was itself a bug:\n\n    echo \"… (or `--no-verify` to bypass).\"\n\nBackticks inside a double-quoted string are command substitution, so the shell\nran `--no-verify`, printed `.husky/pre-commit: 1: --no-verify: not found`, and\nrendered the advice with a hole in it — while the hook was reporting someone\nelse''s error. Single-quoted now, so it says what it means.\n\nVerified by running the old line and the new one side by side, and the hook\nunder CI=true, GITHUB_ACTIONS=true, and neither.","tree":{"sha":"0eff89259948805406a393fa6f6c0ec28377cd96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/0eff89259948805406a393fa6f6c0ec28377cd96"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/1f61c63c85e3d960a9564596f1e581eeb670a549","verification":{"payload":"tree 0eff89259948805406a393fa6f6c0ec28377cd96\nparent d20e142f059e6cdad75d541942f19cf6aa8c616e\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788646010 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788646010 -0700\n\nfix(husky): the hook ran in CI, and its own error message ran a command\n\nTwo defects, both visible in the same failed run of the @wolffm auto-update\nworkflow''s \"Commit and push if changed\" step.\n\nThe hook fired in CI at all. Its typecheck triggers a `pnpm install`, and that\nstep has no NODE_AUTH_TOKEN, so it died on ERR_PNPM_FETCH_401 fetching a\nprivate @wolffm package — a dependency-update commit failing on the registry\nauth of a gate CI had already run as its own job. Nothing here is load-bearing\nin CI: ci.yml typechecks separately, and publish.yml has its own version-bump\nfallback that walks to an unpublished version. So it now exits early on CI /\nGITHUB_ACTIONS, alongside the HUSKY=0 escape that was already there.\n\nAnd the failure message was itself a bug:\n\n    echo \"… (or `--no-verify` to bypass).\"\n\nBackticks inside a double-quoted string are command substitution, so the shell\nran `--no-verify`, printed `.husky/pre-commit: 1: --no-verify: not found`, and\nrendered the advice with a hole in it — while the hook was reporting someone\nelse''s error. Single-quoted now, so it says what it means.\n\nVerified by running the old line and the new one side by side, and the hook\nunder CI=true, GITHUB_ACTIONS=true, and neither.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLcp1eNloQ3T/OHoSf4/Z1K0PpILx84VeH41QOYrTUAHzMpF1jTTC6hAniF0BU5aLb\nBQI5HwOEpw55S26Oj/+gc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-05T22:07:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/1f61c63c85e3d960a9564596f1e581eeb670a549","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKDFmNjFjNjNjODVlM2Q5NjBhOTU2NDU5NmYxZTU4MWVlYjY3MGE1NDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/d20e142f059e6cdad75d541942f19cf6aa8c616e","sha":"d20e142f059e6cdad75d541942f19cf6aa8c616e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/d20e142f059e6cdad75d541942f19cf6aa8c616e"}],"sha":"1f61c63c85e3d960a9564596f1e581eeb670a549","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/1f61c63c85e3d960a9564596f1e581eeb670a549"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/d20e142f059e6cdad75d541942f19cf6aa8c616e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T21:27:31Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T21:27:31Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix: dropping background work is now loud instead of silent\n\ntriggerSearchBg — the scrape kicked when a company or keyword is added — did\nnothing at all until yesterday''s ExecutionContext fix. It could not have been\nnoticed, because of the shape it was written in:\n\n    try { c.executionCtx?.waitUntil(work); } catch { void work; }\n\nHono THROWS from that getter when the runtime supplied no context, which is\nwhat happens the moment a host forwards (request, env) and drops the third\nargument. The catch turned a broken deployment into an invisible one: the\nrequest still returned 200, the work never ran, nothing was logged. The rank\nbuild I added a day earlier had inherited the same shape.\n\nBoth now go through runAfterResponse, which reports a missing context as an\nerror naming the task that was dropped, and hints at the cause — a host that\nmust forward ctx. The work is still started, since best-effort beats nothing\nwhere the runtime allows it, but it is no longer mistaken for success. Failures\ninside the work are logged with the task name too, and the promise handed to\nwaitUntil is the guarded one, so a rejection cannot take the invocation down.\n\nFour unit tests, the important one being that a context which throws produces a\nloud complaint rather than a shrug. That is the test that would have caught\nthis in the first place.\n\nAlso settles pending waitUntil work before disposing the harness. A rank build\noutliving its test hit a Miniflare stub that had already been torn down and\nlogged a failure with nothing to do with the code under test.","tree":{"sha":"3a352e0109310506e8b4bd02f8e67b71f31884fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/3a352e0109310506e8b4bd02f8e67b71f31884fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/d20e142f059e6cdad75d541942f19cf6aa8c616e","verification":{"payload":"tree 3a352e0109310506e8b4bd02f8e67b71f31884fd\nparent 1154308fae50a800140c5323f53fbbe8ff22cdcd\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788643651 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788643651 -0700\n\nfix: dropping background work is now loud instead of silent\n\ntriggerSearchBg — the scrape kicked when a company or keyword is added — did\nnothing at all until yesterday''s ExecutionContext fix. It could not have been\nnoticed, because of the shape it was written in:\n\n    try { c.executionCtx?.waitUntil(work); } catch { void work; }\n\nHono THROWS from that getter when the runtime supplied no context, which is\nwhat happens the moment a host forwards (request, env) and drops the third\nargument. The catch turned a broken deployment into an invisible one: the\nrequest still returned 200, the work never ran, nothing was logged. The rank\nbuild I added a day earlier had inherited the same shape.\n\nBoth now go through runAfterResponse, which reports a missing context as an\nerror naming the task that was dropped, and hints at the cause — a host that\nmust forward ctx. The work is still started, since best-effort beats nothing\nwhere the runtime allows it, but it is no longer mistaken for success. Failures\ninside the work are logged with the task name too, and the promise handed to\nwaitUntil is the guarded one, so a rejection cannot take the invocation down.\n\nFour unit tests, the important one being that a context which throws produces a\nloud complaint rather than a shrug. That is the test that would have caught\nthis in the first place.\n\nAlso settles pending waitUntil work before disposing the harness. A rank build\noutliving its test hit a Miniflare stub that had already been torn down and\nlogged a failure with nothing to do with the code under test.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQOKckG+nlceKqrZdpkDZ6jdrPAjQXOt8CZeuSK8rJkxFerATtqSetf4iwQHw49368C\n7Ax73Jd9u4epDnl6FPDwc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-05T21:27:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/d20e142f059e6cdad75d541942f19cf6aa8c616e","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKGQyMGUxNDJmMDU5ZTZjZGFkNzVkNTQxOTQyZjE5Y2Y2YWE4YzYxNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/1154308fae50a800140c5323f53fbbe8ff22cdcd","sha":"1154308fae50a800140c5323f53fbbe8ff22cdcd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/1154308fae50a800140c5323f53fbbe8ff22cdcd"}],"sha":"d20e142f059e6cdad75d541942f19cf6aa8c616e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/d20e142f059e6cdad75d541942f19cf6aa8c616e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/1154308fae50a800140c5323f53fbbe8ff22cdcd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T21:21:51Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T21:22:06Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat: profile routes accept ?owner, so a service can reach the rows that drive scraping\n\nThe directives that decide WHAT GETS SCRAPED are `SELECT DISTINCT ats, slug\nFROM profile_companies`. Four of those rows hold a hostname guess —\n''pinterestcareers'' for the board ''pinterest'', and the same for datadoghq,\ntoasttab and withwaymo — so the orchestrator asks for a slug whose board 404s,\nthat target auto-disabled, and the real board sits active and never requested.\nDatadog, Pinterest, Toast and Waymo have not been scraped since 2026-08-20\nwhile every run reported success.\n\nRepointing them means writing to the owner''s rows from a service caller, and\nthese routes were scoped to the caller with no way to name anyone.\n\nResolved in `requireIdentity` rather than in `currentUserId`. The middleware is\nalready the layer that returns responses; doing it in the helper seven routes\ncall would mean throwing, and an identity refusal would surface as a 500\ninstead of the 403/404/409/503 it is. The resolved userId is stashed on the\ncontext and `currentUserId` prefers it, so all seven call sites are covered\nwithout touching one of them.\n\nSERVICE OR ADMIN ONLY. A friend-tier caller is a signed-in human in a browser;\nletting one pass a name would make every profile route a way to read and edit\nsomeone else''s companies and scoring — and through the directives, what the\nwhole fleet scrapes. An unknown name is 404 and never a silent fallback to the\ncaller.","tree":{"sha":"29ff22358b824b9da32a1a957718e5bef3e48bf0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/29ff22358b824b9da32a1a957718e5bef3e48bf0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/1154308fae50a800140c5323f53fbbe8ff22cdcd","verification":{"payload":"tree 29ff22358b824b9da32a1a957718e5bef3e48bf0\nparent e25c9eba1175610bdd7680cf1df070a958f169b8\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788643311 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788643326 -0700\n\nfeat: profile routes accept ?owner, so a service can reach the rows that drive scraping\n\nThe directives that decide WHAT GETS SCRAPED are `SELECT DISTINCT ats, slug\nFROM profile_companies`. Four of those rows hold a hostname guess —\n''pinterestcareers'' for the board ''pinterest'', and the same for datadoghq,\ntoasttab and withwaymo — so the orchestrator asks for a slug whose board 404s,\nthat target auto-disabled, and the real board sits active and never requested.\nDatadog, Pinterest, Toast and Waymo have not been scraped since 2026-08-20\nwhile every run reported success.\n\nRepointing them means writing to the owner''s rows from a service caller, and\nthese routes were scoped to the caller with no way to name anyone.\n\nResolved in `requireIdentity` rather than in `currentUserId`. The middleware is\nalready the layer that returns responses; doing it in the helper seven routes\ncall would mean throwing, and an identity refusal would surface as a 500\ninstead of the 403/404/409/503 it is. The resolved userId is stashed on the\ncontext and `currentUserId` prefers it, so all seven call sites are covered\nwithout touching one of them.\n\nSERVICE OR ADMIN ONLY. A friend-tier caller is a signed-in human in a browser;\nletting one pass a name would make every profile route a way to read and edit\nsomeone else''s companies and scoring — and through the directives, what the\nwhole fleet scrapes. An unknown name is 404 and never a silent fallback to the\ncaller.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQDPG25WiuyiIgPfBa/hlM/4X4yU0xPxS674XeOVGKSzuXVngQNoeds925aD/UAjYnI\nAW+INJADOLtmUh34LDkQY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-05T21:22:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/1154308fae50a800140c5323f53fbbe8ff22cdcd","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKDExNTQzMDhmYWU1MGE4MDAxNDBjNTMyM2Y1M2ZiYmU4ZmYyMmNkY2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/e25c9eba1175610bdd7680cf1df070a958f169b8","sha":"e25c9eba1175610bdd7680cf1df070a958f169b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/e25c9eba1175610bdd7680cf1df070a958f169b8"}],"sha":"1154308fae50a800140c5323f53fbbe8ff22cdcd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/1154308fae50a800140c5323f53fbbe8ff22cdcd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/e25c9eba1175610bdd7680cf1df070a958f169b8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T21:12:20Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T21:12:20Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix: background work was being dropped, and the tests could not tell\n\ncreateFetchHandler called app.fetch(request, env) with no ExecutionContext, so\nevery `c.executionCtx?.waitUntil()` in this worker threw and the work behind it\nwas left unattached — which on Workers means killed the moment the response\nreturns. Not a degraded mode: the request succeeds and the work silently never\nhappens. The feed''s lazy rank build did nothing in production, and neither, for\nhowever long, has triggerSearchBg''s \"kick a scrape when a directive is added\".\n\nFound by checking production rather than trusting the suite: I cleared a\nprofile''s ranking, hit the feed, and it never came back.\n\nThe suite could not have caught it, which is the more important half. The\nharness also omitted the ExecutionContext, so the same throw happened there —\nbut node runs an unattached promise to completion, so the work DID occur and a\ntest that polled for its effect passed. Green for a reason that does not hold\nin production.\n\nSo the harness now passes a real ExecutionContext and collects what is handed\nto it, and `h.settle()` returns how many there were. The rank tests assert that\ncount is non-zero: they check the work was BACKGROUNDED, not merely that it\neventually happened, which is the distinction that decides whether it runs at\nall on Workers.\n\nTwo things fell out of the harness finally having a context, both worth having:\nthe tests were pointed at the real scraper (SCRAPER_BASE_URL now loopbacks to a\nclosed port, so a profile write cannot POST to production), and one test raced\nits own background build by deleting a job mid-insert. Production survives that\nrace — the build fails, the marker is not set, the feed falls back and the next\nrequest retries — but a test should not assert through it.\n\nThe host worker in hadoku_site has to pass ctx too; `ctx` is optional here only\nso it keeps compiling in the meantime.","tree":{"sha":"2c45d2639bf5d3342fa1ab71999004f8bc431974","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/2c45d2639bf5d3342fa1ab71999004f8bc431974"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/e25c9eba1175610bdd7680cf1df070a958f169b8","verification":{"payload":"tree 2c45d2639bf5d3342fa1ab71999004f8bc431974\nparent 641e99c2ae308db4755eeb7764d8d37450ff39a4\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788642740 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788642740 -0700\n\nfix: background work was being dropped, and the tests could not tell\n\ncreateFetchHandler called app.fetch(request, env) with no ExecutionContext, so\nevery `c.executionCtx?.waitUntil()` in this worker threw and the work behind it\nwas left unattached — which on Workers means killed the moment the response\nreturns. Not a degraded mode: the request succeeds and the work silently never\nhappens. The feed''s lazy rank build did nothing in production, and neither, for\nhowever long, has triggerSearchBg''s \"kick a scrape when a directive is added\".\n\nFound by checking production rather than trusting the suite: I cleared a\nprofile''s ranking, hit the feed, and it never came back.\n\nThe suite could not have caught it, which is the more important half. The\nharness also omitted the ExecutionContext, so the same throw happened there —\nbut node runs an unattached promise to completion, so the work DID occur and a\ntest that polled for its effect passed. Green for a reason that does not hold\nin production.\n\nSo the harness now passes a real ExecutionContext and collects what is handed\nto it, and `h.settle()` returns how many there were. The rank tests assert that\ncount is non-zero: they check the work was BACKGROUNDED, not merely that it\neventually happened, which is the distinction that decides whether it runs at\nall on Workers.\n\nTwo things fell out of the harness finally having a context, both worth having:\nthe tests were pointed at the real scraper (SCRAPER_BASE_URL now loopbacks to a\nclosed port, so a profile write cannot POST to production), and one test raced\nits own background build by deleting a job mid-insert. Production survives that\nrace — the build fails, the marker is not set, the feed falls back and the next\nrequest retries — but a test should not assert through it.\n\nThe host worker in hadoku_site has to pass ctx too; `ctx` is optional here only\nso it keeps compiling in the meantime.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQMi8n5pa0dM1NgoyUnO/kujXCjGzIwzjOyxUE0ubtJuF8pbw9z326cEEiQC+ezlLWn\nWZ9rmAz7MtM5yDrRuQpQ0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-05T21:12:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/e25c9eba1175610bdd7680cf1df070a958f169b8","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKGUyNWM5ZWJhMTE3NTYxMGJkZDc2ODBjZjFkZjA3MGE5NThmMTY5Yjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/641e99c2ae308db4755eeb7764d8d37450ff39a4","sha":"641e99c2ae308db4755eeb7764d8d37450ff39a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/641e99c2ae308db4755eeb7764d8d37450ff39a4"}],"sha":"e25c9eba1175610bdd7680cf1df070a958f169b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/e25c9eba1175610bdd7680cf1df070a958f169b8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/641e99c2ae308db4755eeb7764d8d37450ff39a4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T20:56:49Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T20:57:04Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat: the feed''s ranking installs itself, on use rather than on existence\n\nThe precomputed ranking only appeared when someone remembered to POST\n/ingest/rebuild-rank, so a profile created today used the slow path forever and\nnothing said so. The obvious fix — build it when a profile is created — is\nwrong here, and worth writing down: ensureDefaultProfile materialises a Default\nfor every identity that so much as calls GET /profiles, so \"build on create\"\nmeans every service key, test credential and one-off probe triggers a 32k-row\nwrite. That is exactly the waste that had to be deleted yesterday: two\nidentities that had never used the app were holding 64,452 rank rows between\nthem, because a rebuild-all had ranked them indiscriminately.\n\nSo the trigger is USE. A feed request that finds no current ranking is served\nlive, as before, and builds one behind itself; the next request is on the fast\npath. A profile nobody opens never costs anything. A profile EDIT rebuilds\neagerly, since editing is a deliberate act by someone plainly using it.\n\nConcurrent builds are deduped per isolate. A build takes ~7s and the feed\nschedules one whenever it finds none, so a burst of requests would otherwise\neach start their own. Two builds would agree — writeRanks upserts, and\nmarkRankBuilt runs last — so this is about wasted writes, not correctness,\nwhich is why an isolate-local Set is the right size for it: it collapses the\ncase that actually happens (one person opening the app) without a claim row\nthat could strand a profile if a build died holding it.\n\nThree tests: the ranking appears behind the first request that needs it and the\nfeed is unchanged once it does; a profile nobody opens gets no rank rows; an\nedit rebuilds against the saved criteria. The harness passes no executionCtx,\nso the background work runs unattached and the tests poll for it — which also\nexercises the fallback, since the request that triggers a build must still be\ncorrect on its own.","tree":{"sha":"75fee00c44ec33076fcc85efeef2254f79e728e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/75fee00c44ec33076fcc85efeef2254f79e728e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/641e99c2ae308db4755eeb7764d8d37450ff39a4","verification":{"payload":"tree 75fee00c44ec33076fcc85efeef2254f79e728e2\nparent 65cf9cb370e56f255dc42ea2db05b15b16f630a0\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788641809 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788641824 -0700\n\nfeat: the feed''s ranking installs itself, on use rather than on existence\n\nThe precomputed ranking only appeared when someone remembered to POST\n/ingest/rebuild-rank, so a profile created today used the slow path forever and\nnothing said so. The obvious fix — build it when a profile is created — is\nwrong here, and worth writing down: ensureDefaultProfile materialises a Default\nfor every identity that so much as calls GET /profiles, so \"build on create\"\nmeans every service key, test credential and one-off probe triggers a 32k-row\nwrite. That is exactly the waste that had to be deleted yesterday: two\nidentities that had never used the app were holding 64,452 rank rows between\nthem, because a rebuild-all had ranked them indiscriminately.\n\nSo the trigger is USE. A feed request that finds no current ranking is served\nlive, as before, and builds one behind itself; the next request is on the fast\npath. A profile nobody opens never costs anything. A profile EDIT rebuilds\neagerly, since editing is a deliberate act by someone plainly using it.\n\nConcurrent builds are deduped per isolate. A build takes ~7s and the feed\nschedules one whenever it finds none, so a burst of requests would otherwise\neach start their own. Two builds would agree — writeRanks upserts, and\nmarkRankBuilt runs last — so this is about wasted writes, not correctness,\nwhich is why an isolate-local Set is the right size for it: it collapses the\ncase that actually happens (one person opening the app) without a claim row\nthat could strand a profile if a build died holding it.\n\nThree tests: the ranking appears behind the first request that needs it and the\nfeed is unchanged once it does; a profile nobody opens gets no rank rows; an\nedit rebuilds against the saved criteria. The harness passes no executionCtx,\nso the background work runs unattached and the tests poll for it — which also\nexercises the fallback, since the request that triggers a build must still be\ncorrect on its own.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQKAb6U9O+as3OLrx/L+Njgfy7hXqX91Fs6dAh/RnqRLO4sIrDeZw2Yb+ijmSyfQqH9\nr8x6RlJo6geNAPMpKZ+wI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-05T20:57:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/641e99c2ae308db4755eeb7764d8d37450ff39a4","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKDY0MWU5OWMyYWUzMDhkYjQ3NTVlZWI3NzY0ZDhkMzc0NTBmZjM5YTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/65cf9cb370e56f255dc42ea2db05b15b16f630a0","sha":"65cf9cb370e56f255dc42ea2db05b15b16f630a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/65cf9cb370e56f255dc42ea2db05b15b16f630a0"}],"sha":"641e99c2ae308db4755eeb7764d8d37450ff39a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/641e99c2ae308db4755eeb7764d8d37450ff39a4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscription