"user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/cc9777e5d12aabc63e2f5ce212d9bd827eb90b9a","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKGNjOTc3N2U1ZDEyYWFiYzYzZTJmNWNlMjEyZDliZDgyN2ViOTBiOWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/a8875b3ddea1461b883a46471f5004886e65bc7b","sha":"a8875b3ddea1461b883a46471f5004886e65bc7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/a8875b3ddea1461b883a46471f5004886e65bc7b"}],"sha":"cc9777e5d12aabc63e2f5ce212d9bd827eb90b9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/cc9777e5d12aabc63e2f5ce212d9bd827eb90b9a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/a8875b3ddea1461b883a46471f5004886e65bc7b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T23:47:35Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T23:47:35Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix: the apply runner could not ask for a job''s drafted answers\n\nPOST /jobs/:id/application-extras required resume_markdown in the body. The\ndashboard has one — it just generated it — so this was invisible there. The\napply runner does not: it is asking \"what are the drafted screening answers for\nthis job?\", and had no reason to be carrying a résumé to ask that. It posted\n`{}`, got a 400, and treats any failure here as \"no drafted answers\" and falls\nback to the owner''s standing ones. So the prefetch never worked, and never\nfailed loudly enough for anyone to notice: five calls, five 400s, in the only\nwindow the request logs still cover.\n\nAn absent résumé now resolves from the packet already minted for this job and\ncaller — job_states.variant_slug is the record of what was actually prepared\nfor it. An explicit resume_markdown still wins, so the dashboard is unchanged.\n\nThe lookup is per-caller, and an expired slug is refused rather than\nsubstituted: resume-api answers an unknown slug with the CANONICAL résumé and\nomits `variant` instead of 404ing, so taking `content` unchecked would tailor a\nkit to the generic résumé and hand it back as job-specific.","tree":{"sha":"3d072261a1478a3f9bdbb83c97b8302de41021af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/3d072261a1478a3f9bdbb83c97b8302de41021af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/a8875b3ddea1461b883a46471f5004886e65bc7b","verification":{"payload":"tree 3d072261a1478a3f9bdbb83c97b8302de41021af\nparent f089ea0f34995637878764aace8c89a99aade836\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788306455 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788306455 -0700\n\nfix: the apply runner could not ask for a job''s drafted answers\n\nPOST /jobs/:id/application-extras required resume_markdown in the body. The\ndashboard has one — it just generated it — so this was invisible there. The\napply runner does not: it is asking \"what are the drafted screening answers for\nthis job?\", and had no reason to be carrying a résumé to ask that. It posted\n`{}`, got a 400, and treats any failure here as \"no drafted answers\" and falls\nback to the owner''s standing ones. So the prefetch never worked, and never\nfailed loudly enough for anyone to notice: five calls, five 400s, in the only\nwindow the request logs still cover.\n\nAn absent résumé now resolves from the packet already minted for this job and\ncaller — job_states.variant_slug is the record of what was actually prepared\nfor it. An explicit resume_markdown still wins, so the dashboard is unchanged.\n\nThe lookup is per-caller, and an expired slug is refused rather than\nsubstituted: resume-api answers an unknown slug with the CANONICAL résumé and\nomits `variant` instead of 404ing, so taking `content` unchecked would tailor a\nkit to the generic résumé and hand it back as job-specific.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQK1A/bvzcS0oDkwEbi7yyxBc5rqNwFkwpHoR390TCQlpo++Qex8qVXMoU1xt2WqIfe\nF3x7JIcURPM9XNa9P2Ow4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T23:51:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/a8875b3ddea1461b883a46471f5004886e65bc7b","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKGE4ODc1YjNkZGVhMTQ2MWI4ODNhNDY0NzFmNTAwNDg4NmU2NWJjN2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/f089ea0f34995637878764aace8c89a99aade836","sha":"f089ea0f34995637878764aace8c89a99aade836","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/f089ea0f34995637878764aace8c89a99aade836"}],"sha":"a8875b3ddea1461b883a46471f5004886e65bc7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/a8875b3ddea1461b883a46471f5004886e65bc7b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/f089ea0f34995637878764aace8c89a99aade836/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T23:22:20Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T23:22:20Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"ci: the reporter cannot report from a hosted runner\n\nd15b150 put the new aggregate `report` job on `ubuntu-latest`, reasoning that\none curl should not occupy a claw. It cannot: run 33570360877 came back\n`curl: (22) ... 403` with a valid key, minutes after the claw had reported the\nidentical job successfully. Same repo, same KEY_SERVICE_JOBPLATFORM, same\npayload, same action -- the runner was the only variable.\n\nNot the Cloudflare UA block documented in hadoku_site\ndocs/operations/CLOUDFLARE_UA_BLOCK.md: from a LAN host the same curl with a\ndeliberately bogus key still reaches edge-router and is answered\n`{\"error\":\"Unauthorized\"}`, so the zone is not refusing curl as such. The exact\ndiscriminator for a GitHub-hosted caller is not established here; what is\nestablished is that the report does not arrive from one.\n\nThat matters more than the runner minute it saves, because report-job never\nfails its job -- it emits a `::warning::` and exits 0. A reporter that silently\ndoes not report is precisely the failure mode this job was added to close, so\nit would have sat there looking green.\n\nBack to the same runner-selection expression as typecheck and lint, so an\nunauthorized fork PR still lands on hosted. The job executes no repo code\neither way: no checkout, and a `uses:` on a pull_request resolves from the base\nbranch. A fork cannot read the secret, so there the action warns and skips.","tree":{"sha":"197d886028409a1dc1b20366763b53c929290c61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/197d886028409a1dc1b20366763b53c929290c61"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/f089ea0f34995637878764aace8c89a99aade836","verification":{"payload":"tree 197d886028409a1dc1b20366763b53c929290c61\nparent d15b15055a3c188fab25a97a2199a9aea5f0b5c2\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788304940 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788304940 -0700\n\nci: the reporter cannot report from a hosted runner\n\nd15b150 put the new aggregate `report` job on `ubuntu-latest`, reasoning that\none curl should not occupy a claw. It cannot: run 33570360877 came back\n`curl: (22) ... 403` with a valid key, minutes after the claw had reported the\nidentical job successfully. Same repo, same KEY_SERVICE_JOBPLATFORM, same\npayload, same action -- the runner was the only variable.\n\nNot the Cloudflare UA block documented in hadoku_site\ndocs/operations/CLOUDFLARE_UA_BLOCK.md: from a LAN host the same curl with a\ndeliberately bogus key still reaches edge-router and is answered\n`{\"error\":\"Unauthorized\"}`, so the zone is not refusing curl as such. The exact\ndiscriminator for a GitHub-hosted caller is not established here; what is\nestablished is that the report does not arrive from one.\n\nThat matters more than the runner minute it saves, because report-job never\nfails its job -- it emits a `::warning::` and exits 0. A reporter that silently\ndoes not report is precisely the failure mode this job was added to close, so\nit would have sat there looking green.\n\nBack to the same runner-selection expression as typecheck and lint, so an\nunauthorized fork PR still lands on hosted. The job executes no repo code\neither way: no checkout, and a `uses:` on a pull_request resolves from the base\nbranch. A fork cannot read the secret, so there the action warns and skips.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLXn+WPzy7gOZrIeoIgw4ROSiJhYEEpTGixM2mCmQciOzwAPEFcsZhfGoZL7WlhU7d\nExOF4vbS1vAuRe+osBxwE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T23:22:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/f089ea0f34995637878764aace8c89a99aade836","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKGYwODllYTBmMzQ5OTU2Mzc4Nzg3NjRhYWNlOGM4OWE5OWFhZGU4MzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/d15b15055a3c188fab25a97a2199a9aea5f0b5c2","sha":"d15b15055a3c188fab25a97a2199a9aea5f0b5c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/d15b15055a3c188fab25a97a2199a9aea5f0b5c2"}],"sha":"f089ea0f34995637878764aace8c89a99aade836","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/f089ea0f34995637878764aace8c89a99aade836"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/d15b15055a3c188fab25a97a2199a9aea5f0b5c2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T23:17:00Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T23:17:41Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"ci: a typecheck failure told nobody, and two reporters would clobber each other\n\nOnly the `lint` job reported its outcome. `typecheck` had neither the start\nmarker nor the report step, so a typecheck-only failure on main reached the\nfleet''s one alerting path as nothing at all -- the exact silence 47820b7 added\nthe reporting to end, wired into half the workflow.\n\nThe obvious fix -- paste the same step into `typecheck` -- is wrong, and\nquietly so. `POST /health/api/jobs` upserts the execution row on run_id ALONE\n(monitoring-api migration 0007, `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX idx_jobs_run_id ON\njob_executions(run_id)`, and `ON CONFLICT(run_id) DO UPDATE` in job-store.ts).\nBoth jobs live in ONE workflow file and therefore share one run_id, so two\nreport steps upsert the SAME row and the job that finishes last overwrites the\nother''s verdict: a green lint erases a red typecheck. site:typecheck and\nsite:lint are safe from this only because they sit in separate workflow FILES,\nwhich means separate runs -- the convention does not transfer.\n\nSo the report moves out to one aggregate job that `needs` both and runs on\n`always()`: one run_id, one row, one `jobplatform:ci` alert key, red if either\njob is red. Cancelled is tested before failure, so a run superseded by\n`cancel-in-progress` stays silent instead of clearing a live failure streak.\n`lint` publishes its start epoch as a job output so the duration stays real.\n\nThe report job takes a hosted runner and no checkout -- it is one curl, and\nreport-job is referenced rather than vendored, so the runner fetches it before\nthe first step. `report` is not a required context (`lint` and `typecheck`\nare), so nothing waits on it.\n\nAlso collapses the \"Runner SELECTION\" comment, pasted twice in both jobs.","tree":{"sha":"6b813708f9d1ca8e2569026c565c1d573373bc33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/6b813708f9d1ca8e2569026c565c1d573373bc33"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/d15b15055a3c188fab25a97a2199a9aea5f0b5c2","verification":{"payload":"tree 6b813708f9d1ca8e2569026c565c1d573373bc33\nparent c0e4378e47ff125ce913fab361f55da2be06d3ac\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788304620 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788304661 -0700\n\nci: a typecheck failure told nobody, and two reporters would clobber each other\n\nOnly the `lint` job reported its outcome. `typecheck` had neither the start\nmarker nor the report step, so a typecheck-only failure on main reached the\nfleet''s one alerting path as nothing at all -- the exact silence 47820b7 added\nthe reporting to end, wired into half the workflow.\n\nThe obvious fix -- paste the same step into `typecheck` -- is wrong, and\nquietly so. `POST /health/api/jobs` upserts the execution row on run_id ALONE\n(monitoring-api migration 0007, `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX idx_jobs_run_id ON\njob_executions(run_id)`, and `ON CONFLICT(run_id) DO UPDATE` in job-store.ts).\nBoth jobs live in ONE workflow file and therefore share one run_id, so two\nreport steps upsert the SAME row and the job that finishes last overwrites the\nother''s verdict: a green lint erases a red typecheck. site:typecheck and\nsite:lint are safe from this only because they sit in separate workflow FILES,\nwhich means separate runs -- the convention does not transfer.\n\nSo the report moves out to one aggregate job that `needs` both and runs on\n`always()`: one run_id, one row, one `jobplatform:ci` alert key, red if either\njob is red. Cancelled is tested before failure, so a run superseded by\n`cancel-in-progress` stays silent instead of clearing a live failure streak.\n`lint` publishes its start epoch as a job output so the duration stays real.\n\nThe report job takes a hosted runner and no checkout -- it is one curl, and\nreport-job is referenced rather than vendored, so the runner fetches it before\nthe first step. `report` is not a required context (`lint` and `typecheck`\nare), so nothing waits on it.\n\nAlso collapses the \"Runner SELECTION\" comment, pasted twice in both jobs.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQHImL7GG/VnXUXZntAO6Xx1i2R4/bwKqQEQ0tVgtBU1G0Rv7B+JrZXSXXbA9+mQhfP\nH8QBZtKUkRd5wcg10xSwk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T23:17:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/d15b15055a3c188fab25a97a2199a9aea5f0b5c2","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKGQxNWIxNTA1NWEzYzE4OGZhYjI1YTk3YTIxOTlhOWFlYTVmMGI1YzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/c0e4378e47ff125ce913fab361f55da2be06d3ac","sha":"c0e4378e47ff125ce913fab361f55da2be06d3ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/c0e4378e47ff125ce913fab361f55da2be06d3ac"}],"sha":"d15b15055a3c188fab25a97a2199a9aea5f0b5c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/d15b15055a3c188fab25a97a2199a9aea5f0b5c2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/c0e4378e47ff125ce913fab361f55da2be06d3ac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T23:16:53Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T23:16:53Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"perf: the scorer rebuilt the same regexes 2.5 million times per request\n\nwordHit compiles `\\bphrase\\b` on every call, and titleTechs compiled all 39\nTITLE_TECH patterns per job. The feed''s light pass runs both over the ENTIRE\nfiltered corpus, so one request against the Default profile (6 keywords, 18\ninterests, 19 avoids, 39 techs = 82 patterns) built 82 x 30,729 = 2.5 million\nRegExp objects to answer 82 distinct questions.\n\nBoth are now compiled once: TITLE_TECH is a module constant so its matchers are\nbuilt at load, and wordHit memoises by phrase. The distinct phrases are the\nunion of every profile''s criteria plus TITLE_TECH — low hundreds — so the map\ndoes not grow with the corpus or with traffic.\n\nMeasured against 4,800 real rows pulled from production D1, with the previous\nscorer imported side by side: scores are IDENTICAL on every row, and scoring\nCPU per feed request falls 735ms -> 249ms. The light pass is 4.3x faster\n(615ms -> 142ms scaled to the 30,729-row corpus); full scoring barely moves\n(120ms -> 107ms), because there the cost is running the pattern over 7.3KB of\ndescription, not building it.\n\nThis is the compute half of the feed''s latency. The other half is moving 13MB\nout of D1 to render 25 rows, which is a separate problem.","tree":{"sha":"1586586f2b25fc4de3df0c656761c5b9a6abbaf6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/1586586f2b25fc4de3df0c656761c5b9a6abbaf6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/c0e4378e47ff125ce913fab361f55da2be06d3ac","verification":{"payload":"tree 1586586f2b25fc4de3df0c656761c5b9a6abbaf6\nparent 761827638625c6f3c8dcc4fa9a9ca68680f67863\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788304613 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788304613 -0700\n\nperf: the scorer rebuilt the same regexes 2.5 million times per request\n\nwordHit compiles `\\bphrase\\b` on every call, and titleTechs compiled all 39\nTITLE_TECH patterns per job. The feed''s light pass runs both over the ENTIRE\nfiltered corpus, so one request against the Default profile (6 keywords, 18\ninterests, 19 avoids, 39 techs = 82 patterns) built 82 x 30,729 = 2.5 million\nRegExp objects to answer 82 distinct questions.\n\nBoth are now compiled once: TITLE_TECH is a module constant so its matchers are\nbuilt at load, and wordHit memoises by phrase. The distinct phrases are the\nunion of every profile''s criteria plus TITLE_TECH — low hundreds — so the map\ndoes not grow with the corpus or with traffic.\n\nMeasured against 4,800 real rows pulled from production D1, with the previous\nscorer imported side by side: scores are IDENTICAL on every row, and scoring\nCPU per feed request falls 735ms -> 249ms. The light pass is 4.3x faster\n(615ms -> 142ms scaled to the 30,729-row corpus); full scoring barely moves\n(120ms -> 107ms), because there the cost is running the pattern over 7.3KB of\ndescription, not building it.\n\nThis is the compute half of the feed''s latency. The other half is moving 13MB\nout of D1 to render 25 rows, which is a separate problem.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQAQKHMeZl1gc+xUi9nC8BvU2MIlMePD3lbMZxTvawHVB9baORPaAMjiK19/bVLgnVX\neEtDrwomlfIZf0Tg6N9QE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T23:17:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/c0e4378e47ff125ce913fab361f55da2be06d3ac","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKGMwZTQzNzhlNDdmZjEyNWNlOTEzZmFiMzYxZjU1ZGEyYmUwNmQzYWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/761827638625c6f3c8dcc4fa9a9ca68680f67863","sha":"761827638625c6f3c8dcc4fa9a9ca68680f67863","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/761827638625c6f3c8dcc4fa9a9ca68680f67863"}],"sha":"c0e4378e47ff125ce913fab361f55da2be06d3ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/c0e4378e47ff125ce913fab361f55da2be06d3ac"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/761827638625c6f3c8dcc4fa9a9ca68680f67863/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T23:06:12Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T23:06:26Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat: answer a multiple-choice question by choosing, not by typing\n\nEvery question in the queue got a text box, including the ones that are really\nradios and dropdowns. That is not a cosmetic mismatch — an answer only lands if\nit matches the board''s option text VERBATIM, because the filler selects by\ncomparing option labels. A text box invites an answer that silently does\nnothing and sends the question straight back to the queue looking unanswered.\n\nReal options, captured from a live Coinbase form 2026-09-01:\n\n    Are you a current government official…\n        \"No, I am not a current or former Government Official\"\n    Are you a close relative of a government official…\n        \"No, I am not a relative of a government official.\"   (trailing period)\n    Please confirm receipt of the … Arbitration Agreement\n        \"Confirmed\"                                            (not \"Yes\")\n    Which best describes how you use AI tools today?\n        five sentence-long choices\n\nFour of Coinbase''s thirteen would have failed for someone answering carefully\nand reasonably. Nobody retypes the fifth correctly.\n\nThe runner now reports what each unanswered question would have accepted, the\nAPI carries it, and the UI shows a picker whenever there are choices and a text\nbox only when the question is genuinely free-form.\n\nFirst sighting wins when two employers ask \"the same\" question: their option\nTEXT differs, and a blended list would be verbatim for neither — which is the\none property an option list has to have. Seeded questions carry no options,\nbecause nothing has ever seen them on a form.\n\nReported by the owner, who noticed the inputs were all free-form and asked\nwhether some of these should not be selectable. They should.","tree":{"sha":"474a2695240664423bdd8b99248a3982a8111345","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/474a2695240664423bdd8b99248a3982a8111345"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/761827638625c6f3c8dcc4fa9a9ca68680f67863","verification":{"payload":"tree 474a2695240664423bdd8b99248a3982a8111345\nparent fab64e06d363f613875175b8201e8389f7f2eb0b\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788303972 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788303986 -0700\n\nfeat: answer a multiple-choice question by choosing, not by typing\n\nEvery question in the queue got a text box, including the ones that are really\nradios and dropdowns. That is not a cosmetic mismatch — an answer only lands if\nit matches the board''s option text VERBATIM, because the filler selects by\ncomparing option labels. A text box invites an answer that silently does\nnothing and sends the question straight back to the queue looking unanswered.\n\nReal options, captured from a live Coinbase form 2026-09-01:\n\n    Are you a current government official…\n        \"No, I am not a current or former Government Official\"\n    Are you a close relative of a government official…\n        \"No, I am not a relative of a government official.\"   (trailing period)\n    Please confirm receipt of the … Arbitration Agreement\n        \"Confirmed\"                                            (not \"Yes\")\n    Which best describes how you use AI tools today?\n        five sentence-long choices\n\nFour of Coinbase''s thirteen would have failed for someone answering carefully\nand reasonably. Nobody retypes the fifth correctly.\n\nThe runner now reports what each unanswered question would have accepted, the\nAPI carries it, and the UI shows a picker whenever there are choices and a text\nbox only when the question is genuinely free-form.\n\nFirst sighting wins when two employers ask \"the same\" question: their option\nTEXT differs, and a blended list would be verbatim for neither — which is the\none property an option list has to have. Seeded questions carry no options,\nbecause nothing has ever seen them on a form.\n\nReported by the owner, who noticed the inputs were all free-form and asked\nwhether some of these should not be selectable. They should.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQK33/Pxo3KYGflJ4eCVTAO1MlACjX7A6ryWkwJUGuQd09C8upBCIHEfBuQrj78BoaE\nATEsPr/FHZ/ylA0rGbSw0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T23:06:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/761827638625c6f3c8dcc4fa9a9ca68680f67863","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKDc2MTgyNzYzODYyNWM2ZjNjOGRjYzRmYTlhOWNhNjg2ODBmNjc4NjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/fab64e06d363f613875175b8201e8389f7f2eb0b","sha":"fab64e06d363f613875175b8201e8389f7f2eb0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/fab64e06d363f613875175b8201e8389f7f2eb0b"}],"sha":"761827638625c6f3c8dcc4fa9a9ca68680f67863","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/761827638625c6f3c8dcc4fa9a9ca68680f67863"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/fab64e06d363f613875175b8201e8389f7f2eb0b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T22:45:23Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T22:45:37Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat: record where a job''s slug came from, so a guess stops looking like a fact\n\nTwo very different processes wrote jobs.slug into one column: the scraper,\nwhich fetched that board BY slug and cannot be wrong, and parseAtsSlug, which\ninvents one from the posting''s hostname because an employer-hosted careers URL\nnames no board at all.\n\nNothing downstream could tell them apart. ''pinterestcareers'' and ''pinterest''\nare both strings; both sort, filter and render fine. The difference only\nsurfaced when the apply runner built a Greenhouse form URL out of an invented\none, got a 404, and spent 45 seconds timing out on a résumé input that was\nnever there — the first time anything actually USED the value, and 12 boards\nand 1,633 postings after the guessing started.\n\nslug_source is ''scraped'' (authoritative), ''guessed'' (parsed from the URL), or\n''verified'' (a guess that was probed and confirmed — nothing writes it yet; it\nis the state the probe path will produce). A re-scrape promotes a guess to\nscraped along with correcting the value.\n\nNULL means the row predates the column, and `asSlugSource` reads it as\n''guessed''. That asymmetry is deliberate: \"we don''t know where this came from\"\nhas to behave exactly like \"we made it up\", or the unsafe case is the one that\nslips through.","tree":{"sha":"67ab8f8a916aa6ad8ed70a743d3f2bda84acaeb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/67ab8f8a916aa6ad8ed70a743d3f2bda84acaeb2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/fab64e06d363f613875175b8201e8389f7f2eb0b","verification":{"payload":"tree 67ab8f8a916aa6ad8ed70a743d3f2bda84acaeb2\nparent 2856dbc6a2f027822bda02b0a995eac22949f5e9\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788302723 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788302737 -0700\n\nfeat: record where a job''s slug came from, so a guess stops looking like a fact\n\nTwo very different processes wrote jobs.slug into one column: the scraper,\nwhich fetched that board BY slug and cannot be wrong, and parseAtsSlug, which\ninvents one from the posting''s hostname because an employer-hosted careers URL\nnames no board at all.\n\nNothing downstream could tell them apart. ''pinterestcareers'' and ''pinterest''\nare both strings; both sort, filter and render fine. The difference only\nsurfaced when the apply runner built a Greenhouse form URL out of an invented\none, got a 404, and spent 45 seconds timing out on a résumé input that was\nnever there — the first time anything actually USED the value, and 12 boards\nand 1,633 postings after the guessing started.\n\nslug_source is ''scraped'' (authoritative), ''guessed'' (parsed from the URL), or\n''verified'' (a guess that was probed and confirmed — nothing writes it yet; it\nis the state the probe path will produce). A re-scrape promotes a guess to\nscraped along with correcting the value.\n\nNULL means the row predates the column, and `asSlugSource` reads it as\n''guessed''. That asymmetry is deliberate: \"we don''t know where this came from\"\nhas to behave exactly like \"we made it up\", or the unsafe case is the one that\nslips through.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQNhbJNyNBetKa6M10FcEO3GOLzn1EJ7UDx2HJTc3wMf4dxToeqpXOlFazVLd6wSH8b\nnTO4FzXttUQReJu4DYFwY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T22:45:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/fab64e06d363f613875175b8201e8389f7f2eb0b","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKGZhYjY0ZTA2ZDM2M2Y2MTM4NzUxNzViODIwMWU4Mzg5ZjdmMmViMGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/2856dbc6a2f027822bda02b0a995eac22949f5e9","sha":"2856dbc6a2f027822bda02b0a995eac22949f5e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/2856dbc6a2f027822bda02b0a995eac22949f5e9"}],"sha":"fab64e06d363f613875175b8201e8389f7f2eb0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/fab64e06d363f613875175b8201e8389f7f2eb0b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/2856dbc6a2f027822bda02b0a995eac22949f5e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T22:37:16Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Matthaeus Wolff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T22:37:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: the publish gate measures a push, not its last commit (#17)\n\n* ci: the publish gate measures a push, not its last commit\n\n`publish.yml` decided what changed with `git diff HEAD~1 HEAD` — the last\nCOMMIT — and then gated the publish, the registry verification and the dispatch\nto hadoku_site on the answer. A push is not one commit.\n\nPush two commits where the worker changes in the first and a chore lands\nsecond, and @wolffm/jobplatform-worker is judged unchanged: not published, not\nverified, not named in the dispatch. hadoku_site then commits only the root\npackage.json — nothing under `workers/**` — so deploy-workers.yml does not fire\neither, and the site runs a new client against the previous worker.\n\nIt fails quietly by construction: every downstream step reads the same flag, so\nthey agree with each other and none of them agrees with the push.\n\nThis repo has not been bitten yet, but it is exposed and the exposure is\nrecent. Of the last 59 pushes, 4 carried more than one commit; 2 of those\ntouched `worker/` and only reached the registry because the TIP commit happened\nto touch it too — both on 2026-09-01. That is a coin flip won twice, not a\nworking gate.\n\n`github.event.before` is the tip before the push, the only base covering every\ncommit in it. It is absent on workflow_dispatch, all-zeroes on a branch''s first\npush, and can be unreachable after a force-push; each case falls back to\n`HEAD~1`, narrower than the truth but never broken. `fetch-depth` goes to 0 so\nthe base is in the clone, and the step prints the range and the file list it\nchose.\n\nSame change as hadoku_site templates/ui-app (PR #358); hadoku-meet has carried\nit since 2026-08-18 and hadoku-hopper since 2026-09-01, where this cost a\nrelease.\n\n* ci: a manual dispatch publishes everything, so it can recover a skipped publish\n\nThe push-range gate still fell back to HEAD~1 on workflow_dispatch, which\nis the one event that has no push. A dispatch after a stranded multi-commit\npush therefore diffed the same tip commit that stranded it and skipped the\nsame worker again; the only recovery was a no-op commit under worker/.\n\nhadoku_site''s publish-worker-utils.yml already treats a dispatch as an\nexplicit \"publish now\". The range step now emits publish_all=true on\ndispatch and both change checks read it before they diff anything. The\nversion walk starts from the registry, so an unconditional dispatch costs\none patch bump and nothing else.\n\nSame change as hadoku_site templates/ui-app (PR #358).","tree":{"sha":"ef00d2ead37388927bcf450f37c61856099a139f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/ef00d2ead37388927bcf450f37c61856099a139f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/2856dbc6a2f027822bda02b0a995eac22949f5e9","verification":{"payload":"tree ef00d2ead37388927bcf450f37c61856099a139f\nparent adaa1f4350cf6e1638a9a06fd18a2a5a961b53f6\nauthor Matthaeus Wolff <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788302236 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788302236 -0700\n\nci: the publish gate measures a push, not its last commit (#17)\n\n* ci: the publish gate measures a push, not its last commit\n\n`publish.yml` decided what changed with `git diff HEAD~1 HEAD` — the last\nCOMMIT — and then gated the publish, the registry verification and the dispatch\nto hadoku_site on the answer. A push is not one commit.\n\nPush two commits where the worker changes in the first and a chore lands\nsecond, and @wolffm/jobplatform-worker is judged unchanged: not published, not\nverified, not named in the dispatch. hadoku_site then commits only the root\npackage.json — nothing under `workers/**` — so deploy-workers.yml does not fire\neither, and the site runs a new client against the previous worker.\n\nIt fails quietly by construction: every downstream step reads the same flag, so\nthey agree with each other and none of them agrees with the push.\n\nThis repo has not been bitten yet, but it is exposed and the exposure is\nrecent. Of the last 59 pushes, 4 carried more than one commit; 2 of those\ntouched `worker/` and only reached the registry because the TIP commit happened\nto touch it too — both on 2026-09-01. That is a coin flip won twice, not a\nworking gate.\n\n`github.event.before` is the tip before the push, the only base covering every\ncommit in it. It is absent on workflow_dispatch, all-zeroes on a branch''s first\npush, and can be unreachable after a force-push; each case falls back to\n`HEAD~1`, narrower than the truth but never broken. `fetch-depth` goes to 0 so\nthe base is in the clone, and the step prints the range and the file list it\nchose.\n\nSame change as hadoku_site templates/ui-app (PR #358); hadoku-meet has carried\nit since 2026-08-18 and hadoku-hopper since 2026-09-01, where this cost a\nrelease.\n\n* ci: a manual dispatch publishes everything, so it can recover a skipped publish\n\nThe push-range gate still fell back to HEAD~1 on workflow_dispatch, which\nis the one event that has no push. A dispatch after a stranded multi-commit\npush therefore diffed the same tip commit that stranded it and skipped the\nsame worker again; the only recovery was a no-op commit under worker/.\n\nhadoku_site''s publish-worker-utils.yml already treats a dispatch as an\nexplicit \"publish now\". The range step now emits publish_all=true on\ndispatch and both change checks read it before they diff anything. The\nversion walk starts from the registry, so an unconditional dispatch costs\none patch bump and nothing else.\n\nSame change as hadoku_site templates/ui-app (PR #358).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJql1OcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQeYQAFazbxxZyDwfJKaJTbf/R3xy\nS4bz/xW5vkUnzJXSnv6AacMOWnMm4TxltPixS5EFhZd1jVJ+BNlgjNgZeCAFdCtR\nAHGqaU3UF9GE2mr86yrgUEM4dLa0zXJUtCEJFZREk5yB0ANvRelPGNOvcsU7VHnL\nmrv+hawG4T9Gfbt0vXlO/M+QzRXCQkQkEK2g461uRhW7M45iFjngI75YWdQ5fXmB\nbCs/xKUn8lZaZKVpgOy0ZHph3UxvHCKq5a5epWcIJw/nViiUQrbNbJviuLjfA2Q+\nds9l36mtFYFj923RGepb7lPl+2ksx3+XFx7FyEdjXlJx1nDPuwfYpLpvwjNtlAL4\nBsh+uYIux69e+llcUJcT8KLtmNbiOyiDwxf079XLJeG1L+gAKmoLdKyTcYUFk18E\nmLm1RiI86EYpsHY0N6FE+k79vz3t2ezSvTzDsCsaLBoJrylvrDq45mvWuI0SZiXU\nSnHJ9uH0yGDp5kkBxH/va6KPUVDiuycxrv1BC40yn0vxOAAtU+mhlOxg6hAYHtc3\niNh5TOhbcvj2gUICCA+PuOjQyvBZa0by5xzcR/miC6avp1tR5Zb7e5UxMSIhjWEp\nl3dqcaXs3JJhOmJIWrWlVjDbUR2XbAhZPEnob252Ojs4TE4BVUV1p58iE0V14a9X\nqtrQcw8PvBfAODOom8WK\n=614l\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T22:37:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/2856dbc6a2f027822bda02b0a995eac22949f5e9","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKDI4NTZkYmM2YTJmMDI3ODIyYmRhMDJiMGE5OTVlYWMyMjk0OWY1ZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/adaa1f4350cf6e1638a9a06fd18a2a5a961b53f6","sha":"adaa1f4350cf6e1638a9a06fd18a2a5a961b53f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/adaa1f4350cf6e1638a9a06fd18a2a5a961b53f6"}],"sha":"2856dbc6a2f027822bda02b0a995eac22949f5e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/2856dbc6a2f027822bda02b0a995eac22949f5e9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/adaa1f4350cf6e1638a9a06fd18a2a5a961b53f6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T22:15:10Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T22:15:10Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix: take the board slug from the scraper instead of guessing it\n\n`parseAtsSlug` derives the board slug from the hostname whenever an employer\nhosts its own careers site, because the URL carries no board name. That guess is\nright often enough to look correct — stripe.com→stripe, coinbase.com→coinbase —\nand it is wrong for 12 of 37 employer-hosted Greenhouse boards, 1,633 postings,\nmeasured 2026-09-01:\n\n    446  careers.datadoghq.com   → datadoghq        real: datadog\n    350  careers.withwaymo.com   → withwaymo        real: waymo\n    307  careers.toasttab.com    → toasttab         real: toast\n    205  www.pinterestcareers.com→ pinterestcareers real: pinterest\n    163  app.careerpuck.com      → app.careerpuck   real: lyft\n\napp.careerpuck.com is the one that shows why no parser fixes this: it is a\nthird-party careers host, and the hostname contains no company name at all.\n\nThe failure was silent until something USED the slug. A wrong slug still looks\nlike a slug — it sorts, it filters, it renders. It only surfaced today when the\napply runner derived a Greenhouse embed URL from it, got a 404 with no form,\nand spent 45 seconds timing out on a résumé input that was never there. The\nowner picked Pinterest at random; it was 1 of 12.\n\nThe scraper knows the answer: it fetched that board by slug. It sends it now,\nand this prefers it over the parse, falling back when it is absent.\n\nSkipped (already-known) rows have their slug corrected on re-encounter, so the\n1,633 heal on their next scrape rather than waiting on a backfill. That write\nonly happens when the scraper supplied an authoritative slug, so it can only\never replace a guess with the truth.","tree":{"sha":"caff765376c75792fb46875da58d886d51c044c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/caff765376c75792fb46875da58d886d51c044c9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/adaa1f4350cf6e1638a9a06fd18a2a5a961b53f6","verification":{"payload":"tree caff765376c75792fb46875da58d886d51c044c9\nparent daa0c54a4e043e8f76940c3146ce11cb0cce6aa8\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788300910 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788300910 -0700\n\nfix: take the board slug from the scraper instead of guessing it\n\n`parseAtsSlug` derives the board slug from the hostname whenever an employer\nhosts its own careers site, because the URL carries no board name. That guess is\nright often enough to look correct — stripe.com→stripe, coinbase.com→coinbase —\nand it is wrong for 12 of 37 employer-hosted Greenhouse boards, 1,633 postings,\nmeasured 2026-09-01:\n\n    446  careers.datadoghq.com   → datadoghq        real: datadog\n    350  careers.withwaymo.com   → withwaymo        real: waymo\n    307  careers.toasttab.com    → toasttab         real: toast\n    205  www.pinterestcareers.com→ pinterestcareers real: pinterest\n    163  app.careerpuck.com      → app.careerpuck   real: lyft\n\napp.careerpuck.com is the one that shows why no parser fixes this: it is a\nthird-party careers host, and the hostname contains no company name at all.\n\nThe failure was silent until something USED the slug. A wrong slug still looks\nlike a slug — it sorts, it filters, it renders. It only surfaced today when the\napply runner derived a Greenhouse embed URL from it, got a 404 with no form,\nand spent 45 seconds timing out on a résumé input that was never there. The\nowner picked Pinterest at random; it was 1 of 12.\n\nThe scraper knows the answer: it fetched that board by slug. It sends it now,\nand this prefers it over the parse, falling back when it is absent.\n\nSkipped (already-known) rows have their slug corrected on re-encounter, so the\n1,633 heal on their next scrape rather than waiting on a backfill. That write\nonly happens when the scraper supplied an authoritative slug, so it can only\never replace a guess with the truth.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQIEDDjOtXeYVgZCC8mcCcFeaVJDAKTxzdEtuBQFcUBSH1NO8ivHn3RGBIPHCeIQuH/\nVp5S1h6vbvnYN3sZOkzww=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T22:15:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/adaa1f4350cf6e1638a9a06fd18a2a5a961b53f6","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKGFkYWExZjQzNTBjZjZlMTYzOGE5YTA2ZmQxOGEyYTVhOTYxYjUzZjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/daa0c54a4e043e8f76940c3146ce11cb0cce6aa8","sha":"daa0c54a4e043e8f76940c3146ce11cb0cce6aa8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/daa0c54a4e043e8f76940c3146ce11cb0cce6aa8"}],"sha":"adaa1f4350cf6e1638a9a06fd18a2a5a961b53f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/adaa1f4350cf6e1638a9a06fd18a2a5a961b53f6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/daa0c54a4e043e8f76940c3146ce11cb0cce6aa8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T22:09:12Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T22:09:12Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix: the queue counted employers where it said applications\n\nA row read \"blocking 2 applications · coinbase\" next to applications=1, because\nthe count was `companies.size`. Two postings at one employer are two\napplications held up; collapsing them to one employer made the same row\ndisagree with itself.\n\nFound on the first real drain rather than by reading the code — two Coinbase\npostings hit the queue and the numbers did not match. The UI renders `blocking`\nand the company list, not this field, so nothing visible was wrong yet; the API\nand its schema were.","tree":{"sha":"3f75dc44e0cb767b577ab7d210fdd7945b7e58ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/3f75dc44e0cb767b577ab7d210fdd7945b7e58ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/daa0c54a4e043e8f76940c3146ce11cb0cce6aa8","verification":{"payload":"tree 3f75dc44e0cb767b577ab7d210fdd7945b7e58ea\nparent 3e5a8a1d03606a62ddd32e2d74e9a922196ba865\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788300552 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788300552 -0700\n\nfix: the queue counted employers where it said applications\n\nA row read \"blocking 2 applications · coinbase\" next to applications=1, because\nthe count was `companies.size`. Two postings at one employer are two\napplications held up; collapsing them to one employer made the same row\ndisagree with itself.\n\nFound on the first real drain rather than by reading the code — two Coinbase\npostings hit the queue and the numbers did not match. The UI renders `blocking`\nand the company list, not this field, so nothing visible was wrong yet; the API\nand its schema were.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQF1fcylGDj0CQmMtUI9X7lldxQLjiRj1M0Os8kw12nMYg/S53EEqWKmVEjvvHMKaS6\n3ZQZgl/vrOCRa9jEQr5w0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T22:09:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/daa0c54a4e043e8f76940c3146ce11cb0cce6aa8","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKGRhYTBjNTRhNGUwNDNlOGY3Njk0MGMzMTQ2Y2UxMWNiMGNjZTZhYTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/3e5a8a1d03606a62ddd32e2d74e9a922196ba865","sha":"3e5a8a1d03606a62ddd32e2d74e9a922196ba865","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/3e5a8a1d03606a62ddd32e2d74e9a922196ba865"}],"sha":"daa0c54a4e043e8f76940c3146ce11cb0cce6aa8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/daa0c54a4e043e8f76940c3146ce11cb0cce6aa8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/3e5a8a1d03606a62ddd32e2d74e9a922196ba865/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T21:10:47Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T21:10:47Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(css): stop job cards overhanging the filter bar\n\nThe host pins `.mf-viewport` to `box-sizing: content-box` and lets `*`\ninherit it, so this app renders under the UA default while its sheets were\nwritten border-box. `.jp-jobcard` is `width: 100%` plus 2x --hdk-space-xl of\npadding and a 1px/3px border, so its content box was already the full\ncontainer width and the padding went on top — the cards ran ~44px past the\nfilter bar above them, which is auto-width and sits flush.\n\nScope a border-box reset to `.job-platform-container`, which is what the\nhost''s own comment expects a child app to do (a class selector outranks its\nbare `*`). Same overhang was latent in `.jp-editor__text`,\n`.jp-questions__add input` and `.jp-drawer__packet-text`.","tree":{"sha":"e71b9115f98e87c20733ea8221d8c55e0a06ae26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/e71b9115f98e87c20733ea8221d8c55e0a06ae26"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/3e5a8a1d03606a62ddd32e2d74e9a922196ba865","verification":{"payload":"tree e71b9115f98e87c20733ea8221d8c55e0a06ae26\nparent a2bdde7c6113a49dc8d8ec6257082969ad76ec91\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788297047 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788297047 -0700\n\nfix(css): stop job cards overhanging the filter bar\n\nThe host pins `.mf-viewport` to `box-sizing: content-box` and lets `*`\ninherit it, so this app renders under the UA default while its sheets were\nwritten border-box. `.jp-jobcard` is `width: 100%` plus 2x --hdk-space-xl of\npadding and a 1px/3px border, so its content box was already the full\ncontainer width and the padding went on top — the cards ran ~44px past the\nfilter bar above them, which is auto-width and sits flush.\n\nScope a border-box reset to `.job-platform-container`, which is what the\nhost''s own comment expects a child app to do (a class selector outranks its\nbare `*`). Same overhang was latent in `.jp-editor__text`,\n`.jp-questions__add input` and `.jp-drawer__packet-text`.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQE8t+iQ2te3HCcdsp95iz3P7IWaF50ETVVZc7ZrE4Rk3fUOrj0fkHjR6t0C1zld2Mj\n7TzMyCvgPbLBJBBSDlsQQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T21:11:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/3e5a8a1d03606a62ddd32e2d74e9a922196ba865","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKDNlNWE4YTFkMDM2MDZhNjJkZGQzMmUyZDc0ZTlhOTIyMTk2YmE4NjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/a2bdde7c6113a49dc8d8ec6257082969ad76ec91","sha":"a2bdde7c6113a49dc8d8ec6257082969ad76ec91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/a2bdde7c6113a49dc8d8ec6257082969ad76ec91"}],"sha":"3e5a8a1d03606a62ddd32e2d74e9a922196ba865","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/3e5a8a1d03606a62ddd32e2d74e9a922196ba865"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/a2bdde7c6113a49dc8d8ec6257082969ad76ec91/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T21:01:47Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T21:02:00Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat: seed the question queue, and stop explaining itself in the UI\n\nTwo things the owner hit within a minute of opening the tab.\n\nTHE SECTION EXPLAINED ITSELF INSTEAD OF DOING ANYTHING. It rendered a panel\nwhose entire content was a sentence saying the panel was empty, above a second\nsentence explaining how to make it not empty. Both are gone. The component now\nreturns null when there is nothing to answer and nothing saved, and no copy in\nit describes the feature to the person already using it. Reasoning that used to\nbe UI text lives in comments, where it belongs.\n\nTHE QUEUE COULD ONLY BE FILLED BY FAILING FIRST. A question had to block an\napplication before there was anywhere to put its answer, so a brand-new install\nshowed an empty tab and no way forward.\n\nIt is seeded now, and the seed is MEASURED rather than guessed: 26 live\nGreenhouse forms sampled on 2026-09-01, every question label counted. The head\nis short and steep, which is what makes seeding work at all —\n\n    15/26  Veteran Status            6/26  How did you hear about this job?\n    13/26  Disability Status         3/26  Are you legally authorized to work in the US?\n    13/26  Are you Hispanic/Latino?  2/26  ...in the country where the job is located?\n    12/26  Location (City)           2/26  Will you require company sponsorship...\n    11/26  Preferred First Name\n\nLocation (City) is the one worth noticing: it wants a bare city, the profile\nholds \"San Jose, California, United States\", and it is what actually stopped a\nreal Coinbase fill today. The sample found it on 12 of 26 boards.\n\nSeeded entries carry no company, so the UI shows employers only where a fill\nreally reported the question, and a seeded row never overwrites a real one that\nalready knows who asked. Answering removes it either way.","tree":{"sha":"2d06843b09d1e7a873dd503f02a75c8660add369","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/2d06843b09d1e7a873dd503f02a75c8660add369"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/a2bdde7c6113a49dc8d8ec6257082969ad76ec91","verification":{"payload":"tree 2d06843b09d1e7a873dd503f02a75c8660add369\nparent b30a15c4f003c4bfa3d9ec943d8fdd478e4b6a36\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788296507 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788296520 -0700\n\nfeat: seed the question queue, and stop explaining itself in the UI\n\nTwo things the owner hit within a minute of opening the tab.\n\nTHE SECTION EXPLAINED ITSELF INSTEAD OF DOING ANYTHING. It rendered a panel\nwhose entire content was a sentence saying the panel was empty, above a second\nsentence explaining how to make it not empty. Both are gone. The component now\nreturns null when there is nothing to answer and nothing saved, and no copy in\nit describes the feature to the person already using it. Reasoning that used to\nbe UI text lives in comments, where it belongs.\n\nTHE QUEUE COULD ONLY BE FILLED BY FAILING FIRST. A question had to block an\napplication before there was anywhere to put its answer, so a brand-new install\nshowed an empty tab and no way forward.\n\nIt is seeded now, and the seed is MEASURED rather than guessed: 26 live\nGreenhouse forms sampled on 2026-09-01, every question label counted. The head\nis short and steep, which is what makes seeding work at all —\n\n    15/26  Veteran Status            6/26  How did you hear about this job?\n    13/26  Disability Status         3/26  Are you legally authorized to work in the US?\n    13/26  Are you Hispanic/Latino?  2/26  ...in the country where the job is located?\n    12/26  Location (City)           2/26  Will you require company sponsorship...\n    11/26  Preferred First Name\n\nLocation (City) is the one worth noticing: it wants a bare city, the profile\nholds \"San Jose, California, United States\", and it is what actually stopped a\nreal Coinbase fill today. The sample found it on 12 of 26 boards.\n\nSeeded entries carry no company, so the UI shows employers only where a fill\nreally reported the question, and a seeded row never overwrites a real one that\nalready knows who asked. Answering removes it either way.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQF50DYMgCycTlgXavXPX1P/5rEuxuFz5k6l35JGXHa1qECrzI1rYwJPIAEmduJCSXw\nZKYymY8dKez5GLJL3o4Ac=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T21:02:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/a2bdde7c6113a49dc8d8ec6257082969ad76ec91","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKGEyYmRkZTdjNjExM2E0OWRjOGQ4ZWM2MjU3MDgyOTY5YWQ3NmVjOTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/b30a15c4f003c4bfa3d9ec943d8fdd478e4b6a36","sha":"b30a15c4f003c4bfa3d9ec943d8fdd478e4b6a36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/b30a15c4f003c4bfa3d9ec943d8fdd478e4b6a36"}],"sha":"a2bdde7c6113a49dc8d8ec6257082969ad76ec91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/a2bdde7c6113a49dc8d8ec6257082969ad76ec91"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/b30a15c4f003c4bfa3d9ec943d8fdd478e4b6a36/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:55:36Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:55:49Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat(ui): answer a question before a fill has ever asked it\n\nThe queue could only be filled by first FAILING an application: a question had\nto block a fill before there was anywhere to put its answer. Which is backwards\nwhenever the owner already knows what a board will ask — and they usually do,\nbecause the compliance and demographic blocks are near-identical across\nemployers. Three real fills today stalled on 29 questions between them, and\nuntil now there was no way to enter a single one of those answers.\n\nReported by the owner, who opened the tab, saw \"Nothing outstanding\", and had\nnowhere to go: the empty state was correct and the feature was still unusable.\n\nCollapsed by default. The queue stays the primary path — this is the escape\nhatch for knowing in advance, not the main road.","tree":{"sha":"6768b6043f233a37930111af16c386990d329215","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/6768b6043f233a37930111af16c386990d329215"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/b30a15c4f003c4bfa3d9ec943d8fdd478e4b6a36","verification":{"payload":"tree 6768b6043f233a37930111af16c386990d329215\nparent 07a6602e9e4afbcf0a508aa0c119a4464b788cb6\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788296136 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788296149 -0700\n\nfeat(ui): answer a question before a fill has ever asked it\n\nThe queue could only be filled by first FAILING an application: a question had\nto block a fill before there was anywhere to put its answer. Which is backwards\nwhenever the owner already knows what a board will ask — and they usually do,\nbecause the compliance and demographic blocks are near-identical across\nemployers. Three real fills today stalled on 29 questions between them, and\nuntil now there was no way to enter a single one of those answers.\n\nReported by the owner, who opened the tab, saw \"Nothing outstanding\", and had\nnowhere to go: the empty state was correct and the feature was still unusable.\n\nCollapsed by default. The queue stays the primary path — this is the escape\nhatch for knowing in advance, not the main road.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQNsIAoe5RWXFBHH0DErzJLVCQsB5AiwdeirY+XtYVG8jC3XJqeHGiM5l4pgBO4wb+a\n4oFM/ps7FzUi6LUKrGjQA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T20:55:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"s