eived_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/7c947a6b2c54fe17d916d94671ed286f8c58fcfb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:52:12Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:52:12Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix: restore what the rebase onto the answers queue dropped\n\nThe version-bump conflicts in this branch were resolved mechanically, and\nApplicationsList.tsx conflicted for a real reason on top of them — so its\nuseResource import went with the version lines. Restores it, and rewrites\neslint.config.js with its original CRLF endings after an edit flattened the\nwhole file to LF.","tree":{"sha":"e4ff1b9f6b5feccc5e0d2ead9da602c43ccd7de3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/e4ff1b9f6b5feccc5e0d2ead9da602c43ccd7de3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/7c947a6b2c54fe17d916d94671ed286f8c58fcfb","verification":{"payload":"tree e4ff1b9f6b5feccc5e0d2ead9da602c43ccd7de3\nparent 7f58744193fd52180664ef77a2e54be8d4921d01\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788295932 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788295932 -0700\n\nfix: restore what the rebase onto the answers queue dropped\n\nThe version-bump conflicts in this branch were resolved mechanically, and\nApplicationsList.tsx conflicted for a real reason on top of them — so its\nuseResource import went with the version lines. Restores it, and rewrites\neslint.config.js with its original CRLF endings after an edit flattened the\nwhole file to LF.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJsKEx+XWwOAm0gFov2bDp19AjpDg/yAGk0ePN56CPXuXyGztG/jXmEz4F12IAZC4T\n+omf/Zq9a+ipF2TXaNZgs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T20:53:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/7c947a6b2c54fe17d916d94671ed286f8c58fcfb","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKDdjOTQ3YTZiMmM1NGZlMTdkOTE2ZDk0NjcxZWQyODZmOGM1OGZjZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/7f58744193fd52180664ef77a2e54be8d4921d01","sha":"7f58744193fd52180664ef77a2e54be8d4921d01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/7f58744193fd52180664ef77a2e54be8d4921d01"}],"sha":"7c947a6b2c54fe17d916d94671ed286f8c58fcfb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/7c947a6b2c54fe17d916d94671ed286f8c58fcfb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/7f58744193fd52180664ef77a2e54be8d4921d01/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:48:58Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:50:06Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"perf: bound the resource cache so postings can''t accumulate unread\n\nA cached job posting carries its full description (~7.5KB average), so a long\nbrowsing session grew the map without limit. Caps it at 120 entries, evicting\noldest-written first, and drops primeResource — nothing called it; writes here\ninvalidate and re-read instead.","tree":{"sha":"6017c1fc25fc24683708fb3a7eced81f4c1b5cb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/6017c1fc25fc24683708fb3a7eced81f4c1b5cb5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/7f58744193fd52180664ef77a2e54be8d4921d01","verification":{"payload":"tree 6017c1fc25fc24683708fb3a7eced81f4c1b5cb5\nparent cc1d27fdda97cdd26ce0509cdfb0af4aa5df3706\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788295738 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788295806 -0700\n\nperf: bound the resource cache so postings can''t accumulate unread\n\nA cached job posting carries its full description (~7.5KB average), so a long\nbrowsing session grew the map without limit. Caps it at 120 entries, evicting\noldest-written first, and drops primeResource — nothing called it; writes here\ninvalidate and re-read instead.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQO+VFH2mrAr7YpLC3bMu+lJB1ZIImfJBJzneN/UOBBN7EoJaA6lxIESlCjm0RFtgfU\neYQdI6hgZC8aEiR76N7g4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T20:53:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/7f58744193fd52180664ef77a2e54be8d4921d01","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKDdmNTg3NDQxOTNmZDUyMTgwNjY0ZWY3N2EyZTU0YmU4ZDQ5MjFkMDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/cc1d27fdda97cdd26ce0509cdfb0af4aa5df3706","sha":"cc1d27fdda97cdd26ce0509cdfb0af4aa5df3706","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/cc1d27fdda97cdd26ce0509cdfb0af4aa5df3706"}],"sha":"7f58744193fd52180664ef77a2e54be8d4921d01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/7f58744193fd52180664ef77a2e54be8d4921d01"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/cc1d27fdda97cdd26ce0509cdfb0af4aa5df3706/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:46:53Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:50:06Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"perf: the rest of the \"Loading…\" lines were refetches of unchanged rows\n\nSame treatment as the feed, for every other view that reads and then waits.\n\nPackets, Applications and a profile''s companies each refetched on mount, so\ntabbing away and back cost a round trip behind a \"Loading packets…\" line. On\na second visit they now paint from cache with no request at all.\n\nThe job drawer refetched the posting every time it opened, including\nreopening the one just closed. Reopen: 786ms -> 38ms. A triage write drops\nthat job''s cache entry, so the drawer never shows a state it just changed.\n\nThe profile editor was the worst of them. Opening it fired one preflight\nprobe per keyword and level — ten parallel requests, and the keyword ones run\nLIKE over all 230MB of descriptions in the corpus, ~1.5s each. They are\ncached now with a 15-minute window, since the counts only move when the\nscraper ingests; reopening the editor fires nothing and the counts still\nrender. Concurrent probes of the same term also share one request rather than\nracing two identical scans.\n\nfetchResource grew a maxAgeMs so a caller can say how long its answer stays\ngood, instead of every reader inheriting the feed''s 30s.","tree":{"sha":"4687def8739b42cc3d0aa11ce2045398fd24d787","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/4687def8739b42cc3d0aa11ce2045398fd24d787"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/cc1d27fdda97cdd26ce0509cdfb0af4aa5df3706","verification":{"payload":"tree 4687def8739b42cc3d0aa11ce2045398fd24d787\nparent ce5d8ae2db710029756ee6575b7a934e22ec8d31\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788295613 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788295806 -0700\n\nperf: the rest of the \"Loading…\" lines were refetches of unchanged rows\n\nSame treatment as the feed, for every other view that reads and then waits.\n\nPackets, Applications and a profile''s companies each refetched on mount, so\ntabbing away and back cost a round trip behind a \"Loading packets…\" line. On\na second visit they now paint from cache with no request at all.\n\nThe job drawer refetched the posting every time it opened, including\nreopening the one just closed. Reopen: 786ms -> 38ms. A triage write drops\nthat job''s cache entry, so the drawer never shows a state it just changed.\n\nThe profile editor was the worst of them. Opening it fired one preflight\nprobe per keyword and level — ten parallel requests, and the keyword ones run\nLIKE over all 230MB of descriptions in the corpus, ~1.5s each. They are\ncached now with a 15-minute window, since the counts only move when the\nscraper ingests; reopening the editor fires nothing and the counts still\nrender. Concurrent probes of the same term also share one request rather than\nracing two identical scans.\n\nfetchResource grew a maxAgeMs so a caller can say how long its answer stays\ngood, instead of every reader inheriting the feed''s 30s.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQEZsVwAkfvG1jmUCSqSiFcUdNX71B7AWYubstewBk5/ZDLvGg3kzZVxee3IVhiB30r\nFx4UFuzenr27s8K4QkVAI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T20:53:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/cc1d27fdda97cdd26ce0509cdfb0af4aa5df3706","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKGNjMWQyN2ZkZGE5N2NkZDI2Y2UwNTA5Y2RmYjBhZjRhYTVkZjM3MDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/ce5d8ae2db710029756ee6575b7a934e22ec8d31","sha":"ce5d8ae2db710029756ee6575b7a934e22ec8d31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/ce5d8ae2db710029756ee6575b7a934e22ec8d31"}],"sha":"cc1d27fdda97cdd26ce0509cdfb0af4aa5df3706","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/cc1d27fdda97cdd26ce0509cdfb0af4aa5df3706"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/ce5d8ae2db710029756ee6575b7a934e22ec8d31/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:40:46Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:50:06Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"perf: the dashboard refetched everything, on every mount, behind a blank\n\nFour things, all of which made the UI slower than the API it sits on.\n\nThe cold load ran in series and threw away its first answer. JobsList fired\non mount, before the sidebar had resolved which profile was selected, so it\nasked for an unscored feed and discarded the reply a second later when the\nscored one replaced it. The feed now waits for the selection, and the\nselection is remembered in localStorage — on a return visit /profiles and the\nscored feed go out together at +831ms instead of one behind the other.\nMeasured cold load, first row painted: 9.8s -> 5.3s first visit, 4.8s after.\n\nNothing was cached. Paging to 2 and back, opening a job and pressing back,\nswitching to Packets and returning: each was a full round trip behind a\n\"Loading…\" line. api/resource.ts is a small stale-while-revalidate map and\nuseResource reads it, so a cached view paints on the first render and\nrefreshes underneath. Page 2 -> page 1 is now 29ms, feed -> packets -> feed\n47ms.\n\nA refetch replaced the list with text. `loading ? \"Loading jobs…\" : list`\nblanked the screen for seconds on a sort change; only a cold read with\nnothing cached does that now, and a refresh dims the rows in place instead.\n\nTriage re-scored the corpus. Marking one job re-ranked 30k rows to learn a\nbadge had changed, and reshuffled the feed under the user mid-triage. It\nwrites a state override through instead, exactly as votes already did, and\nthe card updates with no feed request at all. refreshKey now belongs to the\nthings that really do re-score — a profile saved, a company added — and keys\nthe cache rather than triggering a refetch.\n\nAlso memoises the `auth` object: it is a dependency of every data hook here,\nso rebuilding it each render re-ran the feed, the sidebar and the drawer on\nany re-render at all.","tree":{"sha":"feadaaf5ff6eefe84ebf7dd95821045991057da5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/feadaaf5ff6eefe84ebf7dd95821045991057da5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/ce5d8ae2db710029756ee6575b7a934e22ec8d31","verification":{"payload":"tree feadaaf5ff6eefe84ebf7dd95821045991057da5\nparent 30f3468d717f355da5a5474fe4c8f8a3d8855dfd\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788295246 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788295806 -0700\n\nperf: the dashboard refetched everything, on every mount, behind a blank\n\nFour things, all of which made the UI slower than the API it sits on.\n\nThe cold load ran in series and threw away its first answer. JobsList fired\non mount, before the sidebar had resolved which profile was selected, so it\nasked for an unscored feed and discarded the reply a second later when the\nscored one replaced it. The feed now waits for the selection, and the\nselection is remembered in localStorage — on a return visit /profiles and the\nscored feed go out together at +831ms instead of one behind the other.\nMeasured cold load, first row painted: 9.8s -> 5.3s first visit, 4.8s after.\n\nNothing was cached. Paging to 2 and back, opening a job and pressing back,\nswitching to Packets and returning: each was a full round trip behind a\n\"Loading…\" line. api/resource.ts is a small stale-while-revalidate map and\nuseResource reads it, so a cached view paints on the first render and\nrefreshes underneath. Page 2 -> page 1 is now 29ms, feed -> packets -> feed\n47ms.\n\nA refetch replaced the list with text. `loading ? \"Loading jobs…\" : list`\nblanked the screen for seconds on a sort change; only a cold read with\nnothing cached does that now, and a refresh dims the rows in place instead.\n\nTriage re-scored the corpus. Marking one job re-ranked 30k rows to learn a\nbadge had changed, and reshuffled the feed under the user mid-triage. It\nwrites a state override through instead, exactly as votes already did, and\nthe card updates with no feed request at all. refreshKey now belongs to the\nthings that really do re-score — a profile saved, a company added — and keys\nthe cache rather than triggering a refetch.\n\nAlso memoises the `auth` object: it is a dependency of every data hook here,\nso rebuilding it each render re-ran the feed, the sidebar and the drawer on\nany re-render at all.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLRbHwoQat1xfAFrij55M+ZRVyxJFCyeQRCOXtTOcpbPq+num946snpioMORF0G+O5\nEnbh+4csarkwXGsywOcQQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T20:53:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/ce5d8ae2db710029756ee6575b7a934e22ec8d31","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKGNlNWQ4YWUyZGI3MTAwMjk3NTZlZTY1NzViN2E5MzRlMjJlYzhkMzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/30f3468d717f355da5a5474fe4c8f8a3d8855dfd","sha":"30f3468d717f355da5a5474fe4c8f8a3d8855dfd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/30f3468d717f355da5a5474fe4c8f8a3d8855dfd"}],"sha":"ce5d8ae2db710029756ee6575b7a934e22ec8d31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/ce5d8ae2db710029756ee6575b7a934e22ec8d31"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/30f3468d717f355da5a5474fe4c8f8a3d8855dfd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:31:58Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:49:54Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"perf: the feed dragged the whole corpus across the wire to render 25 rows\n\nA scored feed request measured 3.9s wall / 2.6s CPU, reading 32,335 rows and\n17.0MB out of D1 (Cloudflare telemetry, 10-request burst). Two causes, both\npaying for rows the response never contains.\n\nStage 1 ranks the entire filtered corpus (30,729 rows here, since a profile\nwith no companies isn''t company-scoped) but selected all sixteen display\ncolumns to do it. The light pass reads five of them; `url` alone is ~2MB\nacross the table. It now selects only what ranking needs, and the shortlist\nfetches the display half alongside the description it was already fetching.\nStage 1 I/O: ~1,320ms -> ~500ms.\n\nStage 2 then fetched 800 descriptions (~7.5KB each, ~6MB) for every sort. But\ndate and salary rank on columns stage 1 already has, so the shortlist is\nALREADY in final order there, and the other 775 descriptions only decorate\nrows the caller cannot see. Those sorts now fetch the page. Stage 2 I/O on\nsort=date: ~1,500ms -> ~78ms.\n\nscore and the lens sorts still score the whole shortlist. Their light-pass\nbound assumes every keyword hits the description, so thousands of candidates\nshare the top bound and no early cut is provable — narrowing the field there\nwould quietly change which jobs you see, which is not a perf decision to make\nsilently.\n\nVerified against production: ids and scores identical for each of\nscore/date/salary/comp/relevance/interest, on pages 1, 2 and 5.","tree":{"sha":"ddf7bb4f5a2f81372bf9487f8dfa23ba04d9c9ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/ddf7bb4f5a2f81372bf9487f8dfa23ba04d9c9ff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/30f3468d717f355da5a5474fe4c8f8a3d8855dfd","verification":{"payload":"tree ddf7bb4f5a2f81372bf9487f8dfa23ba04d9c9ff\nparent 0dee1be8047d9aaaa49d8121f1b5742ee79bd836\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788294718 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788295794 -0700\n\nperf: the feed dragged the whole corpus across the wire to render 25 rows\n\nA scored feed request measured 3.9s wall / 2.6s CPU, reading 32,335 rows and\n17.0MB out of D1 (Cloudflare telemetry, 10-request burst). Two causes, both\npaying for rows the response never contains.\n\nStage 1 ranks the entire filtered corpus (30,729 rows here, since a profile\nwith no companies isn''t company-scoped) but selected all sixteen display\ncolumns to do it. The light pass reads five of them; `url` alone is ~2MB\nacross the table. It now selects only what ranking needs, and the shortlist\nfetches the display half alongside the description it was already fetching.\nStage 1 I/O: ~1,320ms -> ~500ms.\n\nStage 2 then fetched 800 descriptions (~7.5KB each, ~6MB) for every sort. But\ndate and salary rank on columns stage 1 already has, so the shortlist is\nALREADY in final order there, and the other 775 descriptions only decorate\nrows the caller cannot see. Those sorts now fetch the page. Stage 2 I/O on\nsort=date: ~1,500ms -> ~78ms.\n\nscore and the lens sorts still score the whole shortlist. Their light-pass\nbound assumes every keyword hits the description, so thousands of candidates\nshare the top bound and no early cut is provable — narrowing the field there\nwould quietly change which jobs you see, which is not a perf decision to make\nsilently.\n\nVerified against production: ids and scores identical for each of\nscore/date/salary/comp/relevance/interest, on pages 1, 2 and 5.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQHjQsyG+cTzx37knTlyXzK4I0OuJNZ7D3H7R2oy0F2rPE3ItCiNTlgtHi7yGxIIXbD\nj3YZYWjlT0DGp3oI4OFw8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T20:53:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/30f3468d717f355da5a5474fe4c8f8a3d8855dfd","node_id":"C_kwDORvwX0NoAKDMwZjM0NjhkNzE3ZjM1NWRhNWE1NDc0ZmU0YzhmOGEzZDg4NTVkZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commit/0dee1be8047d9aaaa49d8121f1b5742ee79bd836","sha":"0dee1be8047d9aaaa49d8121f1b5742ee79bd836","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/0dee1be8047d9aaaa49d8121f1b5742ee79bd836"}],"sha":"30f3468d717f355da5a5474fe4c8f8a3d8855dfd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/30f3468d717f355da5a5474fe4c8f8a3d8855dfd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/commits/0dee1be8047d9aaaa49d8121f1b5742ee79bd836/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:37:43Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:37:56Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat: an unanswered-questions queue, so an answer is given once\n\nThe runner can only answer a question it has seen before, and it already\nreports the ones it cannot — they ride along in applications.evidence as\n`unmatched` on every fill. That report dead-ended: the owner had to read a CLI\nlisting and hand-edit a JSON file on the runner''s machine, so in practice the\nsame question blocked application after application. Three real Coinbase and\nPinterest fills stalled on 13, 13 and 3 questions today, mostly the same ones.\n\nThe Applications tab now shows them, ordered by what each is COSTING — how many\napplications it actually stopped — because it is a work list, not a log.\nAnswering stores it against the NORMALIZED question, so the next board that\nwords it differently gets the same answer. That is the whole feature: \"Preferred\nPronouns\", \"preferred pronouns *\" and \"Preferred pronouns:\" are one question.\n\nThe queue is DERIVED from evidence rather than kept in a table of its own. The\nrunner already posts what it could not answer, so a second write path would be\nanother thing to keep in step — and one that could disagree with the evidence\nthe owner is reading on the same screen.\n\nAn empty answer is allowed and means \"leave this blank on the form\". Without it\na question the owner wants skipped could never leave the queue.\n\nPRIVACY: this reverses an explicit earlier decision, and the reversal is the\npoint of the feature, so it is written down rather than absorbed.\nhadoku-scrape''s ApplicantProfile keeps demographic answers on the runner''s disk\n\"so they never travel through an API that a board, a proxy or a log could see\".\nAnswers saved here DO cross the API and DO sit in D1. It applies only to\nanswers the owner types into the UI: nothing in the local file is migrated, and\nthe runner still reads that file.\n\nworker/src/questionKey.ts mirrors _answers.py::normalize and says so in both\nplaces. If they drift the site will cheerfully save an answer the runner never\nfinds, and the question will keep returning to the queue looking unanswered —\na silent failure with no error anywhere.","tree":{"sha":"adc5a2122f3cbd0cb8d7b741d12ff9de8a10fc42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/trees/adc5a2122f3cbd0cb8d7b741d12ff9de8a10fc42"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-jobplatform/git/commits/0dee1be8047d9aaaa49d8121f1b5742ee79bd836","verification":{"payload":"tree adc5a2122f3cbd0cb8d7b741d12ff9de8a10fc42\nparent d2049a34a94b467172f06159861e6748e5c216dd\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788295063 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788295076 -0700\n\nfeat: an unanswered-questions queue, so an answer is given once\n\nThe runner can only answer a question it has seen before, and it already\nreports the ones it cannot — they ride along in applications.evidence as\n`unmatched` on every fill. That report dead-ended: the owner had to read a CLI\nlisting and hand-edit a JSON file on the runner''s machine, so in practice the\nsame question blocked application after application. Three real Coinbase and\nPinterest fills stalled on 13, 13 and 3 questions today, mostly the same ones.\n\nThe Applications tab now shows them, ordered by what each is COSTING — how many\napplications it actually stopped — because it is a work list, not a log.\nAnswering stores it against the NORMALIZED question, so the next board that\nwords it differently gets the same answer. That is the whole feature: \"Preferred\nPronouns\", \"preferred pronouns *\" and \"Preferred pronouns:\" are one question.\n\nThe queue is DERIVED from evidence rather than kept in a table of its own. The\nrunner already posts what it could not answer, so a second write path would be\nanother thing to keep in step — and one that could disagree with the evidence\nthe owner is reading on the same screen.\n\nAn empty answer is allowed and means \"leave this blank on the form\". Without it\na question the owner wants skipped could never leave the queue.\n\nPRIVACY: this reverses an explicit earlier decision, and the reversal is the\npoint of the feature, so it is written down rather than absorbed.\nhadoku-scrape''s ApplicantProfile keeps demographic answers on the runner''s disk\n\"so they never travel through an API that a board, a proxy or a log could see\".\nAnswers saved here DO cross the API and DO sit in D1. It applies only to\nanswers the owner types into the UI: nothing in the local file is migrated, and\nthe runner still reads that file.\n\nworker/src/questionKey.ts mirrors _answers.py::normalize and says so in both\nplaces. If they drift the site will cheerfully save an answer the runner never\nfinds, and the question will keep returning to the queue looking unanswered —\na silent failure with no error anywhere.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQOF56VT5fO0XL+VDL2FxXN4cqn9nYgbpho42mUP4cAEYyX4OWdhIxrWnLGq56FDA3A\n9D4zbM47nJt/KFV3mgPAM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T20:40:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/follo