ame":"Praveen VR"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-30T16:56:47Z","committedDate":"2026-08-30T16:56:47Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"praveen-vr-moonhive","providerType":"User"},"email":"praveen.vr@moonhive.in","name":"Praveen VR"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:20:56.696Z","repositoryId":1191052108,"sha":"72ee41cded87f0c4d11cfcac5b7a6b7eaf65b5a2"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"praveen-vr-moonhive","providerType":"User"},"email":"praveen.vr@moonhive.in","name":"Praveen VR"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-30T13:03:34Z","committedDate":"2026-08-30T13:03:34Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"praveen-vr-moonhive","providerType":"User"},"email":"praveen.vr@moonhive.in","name":"Praveen VR"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:20:56.696Z","repositoryId":1191052108,"sha":"73e19624a6e8ce9ac0b55f2c1fbf41f57d88ac8f"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"praveen-vr-moonhive","providerType":"User"},"email":"praveen.vr@moonhive.in","name":"Praveen VR"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-30T12:32:30Z","committedDate":"2026-08-30T12:38:05Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"praveen-vr-moonhive","providerType":"User"},"email":"praveen.vr@moonhive.in","name":"Praveen VR"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:20:56.696Z","repositoryId":1191052108,"sha":"b601a94eea67ab0ce07c13b6a8c1169ed35abaac"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:20:56.696Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/201938844?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anusreekpcreatives/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anusreekpcreatives/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anusreekpcreatives/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anusreekpcreatives/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anusreekpcreatives","id":201938844,"login":"anusreekpcreatives","node_id":"U_kgDODAlXnA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anusreekpcreatives/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anusreekpcreatives/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anusreekpcreatives/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anusreekpcreatives/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anusreekpcreatives/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anusreekpcreatives","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-crm-fe/commits/c5cf84a66aa38fbed1842d39616dacef2e3521b1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T13:12:53Z","email":"anusree.k.p@creatives.moonhive.in","name":"anusreekpcreatives"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T13:12:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(crm-fe): searchable, paged Project picker for tasks and deal project link (b9e59049) (#67)\n\n* fix(crm-fe): searchable, paged Project picker for tasks and deal project link\n\nThe Project field in the task modal was a native <select> fed by one\ngetProjects() call capped at limit=100: it could not be searched, projects\nbeyond the first 100 were unreachable, a failed load looked like \"no\nprojects\", and a selected project outside the first page had no option.\n\nAdd ProjectSelect: debounced server-side search + paging against the Projects\nbackend, error state with Retry, selection resolved by id, closed\n(completed/cancelled/archived) projects hidden, keyboard support. Add\ncrmService.searchProjects (strips PostgREST filter syntax, lets errors\npropagate). Use the picker in TaskModal and in DealDetailPage''s \"Link\nExisting Project\" step. Pulse task b9e59049.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(crm-fe): keep the Lead Quick View panel invisible when no lead is selected\n\nThe panel was hidden only by translate-x-full. When that transform did not\napply (seen on a feature-branch preview) an empty white 420px panel covered the\nright side of the Leads grid. Closed now also means invisible, non-interactive\nand aria-hidden; visibility transitions with the transform so the slide-out\nanimation is unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(crm-fe): render the Lead Quick View on document.body, below the shell NavBar\n\nOn a feature-branch preview the Quick View opened half under the shell header\nwith the grid''s header cells painting over it and the tabs run together.\nThe panel was `fixed top-0 z-[500]` inside the page: any transformed or\nfiltered ancestor in the shell layout changes what `fixed` positions against,\nand z-500 tied with the NavBar (z-500; the shell reserves z-490 as the MFE\nceiling).\n\nRender it through a portal on document.body so it always positions against the\nviewport, and place it below the 56px NavBar (top-14) at z-[490] (backdrop\nz-[480]). Open/close behaviour and animation are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Revert \"fix(crm-fe): render the Lead Quick View on document.body, below the shell NavBar\"\n\nThis reverts commit fee6bdb47102eba5e8b0784d720772caf4c34588.\n\n* test(crm-fe): 100% line/branch/function coverage for the Project picker\n\nAdds BDD specs closing every gap in ProjectSelect.tsx and\ncrmService.searchProjects: label/code fallbacks, rows without status, empty\nor malformed responses, selection resolved by id (null, failure, stale\nanswers), outside click, arrow/enter/escape keys, disabled state, de-duplicated\npaging, stale search failures, and response-shape defaults.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(crm-fe): Project picker corner cases - closed-page read-ahead, quote sanitising, a11y\n\n- A page made up entirely of closed (completed/cancelled/archived) projects no\n  longer shows \"No projects found\" over more pages: reading continues, bounded\n  to 5 pages, then \"Load more\" stays available. The stored page now tracks the\n  last page actually read, so \"Load more\" never skips one.\n- searchProjects also strips double quotes from the term (PostgREST filter syntax).\n- Listbox semantics: unique ids, aria-controls, and aria-activedescendant so the\n  highlighted option is announced.\n- Tests: read-ahead cases, a11y, quotes, and the deal \"Link Existing Project\"\n  flow through the picker (link, nothing picked, link failure).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Revert \"fix(crm-fe): keep the Lead Quick View panel invisible when no lead is selected\"\n\nThis reverts commit 475795548a23e8255ab13ffdd0b4b1c1a6f43574.\n\n* fix(crm-fe): keyboard-accessible Project picker, memoised label, drop leftover fragment\n\n- ProjectSelect: closed control is a real button (role=combobox, aria-haspopup,\n  aria-expanded, aria-controls) opened by Enter/Space/ArrowDown/ArrowUp; open\n  state keeps focus in the search box with aria-activedescendant, Escape and\n  selection return focus to the trigger, Tab closes without trapping.\n  Clear button is now a sibling control, not nested in the combobox.\n- ProjectSelect: selected label derived with useMemo; getProjectById runs once\n  per selected id instead of on every options change.\n- DealDetailPage: unwrap the leftover {(<>...</>)} around the link controls.\n- Add keyboard/aria/memoisation tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"01835d03d8d2408909dd06b9499cd99c09d0e3cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-crm-fe/git/trees/01835d03d8d2408909dd06b9499cd99c09d0e3cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-crm-fe/git/commits/c5cf84a66aa38fbed1842d39616dacef2e3521b1","verification":{"payload":"tree 01835d03d8d2408909dd06b9499cd99c09d0e3cb\nparent 0abf5589defa1934cc40d33f475ddf2ea8e78cf1\nauthor anusreekpcreatives <anusree.k.p@creatives.moonhive.in> 1791292373 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791292373 +0400\n\nfix(crm-fe): searchable, paged Project picker for tasks and deal project link (b9e59049) (#67)\n\n* fix(crm-fe): searchable, paged Project picker for tasks and deal project link\n\nThe Project field in the task modal was a native <select> fed by one\ngetProjects() call capped at limit=100: it could not be searched, projects\nbeyond the first 100 were unreachable, a failed load looked like \"no\nprojects\", and a selected project outside the first page had no option.\n\nAdd ProjectSelect: debounced server-side search + paging against the Projects\nbackend, error state with Retry, selection resolved by id, closed\n(completed/cancelled/archived) projects hidden, keyboard support. Add\ncrmService.searchProjects (strips PostgREST filter syntax, lets errors\npropagate). Use the picker in TaskModal and in DealDetailPage''s \"Link\nExisting Project\" step. Pulse task b9e59049.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(crm-fe): keep the Lead Quick View panel invisible when no lead is selected\n\nThe panel was hidden only by translate-x-full. When that transform did not\napply (seen on a feature-branch preview) an empty white 420px panel covered the\nright side of the Leads grid. Closed now also means invisible, non-interactive\nand aria-hidden; visibility transitions with the transform so the slide-out\nanimation is unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(crm-fe): render the Lead Quick View on document.body, below the shell NavBar\n\nOn a feature-branch preview the Quick View opened half under the shell header\nwith the grid''s header cells painting over it and the tabs run together.\nThe panel was `fixed top-0 z-[500]` inside the page: any transformed or\nfiltered ancestor in the shell layout changes what `fixed` positions against,\nand z-500 tied with the NavBar (z-500; the shell reserves z-490 as the MFE\nceiling).\n\nRender it through a portal on document.body so it always positions against the\nviewport, and place it below the 56px NavBar (top-14) at z-[490] (backdrop\nz-[480]). Open/close behaviour and animation are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Revert \"fix(crm-fe): render the Lead Quick View on document.body, below the shell NavBar\"\n\nThis reverts commit fee6bdb47102eba5e8b0784d720772caf4c34588.\n\n* test(crm-fe): 100% line/branch/function coverage for the Project picker\n\nAdds BDD specs closing every gap in ProjectSelect.tsx and\ncrmService.searchProjects: label/code fallbacks, rows without status, empty\nor malformed responses, selection resolved by id (null, failure, stale\nanswers), outside click, arrow/enter/escape keys, disabled state, de-duplicated\npaging, stale search failures, and response-shape defaults.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(crm-fe): Project picker corner cases - closed-page read-ahead, quote sanitising, a11y\n\n- A page made up entirely of closed (completed/cancelled/archived) projects no\n  longer shows \"No projects found\" over more pages: reading continues, bounded\n  to 5 pages, then \"Load more\" stays available. The stored page now tracks the\n  last page actually read, so \"Load more\" never skips one.\n- searchProjects also strips double quotes from the term (PostgREST filter syntax).\n- Listbox semantics: unique ids, aria-controls, and aria-activedescendant so the\n  highlighted option is announced.\n- Tests: read-ahead cases, a11y, quotes, and the deal \"Link Existing Project\"\n  flow through the picker (link, nothing picked, link failure).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Revert \"fix(crm-fe): keep the Lead Quick View panel invisible when no lead is selected\"\n\nThis reverts commit 475795548a23e8255ab13ffdd0b4b1c1a6f43574.\n\n* fix(crm-fe): keyboard-accessible Project picker, memoised label, drop leftover fragment\n\n- ProjectSelect: closed control is a real button (role=combobox, aria-haspopup,\n  aria-expanded, aria-controls) opened by Enter/Space/ArrowDown/ArrowUp; open\n  state keeps focus in the search box with aria-activedescendant, Escape and\n  selection return focus to the trigger, Tab closes without trapping.\n  Clear button is now a sibling control, not nested in the combobox.\n- ProjectSelect: selected label derived with useMemo; getProjectById runs once\n  per selected id instead of on every options change.\n- DealDetailPage: unwrap the leftover {(<>...</>)} around the link controls.\n- Add keyboard/aria/memoisation tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxPPVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPPIQAK9Fd1yxTcm5zJ69Zh3FcQDW\nvn3mKvOwTYt2bZdaMkbr+4fufwfiZYKIM7YyjnhOW2EsbQo9zOg56KmSRgy29+Fq\nCXF1vR8IzKxwHpQn8H/gHKxB7eQJtrJIDH8WwZ6ABMAGH4hvJPwjrZJIC/1mSclh\nhCuf30H7HahTuuJPuViqmtu6pw6FtCF3ZV3IfRsMNh9xfC753ORSpVNl1443cl85\ndvInqaHnOiNtQKt5m51zmG3Df8b9FDkNfM8wA5C52q0gB/eZs0CvsbIIYTRrO3qz\nZOwWIzGEkyTVwV+ZrTTViNK6XUAjRDi6lnNm2AESm6RXI2YeuRIlDNW0JdZuLiTS\ngHFSgO8lut0OvX+7QNguVajjK/gj9n0AO8WtCtHcK2Um4iaS5zXMpHLAXFl2Po32\nOWbpmiZhzjBF9hmXjPPVjCz6SJpIYrTWeJu9vawhEkV3oNySb7a6QlhK9eCKGHBZ\npTmhXe97zZPrh4xUHyz0U1BOuX5/mcshXK175UrdkjPZc0uDu6dIkAh3A5L7rsL3\nQxSpeOv/uM0anXYnDVsbXWO5YCjtmHNWue2v9trJ5BTrr+BpcZwWAGHd/qm7dVBt\nuAqfxp4DoCc7Xlx+KS2EUVCTia3n8uUDgBnL6Etd06jRjAgvLx2MQhidfmeSDt/q\nv3lFoCHQU/uoomD+wtEF\n=NyWj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T13:12:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Neonbee-ai/so360-crm-fe/commit/c5cf84a66aa38fbed1842d39616dacef2e3521b1","node_id":"C_kwDORv4DTNoAKGM1Y2Y4NGE2NmFhMzhmYmVkMTg0MmQzOTYxNmRhY2VmMmUzNTIxYjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Neonbee-ai/so360-crm-fe/commit/0abf5589defa1934cc40d33f475ddf2ea8e78cf1","sha":"0abf5589defa1934cc40d33f475ddf2ea8e78cf1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-crm-fe/commits/0abf5589defa1934cc40d33f475ddf2ea8e78cf1"}],"sha":"c5cf84a66aa38fbed1842d39616dacef2e3521b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-crm-fe/commits/c5cf84a66aa38fbed1842d39616dacef2e3521b1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/201938844?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anusreekpcreatives/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anusreekpcreatives/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anusreekpcreatives/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anusreekpcreatives/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anusreekpcreatives","id":201938844,"login":"anusreekpcreatives","node_id":"U_kgDODAlXnA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anusreekpcreatives/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anusreekpcreatives/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anusreekpcreatives/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anusreekpcreatives/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anusreekpcreatives/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anusreekpcreatives","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-crm-fe/commits/0abf5589defa1934cc40d33f475ddf2ea8e78cf1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T10:55:45Z","email":"anusree.k.p@creatives.moonhive.in","name":"anusreekpcreatives"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T10:55:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(crm-fe): single-flight, authoritative Lead Detail profile save (29299155) (#59)\n\n* fix(crm-fe): make Lead Detail profile save single-flight and authoritative\n\nThe profile Save could be clicked repeatedly while the PATCH was in flight,\nand the editor closed before the persisted lead was reloaded. Save is now\ndisabled with a spinner while saving, and edit mode exits only after the\nrefetched lead is on screen. Failed saves keep the editor open (task 29299155).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(crm-fe): BDD scenarios for single-flight, authoritative lead profile save\n\nDrops the in-handler isSavingInfo guard: the button is disabled while\nsaving, so React never dispatches the click and the branch was unreachable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(crm-fe): keep lead editor open when the post-save reload fails\n\nfetchLeadData now resolves true/false; the profile save keeps edit mode open with the user''s values and shows an error if the reload fails. Other callers unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"355de3951664054ae546cf1088c52fce0629719b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-crm-fe/git/trees/355de3951664054ae546cf1088c52fce0629719b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-crm-fe/git/commits/0abf5589defa1934cc40d33f475ddf2ea8e78cf1","verification":{"payload":"tree 355de3951664054ae546cf1088c52fce0629719b\nparent 5635460e6e500cb0499527e63432b16407e80201\nauthor anusreekpcreatives <anusree.k.p@creatives.moonhive.in> 1791284145 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791284145 +0400\n\nfix(crm-fe): single-flight, authoritative Lead Detail profile save (29299155) (#59)\n\n* fix(crm-fe): make Lead Detail profile save single-flight and authoritative\n\nThe profile Save could be clicked repeatedly while the PATCH was in flight,\nand the editor closed before the persisted lead was reloaded. Save is now\ndisabled with a spinner while saving, and edit mode exits only after the\nrefetched lead is on screen. Failed saves keep the editor open (task 29299155).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(crm-fe): BDD scenarios for single-flight, authoritative lead profile save\n\nDrops the in-handler isSavingInfo guard: the button is disabled while\nsaving, so React never dispatches the click and the branch was unreachable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(crm-fe): keep lead editor open when the post-save reload fails\n\nfetchLeadData now resolves true/false; the profile save keeps edit mode open with the user''s values and shows an error if the reload fails. Other callers unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxNOxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3VwQAC7HR/BT6FdBI2VV7rlbGGwl\ngVpRhbbkua2AgvDrz5WaZTTttp2Ee9RZFjpTIte+GGSHm6gpVcmIzXZbye1AqAza\nWOt21i54CcDy/vU45fuDDs/7Qp5M91Rmy4kHi9KgO3Qe/MyBfw77VJ0qAXQ7Xe65\nHk/LIGenqmxFR29Zd3xAaP3q3+mygSQb8vUOptqkzk8lW+EPUVkDNVN9O0y1kW+F\n2LPJrTaT1fTwMlGeL7d/izvzD7Os4qLbdMRP7CuJNI4CL1tywHieWacqe6FvLKxr\nDcTkSSiuHE4jLErpZ6+vvuszjdHV7oyEpNNWGRZN6A7Dqdl3Pqgpws5cxmy