vr-moonhive/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-crm-fe/commits/8e5467529cd707df895596c3bbc42c7612698d9a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T15:09:56Z","email":"165479734+praveen-vr-moonhive@users.noreply.github.com","name":"praveen-vr-moonhive"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T15:09:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(crm-fe): scope the CRM users cache to the current org (#47)\n\n* test(crm-fe): cover 409 conflict and status-less network errors in TaskModal (#45)\n\nTask creation error surfacing (src/pages/components/TaskModal.tsx:198-211)\nalready routes 4xx messages to the user and falls back to a generic message\nfor 5xx/network failures. Investigation confirmed this is the only task\ncreation entry point across the CRM FE and the logic is already correct —\nno production code change needed. Adds the two missing BDD cases the task\ncalled out explicitly: a 409 conflict reason reaching the user, and a\nstatus-less network/timeout error (axios-shaped) correctly falling back to\nthe generic message instead of leaking \"Network Error\".\n\nPulse: 512f7793\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X7ekRzGgY7zcmJoAkbLwHJ\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(crm-fe): scope the CRM users cache to the current org\n\nUSERS_CACHE (the client-side cache mapUser() falls back to when the backend\ndoesn''t embed an owner object on leads/deals) was a single module-level Map\nkeyed only by user id, populated by getUsers() and never cleared or\norg-scoped. Switching organizations in the same tab left previously-cached\nUser objects in place, so a lead''s owner_id could resolve against a stale\nentry from a different org — producing exactly the reported name/avatar\nmismatch on the Leads list.\n\nCache entries are now keyed by `${orgId}:${userId}`, and the cache is cleared\non setOrgId() so entries can''t accumulate indefinitely across a long session.\n\nPulse: b764367a\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CoPFunsa4pyJ3kFfQzcEzM\n\n* test(crm-fe): cover org-scoped owner cache + fix a stale-cache edge case it found\n\nAdded BDD coverage for the b764367a fix (USERS_CACHE keyed by org, cleared on\nswitch). Writing the \"switch to org B, then back to org A\" scenario surfaced a\nreal gap in the original fix: getUsers() is memoized in orgStaticCache, so\nswitching back to a recently-visited org within its 30s TTL served the cached\nuser list from a cache-hit that skips the fetcher entirely — and skips the\nUSERS_CACHE repopulation side effect inside it, since USERS_CACHE had just\nbeen cleared by setOrgId(). Leads would show \"Unknown User\" until the TTL\nexpired.\n\nFixed by invalidating the target org''s orgStaticCache `users|<id>` entry on\nswitch, forcing a fresh fetch that repopulates USERS_CACHE correctly.\n\nPulse: b764367a\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CoPFunsa4pyJ3kFfQzcEzM\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d0ae41d32614d0ebb97e7e5d7d39ff7f7beb8e00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-crm-fe/git/trees/d0ae41d32614d0ebb97e7e5d7d39ff7f7beb8e00"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-crm-fe/git/commits/8e5467529cd707df895596c3bbc42c7612698d9a","verification":{"payload":"tree d0ae41d32614d0ebb97e7e5d7d39ff7f7beb8e00\nparent 9c4cb5884f9e3ccfba5abb6937a56af0ad0b1770\nauthor praveen-vr-moonhive <165479734+praveen-vr-moonhive@users.noreply.github.com> 1790003396 +0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790003396 +0400\n\nfix(crm-fe): scope the CRM users cache to the current org (#47)\n\n* test(crm-fe): cover 409 conflict and status-less network errors in TaskModal (#45)\n\nTask creation error surfacing (src/pages/components/TaskModal.tsx:198-211)\nalready routes 4xx messages to the user and falls back to a generic message\nfor 5xx/network failures. Investigation confirmed this is the only task\ncreation entry point across the CRM FE and the logic is already correct —\nno production code change needed. Adds the two missing BDD cases the task\ncalled out explicitly: a 409 conflict reason reaching the user, and a\nstatus-less network/timeout error (axios-shaped) correctly falling back to\nthe generic message instead of leaking \"Network Error\".\n\nPulse: 512f7793\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X7ekRzGgY7zcmJoAkbLwHJ\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(crm-fe): scope the CRM users cache to the current org\n\nUSERS_CACHE (the client-side cache mapUser() falls back to when the backend\ndoesn''t embed an owner object on leads/deals) was a single module-level Map\nkeyed only by user id, populated by getUsers() and never cleared or\norg-scoped. Switching organizations in the same tab left previously-cached\nUser objects in place, so a lead''s owner_id could resolve against a stale\nentry from a different org — producing exactly the reported name/avatar\nmismatch on the Leads list.\n\nCache entries are now keyed by `${orgId}:${userId}`, and the cache is cleared\non setOrgId() so entries can''t accumulate indefinitely across a long session.\n\nPulse: b764367a\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CoPFunsa4pyJ3kFfQzcEzM\n\n* test(crm-fe): cover org-scoped owner cache + fix a stale-cache edge case it found\n\nAdded BDD coverage for the b764367a fix (USERS_CACHE keyed by org, cleared on\nswitch). Writing the \"switch to org B, then back to org A\" scenario surfaced a\nreal gap in the original fix: getUsers() is memoized in orgStaticCache, so\nswitching back to a recently-visited org within its 30s TTL served the cached\nuser list from a cache-hit that skips the fetcher entirely — and skips the\nUSERS_CACHE repopulation side effect inside it, since USERS_CACHE had just\nbeen cleared by setOrgId(). Leads would show \"Unknown User\" until the TTL\nexpired.\n\nFixed by invalidating the target org''s orgStaticCache `users|<id>` entry on\nswitch, forcing a fresh fetch that repopulates USERS_CACHE correctly.\n\nPulse: b764367a\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CoPFunsa4pyJ3kFfQzcEzM\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsUjECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZZ0QAHsCSq+h7IWIWZW7hKFyW9YP\n9wR1wYFjRdOacKraDl7aIphwBBOh5H8Ldqv0isjm1RaXzFTT2FFBxyrRhawkRGCA\nWgjPVJL92VJPXDOIdfSL4hnOna5PwZ5ZFzyECmPceSXgp/XnyOg3/krwg00N6EZG\nUfYnYwZFG19vu5/HOgT94mwpCU4YDTxziQOpHt9R8DlYsN96JUR4bg/ITjZD1mQ2\nzX1se4Dqi2uhWXeeO3vFvDhCrciJ+yDaZ4IRWHV1pvzLkoxRjJePlbL6XQcOuOQI\nTxamzGEzbsoG4twrcNQhXESUmck7IeRvFFdJqCWoIw95qKyYj0wOxwcj9FSi4jdc\neuQa1yRLMMTxmVWf1+tH54Avh/0UU1/z5otoP+W49bQOKyrp9vmtMchPORgzbPs8\nc+eTDPTT7JDP4C5JJIt6Abc9NK0edVNC05vOFihlN7DR3psRdxaJXqxjjZXOvcAr\nuL6+4IZQZZFy45cR9XTEvZAuWwqvL4JbgmTW1ou0feId2GXFGk/0Hq9s2nHty1r2\njDr7uouDhuJFeF3Y/JJjH7HgGdQwKLWy9bmeyT/tHwx725KTNBSBVDS2020RhkPH\nZdwrCdjtQF4k6nExnyNfp/k0mbqoLBcnJWem/Z6RW37ALLMBbmEgU20NCZ21IRB2\nMKXJFz+L+yfhjIWOqlOz\n=u+OI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T15:09:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Neonbee-ai/so360-crm-fe/commit/8e5467529cd707df895596c3bbc42c7612698d9a","node_id":"C_kwDORv4DTNoAKDhlNTQ2NzUyOWNkNzA3ZGY4OTU1OTZjM2JiYzQyYzc2MTI2OThkOWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Neonbee-ai/so360-crm-fe/commit/9c4cb5884f9e3ccfba5abb6937a56af0ad0b1770","sha":"9c4cb5884f9e3ccfba5abb6937a56af0ad0b1770","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-crm-fe/commits/9c4cb5884f9e3ccfba5abb6937a56af0ad0b1770"}],"sha":"8e5467529cd707df895596c3bbc42c7612698d9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-crm-fe/commits/8e5467529cd707df895596c3bbc42c7612698d9a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/165479734?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/praveen-vr-moonhive","id":165479734,"login":"praveen-vr-moonhive","node_id":"U_kgDOCd0FNg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-crm-fe/commits/9c4cb5884f9e3ccfba5abb6937a56af0ad0b1770/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T14:26:27Z","email":"165479734+praveen-vr-moonhive@users.noreply.github.com","name":"praveen-vr-moonhive"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T14:26:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(crm-fe): Deal Lifecycle stepper reads real configured pipeline stages (#46)\n\n* test(crm-fe): cover 409 conflict and status-less network errors in TaskModal (#45)\n\nTask creation error surfacing (src/pages/components/TaskModal.tsx:198-211)\nalready routes 4xx messages to the user and falls back to a generic message\nfor 5xx/network failures. Investigation confirmed this is the only task\ncreation entry point across the CRM FE and the logic is already correct —\nno production code change needed. Adds the two missing BDD cases the task\ncalled out explicitly: a 409 conflict reason reaching the user, and a\nstatus-less network/timeout error (axios-shaped) correctly falling back to\nthe generic message instead of leaking \"Network Error\".\n\nPulse: 512f7793\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X7ekRzGgY7zcmJoAkbLwHJ\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(crm-fe): Deal Lifecycle stepper now reads the real configured pipeline stages\n\nDealLifecycleStepper was fully hardcoded (FORWARD_STATES/STATE_LABELS: a fixed\nnew/qualified/proposal/negotiation/won map), so it silently ignored each org''s\nactual pipeline_stages configuration and always rendered the same 5 generic\nEnglish labels. The Deal Stage dropdown next to it was already correct — it\nreads real dealStages from Settings — which made the dropdown look \"wrong\"\nnext to the Lifecycle stepper''s fake-but-readable labels.\n\nThe stepper now takes the same dealStages (id/name/type) already fetched for\nthe dropdown and the deal''s actual stage_id, so both components share one\nsource of truth per the ticket''s acceptance criteria. Stage type (WON/LOST)\nnow drives the terminal/lost-banner behavior instead of string-matching a\nfixed key.\n\nPulse: 495b4831\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CoPFunsa4pyJ3kFfQzcEzM\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"82dc7d4483777c71e4f764fa54d649269d844dab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-crm-fe/git/trees/82dc7d4483777c71e4f764fa54d649269d844dab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-crm-fe/git/commits/9c4cb5884f9e3ccfba5abb6937a56af0ad0b1770","verification":{"payload":"tree 82dc7d4483777c71e4f764fa54d649269d844dab\nparent 2ffc2a10d77203595dde0a663f6e6035bc26060d\nauthor praveen-vr-moonhive <165479734+praveen-vr-moonhive@users.noreply.github.com> 1790000787 +0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790000787 +0400\n\nfix(crm-fe): Deal Lifecycle stepper reads real configured pipeline stages (#46)\n\n* test(crm-fe): cover 409 conflict and status-less network errors in TaskModal (#45)\n\nTask creation error surfacing (src/pages/components/TaskModal.tsx:198-211)\nalready routes 4xx messages to the user and falls back to a generic message\nfor 5xx/network failures. Investigation confirmed this is the only task\ncreation entry point across the CRM FE and the logic is already correct —\nno production code change needed. Adds the two missing BDD cases the task\ncalled out explicitly: a 409 conflict reason reaching the user, and a\nstatus-less network/timeout error (axios-shaped) correctly falling back to\nthe generic message instead of leaking \"Network Error\".\n\nPulse: 512f7793\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X7ekRzGgY7zcmJoAkbLwHJ\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(crm-fe): Deal Lifecycle stepper now reads the real configured pipeline stages\n\nDealLifecycleStepper was fully hardcoded (FORWARD_STATES/STATE_LABELS: a fixed\nnew/qualified/proposal/negotiation/won map), so it silently ignored each org''s\nactual pipeline_stages configuration and always rendered the same 5 generic\nEnglish labels. The Deal Stage dropdown next to it was already correct — it\nreads real dealStages from Settings — which made the dropdown look \"wrong\"\nnext to the Lifecycle stepper''s fake-but-readable labels.\n\nThe stepper now takes the same dealStages (id/name/type) already fetched for\nthe dropdown and the deal''s actual stage_id, so both components share one\nsource of truth per the ticket''s acceptance criteria. Stage type (WON/LOST)\nnow drives the terminal/lost-banner behavior instead of string-matching a\nfixed key.\n\nPulse: 495b4831\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CoPFunsa4pyJ3kFfQzcEzM\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsT6TCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/iMQABrm3oppTLLw6cu0pA2Sei9R\nEkGyEEl8OW9Pb5ELBBucsxcKWgIk8IghC61fhbGLZkxdg8RObez/lVdsIqtLQJRQ\nSVetKC2w1HBGNwiZXGQnbuTMBvEEsz1a2hHI4IVFjkDzE3VS3BWJLitYAjq+Tb0/\nPumZhxIyzEzwU9ZyVBssr4GhzeERZ/jUABpxJU2Zt3zJCNCiUncHc0YcFUniwLMV\n5BFDLkR47jmYKMAoALJ9ru11dozPsqhePeM16Lx7zh+UsSLOuenungif5RxyNTHe\nkKQhmlwf06XZS6bndJfLjZ9BUxHqoxuCwaygP5NAA4Yh3IO/9oJlTximyyDRXn9i\nAdOzKmM3AEfXPSmxinNyEqXZl1WA+bS1by/UMt5RMGqqAkH2AlMMW6gT9+bBRhlr\ncl4Y7bvY6H/ByBBpEFpZpUiZ6XHsRSIDrrf6qk+81WBgjtR/fhYFY+Ho7ZNd6cRm\niuSyXQmEyFiGNiMqcdaSHNtJo9AeedRoG+T4B0vdPf5S7CwPjtLMd6a0e4PdA0xk\nkVijNt2Ve+ReMDR35UAI75HtBVUaxHkEvGSBleVrm5lFMrnX9W2hPukGN