starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-crm-fe/commits/5d26c55a8aab6ecd4cf323cc97b9d1947311d234/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T10:19:31Z","email":"praveen.vr@moonhive.in","name":"Praveen VR"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T10:19:31Z","email":"praveen.vr@moonhive.in","name":"Praveen VR"},"message":"feat(crm-fe): redesign notes timeline for thread clarity\n\nPulse dfae6177 — Customer Notes Timeline redesign. LeadDetailPage''s Notes\ntab (shared by both Lead and Customer detail routes) gets:\n\n- Each top-level note wrapped in its own card (bg-slate-900/40 border\n  border-slate-800 rounded-xl), replacing the flat amber-border list.\n- Replies nested under a clear connector (border-l-2 border-slate-700/60)\n  visually distinct from the parent card''s own border.\n- Reply composer collapsed behind a \"Reply\" affordance, expanding on\n  click and collapsing again after a successful submit.\n- Consecutive replies from the same author grouped under one\n  author/timestamp header instead of repeating it per reply.\n- Empty-state copy now reads \"lead\" or \"customer\" based on\n  isCustomerDetailRoute instead of always saying \"lead\".\n\nDealDetailPage.tsx has its own separate Notes tab and is untouched.\n\nAdds BDD coverage in LeadDetailPage.bdd.test.tsx for card isolation,\nreply nesting/indentation, composer collapse/expand-on-submit, reply\ngrouping, and entity-agnostic empty-state copy on both routes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ea943a8424bf684834433314a630155c4f39a0fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-crm-fe/git/trees/ea943a8424bf684834433314a630155c4f39a0fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-crm-fe/git/commits/5d26c55a