r-moonhive/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-crm-fe/commits/937b3366fa1ecab3dd341c2e24e67b498a52a160/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T17:26:31Z","email":"praveen.vr@moonhive.in","name":"Praveen VR"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T17:26:31Z","email":"praveen.vr@moonhive.in","name":"Praveen VR"},"message":"fix(targets): require an owner before an individual plan can be saved\n\nThe New Plan form let owner_type stay ''rep'' with no PersonPicker\nselection, silently omitting owner_id from the create payload. The\nbackend then persisted the plan with owner_id NULL, which the Overview\npage''s owner-scoped query can never match — the plan existed but\nOverview kept showing \"No active target plan for this period\".\n\ncanSubmit now also requires ownerId when ownerType is ''rep'', matching\nthe new backend guard in so360-crm-be. org/team plans are unaffected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XDU8JqXooyw6YUNoNW74be","tree":{"sha":"dd88ff7950a3ded451d75a2b9089093a3e88a415","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-crm-fe/git/trees/dd88ff7950a3ded451d75a2b9089093a3e88a415"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-crm-fe/git/commits/937b3366fa1ecab3dd341c2e24e67b498a52a160","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/165479734?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive/events{/privacy}","followers