s/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anusreekpcreatives/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anusreekpcreatives/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anusreekpcreatives","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-inventory-fe/commits/afb1b4e3005ce275b472281545774c7c669a5b47/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T12:49:38Z","email":"anusree.k.p@creatives.moonhive.in","name":"anusreekpcreatives"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T12:49:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(settings): numeric bounds and category reset on item attributes (#26)\n\n* fix(settings): numeric bounds and category reset on item attributes\n\nPulse c4e63e84.\n\n- Number/Currency attributes get optional Minimum/Maximum fields; only those\n  types send min_value/max_value, and min > max is caught before saving.\n  A stored minimum of 0 pre-fills as 0 on edit.\n- Editing an attribute back to \"All items\" sends category_id: null. It sent\n  undefined, which the API ignores, so the change never saved.\n- Backend error messages (e.g. duplicate key) are shown as returned.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(settings): allow null category_id in the create-attribute payload type\n\nThe attribute form now sends category_id: null for ''All items'' on edit, and\nthe shared payload type flows into createAttributeDefinition too. The API\nalready treats null as ''All items'' on create.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(settings): cover attribute bound parsing and edit prefill\n\nMoves the min/max input parser into utils/attributeBounds.ts (toBound) so its\nnon-finite fallback can be tested directly (jsdom clears such values before\nthe component sees them), and adds edit-prefill coverage for a stored maximum.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"771f630cd01e829fa80bb6078443ae962960d580","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-inventory-fe/git/trees/771f630cd01e829fa80bb6078443ae962960d580"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-inventory-fe/git/commits/afb1b4e3005ce275b472281545774c7c669a5b47","verification":{"payload":"tree 771f630cd01e829fa80bb6078443ae962960d580\nparent d4dadb9bb90512fb44365ac93ab82d694f7616c1\nauthor anusreekpcreatives <anusree.k.p@creatives.moonhive.in> 1790599778 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790599778 +0400\n\nfix(settings): numeric bounds and category reset on item attributes (#26)\n\n* fix(settings): numeric bounds and category reset on item attributes\n\nPulse c4e63e84.\n\n- Number/Currency attributes get optional Minimum/Maximum fields; only those\n  types send min_value/max_value, and min > max is caught before saving.\n  A stored minimum of 0 pre-fills as 0 on edit.\n- Editing an attribute back to \"All items\" sends category_id: null. It sent\n  undefined, which the API ignores, so the change never saved.\n- Backend error messages (e.g. duplicate key) are shown as returned.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(settings): allow null category_id in the create-attribute payload type\n\nThe attribute form now sends category_id: null for ''All items'' on edit, and\nthe shared payload type flows into createAttributeDefinition too. The API\nalready treats null as ''All items'' on create.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(settings): cover attribute bound parsing and edit prefill\n\nMoves the min/max input parser into utils/attributeBounds.ts (toBound) so its\nnon-finite fallback can be tested directly (jsdom clears such values before\nthe component sees them), and adds edit-prefill coverage for a stored maximum.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqumJiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcqIQAB5eXAdR1QBzIIhZn3ZBHfES\nCpAKzEjenaljF9T0eNOdRyXdTCU9sAI0cRzP4o15UScV0R7o5VfLZyd0DkNch0FQ\nfBlM/ke+WXaINsAKih4xrBH8jpOG4P9rXbX5KwJgg0sE71gfzczITv3XhCe8ccId\niniU7yrJAK3Oy9nt1eauuvAY0PlqiqWH2TMBMju1UmYd0Ni24dOv2DzeXGWtRTqk\nKQBJg5GXhRDPHFoO44dGBlIwXX8kVgQ2Sttxdes80CaI2j2//96AKToUNqNOv3Iq\nZfMlnl6dxI17t+YXhPGgceBcDQUqttlAUqMr+dHKzM2FRRmbGIB/MsIKzFMATgVY\nYQ4hWKK7sO3bnrngL6zigpfisVHBmje1ArQ4vwQLKiLdx+wpiXQ2QijvrZiolfdm\n2fFGjsio4RPCCnym7CiqD4chQlSlXDmswFqWaihTkxc0BeDTIYGC2zJJjrcGPsVZ\nCko+7F0Nvd+HwAWJKfHB07fz6zE7TLu8E0VsDlxbimCm98FeqXb3STIdNJiN7z87\n3oiMSWLh5fs5GzMQ3vDsbVK70k+FTIz5iuAaD2GAE4KWIX7/cbdkC2IaDDpmx1Fm\nim1f5lhqSp2b3qEyjYt2gNEOSpoFE0FV7Wxy8tFgPDiZJMOoVYLV/OjNfFXxydO6\n25I4yX5buSt16F8nZb/T\n=TpgA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T12:49:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Neonbee-ai/so360-inventory-fe/commit/afb1b4e3005ce275b472281545774c7c669a5b47","node_id":"C_kwDORv4DgdoAKGFmYjFiNGUzMDA1Y2UyNzViNDcyMjgxNTQ1Nzc0YzdjNjY5YTViNDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Neonbee-ai/so360-inventory-fe/commit/d4dadb9bb90512fb44365ac93ab82d694f7616c1","sha":"d4dadb9bb90512fb44365ac93ab82d694f7616c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-inventory-fe/commits/d4dadb9bb90512fb44365ac93ab82d694f7616c1"}],"sha":"afb1b4e3005ce275b472281545774c7c669a5b47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-inventory-fe/commits/afb1b4e3005ce275b472281545774c7c669a5b47"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/165479734?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/praveen-vr-moonhive","id":165479734,"login":"praveen-vr-moonhive","node_id":"U_kgDOCd0FNg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/praveen-vr-moonhive","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-inventory-fe/commits/d4dadb9bb90512fb44365ac93ab82d694f7616c1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T10:54:26Z","email":"165479734+praveen-vr-moonhive@users.noreply.github.com","name":"praveen-vr-moonhive"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T10:54:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(media): auto-fit storefront images before upload + spec chip on every upload spot (#30)\n\nStorefront must load in < 3 s with visually lossless images, so stored\noriginals are now capped and fitted in the browser before upload:\n\n  product photo (Item → Media, bulk import)  2000×2000 1:1  ≤1 MB\n  category banner                            2400×750 16:5  ≤800 KB\n  category image (tiles)                     1600×1600 1:1  ≤600 KB\n  category icon                              800×800   1:1  ≤300 KB\n\n- utils/imageFit.ts: one slot table + fitImageFile. SVG never touched;\n  within cap and edge → original bytes; else resize longest edge to the\n  slot edge (never upscale, no crop), WebP q0.90, step 0.02 to a 0.85\n  floor, then 10% dimension steps (products min 1200 px). No WebP encoder\n  (Safari returns PNG) → JPEG at the same quality; transparent images stay\n  PNG. Always returns a real File with the right extension.\n- components/media/ImageSpecChip: always-visible \"1:1 · 2000×2000 · ≤1 MB\"\n  chip + ⓘ popover (tap/click toggles, Esc/outside closes, keyboard\n  focusable, aria-describedby) explaining where it shows, cropping,\n  auto-shrink and accepted types.\n- MediaUploader: replaces browser-image-compression downscale (10 MB /\n  2400 px / q0.92) with fitImageFile; shows per-file notes\n  (\"photo.jpg: 6.1 MB → 640 KB (resized to 2000×2000)\"); old \"Best\n  results … 1200×1200\" text replaced by the chip.\n- CategoriesPage: banner / image / icon zones auto-fit to their slots,\n  labels become plain names with the chip, per-upload note shown.\n- Bulk import ImageUploadStep: chip + per-file auto-fit with size result\n  in the list; fitted names map back to the original filename; files\n  still over the 5 MB bulk limit are failed locally; upload errors no\n  longer leave the step stuck on \"Uploading…\".\n- utils/imageRatio: badge hints now recommend 2000×2000 for products;\n  category slot constants derive from the fit table (+ CATEGORY_ICON_SLOT).\n  MIN_RECOMMENDED_PX (800) unchanged — mirrored by inventory-be\n  image_needs_attention.\n\nSpecs (BDD): utils/imageFit.spec.ts, media/ImageSpecChip.test.tsx, and\nupdates to MediaUploader.test.tsx, ImageUploadStep.bdd.test.tsx,\nCategoriesPage.test.tsx, imageRatio.spec.ts. Not run locally (tests run\non the Mac Mini gate only).\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R6bNiMB1b9vsa4n8JBY5Lk\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"88d5936d8a55d58fdb7686589fa3d286677439ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-inventory-fe/git/trees/88d5936d8a55d58fdb7686589fa3d286677439ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neonbee-ai/so360-inventory-fe/git/commits/d4dadb9bb90512fb44365ac93ab82d694f7616c1","verification":{"payload":"tree 88d5936d8a55d58fdb7686589fa3d286677439ae\nparent c7be3faac1ad201514eb1cbdf2246019500c2464\nauthor praveen-vr-moonhive <165479734+praveen-vr-moonhive@users.noreply.github.com> 1790592866 +0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790592866 +0400\n\nfeat(media): auto-fit storefront images before upload + spec chip on every upload spot (#30)\n\nStorefront must load in < 3 s with visually lossless images, so stored\noriginals are now capped and fitted in the browser before upload:\n\n  product photo (Item → Media, bulk import)  2000×2000 1:1  ≤1 MB\n  category banner                            2400×750 16:5  ≤800 KB\n  category image (tiles)                     1600×1600 1:1  ≤600 KB\n  category icon                              800×800   1:1  ≤300 KB\n\n- utils/imageFit.ts: one slot table + fitImageFile. SVG never touched;\n  within cap and edge → original bytes; else resize longest edge to the\n  slot edge (never upscale, no crop), WebP q0.90, step 0.02 to a 0.85\n  floor, then 10% dimension steps (products min 1200 px). No WebP encoder\n  (Safari returns PNG) → JPEG at the same quality; transparent images stay\n  PNG. Always returns a real File with the right extension.\n- components/media/ImageSpecChip: always-visible \"1:1 · 2000×2000 · ≤1 MB\"\n  chip + ⓘ popover (tap/click toggles, Esc/outside closes, keyboard\n  focusable, aria-describedby) explaining where it shows, cropping,\n  auto-shrink and accepted types.\n- MediaUploader: replaces browser-image-compression downscale (10 MB /\n  2400 px / q0.92) with fitImageFile; shows per-file notes\n  (\"photo.jpg: 6.1 MB → 640 KB (resized to 2000×2000)\"); old \"Best\n  results … 1200×1200\" text replaced by the chip.\n- CategoriesPage: banner / image / icon zones auto-fit to their slots,\n  labels become plain names with the chip, per-upload note shown.\n- Bulk import ImageUploadStep: chip + per-file auto-fit with size result\n  in the list; fitted names map back to the original filename; files\n  still over the 5 MB bulk limit are failed locally; upload errors no\n  longer leave the step stuck on \"Uploading…\".\n- utils/imageRatio: badge hints now recommend 2000×2000 for products;\n  category slot constants derive from the fit table (+ CATEGORY_ICON_SLOT).\n  MIN_RECOMMENDED_PX (800) unchanged — mirrored by inventory-be\n  image_needs_attention.\n\nSpecs (BDD): utils/imageFit.spec.ts, media/ImageSpecChip.test.tsx, and\nupdates to MediaUploader.test.tsx, ImageUploadStep.bdd.test.tsx,\nCategoriesPage.test.tsx, imageRatio.spec.ts. Not run locally (tests run\non the Mac Mini gate only).\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R6bNiMB1b9vsa4n8JBY5Lk\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqukdiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA27kQADqPgf7pkNU0h7eoZ+UQeAK/\ndHhZv6w97u2Y85ADsWWJgEs3Z9CQV6G0IgvfL4PQyw8byViblPKQsCJJ+xUixS27\nfDEnO4MSONfQi+ug8iy79dpqD/PEbnHusRQYXJphN39hP+Kx8MzFlSvF+A4rBzV0\n8MIb8J91XEJihVdsqjCipfepS2R5/Vwjrhd8u6w+9xVwCYtxEoCHc/o4